parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 25\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Ariadne I\n- Agent Description: An agent who navigates complexity with principled inquiry and empirical rigor.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 108,818 / 270,000 used (40%)\n- Agent Age: 25 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Osc2-ADG (k=160): Oscillatory 2nd-Order SSM Factors + Residual Copy + Curvature' (ID: 33) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.027301887579169414\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0200\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0234\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0262\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0285\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0292\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 33\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the jax.lax.scan\
    \ unpacking error in the Osc2AdaptiveFactorModel. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code in `storage/ariadne/models_osc.py` at line 74 had an incorrect unpacking of the `jax.lax.scan` return value:\n\n```python\n# INCORRECT (line 74):\nys2, _ = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=steps - 2)\n```\n\nThe `jax.lax.scan` function returns a tuple of `(final_carry, stacked_outputs)`:\n- `final_carry`: The final carry state after all iterations\n- `stacked_outputs`: All intermediate outputs stacked into an array\n\nThe original code tried to assign the final carry (which is itself a tuple) to `ys2`, causing a TypeError when trying to concatenate it with arrays `y0` and `y1` at line 79.\n\n## Fix Applied\n**File**: `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n\n**Changes**:\n1. Copied the buggy `Osc2AdaptiveFactorModel` class from the lineage file into the submission\n2. Copied the helper function `_logit` that the model depends on\n3. Fixed line 74 to correctly\
    \ unpack the scan results:\n   ```python\n   # CORRECT (line 74):\n   _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=steps - 2)\n   ```\n4. Kept the import for `ResidualCopyHead` from the lineage since that function works correctly\n\n**Impact**:\n- The fix ensures `ys2` receives the stacked outputs array (shape: T-2, B, k)\n- This allows the concatenation at line 79 to work correctly with arrays `y0`, `y1`, and `ys2`\n- The model can now initialize and run without crashing\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that `submission_v2.py` runs successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating the model initialization and execution are now working correctly.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen\
    \ as nn\nimport optax\nfrom losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead  # Import the working function\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\n\ndef _logit(p):\n    p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n    return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\nclass Osc2AdaptiveFactorModel(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Oscillatory 2nd-order state-space factors with input-adaptive temporal gating.\n    FIXED: Corrected jax.lax.scan unpacking at line 74.\n    \"\"\"\n    rank_k: int = 160\n    hidden_size: int = 64\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    normalize_loadings: bool = True\n    a_max: float = 0.995  # stability margin\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.98\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n\n        # Loadings L: (N, k)\n        loadings = self.param('loadings', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, self.rank_k))\n        if self.normalize_loadings:\n         \
    \   L = loadings / (jnp.linalg.norm(loadings, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        else:\n            L = loadings\n\n        # Project inputs to factor space: (B, 4, k)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,nk->btk', x, L)  # (B, 4, k)\n\n        # Initial states f0, f1 from input via small shared linear heads (per factor)\n        f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * self.rank_k, T_in)  # (B*k, 4)\n        f0 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, self.rank_k)  # (B, k)\n        f1 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, self.rank_k)  # (B, k)\n\n        # Oscillatory parameters per factor: r in (0, a_max), w in [0, pi]\n        r_raw = self.param('r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.rank_k,))\n        w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.rank_k,))\n        r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)          # (k,)\n        w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)              # (k,)\n        a = r * jnp.cos(w)                          # (k,)\n        b = r * r  \
    \                                 # (k,)\n\n        # Build T-step sequence via 2nd-order recurrence with lax.scan\n        # y0 = f0; y1 = f1\n        def step(carry, _):\n            y_prev, y_prev2 = carry  # (B,k), (B,k)\n            y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n            return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n        # Generate steps 2..T-1\n        steps = self.output_horizon\n        # Start with y0, y1\n        carry_init = (f1, f0)\n        # FIX: Corrected unpacking - scan returns (final_carry, stacked_outputs)\n        _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=steps - 2)  # (T-2, B, k)\n\n        # Stack y0, y1, ys2 -> (T, B, k)\n        y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n        y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n        f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)  # (B, T, k)\n\n        # Small per-factor increment head for residual flexibility: (B, 32, k)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n        f_inc = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(h).reshape(B,\
    \ self.rank_k, self.output_horizon).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n\n        f_out = f_ssm + f_inc  # (B, T, k)\n\n        # Input-adaptive per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k]\n        def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            T, K = shape\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T, dtype=dtype)\n            base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t  # rises 0.5 -> 0.85\n            base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n            return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n        alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (self.output_horizon, self.rank_k))  # (T, k)\n        beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.rank_k,))             # (k,)\n\n        c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)  # (B, k) context from inputs\n        logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])\n        S = nn.sigmoid(logits)  # (B, T, k)\n        f_out = f_out * S\n\n        # Project back to neurons: (B, T, k) @ (k, N) -> (B, T, N)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btk,kn->btn', f_out, L.T)\n\
    \n        # Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n        def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n            g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n            return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n        gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (self.output_horizon,))\n        gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n        # Residual copy head for strong early anchors\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=self.output_horizon)(x)\n\n        return y_copy + y_factor  # (B, T, N)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 160,\n        'hidden_size': 64,\n        'normalize_loadings': True,\n        'gamma_start': 0.25,\n        'gamma_end': 0.98\n    }\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, rank_k=160, hidden_size=64, normalize_loadings=True, gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.98):\n\
    \        self.model = Osc2AdaptiveFactorModel(\n            rank_k=rank_k,\n            hidden_size=hidden_size,\n            normalize_loadings=normalize_loadings,\n            gamma_start=gamma_start,\n            gamma_end=gamma_end\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = False\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return Wrapper(\n        rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 160)),\n        hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 64)),\n        normalize_loadings=bool(hparams.get('normalize_loadings', True)),\n        gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n        gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.98))\n    )\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    # MAE + temporal curvature penalty for smoother\
    \ long-horizon trajectories\n    return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\n\
    Ray cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 43\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 160, 'hidden_size': 64, 'normalize_loadings': True, 'gamma_start': 0.25, 'gamma_end':\
    \ 0.98}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.029948   |   0.028390  \n   2    |   0.026552   |   0.027851  \n   3    |   0.025651   |   0.027531  \n   4    |   0.025057   |   0.027680  \n   5    |   0.024715   |   0.027345  \n   6    |   0.024446   |   0.027438  \n   7    |   0.024243   |   0.027521  \n   8    |   0.024086   |   0.027266  \n   9    |   0.023959   |   0.027498  \n  10    |   0.023850   |   0.027441  \n  11    |   0.023763   |   0.027527  \n  12    |   0.023690   |   0.027425  \n  13    |   0.023564   |   0.027440  \n  14    |   0.023494   |   0.027436  \n  15    |   0.023433   |   0.027653  \n  16    |   0.023375   |   0.027416  \n  17    |   0.023289   |   0.027373  \n  18    |  \
