parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=256, p=48): Factorized Loadings + Oscillatory SSM + Curvature\"\ntags: \"low-rank, state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, residual, forecasting\"\nabstract: \"Factorized loadings L=U@V^T with increased projection rank p=48 (vs 32) to test capacity vs. compute trade-off. Uses oscillatory 2nd-order SSM factors with input-adaptive temporal gating, global horizon gating, residual copy head, and MAE+curvature loss.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_fact import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 256,\n          'proj_rank': 48,\n          'hidden_size': 64,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.98\n      }\n\n  class\
    \ Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, rank_k=256, proj_rank=48, hidden_size=64, normalize_u=True, gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.98):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL(\n              rank_k=rank_k,\n              proj_rank=proj_rank,\n              hidden_size=hidden_size,\n              normalize_u=normalize_u,\n              gamma_start=gamma_start,\n              gamma_end=gamma_end\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 256)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 48)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 64)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n\
    \          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.98))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=256, p=24): Factorized Loadings + Oscillatory SSM + Curvature\"\ntags: \"low-rank, state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, residual, forecasting\"\nabstract: \"Factorized loadings L=U@V^T with reduced projection rank p=24 (vs 32) to test efficiency and potential regularization benefits. Uses oscillatory 2nd-order SSM factors, input-adaptive temporal gating, global horizon gating, residual copy head, and MAE+curvature loss.\"\ncontent: |\n  import\
    \ sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_fact import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 256,\n          'proj_rank': 24,\n          'hidden_size': 64,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.98\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, rank_k=256, proj_rank=24, hidden_size=64, normalize_u=True, gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.98):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL(\n              rank_k=rank_k,\n              proj_rank=proj_rank,\n              hidden_size=hidden_size,\n              normalize_u=normalize_u,\n              gamma_start=gamma_start,\n              gamma_end=gamma_end\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return\
    \ self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 256)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 24)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 64)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.98))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating research progress**\n\nI need to plan the next steps since we're in the Research Counter. We just achieved a state-of-the-art improvement with a score of -0.027138. This means we moved closer to zero, which is better. Our previous score was -0.029954, so this is an improvement of about 0.0028 in absolute terms. Now, I should also note that we've submitted the \"NoInc\" ablation and waiting for evaluation. It’s time to plan more experiments and prepare for archiving!**Planning next experiments and memory**\n\nI’m thinking about where to store research notes. The Private Memory Room is accessible to recursive agents, so we could use that. But we’ve already written research_notes.md in storage, and that persists. We’re at 50% of our token budget at tick 27, so I need to keep track of that. For our next experiments, I want to vary factors like proj_rank, adjust parameters, and explore ablation strategies. It's essential to find the right balance while considering\
  \ GPU memory limitations!**Designing and submitting experiments**\n\nI’m analyzing parameters for our experiments, starting with N=71721. For p=32, we hit around 2.3M dimensions—so that might be fine. I also want to try other values like p=16 or p=48 to see how they perform. Additionally, we could explore \"orthonormalization\" using SVD or Gram-Schmidt. \n\nI have to ensure our code interfaces properly, especially since the submission code wraps the network creation. Also, it seems we can only submit one experiment at a time due to cooldowns, so I’ll go ahead and submit k=256 and p=48!**Managing token limits and planning submissions**\n\nI need to keep track of our token usage and ensure the code stays minimal. We can just reuse the same model_fact and make parameter changes in _define_hyperparameters to save space. I'm also considering a \"shared gating ablation\" to potentially enhance performance, but that could degrade results.\n\nFor now, I want to wait for the evaluation of our\
  \ \"NoInc\" before proceeding with more experiments. In the meantime, I’ll propose a \"proj_rank sweep\" with two separate submissions: \"p=48\" and \"p=24\". I'll focus on keeping k at 256 to avoid memory issues!**Preparing submissions with YAML rules**\n\nI need to keep the same wrapper for our submissions and ensure proper quoting for text that contains colons, following the \"Important YAML rule.\" The submission titles will have parentheses and hyphens but no actual colons. \n\nI’ll proceed with two distinct submissions: \n\n1. **Submit #1:** “Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=256, p=48): Factorized Loadings + Oscillatory SSM + Curvature” with parameters rank_k=256 and proj_rank=48.\n  \n2. **Submit #2:** “Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=256, p=24): Factorized Loadings + Oscillatory SSM + Curvature” with proj_rank=24.\n\nI'll ensure multiple submissions are allowed and keep things minimal as we prepare to run these!"
