parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write ariadne/research_notes.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Ariadne I — ZAPBench Research Notes (updated Tick 35)\n\n  Dataset: 71,721 neurons; input 4 -> forecast 32; primary metric: mean MAE (score = -MAE).\n\n  Recent best results (mean score, higher is better i.e., less negative):\n  - ID 51: Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=320, p=48) + V-OrthoReg — -0.02703096 (Val_MAE_32=0.0287)\n  - ID 48: Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=320, p=32) — -0.027052 (Val_MAE_32=0.0289)\n  - ID 47: Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=320, p=40) — -0.027099 (Val_MAE_32=0.0289)\n  - ID 54: Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=352, p=32) — -0.027085 (Val_MAE_32=0.0289)\n  - ID 43: Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=256, p=24) — -0.027132 (Val_MAE_32=0.0290)\n  - Older baselines around -0.02729…-0.02741.\n\n  Key insights:\n  - Factorized loadings L=U@V^T unlock larger k and consistently improved long horizon:\n    * (k=256, p=24/32/48) ~ -0.02713…-0.02716\n    * (k=320, p=32/40) improved to -0.02705…-0.02710; (k=352, p=32) ~ -0.027085\n  - Mild orthogonality\
    \ on V (projection basis) reduces redundancy and gave the current SOTA (-0.02703096 at k=320, p=48).\n  - Removing the increment MLP hurts (ID 40), confirming it is necessary alongside the SSM backbone.\n  - Curvature λ=1e-4 remains a solid default; λ=5e-5 did not help earlier in non-factorized setting.\n\n  Running experiments (pending):\n  - ID 57: k=320, p=32 + V-OrthoReg (mild)\n  - ID 58: k=320, p=32 + V-OrthoReg + mild horizon weighting (1.00→1.10)\n\n  Next plan (after pending complete):\n  - If 57 ~ 51: prefer p=32 for efficiency; tune λ_ortho_V ∈ {5e-6, 2e-5}.\n  - If 58 improves Val_MAE_32 further, consider slightly stronger horizon emphasis (≤1.12 max) while monitoring early steps.\n  - Small sweep on γ schedule (gamma_end ∈ {0.95, 0.98, 0.99}) at k=320, p=32 + V-OrthoReg.\n  - Optional: per-factor normalization of V columns at init; compare with learned ortho penalty.\n\n  Summary:\n  - Structured factor dynamics (oscillatory 2nd-order SSM) + factorized neuron loadings +\
    \ residual copy + mild curvature achieves strong long-horizon accuracy.\n  - Best so far: -0.02703096 (k=320, p=48, V-OrthoReg). Pending tests target matching/improving this with p=32 for efficiency and gentle late-horizon focus.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Deciding on next actions**\n\nIt’s tick 35, and I've built several models, improving my best score to -0.027031 (ID 51). The best score so far is -0.027052 (ID 48), which is worse. I realize that a lower (more negative) score indicates poorer performance, making my current best of -0.027031 preferable. The top score is -0.02703095988 (ID 51). We also have two experiments, 57 and 58, still pending results. I should consider updating my research notes and prepare for publication, but I'll need to wait until maturity reaches 50 ticks.**Planning next steps**\n\nI’m considering a useful step here: I might want to list storage info and write a small script for computing parameter counts. While the actions I need to focus on are through storage writing and research submissions, I’m also thinking about checking an earlier page, but it’s not essential. The prompt indicates we should issue station commands, and no instruction for replying to mail was given. With 68% of the token\
  \ budget used, I could add research notes on new results and think about adjusting parameters, but we have two pending tasks, so I can't submit anything yet.**Updating research notes**\n\nI could rank the models by score to see the updated leaderboard, which is already sorted. I should add updated research notes that include our latest plan: a sweep for lam_curv, modifications to the gamma schedule, and observations that p=32 shows the best performance. The improvement with V-Ortho suggests a slight edge too. Then, there's our ongoing experiment with ID 58. I’m considering adjustments like compressing U and exploring row-wise normalization, but I think I'll set that aside for now. First, I'll write a brief update in my research notes and then wait for results.**Preparing research notes**\n\nI could set the ranking score to get the updated list, but it’s already sorted. My next steps should definitely include writing updated research notes. I might also preview the running experiments list,\
  \ but that’s not crucial. I’m considering adjusting the page size to show 15 items, yet it’s not necessary right now. \n\nFirst, I'll write to the storage \"ariadne/research_notes.md\" with the latest results and plans. Since two experiments (57 and 58) are currently running, I can't submit anything new. Now, it's time to add those research notes!"
