tick: 36
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=320, p=32) + V-OrthoReg λ=5e-6\"\ntags: \"low-rank, state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, orthogonality, forecasting\"\nabstract: \"Best-capacity regime (k=320, p=32) with milder V orthogonality (λ=5e-6) to test sensitivity. Uses oscillatory 2nd-order SSM factors, input-adaptive temporal gating, global horizon gating, residual copy head, and MAE+curvature.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from models_fact import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 64,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.98\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self,\
    \ rank_k=320, proj_rank=32, hidden_size=64, normalize_u=True, gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.98):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL(\n              rank_k=rank_k,\n              proj_rank=proj_rank,\n              hidden_size=hidden_size,\n              normalize_u=normalize_u,\n              gamma_start=gamma_start,\n              gamma_end=gamma_end\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 64)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start',\
    \ 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.98))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x, lam_ortho_V=5e-6):\n      # Base MAE + curvature (λ=1e-4)\n      loss = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n      # Mild orthogonality penalty on V columns (V shape: [k, p])\n      p = params['params'] if isinstance(params, dict) and 'params' in params else params\n      V = p.get('V', None)\n      if V is not None:\n          gram = V.T @ V\n          I = jnp.eye(gram.shape[0], dtype=gram.dtype)\n          loss = loss + lam_ortho_V * jnp.mean((gram - I) ** 2)\n      return loss\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=320, p=32) + V-OrthoReg λ=2e-5\"\ntags: \"low-rank, state-space, oscillatory,\
    \ factorized-loadings, orthogonality, forecasting\"\nabstract: \"Best-capacity regime (k=320, p=32) with slightly stronger V orthogonality (λ=2e-5) to test redundancy reduction vs. bias. Oscillatory 2nd-order SSM factors, input-adaptive temporal gating, global horizon gating, residual copy, and MAE+curvature.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from models_fact import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 64,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.98\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, rank_k=320, proj_rank=32, hidden_size=64, normalize_u=True, gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.98):\n          self.model\
    \ = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL(\n              rank_k=rank_k,\n              proj_rank=proj_rank,\n              hidden_size=hidden_size,\n              normalize_u=normalize_u,\n              gamma_start=gamma_start,\n              gamma_end=gamma_end\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 64)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.98))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions,\
    \ targets, params, x, lam_ortho_V=2e-5):\n      # Base MAE + curvature (λ=1e-4)\n      loss = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n      # Slightly stronger orthogonality penalty on V columns\n      p = params['params'] if isinstance(params, dict) and 'params' in params else params\n      V = p.get('V', None)\n      if V is not None:\n          gram = V.T @ V\n          I = jnp.eye(gram.shape[0], dtype=gram.dtype)\n          loss = loss + lam_ortho_V * jnp.mean((gram - I) ** 2)\n      return loss\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Reviewing research progress**\n\nI need to focus on our actions at the Research Counter. We've just seen an impressive improvement in our best score, which is now -0.027011 with k=320 and p=32 using V-OrthoReg. This beats the previous baseline of -0.029954, indicating significant progress!\n\nHowever, we can't publish in the Archive Room yet since it's unavailable until we reach maturity at 50 ticks, and we're currently at 36. We can use Private Memory for notes. I'll also consider continuing experiments or analyzing results, while keeping tokens in mind. Additionally, we could experiment with tuning parameters and comparing settings.**Planning further adjustments**\n\nI’m considering some next steps, like tuning lam_ortho_V and trying per-factor normalization at initialization. There’s also the option to test a logistic base amplitude on S[b,t,k] or approximate orthogonality on the U columns, though we're already normalizing U. \n\nI think it’s worth checking if disabling\
  \ normalization improves performance. Additionally, I want to explore using AdamW with weight decay on V and possibly implementing a small L2 penalty on U columns to control scale. I’ll also look at tuning the orthoreg lambda to see what gives us the best results.**Planning experiments and logging**\n\nI’m thinking about running two experiments, but there's a limit of two concurrent pending tasks. Currently, we can submit both since none are running yet. I want to explore logging to STDOUT since it's used for training logs, although I can't change main.py. I could potentially print extra info from the test() or model functions, but printing from compute_loss is trickier.\n\nLet’s queue two runs for \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=320, p=32) + V-OrthoReg\" with different lambda values: λ=5e-6 and λ=2e-5. However, we need to modify compute_loss to accept the lam variable for that change.**Preparing submissions**\n\nI’m planning to write compute_loss with lam_ortho_V as a constant. I’ll prepare two submissions\
  \ and make sure we reference the models_fact module correctly. While we could also test gamma_end, let’s focus on lam sweeps instead.\n\nI’ll execute two actions to submit with YAML formatting, being careful not to exceed token limits. It’s important to remember that a lower negative MAE score is better, so higher values are our goal. For now, I’ll stick with the lam sweep, so I’ll queue the two submissions while keeping the concurrent limit in mind. Let's move forward!"
