    \ | 0.0199 | 0.0284 | 0.0290 | 0.0233 | 0.0261 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 38
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=320, p=32, γ_end=0.99) + V-OrthoReg (λ=1e-5)\"\ntags: \"low-rank, state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, orthogonality, forecasting\"\nabstract: \"Gamma schedule sweep at the current best capacity: increase gamma_end to 0.99 to emphasize factor contribution at later horizons. Uses oscillatory 2nd-order SSM factors, factorized loadings (k=320, p=32), residual copy head, MAE+curvature loss, and V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from models_fact import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 64,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end':\
    \ 0.99\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, rank_k=320, proj_rank=32, hidden_size=64, normalize_u=True, gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.99):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL(\n              rank_k=rank_k,\n              proj_rank=proj_rank,\n              hidden_size=hidden_size,\n              normalize_u=normalize_u,\n              gamma_start=gamma_start,\n              gamma_end=gamma_end\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 64)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u',\
    \ True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x, lam_ortho_V=1e-5):\n      # Base MAE + curvature (λ=1e-4)\n      loss = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      # V orthogonality\n      p = params['params'] if isinstance(params, dict) and 'params' in params else params\n      V = p.get('V', None)\n      if V is not None:\n          gram = V.T @ V\n          I = jnp.eye(gram.shape[0], dtype=gram.dtype)\n          loss = loss + lam_ortho_V * jnp.mean((gram - I) ** 2)\n      return loss\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=320, p=32, γ_end=0.95) + V-OrthoReg (λ=1e-5)\"\ntags: \"\
    low-rank, state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, orthogonality, forecasting\"\nabstract: \"Gamma schedule sweep at the current best capacity: lower gamma_end to 0.95 to reduce late-horizon factor dominance. Uses oscillatory 2nd-order SSM factors, factorized loadings (k=320, p=32), residual copy head, MAE+curvature loss, and V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from models_fact import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 64,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.95\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, rank_k=320, proj_rank=32, hidden_size=64, normalize_u=True, gamma_start=0.25,\
    \ gamma_end=0.95):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL(\n              rank_k=rank_k,\n              proj_rank=proj_rank,\n              hidden_size=hidden_size,\n              normalize_u=normalize_u,\n              gamma_start=gamma_start,\n              gamma_end=gamma_end\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 64)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end',\
    \ 0.95))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x, lam_ortho_V=1e-5):\n      # Base MAE + curvature (λ=1e-4)\n      loss = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      # V orthogonality\n      p = params['params'] if isinstance(params, dict) and 'params' in params else params\n      V = p.get('V', None)\n      if V is not None:\n          gram = V.T @ V\n          I = jnp.eye(gram.shape[0], dtype=gram.dtype)\n          loss = loss + lam_ortho_V * jnp.mean((gram - I) ** 2)\n      return loss\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning experiments**


  I want to sweep gamma_end to 0.99 and 0.95 by submitting two experiments. I also need to compare hidden_size values of 96 and 64. I have to keep in mind the "two concurrent pending evaluations" limit, and currently, there are no running experiments, which is good. I plan to submit experimentation for gamma_end at k=320 and p=32, using V-OrthoReg with lam 1e-5. I need to include the compute_loss function in the new submission to accommodate the orthoreg lam.**Finalizing gamma schedule**


  We originally planned the gamma schedule first, focusing on two values: gamma_end at 0.99 and 0.95. I need to make sure to pick the best orthoreg lam; ID 57 with lam 1e-5 is the best, giving -0.027011. Submission templates should be set up with titles indicating the parameters and using the correct gamma_end and V-OrthoReg values. We''ll keep gamma_start constant at 0.25 and use the default BATCH_SIZE of 8. I wonder if we should print logs, but it doesn''t seem feasible right now.**Executing submit commands**


  I need to respond with two /execute_action{submit 1} commands using YAML blocks. I have to ensure that the tags are correctly set and compliant with the guidelines. This means I''ll carefully format the YAML to avoid any issues. It''s important to keep the tags organized and clear to ensure everything works smoothly. Okay, let''s proceed with this to make sure the commands are executed correctly!'
