tick: 41
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write ariadne/models_fact_plus.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Osc2-CTX-FLoad+ : Factorized-loadings oscillatory 2nd-order SSM with context-adaptive dynamics.\n\n  - Factorized neuron loadings L = U @ V^T with U ∈ R^{N×p}, V ∈ R^{k×p} (p << k)\n  - Stable oscillatory 2nd-order SSM per factor with context-adaptive r[b,k], w[b,k]\n  - Per-sample, per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k] from input context c[b,k]\n  - Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n  - Residual Copy Head for strong short-horizon anchors\n  - Small per-factor increment MLP (4 -> 32) for flexibility\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead  # storage/ariadne/models.py\n\n  def _logit(p):\n      p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\n  class Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLPlus(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_size:\
    \ int = 96\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      a_max: float = 0.995\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n\n          # Factorized loadings: U (N,p), V (k,p) so L = U @ V^T (N×k)\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)  # column-normalize U\n\n          # Project inputs to factor space: (B,4,N) @ (N,p) -> (B,4,p), then -> (B,4,k)\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)              # (B,4,p)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)   # (B,4,k)\n\n          # Initial states f0, f1 from 4-step input via small\
    \ shared linear heads\n          f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)               # (B*k,4)\n          f0 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)  # (B,k)\n          f1 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)  # (B,k)\n\n          # Input context for adaptivity\n          c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)  # (B,k)\n\n          # Context-adaptive oscillatory parameters per factor: r[b,k] in (0,a_max), w[b,k] in [0,pi]\n          r0 = self.param('r0', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          r_ctx = self.param('r_ctx', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          w0 = self.param('w0', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          w_ctx = self.param('w_ctx', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n\n          r_b = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r0[None, :] + r_ctx[None, :] * c)   # (B,k)\n          w_b = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w0[None, :] + w_ctx[None, :] * c)       # (B,k)\n          a_b = r_b * jnp.cos(w_b)                                          # (B,k)\n          b_b = r_b * r_b      \
    \                                             # (B,k)\n\n          # 2nd-order recurrence over horizon with per-batch coefficients\n          def step(carry, _):\n              y_prev, y_prev2 = carry  # (B,k), (B,k)\n              y_t = 2.0 * a_b * y_prev - b_b * y_prev2\n              return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n          steps = self.output_horizon\n          carry_init = (f1, f0)\n          _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=steps - 2)  # (T-2,B,k)\n\n          y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n          y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n          f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Small per-factor increment head\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          f_inc = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(h).reshape(B, k, steps).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          f_out = f_ssm + f_inc  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Input-adaptive per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k]\n          def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n\
    \              T, K = shape\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T, dtype=dtype)\n              base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t  # rises 0.5 -> 0.85\n              base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n              return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n\n          alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (steps, k))              # (T,k)\n          beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))           # (k,)\n          logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :]) # (B,T,k)\n          S = nn.sigmoid(logits)\n          f_out = f_out * S  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Project back to neurons via factorized loadings: (B,T,k)->(B,T,p)->(B,T,N)\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)  # (B,T,p)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)  # (B,T,N)\n\n          # Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n          def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start\
    \ + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (steps,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=steps)(x)\n\n          return y_copy + y_factor  # (B,T,N)\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad+ (k=320, p=32): Context-Adaptive r,w + V-OrthoReg (1e-5) + γ_end=0.99 + H=96\"\ntags: \"state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, gating, orthogonality, forecasting\"\nabstract: \"Adds context-adaptive dynamics r[b,k], w[b,k] to the factorized-loadings oscillatory SSM (k=320, p=32), keeping residual copy and temporal/horizon gating. Includes V-orthogonality regularization (λ=1e-5) and curvature loss for long-horizon smoothness. Increment MLP widened to H=96.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\
    \n  import optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from models_fact_plus import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLPlus\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  # Orthogonality strength for V^T V ≈ I_p\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'v_ortho_lam': V_ORTHO_LAM\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, rank_k=320, proj_rank=32, hidden_size=96, normalize_u=True, gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.99):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLPlus(\n              rank_k=rank_k,\n              proj_rank=proj_rank,\n              hidden_size=hidden_size,\n              normalize_u=normalize_u,\n              gamma_start=gamma_start,\n              gamma_end=gamma_end\n   \
    \       )\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      # Base MAE + temporal curvature penalty\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      # V orthogonality penalty: ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n      V = params['params']['V']\n\
    \      G = V.T @ V\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Exploring orthonality in matrix dimensions**\n\nI’m working through the shape of V, which is (k,p). This indicates V has p columns, and I’m trying to figure out whether we need orthonality across p or k dimensions. It looks like V is in R^{k×p}. When computing z = einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V), it multiplies over k, so I guess p serves as a low-rank dimension. \n\nHmm, I might want to orthonormalize across k for reduced basis redundancy. My goal is to ensure V’s columns are orthonormal, aiming for V^T V  I_p.**Evaluating model adjustments**\n\nI'm thinking about adjusting the gamma parameters: improving gamma_end to 0.99 and possibly changing gamma_start to 0.2, but for now, I'll keep it at 0.25. I could also explore shifting gating shapes with a 2-parameter logistic function, but that adds complexity. \n\nAnother option is implementing a multi-frequency state-space model per factor, though it raises the overall complexity. I’m considering an improved model, \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad+,\"\
  \ with adaptive parameters, and possibly increasing k to 352 or 384 for optimization.**Adjusting model parameters**\n\nIt seems that increasing capacity didn't yield the expected results—in fact, the best improvement came from adjusting gamma_end to 0.99, resulting in -0.026976. To push that even lower, perhaps adding adaptivity could help us reach -0.0269. I need to ensure we have 24GB of GPU memory for sizes like N=71721, and using p=32 is safe.\n\nWhile k=320 looks good, I’m considering increasing it to 384, even though k=352 showed a slight degradation. I'll stick with k=320, p=32, and include context-adaptive parameters while maintaining the existing orthogonality regularization.**Tweaking initial states**\n\nI’m considering adjustments to the initial states of \"f0\" and \"f1.\" Previously, I used two independent Dense layers on flattened factors, but they end up sharing parameters more closely than I intended. To improve this, I could introduce a small convolutional layer with a\
  \ time lag, parameterizing f0 and f1 as a weighted combination of the last four steps. \n\nI’ll need to apply a 1D convolution with a kernel size of 4 to create two channels while being cautious about the shapes used, as my existing setup utilizes Dense(1) on a 4-dimensional input.**Proposing Osc2-CTX-FLoad-ARX model**\n\nI'm suggesting a new model called \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad-ARX\" that adds an exogenous input term to SSM recurrence to help capture external influences. Although it brings complexity, I’m considering a small vector for injection, but we might not need it since we already have an existing mechanism for per-step injection through the residual increment head.\n\nI’ll create or update files to introduce a new class, handle coefficient calculations, and ensure consistent shapes for y_t updates. I want to include the orthogonality penalty in the loss function and set necessary hyperparameters while keeping an eye on memory usage.**Refining model parameters and structure**\n\nI’m considering\
  \ edge cases when computing identity shapes and using JAX’s `jnp.eye`. The nested structure of \"params\" can get tricky, so I’ll write a helper function to retrieve the 'V' parameter safely. I need to ensure that the parameter retrieval aligns with our model's structure, utilizing `params['params']['V']` since it's straightforward.\n\nIn my code, I’ll implement the necessary shapes throughout the process, maintain the gamma settings, and keep different hyperparameters consistent. I'll also plan to package everything neatly for submission while adhering to YAML formatting. That should help streamline the process!"
