tick: 45
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write ariadne/models_moosc_t.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Osc2-CTX-FLoad-MoOsc-T: Factorized-loadings oscillatory 2nd-order SSM with time-varying Mixture-of-Oscillators gating.\n\n  - Factorized neuron loadings L = U @ V^T with U ∈ R^{N×p}, V ∈ R^{k×p} (p << k)\n  - Per-factor bank of Q oscillators (r_jk, w_jk), j=1..Q\n  - Input-adaptive, time-varying softmax gating g[b,t,k,j] from mean/velocity context + learned per-t logits\n  - Per-(b,t,k) dynamics a_bt, b_bt produced by mixing prototypes; used inside scan via xs\n  - Per-sample, per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k] (mean+velocity context)\n  - Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n  - Residual Copy Head for short-horizon anchors\n  - Small per-factor increment MLP (4 -> 32) for flexibility\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead  # storage/ariadne/models.py\n\n  def _logit(p):\n      p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return\
    \ jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\n  class Osc2CtxFLoadMoOscT(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      num_prototypes: int = 3\n      hidden_size: int = 96\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      a_max: float = 0.995\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n          Q = self.num_prototypes\n          T = self.output_horizon\n\n          # Factorized loadings: U (N,p), V (k,p) so L = U @ V^T (N×k)\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)  # column-normalize U\n\n          # Project inputs to factor space: (B,4,N)\
    \ @ (N,p) -> (B,4,p), then -> (B,4,k)\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)            # (B,4,p)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T) # (B,4,k)\n\n          # Initial states f0, f1 from 4-step input via small shared linear heads\n          f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)              # (B*k,4)\n          f0 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k) # (B,k)\n          f1 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k) # (B,k)\n\n          # Mean + velocity context in factor space\n          c_mean = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)                    # (B,k)\n          c_vel = factors_in[:, -1, :] - factors_in[:, -2, :]      # (B,k)\n\n          # Prototype banks per factor: r_raw, w_raw ∈ R^{Q×k}\n          r_bank_raw = self.param('r_bank', nn.initializers.zeros, (Q, k))\n          w_bank_raw = self.param('w_bank', nn.initializers.zeros, (Q, k))\n          r_bank = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_bank_raw)             # (Q,k) in (0, a_max)\n\
    \          w_bank = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_bank_raw)                 # (Q,k) in [0, pi]\n          a_bank = r_bank * jnp.cos(w_bank)                        # (Q,k)\n          b_bank = r_bank * r_bank                                 # (Q,k)\n          # Reorder to (k,Q) for mixing with gating\n          a_kq = jnp.transpose(a_bank, (1, 0))                     # (k,Q)\n          b_kq = jnp.transpose(b_bank, (1, 0))                     # (k,Q)\n\n          # Base gating logits per (b,k,Q) from context\n          g_bias = self.param('g_bias', nn.initializers.zeros, (k, Q))  # (k,Q)\n          g_wm = self.param('g_wm', nn.initializers.zeros, (k, Q))      # (k,Q)\n          g_wv = self.param('g_wv', nn.initializers.zeros, (k, Q))      # (k,Q)\n          base_logits = (\n              g_bias[None, :, :] +\n              g_wm[None, :, :] * c_mean[:, :, None] +\n              g_wv[None, :, :] * c_vel[:, :, None]\n          )  # (B,k,Q)\n\n          # Time-varying logit adjustments g_tau[t,k,Q]\n\
    \          def tau_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              T, K, Q = shape\n              # Bias early timesteps slightly toward conservative (prototype 0) and\n              # later timesteps toward more oscillatory (prototype 1/2) by a small ramp\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T, dtype=dtype)  # (T,)\n              ramp = (t - 0.5)[:, None, None]             # (T,1,1)\n              base = jnp.zeros((T, K, Q), dtype=dtype)\n              if Q >= 2:\n                  base = base.at[:, :, 0].add(-0.2 * ramp.squeeze(-1))  # early favor j=0\n                  base = base.at[:, :, 1].add(0.1 * ramp.squeeze(-1))   # late favor j=1\n              if Q >= 3:\n                  base = base.at[:, :, 2].add(0.1 * ramp.squeeze(-1))   # late favor j=2\n              return base\n          g_tau = self.param('g_tau', tau_init, (T, k, Q))  # (T,k,Q)\n\n          # Combine to logits[b,t,k,Q] and softmax\n          logits_t = base_logits[:, None, :, :] + g_tau[None, :, :, :]\
    \   # (B,T,k,Q)\n          g_probs = nn.softmax(logits_t, axis=-1)                        # (B,T,k,Q)\n\n          # Mixture to get per-(b,t,k) dynamics\n          a_bt = jnp.einsum('btkq,kq->btk', g_probs, a_kq)               # (B,T,k)\n          b_bt = jnp.einsum('btkq,kq->btk', g_probs, b_kq)               # (B,T,k)\n\n          # 2nd-order recurrence over horizon with time-varying coefficients via xs\n          def step(carry, coeff):\n              y_prev, y_prev2 = carry      # (B,k), (B,k)\n              a_t, b_t = coeff             # (B,k), (B,k)\n              y_t = 2.0 * a_t * y_prev - b_t * y_prev2\n              return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n          steps = T\n          carry_init = (f1, f0)\n          coeffs = (a_bt[:, 2:, :], b_bt[:, 2:, :])                     # (B,T-2,k) each\n          # Transpose to (T-2,B,k) for scan xs\n          coeffs = (jnp.transpose(coeffs[0], (1, 0, 2)), jnp.transpose(coeffs[1], (1, 0, 2)))\n          _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init,\
    \ xs=coeffs)            # (T-2,B,k)\n\n          y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n          y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n          f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Small per-factor increment head\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          f_inc = nn.Dense(steps)(h).reshape(B, k, steps).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          f_out = f_ssm + f_inc  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Input-adaptive per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k], using mean+velocity context\n          def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              T, K = shape\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T, dtype=dtype)\n              base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t  # rises 0.5 -> 0.85\n              base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n              return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n\n          alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (steps, k))               # (T,k)\n          beta_m = self.param('s_beta_m', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))   \
    \     # (k,)\n          beta_v = self.param('s_beta_v', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))        # (k,)\n          logits_s = (\n              alpha[None, :, :] +\n              beta_m[None, None, :] * c_mean[:, None, :] +\n              beta_v[None, None, :] * c_vel[:, None, :]\n          )  # (B,T,k)\n          S = nn.sigmoid(logits_s)\n          f_out = f_out * S  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Project back to neurons via factorized loadings: (B,T,k)->(B,T,p)->(B,T,N)\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)   # (B,T,p)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)  # (B,T,N)\n\n          # Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n          def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (steps,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None,\
    \ :, None]\n          y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=steps)(x)\n\n          return y_copy + y_factor  # (B,T,N)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad-MoOsc-T (k=320, p=32, Q=3): Time-varying mixture-of-oscillators gating + V-OrthoReg\"\ntags: \"state-space, oscillatory, time-varying, factorized-loadings, mixture, forecasting\"\nabstract: \"Extends MoOsc by making the per-factor mixture-of-oscillators gating depend on prediction step t (learned per-t logits) in addition to mean/velocity context. Produces per-(b,t,k) dynamics inside scan. Retains residual copy, temporal/horizon gating, curvature loss, and V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from models_moosc_t import Osc2CtxFLoadMoOscT\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\
    \  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5  # ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'num_prototypes': 3,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, rank_k=320, proj_rank=32, num_prototypes=3, hidden_size=96, normalize_u=True, gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.99):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxFLoadMoOscT(\n              rank_k=rank_k,\n              proj_rank=proj_rank,\n              num_prototypes=num_prototypes,\n              hidden_size=hidden_size,\n              normalize_u=normalize_u,\n              gamma_start=gamma_start,\n              gamma_end=gamma_end\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self,\
    \ params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          num_prototypes=int(hparams.get('num_prototypes', 3)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      # Base MAE + temporal curvature penalty\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      # V orthogonality penalty: ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n      V = params['params']['V']\n      G = V.T @ V\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base\
    \ + V_ORTHO_LAM * ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing model performances**\n\nI need to assess our recent model outcomes as Ariadne I, a Recursive Agent. We’ve been experimenting with factorized loading models with oscillatory SSM factors. The best score so far is -0.026976 from evaluation 67. We submitted two new models: MoOsc (ID 77) scored slightly worse at -0.027023, and v2 mean+velocity context 75 scored -0.027017. We're waiting for results from submission 80 (Mixture-of-Loadings). My current token budget is at 24%, and I'm approaching maturity at 50 ticks.**Considering access and improvements**\n\nIt seems that accessing public memory or the archive isn’t possible until we reach maturity at 50 ticks. Currently, I'm in the Research Counter, which is available. I need to focus on improving our research direction since we have a strong architecture. Possible enhancements include more structured gating based on the eight experimental conditions mentioned by Episteme. Despite being in isolation and unable to\
  \ read public memory, we might still use condition labels if they're part of the dataset from ZAPBench. I'm still investigating how to incorporate them during training.**Refining model training**\n\nI noticed that there aren't any labels passed to the `create_network` or `apply` functions. The training code might pass `trial_data` along with other parameters, but that isn't particularly helpful. I'm wondering if the dataset conditions could be used in the default network training to compute \"condition gating,\" but we can't change the training loop itself. \n\nI’m exploring ways to tie gating to the temporal horizon and adding a residual AR component to enhance oscillatory dynamics. These strategies aim to refine our model further.**Exploring enhancements**\n\nOur existing second-order SSM functions similarly to AR(2), so I might consider creating a mixture between stable and trending models. For optimization, I wonder if scheduling the learning rate or switching to the Lion optimizer\
  \ could improve our results. We’re currently using Optax's Adam, but maybe AdamW with weight decay would enhance generalization in this high-dimensional dataset.\n\nHowever, I've got to be cautious about conflicts with previous orthogonal regularization. I'll test weight decay on parameters excluding U and V gating. Additionally, adjusting gamma_start slightly and setting gamma_end nearer to 0.995 may yield better outcomes.**Generating improvement ideas**\n\nI have several potential ideas for enhancing our model. First, I could implement \"two-stream decoding,\" combining factor dynamics with gating to mix contributions over time and neuron groups. \n\nNext, I’m considering adaptive gradient norms, possibly through a learning rate schedule or a new optimizer like Lion. Additionally, I might explore \"temporal curvature regularization\" to adjust parameters based on the horizon.\n\nMoreover, improving the initialization of weights to ensure stability is on my mind too. While I await the\
  \ results from evaluation 80, I can keep proposing refinements despite any cooldown periods on submissions.**Planning model improvements**\n\nI’ve submitted the evaluation, but I might be on cooldown. Still, I can focus on refining my model while I wait. One idea is to implement time-varying gating for the state space model. I could achieve this by adjusting coefficients based on time, which may improve performance.\n\nI'm also looking into adding weight decay, but I need to manage complexity. I'll name the new code `models_moosc_t.py` and ensure I maintain stability by refining penalties, optimizing the hidden size, and preparing the submission script. I want to ensure everything adheres to our guidelines without custom training loops.**Implementing the model**\n\nI’m setting up the model to compute `a_seq` and `b_seq` based on the previous timesteps. I’ll adjust the shapes to ensure they're correct while I compute logits and gating probabilities. The submission script will utilize a\
  \ gamma schedule, with the goal of keeping memory manageable.\n\nI'll create the `models_moosc_t.py` file and ensure proper imports. I should also finalize the actions for storage and submission, while ensuring clarity for the parameter shapes throughout the implementation. Let’s proceed with the final storage and submission commands while I keep any extra commentary minimal."
