role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write ariadne/models_fload_dg.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Osc2-CTX-FLoad-DG: Factorized-loadings oscillatory 2nd-order SSM with\n  - Copy-decay gate over horizon (scales residual copy head)\n  - Tiny dropout on increment head for regularization\n  - Same core as best Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=320, p=32), with temporal and horizon gating\n\n  Components:\n    - Factorized neuron loadings: U ∈ R^{N×p}, V ∈ R^{k×p} (p << k)\n    - Stable oscillatory 2nd-order SSM per factor (r,w) with residual increment head\n    - Per-sample, per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k] from input context c[b,k] (mean over input window)\n    - Global horizon gate gamma[t] on factor branch\n    - Copy-decay gate copy_gamma[t] on residual copy branch\n    - Dropout on increment head (rate ~0.03) for mild regularization\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead  # storage/ariadne/models.py\n\n  def _logit(p):\n\
    \      p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\n  class Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLDG(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_size: int = 64\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      a_max: float = 0.995\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.03  # tiny dropout on increment head\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n          T = self.output_horizon\n\n          # Factorized loadings: U (N,p), V (k,p) so L = U @ V^T (N×k)\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)  # column-normalize\
    \ U\n\n          # Project inputs to factor space: (B,4,N) @ (N,p) -> (B,4,p), then -> (B,4,k)\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)              # (B,4,p)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)   # (B,4,k)\n\n          # Initial states f0, f1 from 4-step input via small shared linear heads\n          f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)               # (B*k,4)\n          f0 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)  # (B,k)\n          f1 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)  # (B,k)\n\n          # Oscillatory parameters per factor: r in (0,a_max), w in [0,pi]\n          r_raw = self.param('r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)         # (k,)\n          w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)             # (k,)\n          a = r * jnp.cos(w)                         # (k,)\n          b = r * r                                  #\
    \ (k,)\n\n          # 2nd-order recurrence via lax.scan\n          def step(carry, _):\n              y_prev, y_prev2 = carry  # (B,k), (B,k)\n              y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n              return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n          carry_init = (f1, f0)\n          _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=T - 2)  # (T-2,B,k)\n\n          y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n          y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n          f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Small per-factor increment head with dropout\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          f_inc = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          f_out = f_ssm + f_inc  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Input-adaptive per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k] using mean context\n          c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)\
    \  # (B,k)\n\n          def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              T0, K = shape\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T0, dtype=dtype)\n              base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t  # rises 0.5 -> 0.85\n              base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n              return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n\n          alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (T, k))  # (T,k)\n          beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))  # (k,)\n          logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])  # (B,T,k)\n          S = nn.sigmoid(logits)\n          f_out = f_out * S  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Project back to neurons using factorized L:\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)   # (B,T,p)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)  # (B,T,N)\n\n          # Global horizon gate gamma[t] for factor branch\n          def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n\
    \              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (T,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n          # Residual copy head with copy-decay gate\n          def copy_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              # Start near 0.98 and decay to ~0.82 across horizon\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              g = 0.98 - 0.16 * t\n              return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n          copy_raw = self.param('copy_gamma_raw', copy_sched_init, (T,))\n          copy_gamma = nn.sigmoid(copy_raw)[None, :, None]  # (1,T,1)\n\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n          y_copy = copy_gamma * y_copy\n\n          return y_copy + y_factor  # (B,T,N)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad-DG (k=320,p=32):\
    \ V/U OrthoReg + Copy-Decay Gate + DropInc(0.03)\"\ntags: \"state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, gating, regularization, forecasting\"\nabstract: \"Builds on the best Osc2-CTX-FLoad with factorized loadings and oscillatory SSMs. Adds copy-decay gating over horizon for the residual copy head, tiny dropout (0.03) on the increment head, and orthogonality regularization on V and U. Keeps γ_end=0.99 and temporal gating; trained with MAE+curvature.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from models_fload_dg import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLDG\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  # Regularization strengths\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5   # ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n  U_ORTHO_LAM = 5e-6   # ||U^T U - I||_F^2\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size':\
    \ 64,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.03,\n          'v_ortho_lam': V_ORTHO_LAM,\n          'u_ortho_lam': U_ORTHO_LAM\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, rank_k=320, proj_rank=32, hidden_size=64, normalize_u=True, gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.99, dropout_rate=0.03):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLDG(\n              rank_k=rank_k,\n              proj_rank=proj_rank,\n              hidden_size=hidden_size,\n              normalize_u=normalize_u,\n              gamma_start=gamma_start,\n              gamma_end=gamma_end,\n              dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n          )\n          # Dropout requires RNG\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          # Pass RNGs through\
    \ for dropout\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 64)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          dropout_rate=float(hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.03))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      # Base MAE + temporal curvature penalty\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      # V orthogonality: ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n      V = params['params']['V']\n      Gv = V.T @ V\n      Iv = jnp.eye(Gv.shape[0], dtype=Gv.dtype)\n      v_ortho = jnp.sum((Gv - Iv) ** 2)\n      # U orthogonality (columns): ||U^T U - I||_F^2\n\
    \      U = params['params']['U']\n      Gu = U.T @ U\n      Iu = jnp.eye(Gu.shape[0], dtype=Gu.dtype)\n      u_ortho = jnp.sum((Gu - Iu) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho + U_ORTHO_LAM * u_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering dropout and gating**\n\nI’m thinking about adding dropout to the f_inc head or gating, but I’ll need to set the network to require random number generation (rng) if I do that. There’s a detailed document in the Research Task description. I could include a small dropout rate of 0.1, which might provide a slight improvement—but honestly, we’re getting close to noise with these changes. The \"copy-decay schedule\" for gating might help, along with optimizing around U orthogonality, applying a penalty for that.**Exploring centered loadings and normalization**\n\nI’m considering if \"centered loadings\" can help by centering columns to a zero mean across N. Without neuron positional info, maybe it isn’t necessary, but adding normalization to achieve zero mean could be beneficial. There’s a memory consideration of O(N p), though. Let’s not forget about \"Z-normalization of factors_in per batch\"; I think that’s not advisable. The \"symplectic constraint\" for oscillations\
  \ seems useful, maintaining conditions like b=r^2. \n\nAlso, there's a thought about publishing a paper in the Archive Room, but it requires maturity, which isn’t possible until I reach 50 ticks.**Proposing new submissions**\n\nI’m working on two new submissions. The first one is \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad-DualGate,\" which will use base ID 67, U-orthoreg, and a copy gate schedule, with perhaps a dropout of 0.05 in the f_inc head. \n\nThe second variant involves making V orthonormal through parameterization with V=QR, using Householder or reparametrizing B as lower triangular. This is more complex with JAX. We could also consider adding \"weight normalization along the p dimension.\" I think keeping the modifications minimal is key, while focusing on the necessary penalties and defining Gv and Gu for loss computation.**Adjusting compute_loss and gating**\n\nI’m thinking about how compute_loss needs to import U and V from params, but in our factorized loadings, we've already defined U and V under\
  \ 'params' as model parameters. For copy gating, I'm planning to introduce the param 'copy_gamma_raw' with the shape (T,) and multiply y_copy by this gating, even though we only had gamma gating on y_factor before. There’s a risk of mixing both gating methods, which could be a problem, so I'll make sure to start copy gating high, near 1, and decay it, perhaps starting from 1 down to 0.85 for safety.**Implementing dropout and gating**\n\nI’m looking to add dropout in the increment head following the gelu activation, probably with a rate of 0.05, and a deterministic flag controlled by a training parameter. I need to ensure that we set network.needs_rng to True and handle rngs properly in the apply function. The idea of mixing dropout with the copy gating needs careful handling. I plan to implement a copy gamma gating schedule and manage shapes accordingly.\n\nOnce the dropout is in place, I'll create the new submission file with the adjustments. It’s essential to maintain stability while\
  \ implementing these modifications."
