- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=320, p=32, γ_end=1.00) + V-OrthoReg (λ=1e-5)\"\ntags: \"state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, gating, orthogonality, forecasting\"\nabstract: \"Base factorized-loadings oscillatory SSM (k=320,p=32) with temporal gating and residual copy. Sweep γ_end to 1.00 to maximize late-horizon factor contribution. Train with MAE+temporal curvature and V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from models_fact import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5  # ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 64,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end':\
    \ 1.00\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, rank_k=320, proj_rank=32, hidden_size=64, normalize_u=True, gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=1.00):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL(\n              rank_k=rank_k,\n              proj_rank=proj_rank,\n              hidden_size=hidden_size,\n              normalize_u=normalize_u,\n              gamma_start=gamma_start,\n              gamma_end=gamma_end\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 64)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u',\
    \ True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 1.00))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      V = params['params']['V']\n      G = V.T @ V\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=320, p=32, γ_end=0.985) + V-OrthoReg (λ=1e-5)\"\ntags: \"state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, gating, orthogonality, forecasting\"\nabstract: \"Base factorized-loadings oscillatory SSM (k=320,p=32) with temporal gating and residual copy. Sweep γ_end to 0.985 to\
    \ softly temper late-horizon factor magnitude. Train with MAE+temporal curvature and V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from models_fact import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5  # ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 64,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.985\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, rank_k=320, proj_rank=32, hidden_size=64, normalize_u=True, gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.985):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL(\n              rank_k=rank_k,\n              proj_rank=proj_rank,\n              hidden_size=hidden_size,\n              normalize_u=normalize_u,\n\
    \              gamma_start=gamma_start,\n              gamma_end=gamma_end\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 64)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.985))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      V = params['params']['V']\n      G = V.T @ V\n\
    \      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Draft: Oscillatory Factorized SSMs for ZAPBench\"\ntags: \"zapbench, forecasting, state-space, low-rank, gating, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Draft paper summarizing method, experiments, and insights for our current best-performing line: factorized-loadings oscillatory SSMs with residual copy and curvature regularization.\"\ncontent: |\n  Working title: Oscillatory Low-Rank State-Space Models with Factorized Neuron Loadings for Whole-Brain Forecasting\n\n  1. Problem\n  Forecast 32 steps of zebrafish neural activity from 4 inputs over 71,721 neurons.\n\n  2. Method\n  - Factorized neuron\
    \ loadings: L = U @ V^T with U ∈ R^{N×p}, V ∈ R^{k×p} (p << k), enabling k≈320.\n  - Factor dynamics: 2nd-order oscillatory SSM per factor y_t = 2 a y_{t-1} − b y_{t-2}, with stability via r∈(0,a_max), w∈[0,π], a = r cos w, b = r^2.\n  - Residual copy head for strong short horizons.\n  - Temporal gates: per-(b,t,k) gate S from input context and a global horizon gate γ[t] on factor branch.\n  - Loss: MAE + temporal curvature (λ=1e-4). Regularization: V-orthogonality ||V^T V−I||^2 (λ≈1e-5).\n  - Training: 3 seeds, early stopping; batch size 8.\n\n  3. Key Results (mean Val MAE; negative MAE score shown by system)\n  Baseline provided: Shared-Neuron MLP −0.029954.\n  Our line:\n  - ID 48: FLoad (k=320,p=32) + curvature → −0.027052\n  - ID 51: FLoad (k=320,p=48) + V-ortho → −0.027031\n  - ID 57: FLoad (k=320,p=32) + V-ortho → −0.027011\n  - ID 68: FLoad (k=320,p=32, γ_end=0.95) + V-ortho → −0.027081\n  - ID 67: FLoad (k=320,p=32, γ_end=0.99) + V-ortho → −0.026976 (current best)\n  Variants\
    \ (context-adaptive/mixtures):\n  - ID 73: Context-adaptive r,w (+H=96) → −0.027076\n  - ID 75: Mean+velocity context; γ_end=0.995; a_max=0.997 → −0.027017\n  - ID 77: Mixture-of-Oscillators (Q=3) → −0.027023\n  - ID 83: Time-varying MoOsc gating → −0.026995\n  - ID 80: Mixture-of-Loadings (J=2) → −0.027058\n  Early ablations:\n  - Remove increment MLP (ID 40) degrades to −0.027635.\n  - Dual-decay and simple LDS variants underperform (−0.02757 to −0.02730).\n\n  4. Insights\n  - Factorized loadings are critical to unlock capacity (k≈320) within memory.\n  - Residual copy anchors t=1–4; factor branch governs long horizon; γ_end≈0.99 best so far.\n  - V-orthogonality (λ≈1e-5) consistently helps by reducing basis redundancy.\n  - Richer context (mean+velocity) and time-varying mixtures provide small gains but not surpassing the simplest FLoad with tuned γ_end.\n  - Curvature λ=1e-4 is a robust default.\n\n  5. Next Experiments (queued/planned)\n  - Fine γ_end sweep around 0.985–1.00 on\
    \ base FLoad (submitted).\n  - Copy-decay gate + slight dropout on increment head (submitted; ID 85).\n  - If improvements stall, explore modest k± (288/352) with fixed p=32 under V-ortho, and lightweight per-factor LayerNorm.\n\n  6. Repro details\n  - Code modules in lineage storage: models_fact.py, models_moosc.py, models_moosc_t.py, models_fload_dg.py.\n  - Training defaults/system per ZAPBench; no custom loop.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Exploring experiment options**\n\nI’m looking at the next experiments. The time-varying gating got a slight improvement to -0.026995, but it's still not as good as ID 67. I wonder if it helps with interpretability rather than actual improvements. I'm considering fine-tuning the γ_end around 0.995 to 1.0 for MoOsc-T, and maybe adjusting curvature strength lam for MAE+curvature. It seems like dropout may hinder performance, so adjusting that could be important too. Lastly, I might increase hidden_size H from 64 to 96 for FLoad.**Adjusting experiment parameters**\n\nI'm planning to keep the hidden size at 64. For per-factor gating, I'm thinking of changing the initial schedule from a range of 0.5 to 0.85 to perhaps 0.6 to 0.9, which might enhance performance in later horizons. Increasing p from 32 to 40 or 48 didn’t yield better results, except for 48 with orthogonal adjustments scoring -0.027031. I’m also considering using the dataset's condition labels to enable per-condition\
  \ gating, but it looks like I can’t access those during training.**Exploring smoother outputs**\n\nI realize I can embed condition inference from x since we already compute mean and velocity across inputs and use gating. I’m thinking of regularizing the difference between consecutive outputs to encourage smoother results, which the curvature regularization already addresses. \n\nAnother potential improvement could be adding an \"AR residual\" path to copy a decayed AR coefficient across 32 steps. I can't modify the existing ResidualCopyHead, but I could create my own \"ResidualARHead\" in the submission script, which should help keep the code minimal.**Considering model improvements**\n\nThe state-of-the-art (SOTA) performance improved with γ_end set to 0.99, but there might not be much room left for further improvement. One idea is to implement per-factor normalization of output magnitude using temporal LayerNorm, but training loop restrictions might prevent this. We can pass jnp normalization\
  \ within the network, but I wonder if nonlinearities across time could disrupt SSM semantics. \n\nAnother idea is parameterizing a and b as functions of a logistic mapping, based on context at time t. Considering we’re at tick 47, I could prepare for publication at tick 50.**Planning submission code**\n\nI need to revisit \"Token Management\" as we approach tick 50 and prune after cooldown ticks. I’m thinking of crafting the code for submission with models_fact. I’ll start with importing necessary libraries and defining the content as shown in earlier submissions like \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad.\" \n\nIt’s important to set gamma_end to 1.0 and ensure we include the V-Ortho penalty. I also want to create a clear submission name, like \"gamma_end=1.0.\" I’ll keep the message length manageable by avoiding lengthy bullet lists as I proceed."
