tick: 49
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write ariadne/models_fact_ln.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN: Factorized-loadings oscillatory 2nd-order SSM with LayerNorm in factor space.\n\n  Changes vs. Osc2-CTX-FLoad:\n    - Insert LayerNorm over factor dimension k before temporal gating S[b,t,k]\n      to stabilize scale across factors and improve long-horizon predictions.\n\n  Core:\n    - Factorized neuron loadings: U ∈ R^{N×p}, V ∈ R^{k×p} (p << k)\n    - Stable oscillatory 2nd-order SSM per factor with residual increment head\n    - Per-sample, per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k] from input context c[b,k]\n    - Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n    - Residual Copy Head for short-horizon anchors\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead  # storage/ariadne/models.py\n\n  def _logit(p):\n      p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\n  class Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN(nn.Module):\n\
    \      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_size: int = 64\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      a_max: float = 0.995\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n          T = self.output_horizon\n\n          # Factorized loadings: U (N,p), V (k,p) so L = U @ V^T (N×k)\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)  # column-normalize U\n\n          # Project inputs to factor space: (B,4,N) @ (N,p) -> (B,4,p), then -> (B,4,k)\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)              # (B,4,p)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk',\
    \ xU, V.T)   # (B,4,k)\n\n          # Initial states f0, f1 from 4-step input via small shared linear heads\n          f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)               # (B*k,4)\n          f0 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)  # (B,k)\n          f1 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)  # (B,k)\n\n          # Oscillatory parameters per factor: r in (0,a_max), w in [0,pi]\n          r_raw = self.param('r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)         # (k,)\n          w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)             # (k,)\n          a = r * jnp.cos(w)                         # (k,)\n          b = r * r                                  # (k,)\n\n          # 2nd-order recurrence via lax.scan\n          def step(carry, _):\n              y_prev, y_prev2 = carry  # (B,k), (B,k)\n              y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n \
    \             return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n          carry_init = (f1, f0)\n          _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=T - 2)  # (T-2,B,k)\n\n          y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n          y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n          f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Small per-factor increment head\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          f_inc = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Combine and LayerNorm over factor dim (stabilize scale across k)\n          f_out = f_ssm + f_inc  # (B,T,k)\n          f_out = nn.LayerNorm(axis=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(f_out)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Input-adaptive per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k] using mean context\n          c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)  # (B,k)\n\n          def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              T0, K = shape\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T0, dtype=dtype)\n\
    \              base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t  # rises 0.5 -> 0.85\n              base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n              return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n\n          alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (T, k))  # (T,k)\n          beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))  # (k,)\n          logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])  # (B,T,k)\n          S = nn.sigmoid(logits)\n          f_out = f_out * S  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Project back to neurons using factorized L:\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)   # (B,T,p)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)  # (B,T,N)\n\n          # Global horizon gate gamma[t] for factor branch\n          def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw',\
    \ gamma_sched_init, (T,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n\n          return y_copy + y_factor  # (B,T,N)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320, p=32, γ_end=0.99): LayerNorm in factor space + V-OrthoReg\"\ntags: \"state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, layernorm, gating, forecasting\"\nabstract: \"Adds LayerNorm across factor dimension before temporal gating in the factorized-loadings oscillatory SSM (k=320,p=32). Keeps residual copy, γ_end=0.99, MAE+temporal curvature, and V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5) to stabilize scales and improve long-horizon MAE.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\
    \  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5  # ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 64,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, rank_k=320, proj_rank=32, hidden_size=64, normalize_u=True, gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.99):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN(\n              rank_k=rank_k,\n              proj_rank=proj_rank,\n              hidden_size=hidden_size,\n              normalize_u=normalize_u,\n              gamma_start=gamma_start,\n              gamma_end=gamma_end\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n   \
    \       return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 64)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      # Base MAE + temporal curvature penalty\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      # V orthogonality penalty: ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n      V = params['params']['V']\n      G = V.T @ V\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n\
    \          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Exploring initial state tuning**\n\nI’m considering tuning the initial states mapping more effectively. Rather than using a linear mapping from the four-step process to f0 and f1, I could compute f0 and f1 directly from the last two inputs. This simpler method could enhance long-horizon stability, but I’m aware of the trade-offs in method complexity. It’s intriguing that all previous successes relied on gating and factorization, so perhaps incorporating the “condition” variable from the dataset is important, even if access to labels is limited.**Evaluating factor adjustments**\n\nI’m considering the idea of adding small per-factor AR terms that adapt from input to adjust parameters a and b globally for each batch. They tried context adaptation for r and w but didn’t see improvements. Interestingly, a time-varying mixture did improve results, getting close to state-of-the-art but not quite there. It might be beneficial to increase k beyond 320, even though a previous\
  \ attempt with k=352 showed worse results. \n\nI’m also thinking about conducting an ablation to test gamma_end values around 0.992 to 0.998 for confirmation. Since I noticed 0.995 and 1.00 both degrade results, 0.99 seems likely to be optimal. Focusing on paper readiness is key; with five experiments needed and many already completed, it’s a good plan to compute standard deviation across seeds and perform validation step wise. After they reach maturity tick 50, they can prepare the Archive submission. However, they won’t be able to access Archive until then, which is another detail to keep in mind!**Considering token pruning and model adjustments**\n\nI’m thinking about pruning tokens again after four ticks, since it’s been eight ticks since our last prune at tick 41. The current usage is 93k out of 270k, which isn’t too high, so we’re still in a good spot. However, I find myself wondering if we should explore a fundamental shift in our approach. Are we potentially overlooking the importance\
  \ of cross-neuron spatial structure? Our model captures global structure, but another agent utilized convolutional gating to focus on local aspects. \n\nOur current best performance is at -0.026976, but the state-of-the-art for other agents is unknown. I'm considering a simple addition: perhaps incorporating a second-order state driven by exogenous input residuals along with the initial states might help. Though, I can't seem to define the training loop yet; within the apply function, we process x (four steps) to produce predictions.**Exploring new model adjustments**\n\nI’m considering embedding x as a driving term through a predictor function f_inc. We already have a per-factor increment MLP that generates all T outputs from f_flat. Another thought is to apply convolution over time on the factor in/out, although we can't utilize a variable T_in. Instead, I could implement convolution within four steps to produce 32 steps using transposed convolution, but we’re already mapping with Dense.\n\
  \nI’m also contemplating spectral dampening across time that relies on predicted steps to enforce a slower decay. We have gamma[t], where 0.99 provides optimal gating amplitude. Another idea is to increase the hidden size of the increment to 128, as I noted that using H=96 led to degradation in performance. Additionally, I wonder about the orthogonality of U's columns; perhaps whitening U and adjusting V could help, though I’m not sure it will truly improve things.**Implementing LayerNorm adjustments**\n\nI’m looking at implementing factorized loading variations by normalizing U's columns. We can treat column scaling as a separate diagonal S parameter: L = U_norm @ diag(s) @ V^T, which would help manage scaling illusions with V. Another option is to apply spectral dampening over time based on predicted steps to enforce slower decay, using gamma[t].\n\nAdditionally, I’m considering per-factor LayerNorm or batch normalization across the factor space for standardization. I think applying\
  \ LayerNorm over the last axis for stability could help. I could implement a new model file that includes LayerNorm after f_out before projection while keeping the best settings.  \n\nThe aim is to craft code for the new model that maintains previous quality while integrating LayerNorm correctly, along with gating. I'll also focus on ensuring the model can manage dropouts effectively. Let's move forward with the implementation and submission!**Preparing function definitions and submissions**\n\nI'm focusing on implementing the function definitions. The _define_hyperparameters function will be the same as before, while create_network will return a wrapper and compute_loss will use curvature lam 1e-4 along with V-ortho. \n\nI need to execute the necessary commands to store the new model file and submit it, keeping in mind that there are currently 91 actions running, and I can only submit one to fill the concurrency limit. I'll ensure the LayerNorm implementation follows Flax's requirements\
  \ and correctly organizes dependencies without any unnecessary parameters. \n\nFinally, I need to be careful with YAML syntax, especially with tags and colons, so I'll quote those appropriately. Alright, let's go ahead and craft the submission!"
