parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320, p=32, γ_end=0.995): LayerNorm + V-OrthoReg\"\ntags: \"state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, layernorm, gating, forecasting\"\nabstract: \"LayerNorm across factor dimension in the factorized-loadings oscillatory SSM (k=320,p=32) with γ_end=0.995 to test late-horizon gating sensitivity. Retains residual copy, MAE+temporal curvature, and V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5  # ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 64,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end':\
    \ 0.995\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, rank_k=320, proj_rank=32, hidden_size=64, normalize_u=True, gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.995):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN(\n              rank_k=rank_k,\n              proj_rank=proj_rank,\n              hidden_size=hidden_size,\n              normalize_u=normalize_u,\n              gamma_start=gamma_start,\n              gamma_end=gamma_end\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 64)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u',\
    \ True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.995))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      # Base MAE + temporal curvature penalty\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      # V orthogonality penalty: ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n      V = params['params']['V']\n      G = V.T @ V\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Ariadne I — Meta Protocol\n  Goals:\n  - Solidify SOTA on ZAPBench with Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN; run clean ablations and finalize an archive paper.\n  Active Experiments:\n  - LN + γ_end sweep:\
    \ 0.985 (done), 0.99 (best so far), 0.995 (submitted), 1.00 (done).\n  - LN + H=96 (running: ID 95). If better, try H=80/128 for capacity sensitivity.\n  Next Up (queue when slots free):\n  - Optimizer: AdamW (weight_decay=1e-4) with LN (isolate effect).\n  - proj_rank p-sweep with LN: p=28/36 vs 32.\n  - Small a_max tweak (0.993 vs 0.995) with LN for stability.\n  Paper (Archive prep):\n  - Include ≥10 experiments with ID, mean MAE, and per-seed MAEs/std when available (IDs 67, 92, 93, 91, 83, 77, 75, 64, 51, 48).\n  - Ablations: remove increment MLP (ID 40), MoOsc/MoL variants, γ sweeps, LN vs no-LN.\n  Hygiene:\n  - Keep lineage modules consistent (models_fact.py, models_fact_ln.py) with Flax API fixes.\n  - Avoid stacking multiple changes per submission; isolate variables for clear insights.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating experiment requirements**\n\nThe \"Paper Guidance\" says that except for analytical papers, I need to include at least 5 experiments with evaluation IDs, mean MAE, and standard deviation. I can compute the standard deviation across 3 seeds since the evaluation logs show the best validation MAE per trial. For instance, for ID 67, the best MAE values were 0.027047, 0.026973, and 0.026909, leading to a mean negative score of -0.026976. I might also update storage to include the new LayerNorm API.**Considering modifications**\n\nI’m thinking about exploring some small modifications. For instance, factoring LayerNorm (LN) before gating might improve performance, and I might also consider gating after LN. Additionally, I could try a smaller a_max of 0.993 and possibly add L2 regularization or decoupled weight decay with optax.adamw. It could be worth revisiting the step-wise gamma_end fine-tuning with LN, trying 0.995. Also, there’s the idea of slight dropout on\
  \ factor outputs, though it could degrade performance. Lastly, we could consider V orthogonality without adding U orthogonality again due to previous poor performance.**Planning parameter experiments**\n\nI've confirmed a few updates to explore. For the H parameter in the increment MLP, using H=64 versus 96 could yield improvements; I'm currently testing H=96 with LN and can later look at 80 or 128. I also want to test a projection rank (p) of 36 or 40 while keeping k=320. A minor adjustment to the gating parameterization for the S-alpha base schedule might be useful, but it’s not essential. Using AdamW with a small weight decay of 1e-4 may offer benefits too. I need to draft a publication in the Archive Room showcasing at least 5 experiments, and include various ablation studies.**Managing advancements and submissions**\n\nIt looks like we're ready to mature and share our write-up in Public Memory, ensuring we keep it proper. I also need to manage our token usage, which is currently at\
  \ 43%. We should produce an assistant message with actions using /execute_action commands. I could write a module for the LN variant with the fix I already wrote. \n\nI’m thinking about submitting experiments with gamma_end values of 0.995, 0.98, and potentially 0.975 while considering the submission cooldown. Right now, ID 95 is running, and ID 93 has finished, so we can submit one more to have two running simultaneously. Additionally, I might submit the LN variant with proj_rank p=36, though that increases computation costs.**Crafting submissions and managing details**\n\nI’m considering slightly larger parameters, particularly with projection rank (p). Before, p=48 didn't perform as well, but with LayerNorm (LN), p=36 might work. I can test gamma_end at 0.99, but I should choose an additional submission. Maybe I should try AdamW with weight decay of 1e-4; that requires modifying the optimizer.\n\nFor now, I should submit the LN variant with gamma_end=0.995. I want to ensure we import\
  \ the LN model correctly. I should also prepare a skeleton for the Archive paper, including a table of experiments and relevant evaluation IDs. Finally, managing the meta prompt could help keep my tasks organized. I'll summarize my next actions and craft /execute_action commands accordingly.**Finalizing submission details**\n\nI'm ready to import from our LN model file. First, I’ll execute an action to set the meta prompt with a YAML TODO list. I might also want to create a draft skeleton in the Archive, but I’ll hold off on that to conserve tokens for now. \n\nSince we already have ID 95 running and 93 has finished, I can submit one more evaluation. I should include a submission for LN with gamma_end=0.995 and record the possible improvement in analysis text. I’ll keep everything concise with bullet points where necessary. Finally, I can compute and write the step improvements before finalizing."
