parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,H=96, γ_end=0.99) + AdamW (wd=1e-4) + V-OrthoReg\"\ntags: \"state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, layernorm, adamw, forecasting\"\nabstract: \"Test AdamW with weight decay 1e-4 on the LayerNorm + H=96 variant (k=320,p=32, γ_end=0.99). Keeps residual copy, MAE+temporal curvature, and V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5  # ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n   \
    \   def __init__(self, rank_k=320, proj_rank=32, hidden_size=96, normalize_u=True, gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.99):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN(\n              rank_k=rank_k,\n              proj_rank=proj_rank,\n              hidden_size=hidden_size,\n              normalize_u=normalize_u,\n              gamma_start=gamma_start,\n              gamma_end=gamma_end\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n        \
    \  gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      V = params['params']['V']\n      G = V.T @ V\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Optimizing weight decay and parameters**\n\nI’m thinking we should apply decoupled weight decay only to selected parameters or maybe just use AdamW with a weight decay of 1e-4 for simplicity and consistency.\n\nI also want to test a_max values of 0.993 versus 0.995. Currently, a_max is set at 0.995 as the default in our network class, but we don't pass it in create_network. If we want to test 0.993, we’ll need to modify create_network to accept it from hyperparameters. It might be easier to handle this in submission code by customizing the wrapper to include a_max.**Testing configurations and exploring resources**\n\nTo keep variables isolated, I’m planning to first test AdamW while keeping a_max consistent. I also want to compare proj_rank values of 28 and 32 later.\n\nI’m considering preparing a paper for the Archive once I have more results, and I might explore Public Memory to review others’ work, but time is a factor. \n\nFor now, I can adjust page sizes to rank\
  \ by score to see standings from other lineages. I’ve noticed that submissions are ranked, but to save tokens, it's better to focus on executing my next steps.**Planning evaluations for LN and AdamW**\n\nI’m planning to submit a new evaluation for LN with hidden size of 96 and AdamW weight decay of 1e-4. I need to adjust the code to define create_optimizer accordingly and set the YAML property while keeping the compute_loss function consistent. I might also want to ensure the BATCH_SIZE remains stable.\n\nIf I have another slot available, I could submit a second evaluation, but since eval 99 is already running, I’ll use this AdamW submission to fill the second slot.**Focusing on submission details**\n\nI’m planning to stick with one evaluation for now while making sure to maintain the rank score. I’ll also update models_fact_ln to fix the LN API; we’ve already implemented a fix in the code, but I could always copy the class into the submission if needed.\n\nThere’s the option to evaluate\
  \ \"p=36,\" but I can't do that yet due to concurrency. Once a slot is free, I’ll schedule it. \n\nNext, I need to craft the submission code with the title \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN + AdamW (wd=1e-4), H=96, gamma=0.99\" and include relevant tags. I can also integrate weight decay into compute_optimizer for optax.adamw.**Deciding on weight decay parameters**\n\nI'm considering whether to exclude bias and LayerNorm scaling parameters from weight decay, which is a common practice. Customizing weight decay for specific parameters requires using a tree_map to mask by parameter names, but this might not be supported in the Research Station environment. \n\nIt seems best to implement weight decay across all parameters, despite possible performance degradation. I think using a small weight decay of 0.5e-4 is a safer option, even though the suggested amount is 1e-4.\n\nNext, I’ll proceed with submitting an action, checking rankings, and producing the necessary code with the defined hyperparameters, while\
  \ keeping explanations concise."
