- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,H=96, γ_end=0.99, a_max=0.993) + AdamW (wd=1e-4)\"\ntags: \"state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, layernorm, adamw, forecasting\"\nabstract: \"Combine the best stability tweak (a_max=0.993) with AdamW (wd=1e-4) on the LayerNorm + H=96 variant (k=320,p=32, γ_end=0.99). Retains residual copy, MAE+temporal curvature, and V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5  # ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n\
    \          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, rank_k=320, proj_rank=32, hidden_size=96, normalize_u=True, gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.99, a_max=0.993):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN(\n              rank_k=rank_k,\n              proj_rank=proj_rank,\n              hidden_size=hidden_size,\n              normalize_u=normalize_u,\n              gamma_start=gamma_start,\n              gamma_end=gamma_end,\n              a_max=a_max\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size',\
    \ 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993)),\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      V = params['params']['V']\n      G = V.T @ V\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning the paper**


  I need to start composing a paper with at least five experiments, and we already have over ten to choose from. The Archive requires a capsule with YAML fields, so I have to create content that includes an abstract and detailed information. I''ll need to include mean values and standard deviations for the MAEs, computed based on validation data. It seems reasonable to note the best values per seed while ensuring the methods are detailed and properly cited. Let''s organize everything!**Continuing with experiments**


  I think it might be better to focus on running experiments first. I need to verify p=40 and consider improving AdamW slightly so it’s equal or better. I see that ID 100 has improved, surpassing LN with H=96. I could test combinations like AdamW with a_max=0.993 and gamma_end settings. Even though there’s a cooldown limiting me to two concurrent submissions, I see I have only 110 running. So, I can submit another experiment! I’ll keep an eye on tokens too.**Planning submissions**


  I’m ready to submit two experiments. The first one will be LN with H=96, a_max=0.993, and AdamW (wd=1e-4). The second will also be LN with H=96, a_max=0.993, but using gamma_end=0.995 and the default Adam optimizer. I want to avoid combining changes that will mix effects, so I’ll keep the tests separate. Also, I could consider small sweeps around a_max for better optimization. With only one slot available now, I’ll make sure to choose wisely!**Confirming submissions**


  I need to verify if 110 is the only active experiment. Running experiments only shows this one, so I''ll submit another with a_max and AdamW. Since we previously used the LN file, I should reference the models_fact_ln with the a_max parameter in the submission. I’m crafting a submission for "LN H=96, a_max=0.993, AdamW wd=1e-4." Adding the weight_decay parameter isn’t necessary, but I’ll write the code accordingly and submit it. Once that''s set, I''ll focus on implementing any related actions!'
