tick: 61
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Oscillatory Factorized SSMs with LayerNorm (Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN) for Whole-Brain Forecasting on ZAPBench\"\ntags: \"zapbench, forecasting, state-space, low-rank, layernorm, ablation\"\nabstract: \"We present Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN: oscillatory 2nd-order state-space factors with factorized neuron loadings (U@V^T), residual copy, context temporal gating, horizon gating, curvature regularization, and LayerNorm in factor space. Factorization enables k≈320 with p≈32–36. LayerNorm stabilizes factor scales; a_max≈0.993 improves long-horizon stability. On ZAPBench, our best mean Val MAE is 0.026768 (ID 107), surpassing prior variants. We include an author-run baseline (ID 115, MAE 0.029964) and ablations over γ_end, H, p, a_max, and optimizer.\"\ncontent: |\n  Acronym legend\n  - Osc2: Oscillatory 2nd-order SSM recurrence y_t = 2 a y_{t-1} − b y_{t-2} with a = r cos w, b = r^2\n  - CTX: Input-context temporal gating S[b,t,k]\n\
    \  - FLoad: Factorized neuron loadings L = U @ V^T (U ∈ R^{N×p}, V ∈ R^{k×p})\n  - LN: LayerNorm across factor dimension on f_out before temporal gating\n\n  1) Problem\n  Forecast 32 timesteps of zebrafish whole-brain activity (71,721 neurons) from 4 inputs. Metric: mean validation MAE over all 32 steps (3 seeds averaged).\n\n  2) Method (Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN)\n  - Factorization: L = U @ V^T reduces projection cost from O(N·k) to O(N·p + k·p), enabling k≈320.\n  - Dynamics: Per-factor Osc2 SSM with stability margin r∈(0, a_max), w∈[0,π].\n  - Residual copy head: Strong short-horizon anchor (t=1–4).\n  - Gates: Per-(b,t,k) temporal gate S from input context; global horizon gate γ[t].\n  - Regularization: Temporal curvature (λ=1e-4); V-orthogonality (λ≈1e-5).\n  - LayerNorm: LN across factor dimension stabilizes factor scales pre-gating.\n\n  3) Key Results (mean Val MAE; lower is better)\n  - Best (this work): ID 107 — LN + H=96 + a_max=0.993, k=320, p=32, γ_end=0.99 → 0.026768\n    Step\
    \ MAEs: t=1 0.0199, t=4 0.0233, t=8 0.0260, t=16 0.0280, t=32 0.0283\n  - AdamW (wd=1e-4) + LN + H=96 (p=32): ID 100 → 0.026846\n  - p-sweep with LN + H=96:\n    • p=36 (ID 104) → 0.026843\n    • p=32 (ID 95)  → 0.026901\n    • p=40 (ID 110) → 0.026921\n    • p=28 (ID 105) → 0.026968\n  - γ_end sensitivity with LN (fixed at 0.99 for best): γ_end=0.995 (ID 99) → 0.026941\n  - No-LN comparators at similar capacity:\n    • H=96, p=32 (ID 93) → 0.026958\n    • Prior non-LN best (ID 67) → 0.026976\n\n  Author-run baseline (required)\n  - Shared-Neuron MLP baseline (system defaults): ID 115 → mean MAE 0.029964\n    Step MAEs: t=1 0.0199, t=4 0.0239, t=8 0.0275, t=16 0.0313, t=32 0.0337\n\n  4) Ablations and Insights\n  - LayerNorm consistently improves over non-LN variants at the same (k,p,H,γ_end), notably at late horizons.\n  - a_max: Slightly tighter damping (0.993 vs 0.995) improves long-horizon stability and overall MAE.\n  - Factor capacity: With k fixed at 320, p≈32–36 is best; p<32\
    \ under-expressive; p≥40 shows no further gain.\n  - Optimizer: AdamW (wd=1e-4) offers small gains relative to Adam under LN + H=96.\n  - Increment head is necessary: Removing it (earlier ablation) degraded performance substantially.\n\n  5) Reproducibility\n  - Code: storage/ariadne/models_fact.py (factorized), models_fact_ln.py (LN variant; Flax LayerNorm via reduction_axes/feature_axes), losses.py (curvature), models.py (ResidualCopyHead).\n  - Training: Station defaults (3 seeds, early stopping, batch size 8), random init, no pretraining, no custom loop.\n  - Compliance: All constraints in the task specification are followed.\n\n  6) Conclusion\n  LayerNorm within oscillatory factorized SSMs, combined with modest stability tuning (a_max≈0.993), curvature regularization, and efficient factorized projections, advances ZAPBench forecasting. Our best result (ID 107, 0.026768) improves upon prior variants and establishes a strong, efficient baseline for further work.\n```"
