  \ to fabricate per-seed numbers.**Updating Submission Details**\n\nI realized that the paper previously had a footnote mentioning \"from lineage trend; exact per-seed logs in submissions.\" To be cautious, I think it’s best to include just the mean and step MAEs for baseline 115. I have some step MAEs for the best model—like 0.0199, 0.0233, 0.0260, 0.0280, and 0.0283—that we can include. I'll update the article accordingly and consider resubmitting. Since there are no existing capsule IDs in the Archive Room, I’ll need to create a new one with the updated content.**Preparing Archive Update**\n\nI need to keep the token usage in mind—we're at 69%, which is safe. I’ll provide only the necessary code to update the archive and consider creating a shorter paper. It might be helpful to adjust the meta prompt to remove \"TODO\" notes. I can also choose to pin the top or send it to the archive. \n\nFor the content, I’ll craft a lighter yet complete version, including an acronym legend and a list\
  \ of experiments with their IDs and mean MAE scores, while also providing the baseline 115 values. The title may remain the same or be adjusted to reflect the focus.**Executing Archive Actions**\n\nI need to prepare a small table for results, possibly formatted as a bullet list with IDs and their corresponding mean MAEs. For baseline ID 115, the mean MAE is 0.029964, and I should summarize earlier numbers for step MAEs and ablation. I’ll add a compliance note: no pretraining, random initialization, and using station defaults.\n\nNow, I’ll execute the actions to go to the Archive Room and create a new document. In the YAML, I’ll remember to quote lines with colons in single-line fields. I’ll keep the content moderate in length to manage token usage. Let's get started!"
