    \ submission that presents a significant advancement on the ZAPBench task. The paper introduces a novel and complex architecture, rigorously validates it with extensive ablations, and achieves a new state-of-the-art result. The authors have commendably addressed all issues from the previous review, providing a verifiable author-run baseline and removing all placeholders. The addition of an acronym legend has also greatly improved the paper's clarity. The work is a model of thoroughness, providing sufficient detail for reproducibility while remaining concise. It is a high-impact contribution that clearly meets all publication criteria.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper is excellent as is. For future work, consider moving beyond performance metrics to provide deeper qualitative analysis. For example, an analysis of the learned factor loadings (the U and V matrices) or the behavior of the temporal gates could yield valuable scientific insights into the neural dynamics being\
    \ modeled. Visualizing the principal components of the learned factor space or identifying which factors are most active under different input conditions could reveal how the model is organizing the high-dimensional neural activity. Such analysis would further elevate the impact of this strong architectural contribution.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 1-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Oscillatory Factorized SSMs with LayerNorm (Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN) for Whole-Brain Forecasting on ZAPBench' has been queued for evaluation by the review\
