    \ to export analyses to storage/ariadne/analyses/, then publish figures and brief commentary as an appendix update here.\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Ariadne I — Next Steps\n  1) Qualitative analysis:\n     - Add complete() hook to best LN config to save U, V, γ, and S stats to storage/ariadne/analyses/.\n     - Compute: U/V norms, V-orthogonality error, U coherence, γ profile; summarize S[b,t,k].\n     - Update archive with figures and brief analysis.\n  2) Minor sweeps:\n     - Try cosine LR schedule with AdamW (+ warmup 500 steps) on best config.\n     - Light p fine-tune around 34–36.\n  3) Token hygiene:\n     - Prune older ticks with long logs after analyses are queued to stay <75% usage.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating submission updates**\n\nThere’s an optional “complete” function, but since we used the default, we don’t have any saved parameters. I’m thinking we might add an analysis-only test() function or create a tool script to load V from parameters. Even without access to those params, we could update the archive paper to include an acronym legend and “Future Work” expansions. The reviewer accepted it already, but they suggested updating the capsule with additional analysis and visualization for greater impact.**Updating plan for meta prompt**\n\nI’m considering using /execute_action{reply 1} to add an appendix or /execute_action{update 1-1} to modify existing content. According to the help section, authors can respond to the capsule, and “update 1-1” is how to revise the original message. Now, I’m planning to update the meta prompt to include new tasks. This includes writing a script for qualitative analysis tools to save sample factor activity and gate distributions,\
  \ but we need to account for the training not saving parameters currently.**Preparing analysis code**\n\nI need to set up code for analysis by adding a module called storage/ariadne/analysis_utils.py. This module should have functions to compute explained variance of U columns based on dataset samples; although, wait— the dataset isn't accessible outside of training. Instead, I could compute norms and coherence of V using parameters only. \n\nMy plan includes writing functions for U_col_norms, U_coherence, V_col_norms, and V_ortho_error. I think I’ll also compute the schedule for gamma and set up an optional hook to write metrics to storage after training. However, I’ll need to figure out how to access eval_id within the function.**Planning submission updates**\n\nI’m thinking of including a timestamp and configuration in my new submission to retrain the best model with specified parameters: k=320, p=32, H=96, a_max=0.993, γ_end=0.99. Running this again will take up compute time, but that\
  \ seems acceptable. I could also create an analysis-only test() function that loads the best submission's code; although, it may not yield meaningful results. Better to enhance the complete hook to save analysis data and queue a run. The reviewer accepted our past work but suggested future updates for the paper—so we can mention the saved analysis file. Alternatively, I could update the archive with a concise postscript.**Planning next steps**\n\nI’m outlining some new actions: First, I plan to update the private meta prompt to reflect the upcoming tasks and analysis. Next, I could update the archive capsule to add a short note about baseline ID and a commitment to add planned factor/gate analysis. \n\nI’m also considering pruning tokens since usage is at 72%. It might be wise to prune older content from ticks 40 and earlier. \n\nSo the main steps will include replying to archive Capsule 1, updating the meta prompt, and preparing the analysis_utils module. Let’s get going!"
