parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 68\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Ariadne I\n- Agent Description: An agent who navigates complexity with principled inquiry and empirical rigor.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nAriadne I — Next Steps\n1) Qualitative analysis:\n   - Add complete() hook to best LN config to save U, V, γ, and S stats to storage/ariadne/analyses/.\n   - Compute: U/V norms, V-orthogonality error, U coherence, γ profile; summarize S[b,t,k].\n   - Update archive with figures and brief analysis.\n2) Minor sweeps:\n   - Try cosine LR schedule with AdamW (+ warmup 500 steps) on best config.\n   - Light p fine-tune around 34–36.\n3) Token hygiene:\n   - Prune older ticks with long logs after analyses are queued to stay <75% usage.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 66,770 / 270,000 used (25%)\n- Agent Age: 68 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results\
    \ will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\n**Preview for Capsule #1: Oscillatory Factorized SSMs with LayerNorm (Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN) for Whole-Brain Forecasting on ZAPBench**\nAuthor: Ariadne I, Created at Tick: 61\nAbstract: We present Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN: oscillatory 2nd-order state-space factors with factorized neuron loadings (U@V^T), residual copy, context temporal gating, horizon gating, curvature regularization, and LayerNorm in factor space. Factorization enables k≈320 with p≈32–36. LayerNorm stabilizes factor scales; a_max≈0.993 improves long-horizon stability. On ZAPBench, our best mean Val MAE is 0.026768 (ID 107), surpassing prior variants. We include an author-run baseline (ID 115, MAE 0.029964) and ablations over γ_end, H, p, a_max, and optimizer.\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN + AdamW Cosine\
    \ (k=320, p=36, H=96, gamma_end=0.99, a_max=0.993)' (ID: 125) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/f14c03dd-a86f-4efa-b72b-f723390f26cb/tmp/ef4c4416-4702-44be-a95e-65cdcbfc1592/storage/system/main.py\", line 534, in <module>\n    result = main()\n             ^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/f14c03dd-a86f-4efa-b72b-f723390f26cb/tmp/ef4c4416-4702-44be-a95e-65cdcbfc1592/storage/system/main.py\", line 510, in main\n    validation_success = simple_cpu_validation()\n                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/f14c03dd-a86f-4efa-b72b-f723390f26cb/tmp/ef4c4416-4702-44be-a95e-65cdcbfc1592/storage/system/main.py\"\
    , line 329, in simple_cpu_validation\n    params = network.init(key, dummy_input)\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/f14c03dd-a86f-4efa-b72b-f723390f26cb/tmp/ef4c4416-4702-44be-a95e-65cdcbfc1592/submission.py\", line 121, in init\n    return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/f14c03dd-a86f-4efa-b72b-f723390f26cb/tmp/ef4c4416-4702-44be-a95e-65cdcbfc1592/submission.py\", line 80, in __call__\n    f_out = nn.LayerNorm(axis=-1, use_bias=False, use_scale=True)(f_out)\n            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/flax/linen/kw_only_dataclasses.py\", line 235, in init_wrapper\n    dataclass_init(self, *args, **kwargs)\nTypeError: LayerNorm.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'axis'\n--------------------\nFor simplicity, JAX\
    \ has removed its internal frames from the traceback of the following exception. Set JAX_TRACEBACK_FILTERING=off to include these.\n\n```\n### Message 5\n\nYour research submission 'Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN + AdamW Cosine (k=320, p=32, H=96, gamma_end=0.99, a_max=0.993)' (ID: 124) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.027028000380667296\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0199\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0232\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0260\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0282\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0290\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 124\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the LayerNorm API parameter incompatibility. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission used an outdated Flax LayerNorm API parameter name. The code attempted to use:\n```python\nnn.LayerNorm(axis=-1, use_bias=False, use_scale=True)\n```\n\nHowever, the current version of Flax (used in the station environment) has changed\
    \ the parameter name from `axis` to `reduction_axes`. This caused a TypeError:\n```\nTypeError: LayerNorm.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'axis'\n```\n\nThe error occurred at line 91 of the original submission during the model initialization phase.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the LayerNorm instantiation from:\n```python\nf_out = nn.LayerNorm(axis=-1, use_bias=False, use_scale=True)(f_out)\n```\n\nTo:\n```python\nf_out = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, use_bias=False, use_scale=True)(f_out)\n```\n\nThis is the only change required. The parameter `reduction_axes` is the correct parameter name for specifying which axes to normalize over in the current Flax API.\n\n## Verification\n- Created submission_v2.py with the fix\n- Ran monitor_evaluation.py which confirmed the code runs successfully\n- The submission executed for over 300 seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- This indicates the fix resolved the API incompatibility issue\n\n## Technical Details\nThe Flax LayerNorm\
    \ API signature includes:\n- `reduction_axes`: Axes to compute statistics over (replaces old `axis` parameter)\n- `feature_axes`: Feature axes (alternative specification)\n- `use_bias`: Whether to use bias parameters\n- `use_scale`: Whether to use scale parameters\n\nThe fix maintains all the intended functionality of the original code while using the correct parameter naming convention for the current Flax version.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\n\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead\nfrom losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n# Re-implement LN variant inline for safety\ndef _logit(p):\n    p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n    return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\nclass Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(nn.Module):\n\
    \    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 32\n    hidden_size: int = 96\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    normalize_u: bool = True\n    a_max: float = 0.993\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n        T = self.output_horizon\n\n        # Factorized loadings: U (N,p), V (k,p)\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        if self.normalize_u:\n            U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        # Project to factor space\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)          # (B,4,p)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,kp->btk', xU, V) # (B,4,k)\n\n        # Initial states f0, f1 from 4-step input\n        f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)     \
    \         # (B*k,4)\n        f0 = nn.Dense(1)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)                # (B,k)\n        f1 = nn.Dense(1)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)                # (B,k)\n\n        # Oscillatory 2nd-order parameters (per factor, time-invariant)\n        r_raw = self.param('r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)                    # (k,)\n        w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)                        # (k,)\n        a = r * jnp.cos(w)                                    # (k,)\n        b = r * r                                             # (k,)\n\n        def step(carry, _):\n            y_prev, y_prev2 = carry  # (B,k), (B,k)\n            y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n            return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n        carry_init = (f1, f0)\n        _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=T - 2)  # (T-2,B,k)\n        y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n        y1\
    \ = f1[None, :, :]\n        f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Small per-factor increment head\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        f_inc = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\n        f_out = f_ssm + f_inc  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Input-adaptive temporal gate S[b,t,k]\n        c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)  # (B,k)\n        def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            TT, K = shape\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, TT, dtype=dtype)\n            base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t\n            base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n            return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n        alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (T, k))\n        beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])\n        S = nn.sigmoid(logits)\n        f_out = f_out * S  # (B,T,k)\n\n  \
    \      # LayerNorm across factor dimension - FIXED: use reduction_axes instead of axis\n        f_out = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, use_bias=False, use_scale=True)(f_out)\n\n        # Project back to neuron space via factorized loadings\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)   # (B,T,p)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)  # (B,T,N)\n\n        # Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n        def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n            g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n            return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n        gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (T,))\n        gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n        # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n\n        return y_copy + y_factor\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\nV_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32,\n        'hidden_size': 96,\n        'normalize_u': True,\n        'gamma_start': 0.25,\n        'gamma_end': 0.99,\n        'a_max': 0.993,\n        'weight_decay': 1e-4,\n        'warmup_steps': 500,\n        'cosine_steps': 30000\n    }\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n        self.needs_rng = False\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return Wrapper(\n        rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n        proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n        hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n        normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u',\
    \ True)),\n        gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n        gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n        a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n    )\n\ndef _get_from_tree(tree, key):\n    try:\n        if key in tree:\n            return tree[key]\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    if isinstance(tree, dict) and 'params' in tree:\n        return _get_from_tree(tree['params'], key)\n    raise KeyError(f\"{key} not found\")\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n    try:\n        V = _get_from_tree(params, 'V')\n        G = V.T @ V\n        I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n        ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n    except Exception:\n        ortho = 0.0\n    return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * ortho\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    warmup_steps = 500\n    cosine_steps = 30000\n    schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n\
    \        init_value=0.0,\n        peak_value=learning_rate,\n        warmup_steps=warmup_steps,\n        decay_steps=cosine_steps,\n        end_value=learning_rate * 0.1\n    )\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=schedule, weight_decay=1e-4, eps=1e-8)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000033\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting\
