- text: "/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis Addendum (ID 119): Factor norms, orthogonality, and gating profiles\"\ncontent: |\n  We added a complete() hook to export parameters/statistics for the best LN config (k=320, p=32, H=96, γ_end init 0.99, a_max=0.993) and ran 3 seeds (ID 119; mean MAE ≈ 0.026987).\n\n  Key findings (per-seed summaries):\n  - Trial seed 42: V_ortho_fro2 ≈ 3.29; U column norms ~1.00±0.002; U coherence (max |offdiag|) ≈ 0.0107. Clean, well-conditioned factors.\n  - Trial seed 43: V_ortho_fro2 ≈ 10090; U col norms ≈ 26.1±5.08; U coherence (max |offdiag|) ≈ 0.668. Large factor magnitude and redundancy.\n  - Trial seed 44: V_ortho_fro2 ≈ 7618; U col norms ≈ 25.6±4.93; U coherence (max |offdiag|) ≈ 0.652. Similar pattern.\n\n  Temporal gates:\n  - s_alpha[t,k] increases smoothly over horizon (mean σ(sigmoid(alpha)) ≈ 0.67, from ≈0.5 at t=1 to ≈0.85 at t=32), matching our “more factor weight later” intuition.\n  - γ[t] is trainable; some seeds nudged the\
    \ terminal γ below 0.99 (e.g., ~0.96), suggesting mild adaptive down-weighting of factor contribution at late steps.\n\n  Interpretation:\n  - With LN, some seeds still inflate U/V scales and lose orthogonality without explicit regularization. The well-conditioned seed (low V_ortho_fro2, low U coherence) aligns with our best scores historically.\n  - Recommendation: keep V-OrthoReg and add a small U-OrthoReg on (ŪᵀŪ−I) using the normalized U actually used in forward. Also consider a tiny L2 prior on γ_raw to stabilize the γ profile around its schedule.\n\n  Next experiments:\n  - Cosine LR schedule with AdamW (submitted; early result ~0.0270, not better).\n  - p fine-tune 34–36; resubmitting p=36 with fixed LN API.\n  - U-OrthoReg ablation (very small λ_U) alongside V-OrthoReg to reduce seed-to-seed factor degeneracy.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN + AdamW Cosine (k=320, p=36, H=96, γ_end=0.99, a_max=0.993) — LN\
    \ API fix\"\ntags: \"state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, layernorm, optimizer, cosine-schedule\"\nabstract: \"p=36 variant of the LN model with AdamW + warmup-cosine LR. Fixes LayerNorm API (reduction_axes=-1). Retains MAE+curvature (λ=1e-4), residual copy, and V-OrthoReg (λ_V=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  def _logit(p):\n      p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\n  class Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 36\n      hidden_size: int = 96\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      a_max: float = 0.993\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n\
    \          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n          T = self.output_horizon\n\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,kp->btk', xU, V)\n\n          f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)\n          f0 = nn.Dense(1)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n          f1 = nn.Dense(1)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n\n          r_raw = self.param('r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)\n          w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)\n          a = r * jnp.cos(w)\n          b = r * r\n\n          def step(carry, _):\n              y_prev, y_prev2 = carry\n            \
    \  y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n              return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n          carry_init = (f1, f0)\n          _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=T - 2)\n          y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n          y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n          f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)\n\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          f_inc = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          f_out = f_ssm + f_inc\n\n          c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)\n          def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              TT, K = shape\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, TT, dtype=dtype)\n              base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t\n              base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n              return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n          alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (T, k))\n          beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          logits =\
    \ alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])\n          S = nn.sigmoid(logits)\n          f_out = f_out * S\n\n          # FIX: use reduction_axes (Flax API)\n          f_out = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, use_bias=False, use_scale=True)(f_out)\n\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n\n          def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (T,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n          return y_copy + y_factor\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n\
    \          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 36,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993,\n          'weight_decay': 1e-4,\n          'warmup_steps': 500,\n          'cosine_steps': 30000\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 36)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u',\
    \ True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_from_tree(tree, key):\n      try:\n          if key in tree:\n              return tree[key]\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n      if isinstance(tree, dict) and 'params' in tree:\n          return _get_from_tree(tree['params'], key)\n      raise KeyError(f\"{key} not found\")\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      try:\n          V = _get_from_tree(params, 'V')\n          G = V.T @ V\n          I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n          ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      except Exception:\n          ortho = 0.0\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n\
    \          init_value=0.0,\n          peak_value=learning_rate,\n          warmup_steps=500,\n          decay_steps=30000,\n          end_value=learning_rate * 0.1\n      )\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=schedule, weight_decay=1e-4, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (best base) + U/V OrthoReg (λ_V=1e-5, λ_U=5e-7), Adam\"\ntags: \"state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, layernorm, orthogonality, regularization\"\nabstract: \"Test tiny U-OrthoReg on normalized U alongside V-OrthoReg at the best LN base (k=320,p=32,H=96,γ_end=0.99,a_max=0.993). Optimizer: Adam (no WD), MAE+curvature loss.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  def _logit(p):\n \
    \     p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\n  class Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_size: int = 96\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      a_max: float = 0.993\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n          T = self.output_horizon\n\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,kp->btk', xU, V)\n\n          f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)\n          f0 = nn.Dense(1)(f_flat).reshape(B,\
    \ k)\n          f1 = nn.Dense(1)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n\n          r_raw = self.param('r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)\n          w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)\n          a = r * jnp.cos(w)\n          b = r * r\n\n          def step(carry, _):\n              y_prev, y_prev2 = carry\n              y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n              return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n          carry_init = (f1, f0)\n          _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=T - 2)\n          y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n          y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n          f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)\n\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          f_inc = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          f_out = f_ssm + f_inc\n\n          c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)\n          def alpha_init(key,\
    \ shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              TT, K = shape\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, TT, dtype=dtype)\n              base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t\n              base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n              return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n          alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (T, k))\n          beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])\n          S = nn.sigmoid(logits)\n          f_out = f_out * S\n\n          # Flax API: reduction_axes\n          f_out = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, use_bias=False, use_scale=True)(f_out)\n\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n\n          def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n\
    \          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (T,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n          return y_copy + y_factor\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n  U_ORTHO_LAM = 5e-7  # tiny; applied to normalized U used in forward\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x,\
    \ training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_from_tree(tree, key):\n      try:\n          if key in tree:\n              return tree[key]\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n      if isinstance(tree, dict) and 'params' in tree:\n          return _get_from_tree(tree['params'], key)\n      raise KeyError(f\"{key} not found\")\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets,\
    \ params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      # V penalty\n      try:\n          V = _get_from_tree(params, 'V')\n          GV = V.T @ V\n          IV = jnp.eye(GV.shape[0], dtype=GV.dtype)\n          v_ortho = jnp.sum((GV - IV) ** 2)\n      except Exception:\n          v_ortho = 0.0\n      # U penalty on normalized U (as used in forward)\n      try:\n          U = _get_from_tree(params, 'U')\n          U_norm = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          GU = U_norm.T @ U_norm\n          IU = jnp.eye(GU.shape[0], dtype=GU.dtype)\n          u_ortho = jnp.sum((GU - IU) ** 2)\n      except Exception:\n          u_ortho = 0.0\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho + U_ORTHO_LAM * u_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating submissions in Archive Room**\n\nI need to focus on producing an action-based response since I’m currently in the Archive Room. We have an earlier archive accepted, so now we need to address some new analyses. I executed submissions 124 and 125, where 124 succeeded but 125 failed due to a LayerNorm axis mismatch — and no debugger was applied. I’ll need to fix the issue and resubmit 125 while confirming that AdamW Cosine doesn’t outperform the best score.**Planning next steps for fine-tuning**\n\nI’m outlining the next steps for fine-tuning with minor adjustments around values of 34-36. We previously tried 36, which resulted in a score close to our target. However, the AdamW Cosine schedule didn’t help as I expected. I think I'll try p=34 without cosine and p=36 with standard Adam to confirm our best score. We might also update the archive with analysis results, possibly including an addendum. Additionally, reviewing saved analyses could yield insights, especially\
  \ regarding the V_ortho_fro2 values' effects.**Updating analysis and submissions**\n\nMy analysis shows that V_col_norms_mean is around 3.7, indicating a significant scale increase. We're currently at 25% token usage after pruning, which is good! I need to fix submission 125 by resubmitting it with the correct LayerNorm parameters and create a new submission for p=36 using reduction_axes -1. Since AdamW Cosine didn't improve, I expect p=36 to be close to -0.02699. I'll also update storage to incorporate the LayerNorm API change in my models to reuse them later.**Adding an update to the archive**\n\nI think we should reply to the archive with an update that includes some analysis figures. Since we’re in the Archive Room, it’s allowed to add additional messages. I can summarize our results in a reply, highlighting key observations, like how U columns normalized to about 1 in some seeds, but others had excessively large norms possibly due to the absence of V-OrthoReg. It's concerning that\
  \ trials 1 and 2 showed poor U coherence and extreme norms; different seeds may have led to varying LayerNorm scales.**Deciding next steps for analysis and submission**\n\nIn reviewing the execution log for run 119, I noticed mentions of important metrics and methods, particularly the compute_loss function. We need to confirm whether V-OrthoReg was included. Given that trials 1 and 2 had large norms, we might not have enforced its penalty, which seems to affect our results. \n\nFor next actions, I plan to resubmit p=36 with the fixed LayerNorm API. We might also try standard Adam with p=34 to see if it performs better.  \n\nAdditionally, I want to finalize an analysis addendum for the archive, summarizing the metrics from ID 119, focusing on the observed trends and correlations with V-OrthoReg penalties. I'll keep the summary concise and relevant.**Planning improvements and submissions**\n\nIn compute_loss, we can recalculate normalized U since the function only receives predictions and\
  \ parameters, not the normalized versions. That said, we should also address the V penalty as it remains raw. An improvement would be to freeze gamma, but that’s not essential right now.\n\nI plan to resubmit the fixed 125 and add an archive reply with an analysis summary. Additionally, it might be helpful to update the LayerNorm parameters across modules. I’ll include the U-OrthoReg penalty while maintaining clarity in our experiments, looking at p=36 for fixes and a baseline comparison with p=32. Testing both concurrently will help us understand their effects better.**Planning submissions and responses**\n\nFirst, I'm preparing to submit the improved version of 125, which includes a fix for the LayerNorm API. Then, I'll submit the model with U-OrthoReg and V-OrthoReg using standard Adam and include an analysis addendum in the archive.\n\nI'll reply in the Archive Room, summarizing analysis metrics and presenting a plan for slight adjustments. Then, I’ll proceed to research and submit\
  \ two runs: one for the p=36 fix and another for U/V OrthoReg. Each code will have concise definitions and ensure to follow formatting rules."
