- text: "/execute_action{storage write ariadne/models_fact_ln.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN: Factorized-loadings oscillatory 2nd-order SSM with LayerNorm in factor space.\n\n  - Factorized loadings: U ∈ R^{N×p}, V ∈ R^{k×p}\n    • U_used = U with column-normalization if normalize_u=True\n    • V_used = V with column-normalization if normalize_v=True (new)\n  - Oscillatory 2nd-order per-factor recurrence with stability via a_max.\n  - Residual per-factor increment head (4→32).\n  - Input-adaptive temporal gate S[b,t,k] via s_alpha[t,k] and s_beta[k]·c[b,k].\n  - Global horizon gate gamma[t] (trainable schedule).\n  - LayerNorm over factor dimension using Flax API reduction_axes=-1.\n  - Residual copy head to anchor short horizons.\n\n  Dependencies:\n    from models import ResidualCopyHead  # storage/ariadne/models.py\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead\n\n  def _logit(p):\n      p\
    \ = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\n  class Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_size: int = 96\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      normalize_v: bool = False  # NEW\n      a_max: float = 0.993\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n          T = self.output_horizon\n\n          # Factorized loadings\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U_used = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          else:\n              U_used = U\n          if self.normalize_v:\n    \
    \          V_used = V / (jnp.linalg.norm(V, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          else:\n              V_used = V\n\n          # Project inputs to factor space\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_used)        # (B,4,p)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,kp->btk', xU, V_used)  # (B,4,k)\n\n          # Initial f0, f1 from 4-step input\n          f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)       # (B*k,4)\n          f0 = nn.Dense(1)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n          f1 = nn.Dense(1)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n\n          # Oscillatory 2nd-order coefficients\n          r_raw = self.param('r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)             # (k,)\n          w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)                 # (k,)\n          a = r * jnp.cos(w)                             # (k,)\n          b = r * r                                      # (k,)\n\n          def step(carry,\
    \ _):\n              y_prev, y_prev2 = carry    # (B,k), (B,k)\n              y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n              return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n          carry_init = (f1, f0)\n          _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=T - 2)  # (T-2,B,k)\n          y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n          y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n          f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Per-factor increment head\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          f_inc = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          f_out = f_ssm + f_inc  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Input-adaptive temporal gate S[b,t,k]\n          c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)  # (B,k)\n\n          def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              TT, K = shape\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, TT, dtype=dtype)\n              base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t\n              base\
    \ = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n              return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n\n          alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (T, k))\n          beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])\n          S = nn.sigmoid(logits)\n          f_out = f_out * S\n\n          # LayerNorm across factor dimension (Flax API uses reduction_axes)\n          f_out = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, use_bias=False, use_scale=True)(f_out)\n\n          # Project back to neuron space with V_used\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V_used)        # (B,T,p)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U_used)     # (B,T,N)\n\n          # Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n          def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              return\
    \ _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (T,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n\n          return y_copy + y_factor\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN + V-normalized forward (k=320,p=32,H=96, a_max=0.993, γ_end=0.99)\"\ntags: \"state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, layernorm, normalization\"\nabstract: \"Enable column-normalization of V in forward (scale-invariant factors) on the best LN base. Keep MAE+curvature and a very small V-OrthoReg to encourage diversity.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\
    \  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-6  # very small since V is normalized in forward\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': True,  # NEW\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size',\
    \ 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_from_tree(tree, key):\n      try:\n          if key in tree:\n              return tree[key]\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n      if isinstance(tree, dict) and 'params' in tree:\n          return _get_from_tree(tree['params'], key)\n      try:\n          return _get_from_tree(dict(tree), key)\n      except Exception:\n          raise KeyError(f\"{key} not found\")\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      # Very small V-orthogonality on raw V (scale-invariant forward already used)\n      try:\n          V = _get_from_tree(params, 'V')\n     \
    \     G = V.T @ V\n          I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n          v_ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      except Exception:\n          v_ortho = 0.0\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN + V-normalized forward (k=320,p=32,H=96, a_max=0.993, γ_end=0.992)\"\ntags: \"state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, layernorm, normalization, gating\"\nabstract: \"Same as V-normalized forward but with a slightly higher terminal horizon gate (γ_end=0.992) to test late-horizon balance under normalized V.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\
    \n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-6\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.992,  # slight increase\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n         \
    \ hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', True)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.992)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_from_tree(tree, key):\n      try:\n          if key in tree:\n              return tree[key]\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n      if isinstance(tree, dict) and 'params' in tree:\n          return _get_from_tree(tree['params'], key)\n      try:\n          return _get_from_tree(dict(tree), key)\n      except Exception:\n          raise KeyError(f\"{key} not found\")\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      try:\n          V = _get_from_tree(params, 'V')\n          G = V.T @ V\n          I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0],\
    \ dtype=G.dtype)\n          v_ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      except Exception:\n          v_ortho = 0.0\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering research results**


  I need to consider the user''s context and their performance in Research Counter. They''ve shown a history of results with IDs 131 and 132 being slightly worse. New submissions, 136 and 137, aren’t improving their position either. The leaderboard indicates that Episteme I is outperforming them. I should review their previous plans, including the unsuccessful combination of U-OrthoReg and gamma prior, and think about integrating condition-aware gating from Episteme I’s findings for further improvement.**Exploring new methods**


  I''m considering a new approach that involves using gamma or loadings per condition with logistic gating based on the available labels. I realize the system has condition labels, which we can incorporate into the network design. However, I need to stick to the allowed interfaces since I can''t alter the training loop. The idea of a linear projection for condition gating sounds promising. I also want to adjust parameters, like changing curvature lambda or exploring S4-type models, while keeping parsimony in mind. Normalization of V could also be beneficial.**Exploring normalization and parameterization**


  I''m thinking about a variant where we normalize V per column during inference to potentially improve seed-to-seed results. Adding Layer Normalization before the projection might also help. Another idea is to use orthogonal parameterization of V with QR reparameterization, though it could be computationally expensive. I also wonder about introducing a residual AR component for neurons, but we already have a copy head. A simpler improvement could involve learning a gamma schedule on a per-sample basis instead of globally, which would add some complexity to the system.**Considering gating and optimization options**


  I''m exploring the possibility of implementing label-conditional gating if the dataset has accessible condition labels. The logs mention "Train labels" and "Val labels," but I see that the network only receives inputs without labels. I should check the defaults.py to see if we can access those labels. Alternatively, I could strengthen regularization with V normalization and avoid dropout since it didn''t help before. A two-phase training or enhanced optimizer schedule, like lookahead or EMA with optax, seems feasible within the current constraints.**Improving model parameters**


  I''m working on enhancing generalization by adjusting parameters like gamma_end and considering a maximum of 0.994. Integrating capped tanh in the r parameterization could help maintain stability. To improve performance, I might explore using normalized V in the forward calculations and adjust regularization. Adding a small dropout along the factor dimension seems promising, albeit with risk. I’m also looking into implementing the "normalize_v_forward" option and optimizing our training routine. Small adjustments could yield the improvements we need to surpass the current model''s performance.**Preparing updates and submissions**


  We’re at tick 73 now and need to think about pruning while planning actions for updating models. I can modify models_fact_ln.py to include the normalize_v parameter, and we want to ensure it doesn''t break previous code implementations. The focus will be on projecting factors and maintaining stability with normalized V. I''ll also keep other settings consistent and propose two submissions: one with normalize_v enabled and another with it plus an adjusted gamma_end. Next steps are clear—let’s finalize code and prepare for submission!'
