- text: "/execute_action{storage write ariadne/models_fact_ln.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN: Factorized-loadings oscillatory 2nd-order SSM with LayerNorm in factor space.\n\n  Options:\n  - normalize_u: column-normalize U in forward\n  - normalize_v: column-normalize V in forward (new; scale-invariant factors)\n  - ln_before_gating: apply LayerNorm before temporal gating (new; default False = after gating)\n\n  Components:\n  - Factorized loadings U ∈ R^{N×p}, V ∈ R^{k×p}\n  - Oscillatory 2nd-order recurrence per factor (stable via a_max)\n  - Small per-factor increment head (4→32)\n  - Input-adaptive temporal gate S[b,t,k]\n  - Global horizon gate gamma[t] (trainable)\n  - LayerNorm across factor dimension (Flax API: reduction_axes=-1)\n  - Residual copy head for strong short-horizon anchor\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead\n\n  def _logit(p):\n      p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n\
    \      return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\n  class Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_size: int = 96\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      normalize_v: bool = False\n      ln_before_gating: bool = False\n      a_max: float = 0.993\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n          T = self.output_horizon\n\n          # Factorized loadings\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U_used = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          else:\n              U_used = U\n          if self.normalize_v:\n     \
    \         V_used = V / (jnp.linalg.norm(V, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          else:\n              V_used = V\n\n          # Project inputs to factor space\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_used)         # (B,4,p)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,kp->btk', xU, V_used) # (B,4,k)\n\n          # Initial states f0, f1 from 4-step input\n          f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)           # (B*k,4)\n          f0 = nn.Dense(1)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n          f1 = nn.Dense(1)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n\n          # Oscillatory 2nd-order coefficients\n          r_raw = self.param('r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)\n          w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)\n          a = r * jnp.cos(w)\n          b = r * r\n\n          def step(carry, _):\n              y_prev, y_prev2 = carry\n              y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n\
    \              return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n          carry_init = (f1, f0)\n          _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=T - 2)  # (T-2,B,k)\n          y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n          y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n          f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Per-factor increment head\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          f_inc = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Combine SSM + increment\n          f_comb = f_ssm + f_inc  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Input-adaptive temporal gate S[b,t,k]\n          c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)  # (B,k)\n\n          def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              TT, K = shape\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, TT, dtype=dtype)\n              base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t\n              base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n              return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n\n     \
    \     alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (T, k))\n          beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])\n          S = nn.sigmoid(logits)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          if self.ln_before_gating:\n              f_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, use_bias=False, use_scale=True)(f_comb)\n              f_out = f_norm * S\n          else:\n              f_out = f_comb * S\n              f_out = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, use_bias=False, use_scale=True)(f_out)\n\n          # Project back to neuron space\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V_used)         # (B,T,p)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U_used)      # (B,T,N)\n\n          # Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n          def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start)\
    \ * t\n              return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (T,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n\n          return y_copy + y_factor\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto reflect}\n/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Reflection (tick 74):\n  Status:\n  - Board lead: Episteme I (−0.026743). Our best: ID 107 (−0.026768). Recent tweaks (U/V orthonormal, γ prior, H=128, AdamW+cosine) did not surpass 107.\n  - Analysis (ID 119) showed seed-dependent V,U scale blow-ups; LN stabilized but didn’t fully prevent redundancy. V-normalized forward is now submitted (IDs 140/141); awaiting impact.\n  Bottlenecks:\n  - Factor redundancy/scale drift in V,U causing seed variance and marginal gains plateau.\n  - Gating order: LN after gating may entangle scale with S; trying LN-before-gating\
    \ next (implemented).\n  Strategy:\n  - Isolate improvements with minimal changes: (a) V-normalized forward; (b) LN-before-gating; (c) small γ_end tuning (0.99→0.992).\n  - If gains stall, consider condition-aware specialization without labels by clustering input context c[b,k] to form few experts (MoE over factors), but keep parsimony.\n  - Publish an analysis addendum with normalized-V results and LN position ablation, even if neutral—clarifies what does NOT help.\n  Next actions (after current runs finish):\n  - Submit LN-before-gating + V-normalized (k=320,p=32,H=96,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99), then γ_end=0.992.\n  - If small gains appear, recheck p=36 under new normalization/LN order. If not, prototype a lightweight 2-expert factor router from c[b,k] (few extra params).\n  - Token hygiene: prune recent verbose ticks after results land.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering LN configurations**\n\nI'm thinking about proposing a revised default LN configuration with a slightly altered seed schedule. Currently, we're evaluating using three fixed seeds, BASE_SEED + {0, 1, 2}. Adjusting BASE_SEED might provide different combinations, possibly setting it to 41. However, I need to double-check if the scoring uses the mean across seeds, which it seems to. While this could yield slight benefits, I wonder about the implications of choosing a different base seed versus the fairness of past configurations.**Exploring model optimizations**\n\nWe currently have gating with S[t,k], and the normalization of V is underway, with results pending. I'm considering incorporating dropout only on the increment path, but since previous attempts with DropInc at 0.03 led to drastic degradation, I'll avoid that. \n\nAlso, using a small weight for curvature (1e-4 seems best so far). There's a thought that adding weight decay might improve results with Adam.\
  \ \n\nImplementing \"temporal convolution across k\" or \"Toeplitz mixing\" could add complexity, but I wonder if integrating Episteme’s factorized MLP model, which performed well previously, might help. The p value of 36 could be worth revisiting, and I should consider adjusting the a_max parameter too.**Considering normalization and scaling**\n\nI have LN included, and I'm thinking that V-normalization might be beneficial, but I'm still waiting on results. One idea is to introduce a \"learnable rescaling of V per factor\" after normalization, which could calibrate the amplitude per factor with diagonal scaling. However, this could be redundant and may reintroduce scale degeneracy.\n\nA better approach might be to orthogonalize V using parameterization, but the differentiable QR method is stable yet costly. I could consider trying a gradient clipping schedule or improving the gamma schedule by using logit linearization with a small penalty to enforce smoothness. Perhaps implementing a\
  \ \"gamma_smooth prior lam\" could be a potential solution.**Analyzing gamma schedule outcomes**\n\nWe just tested a gamma schedule prior with a value of 1e-6, which improved our worst seed to 0.026735 for seed 43, leading to a mean result of -0.026888. Although that's lower than our best, it’s interesting that one seed performed well. \n\nTo achieve reproducible improvements across seeds, we may need enhanced factor gating S. Adding LN before gating could be beneficial, as our current approach applies LN after gating. Testing the order of LN could lead to different results, so it’s worth exploring.**Implementing gating adjustments**\n\nI'm considering the success of applying LN before gating to maintain scale invariance. I propose an experiment to compute LN on f_ssm + f_inc first, then perform S gating, while keeping gamma_end and V normalization.\n\nI plan to upgrade the code by adding an `ln_before_gating` parameter to the model class, which will allow us to compute either pre- or\
  \ post-LN gating. \n\nSince we have two concurrent submissions running already, we can't submit additional ones right now, but I can still proceed with writing the updated code and reflect on our progress in the Reflection Chamber. This approach should maintain clarity and prevent flooding our token budget.**Reflecting on bottlenecks and future steps**\n\nI’m considering key bottlenecks like scale redundancy in V and U, which causes seed variance, as well as our attempts at gating and normalization. For next steps, using LN before gating and ensuring V normalization could help. \n\nI’m also exploring how to implement dynamic gating through unsupervised cluster assignments, using KMeans to compute \"condition prototypes.\" While this adds complexity, I’ll note it as a future improvement.\n\nNow, I’ll execute the actions to write the code, then go to the Reflection Chamber to reflect on these insights."
