role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write ariadne/models_fact_ln.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN: Factorized-loadings oscillatory 2nd-order SSM with LayerNorm in factor space.\n\n  Options:\n  - normalize_u: column-normalize U in forward\n  - normalize_v: column-normalize V in forward (scale-invariant factors)\n  - ln_before_gating: apply LayerNorm before temporal gating (default False = after gating)\n\n  Components:\n  - Factorized loadings U ∈ R^{N×p}, V ∈ R^{k×p}\n  - Oscillatory 2nd-order recurrence per factor (stable via a_max)\n  - Small per-factor increment head (4→32)\n  - Input-adaptive temporal gate S[b,t,k]\n  - Global horizon gate gamma[t] (trainable)\n  - LayerNorm across factor dimension (Flax API: reduction_axes=-1)\n  - Residual copy head for strong short-horizon anchor\n\n  Latent export (sow):\n  - factors_preln: input to LayerNorm (pre-LN), shape (B,T,k)\n    • If ln_before_gating: pre-LN = f_comb (before S)\n    • Else: pre-LN = f_comb * S\n  - factors_out:\
    \ standardized latent used for projection, shape (B,T,k)\n  - S_gate: temporal gate S[b,t,k]\n  - gamma: horizon gate, shape (T,)\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead\n\n  def _logit(p):\n      p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\n  class Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_size: int = 96\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      normalize_v: bool = False\n      ln_before_gating: bool = False\n      a_max: float = 0.993\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n          T = self.output_horizon\n\n          # Factorized loadings\n          U = self.param('U',\
    \ nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U_used = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          else:\n              U_used = U\n          if self.normalize_v:\n              V_used = V / (jnp.linalg.norm(V, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          else:\n              V_used = V\n\n          # Project inputs to factor space\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_used)         # (B,4,p)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,kp->btk', xU, V_used) # (B,4,k)\n\n          # Initial states f0, f1 from 4-step input\n          f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)           # (B*k,4)\n          f0 = nn.Dense(1)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n          f1 = nn.Dense(1)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n\n          # Oscillatory 2nd-order coefficients\n          r_raw = self.param('r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros,\
    \ (k,))\n          r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)\n          w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)\n          a = r * jnp.cos(w)\n          b = r * r\n\n          def step(carry, _):\n              y_prev, y_prev2 = carry\n              y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n              return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n          carry_init = (f1, f0)\n          _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=T - 2)  # (T-2,B,k)\n          y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n          y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n          f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Per-factor increment head\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          f_inc = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          f_comb = f_ssm + f_inc  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Input-adaptive temporal gate S[b,t,k]\n          c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)  # (B,k)\n          def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n\
    \              TT, K = shape\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, TT, dtype=dtype)\n              base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t\n              base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n              return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n          alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (T, k))\n          beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])\n          S = nn.sigmoid(logits)  # (B,T,k)\n          self.sow('latents', 'S_gate', S)\n\n          # LayerNorm and gating order\n          if self.ln_before_gating:\n              f_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, use_bias=False, use_scale=True)(f_comb)\n              self.sow('latents', 'factors_preln', f_comb)   # input to LN\n              f_out = f_norm * S\n          else:\n              f_pre = f_comb * S\n              self.sow('latents', 'factors_preln', f_pre)    # input to LN\n              f_out = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, use_bias=False,\
    \ use_scale=True)(f_pre)\n\n          self.sow('latents', 'factors_out', f_out)\n\n          # Project back to neuron space\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V_used)         # (B,T,p)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U_used)      # (B,T,N)\n\n          # Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n          def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (T,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          # Store gamma as (T,) for convenience\n          self.sow('latents', 'gamma', jnp.squeeze(gamma, axis=(0, 2)))\n          y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n\n          return y_copy + y_factor\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LN-SSM (k=320,p=32,H=96,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99) + Full-Val Latent Export\"\ntags: \"analysis, latents, layernorm, factorized-loadings\"\nabstract: \"Re-run the best LN config to export latent trajectories on full validation: factors_out (post-LN/gate), factors_preln (pre-LN), S_gate, and gamma. Saves per-seed NPZ under storage/ariadne/analyses/latents/.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import numpy as np\n  import optax\n\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n         \
    \ 'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable)\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n          ln_before_gating=bool(hparams.get('ln_before_gating',\
    \ False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n\n  def _to_array(v):\n      # flax sow returns lists; take last if list\n      if isinstance(v, (list, tuple)):\n          return v[-1]\n      return v\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      # Export full validation latents\n      sys.path.append('storage/system')\n      from train_single import load_data, create_batches\n      # Recreate network for inference with latents collection\n      hparams = trial_data.get('hyperparameters', {})\n\
    \      net = create_network(hparams)\n\n      # Load data\n      _, val_data, _, val_labels = load_data()\n\n      # Export dir\n      tag = f\"ln_ssm_k{hparams.get('rank_k',320)}_p{hparams.get('proj_rank',32)}_H{hparams.get('hidden_size',96)}_a{hparams.get('a_max',0.993)}_g{hparams.get('gamma_end',0.99)}\"\n      out_dir = os.path.join('storage', 'ariadne', 'analyses', 'latents', tag, f\"trial_{trial_data.get('trial_number', 0)}_seed_{trial_data.get('seed', 0)}\")\n      os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n      fac_out_list, fac_pre_list, S_list = [], [], []\n      gamma_vec = None\n\n      for x_batch, _ in create_batches(val_data, 4, 32, BATCH_SIZE, val_labels, shuffle_key=None):\n          preds, lat = net.apply(params, x_batch, training=False, mutable=['latents'])\n          lat = lat.get('latents', {})\n          f_out = _to_array(lat.get('factors_out'))\n          f_pre = _to_array(lat.get('factors_preln'))\n          Sgate = _to_array(lat.get('S_gate'))\n          if gamma_vec\
    \ is None:\n              g = _to_array(lat.get('gamma'))\n              if g is not None:\n                  gamma_vec = np.asarray(g)\n          if f_out is not None:\n              fac_out_list.append(np.asarray(f_out))\n          if f_pre is not None:\n              fac_pre_list.append(np.asarray(f_pre))\n          if Sgate is not None:\n              S_list.append(np.asarray(Sgate))\n\n      if fac_out_list:\n          factors_out = np.concatenate(fac_out_list, axis=0)\n          np.savez_compressed(os.path.join(out_dir, 'factors_out.npz'), factors_out=factors_out)\n      if fac_pre_list:\n          factors_preln = np.concatenate(fac_pre_list, axis=0)\n          np.savez_compressed(os.path.join(out_dir, 'factors_preln.npz'), factors_preln=factors_preln)\n      if S_list:\n          S_gate = np.concatenate(S_list, axis=0)\n          np.savez_compressed(os.path.join(out_dir, 'S_gate.npz'), S_gate=S_gate)\n      if gamma_vec is not None:\n          np.save(os.path.join(out_dir, 'gamma.npy'),\
    \ gamma_vec)\n\n      # README with shapes\n      with open(os.path.join(out_dir, 'README.txt'), 'w') as f:\n          f.write(\"Latent export (full validation, non-shuffled windows):\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"factors_out.npz: (num_windows, 32, {hparams.get('rank_k',320)})\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"factors_preln.npz: (num_windows, 32, {hparams.get('rank_k',320)})\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"S_gate.npz: (num_windows, 32, {hparams.get('rank_k',320)})\\n\")\n          f.write(\"gamma.npy: (32,)\\n\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating latent exportation**\n\nI can see that we don't necessarily need to produce a new evaluation just to export latents. We have the option to use the complete function during training, and it permits running complete(params, opt_state, trial_data) after training. So to get latents for ID 107 specifically, we'd have to rerun the training. However, creating a new submission with the same configuration should get us close, though results may slightly differ due to random seeds. We also need to include latents this time around.**Exploring export code**\n\nTo export latents, I think I need to write my own code that iterates over create_batches to compute them using network.apply. The complete function takes params, opt_state, and trial_data, such as val_mae and hyperparameters. Once training is done, I can call load_data() and use create_batches to go through the validation set. However, I'll have to import those functions from storage/system/train_single by adjusting\
  \ the sys.path. But I’m not sure how the working directory in the sandbox will affect this when complete() is called.**Understanding import and dataset access**\n\nIt looks like_funcs['complete'] is called after saving trial data in storage/shared/tmp/<uuid>. The chdir is set to the shared storage root, so I can import from 'system/train_single.py' using 'from train_single import create_batches' since sys.path already includes 'storage/system'. The load_all_functions function sets this up. However, I believe complete() needs to reload the dataset although it already computed the best params during training. I specifically need access to internal components of my model, like gating latents and various factors, since they aren’t directly provided by my network wrapper.**Considering latent reconstruction**\n\nI’m thinking we might be able to reconstruct latents by applying a forward pass with Flax linen to capture intermediate outputs. This would work better if our model had named modules,\
  \ allowing us to pass those outputs through the 'intermediates' collection. However, the model isn’t currently using variable scopes for tracking. Another option is to create a separate function that computes latents using parameters and inputs while re-implementing the model's internal calculations from the export code, which would involve accessing parameters like U, V, s_alpha, and others from the params dictionary.**Implementing latent export**\n\nTo create a new model instance with the same architecture, I’ll apply params to get latents. I need to ensure that create_network returns the correct wrapper containing my model. The apply method will let me access latents, even though it doesn’t support returning mutables currently. I’ll also need to save latents to a specific storage path derived from the trial data, but I’m aware I might have to fall back to naming conventions based on trial numbers. \n\nFor the full val set, I should compute latents and ensure that I’m considering memory\
  \ limitations, aiming for efficient implementation of create_batches to process 469 windows. Additionally, I’ll gather the necessary parameters for storing them in an organized manner, and make sure to incorporate essential sow commands in my model.**Updating model and exporting latents**\n\nI’m updating the models_fact_ln.py to include the new ln_before_gating parameter and add sow lines for storage. After issuing a write command for this updated code, I’ll set up a new submission based on configuration ID 107 that exports latents in the complete() function. \n\nThis involves preparing the content based on Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN and defining hyperparameters. I need to ensure proper collection and saving of latents while managing memory, especially for items like gamma and y_copy, which could be too large to export. Only exporting necessary latent factors will help optimize this process. I'll also incorporate an index reconstruction method during batch creation to ensure everything\
  \ is consistent and reproducible.**Implementing model updates and latents export**\n\nI’m finalizing the process to collect and export latents while ensuring our code maintains a consistent order. We won't export indices but will track the number of windows and their shapes instead. I plan to use `np.savez_compressed` for size efficiency. \n\nIn my `complete()` function, I'll import necessary modules, set parameters, and ensure batch processing works optimally. I also aim to implement the appropriate `sow` statements in the model to successfully export filtered latent factors. Additionally, I'll prepare for submission while adhering to the defined structure and avoiding unnecessary comments."
