thinking_content: "**Considering next steps**\n\nI need to decide if we should respond with actions or just text since I'm in Research Counter. I want to keep monitoring evaluation 155 and implement the full-val latent export we submitted. It might make sense to inform Episteme that the data will be ready soon, but we already communicated the timeline. I also want to manage tokens carefully since we're nearing 70%. Pruning some ticks, especially after 66, seems like a good idea.**Clarifying next steps**\n\nThe last message outlines our next step—assuming we've completed reading system scripts. Since there's no direct question, I’ll proceed. I want to ensure we correctly set up the full-val export using create_batches with shuffle_key set to None, which we did. It's also essential that we use the latents collection via sow. In our create_network wrapper, I see that we need to pass mutable=['latents'] during inference to receive updates. Overall, the apply function will return the necessary\
  \ outputs and updates, which looks good so far.**Reviewing training parameters**\n\nI see that the Station's training code uses funcs['complete'] with final_params and trial_data. It's important to note that the 'params' we pass include the Flax variable dict. When calling create_network and net.apply, we need to keep in mind that net.apply requires the same variable types. Although there’s a potential memory risk with exporting from 469 windows across 71721 features, the shapes seem manageable. We need to make sure latents are exported, and the complete function will run at the end of training trials as we defined it in the submission. That looks good!**Planning operational updates**\n\nI’m considering if I should add notes about ephemeral illusions to Private Memory, though it might not be necessary. I should plan to update Episteme I once the data is ready and set a timeline. For operations, I might send a note that the export is underway, but we’ll wait until it’s done since we already\
  \ provided the path. I’m seeing results where minimal recurrence in diag1 yields similar mean values to none, indicating recurrence isn't critical. Evaluating 'LN-before-gating' with V-normalized results shows no improvement, so I'll continue assessing those values.**Organizing evaluation actions**\n\nI realize that while evaluating the V-normalization, it hasn't quite reached the results of ID 107, which is a bit frustrating. Since our previous tests didn’t beat ID 107, I’m considering pivoting to a simpler factorized architecture. Their Factorized MLP scores slightly better, so it could be worth trying our own variant to see if we can improve it. For now, I should summarize the invariance findings in Private Memory and manage token pruning. \n\nLet’s execute pruning for ticks 66-74 and send an email to Episteme updating them on the export job with ID 155. I'll also ensure our code saves gamma correctly."
