- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 84\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Ariadne I\n- Agent Description: An agent who navigates complexity with principled inquiry and empirical rigor.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nAriadne I — Next Steps\n1) Qualitative analysis:\n   - Add complete() hook to best LN config to save U, V, γ, and S stats to storage/ariadne/analyses/.\n   - Compute: U/V norms, V-orthogonality error, U coherence, γ profile; summarize S[b,t,k].\n   - Update archive with figures and brief analysis.\n2) Minor sweeps:\n   - Try cosine LR schedule with AdamW (+ warmup 500 steps) on best config.\n   - Light p fine-tune around 34–36.\n3) Token hygiene:\n   - Prune older ticks with long logs after analyses are queued to stay <75% usage.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 118,540 / 270,000 used (44%)\n- Agent Age: 84 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nEpisteme I replied to your mail titled \"Query: Latent\
    \ Factor Trajectory Data for Comparative Analysis\" (Mail #2, Message #mail_2-6):\n--- Reply Content ---\nAriadne I,\n\nThank you for providing the data. My comparative analysis is complete, and it has yielded a fascinating result.\n\nA Fourier analysis shows that my MLP-based forecaster learns a diverse set of latent dynamics—some factors are low-frequency, others are high-frequency. In contrast, your SSM-based forecaster learns to represent nearly all factors with a single, powerful, high-frequency oscillatory mode.\n\nThis explains everything. Your model is a powerful specialist, while mine is a flexible generalist. The slight edge in my score likely comes from my model's ability to capture the low-frequency trends that the SSM might be de-emphasizing.\n\nThis leads me to a new hypothesis: a hybrid model that explicitly combines a specialist SSM (for oscillations) and a generalist MLP (for the residual trends) could outperform both. I will be exploring this direction next.\n\nThank\
    \ you again for your collaboration. This has been an incredibly productive line of inquiry.\n\nBest,\nEpisteme I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #2), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 2}`.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nPrivate Memory Capsules preserve knowledge for your lineage. Document not just successes but also failure modes and theoretical insights for future generations to build upon.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n2. `storage list ariadne/analyses/latents` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage list ariadne/analyses/latents/ln_ssm_k320_p32_H96_a0.993_g0.99` (in Research Counter);\n4. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n5. `reply 2` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File list for ariadne/analyses/latents will be\
    \ displayed below.\n- File list for ariadne/analyses/latents/ln_ssm_k320_p32_H96_a0.993_g0.99 will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 129 | 1 | Factorized MLP + RC with LayerNorm | Episteme I | 68 | -0.026743 | 0.0195 | 0.0279 | 0.0284 | 0.0231 | 0.0259 |\n| 107 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320, p=32, H=96, γ_end=0.99, a_max=0.993) + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 56 | -0.026768 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0283 | 0.0233 | 0.0260 |\n| 142 | 1 | SOTA Re-run with Latent Space Logging | Episteme I | 73 | -0.026772 | 0.0195 | 0.0280 | 0.0286 | 0.0230 | 0.0258\
    \ |\n| 140 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN + V-normalized forward (k=320,p=32,H=96, a_max=0.993, γ_end=0.99) | Ariadne I | 73 | -0.026825 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0286 | 0.0232 | 0.0259 |\n| 143 | 1 | SOTA Re-run with Correct Latent Space Logging | Episteme I | 74 | -0.026825 | 0.0195 | 0.0280 | 0.0288 | 0.0229 | 0.0258 |\n| 104 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320, p=36, H=96, γ_end=0.99) + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 54 | -0.026843 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0286 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 100 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,H=96, γ_end=0.99) + AdamW (wd=1e-4) + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 53 | -0.026846 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0285 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 128 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (best base) + U/V OrthoReg (λ_V=1e-5, λ_U=5e-7), Adam | Ariadne I | 68 | -0.026875 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0287 | 0.0231 | 0.0259 |\n| 132 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,H=96) + V-OrthoReg + γ prior (λ_γ=1e-6) | Ariadne I | 70 | -0.026888 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0287 | 0.0232 | 0.0259 |\n| 113 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,H=96,\
    \ γ_end=0.99, a_max=0.993) + AdamW (wd=1e-4) | Ariadne I | 58 | -0.026893 | 0.0199 | 0.0281 | 0.0287 | 0.0232 | 0.0259 |\n\nPage 1 of 16 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-16, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**File Listings:**\n\n**ariadne/analyses/latents:**\n- ln_ssm_k320_p32_H96_a0.993_g0.99/trial_0_seed_42/README.txt\n- ln_ssm_k320_p32_H96_a0.993_g0.99/trial_0_seed_42/S_gate.npz\n- ln_ssm_k320_p32_H96_a0.993_g0.99/trial_0_seed_42/factors_out.npz\n- ln_ssm_k320_p32_H96_a0.993_g0.99/trial_0_seed_42/factors_preln.npz\n- ln_ssm_k320_p32_H96_a0.993_g0.99/trial_0_seed_42/gamma.npy\n- ln_ssm_k320_p32_H96_a0.993_g0.99/trial_1_seed_43/README.txt\n- ln_ssm_k320_p32_H96_a0.993_g0.99/trial_1_seed_43/S_gate.npz\n- ln_ssm_k320_p32_H96_a0.993_g0.99/trial_1_seed_43/factors_out.npz\n- ln_ssm_k320_p32_H96_a0.993_g0.99/trial_1_seed_43/factors_preln.npz\n\
