role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write ariadne/models_hybrid.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  HybridOscSSMTrend_LN: Hybrid forecaster combining oscillatory SSM factors (specialist for high‑freq)\n  with an explicit low‑frequency trend head (level + slope) in factor space, mixed per factor.\n\n  Design:\n  - Factorized loadings: U ∈ R^{N×p}, V ∈ R^{k×p} (optional column normalization for invariance)\n  - Oscillatory 2nd‑order SSM per factor (stable via a_max)\n  - Trend head: predicts per‑factor level and slope from the 4‑step context, then extrapolates\n    linearly over the 32‑step horizon: f_trend[t] = level + (t_norm)*slope\n  - Per‑factor mixture gate m[b,k] blends SSM vs Trend: f_mix = m * f_ssm + (1−m) * f_trend\n    (m is input‑adaptive via context c[b,k] = mean_t factors_in[b,t,k])\n  - Residual increment head (4→32) adds flexibility\n  - Temporal gate S[b,t,k] from s_alpha[t,k] and s_beta[k]·c[b,k]\n  - LayerNorm across factor dimension AFTER\
    \ temporal gating (empirically best)\n  - Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n  - Residual copy head anchors short horizon\n\n  Returns:\n    y = y_copy + gamma[t] * Proj(f_out)\n\n  Notes:\n    - This implements a “specialist + generalist” hybrid as suggested by comparative analyses,\n      aiming to capture both high‑freq oscillations and low‑freq trends.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead  # storage/ariadne/models.py\n\n  def _logit(p):\n      p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\n  class HybridOscSSMTrend_LN(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_size: int = 96\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      normalize_v: bool = False\n      a_max: float = 0.993\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n    \
    \      # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n          T = self.output_horizon\n\n          # Factorized loadings\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_used = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) if self.normalize_u else U\n          V_used = V / (jnp.linalg.norm(V, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) if self.normalize_v else V\n\n          # Project inputs to factor space\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_used)           # (B,4,p)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,kp->btk', xU, V_used)  # (B,4,k)\n\n          # Initial states f0, f1 from 4-step input\n          f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)            # (B*k,4)\n          f0 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n          f1 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n\n          # Oscillatory\
    \ 2nd-order SSM (specialist, high-frequency capable)\n          r_raw = self.param('r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)                  # (k,)\n          w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)                      # (k,)\n          a = r * jnp.cos(w)\n          b = r * r\n\n          def step(carry, _):\n              y_prev, y_prev2 = carry  # (B,k), (B,k)\n              y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n              return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n          carry_init = (f1, f0)\n          _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=T - 2)  # (T-2,B,k)\n          y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n          y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n          f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Low-frequency Trend head (generalist): level + slope * t_norm\n          th = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat)\n          th = nn.gelu(th)\n\
    \          trend_params = nn.Dense(2)(th).reshape(B, k, 2)     # (B,k,2): level, slope\n          level = trend_params[:, :, 0]                       # (B,k)\n          slope = trend_params[:, :, 1]                       # (B,k)\n          t_norm = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T, dtype=level.dtype)  # (T,)\n          f_trend = level[:, None, :] + slope[:, None, :] * t_norm[None, :, None]  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Residual increment head for flexibility\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          f_inc = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Context and per-factor mixture gate m[b,k] blending SSM vs Trend\n          c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)  # (B,k)\n          m0 = self.param('mix_bias', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          m_ctx = self.param('mix_ctx', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          m = nn.sigmoid(m0[None, :] + m_ctx[None, :] * c)    # (B,k)\n          f_mix = m[:, None, :] * f_ssm + (1.0 - m[:, None,\
    \ :]) * f_trend  # (B,T,k)\n\n          f_comb = f_mix + f_inc  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Temporal gate S[b,t,k] using c[b,k]\n          def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              TT, K = shape\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, TT, dtype=dtype)\n              base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t\n              base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n              return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n          alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (T, k))\n          beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])\n          S = nn.sigmoid(logits)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # LayerNorm AFTER gating (empirically preferred)\n          f_pre = f_comb * S\n          f_out = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, use_bias=False, use_scale=True)(f_pre)\n\n          # Project back to neurons: (B,T,k)->(B,T,p)->(B,T,N)\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V_used)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn',\
    \ z, U_used)\n\n          # Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n          def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (T,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n\n          return y_copy + y_factor\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN + TrendMix: Specialist SSM + Generalist Trend (k=320,p=32,H=96)\"\ntags: \"hybrid, state-space, trend, layernorm, factorized-loadings, gating\"\nabstract: \"Implements a hybrid of oscillatory SSM factors (specialist for high‑freq) and an explicit low‑freq trend head (level+slope) mixed per factor via input‑adaptive\
    \ gate m[b,k]. LayerNorm after gating, residual copy head, curvature regularization, and V-orthogonality.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n\n  from models_hybrid import HybridOscSSMTrend_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5  # Encourage diverse factor basis in V\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = HybridOscSSMTrend_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key,\
    \ dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_from_tree(tree, key):\n      try:\n          if key in tree:\n              return tree[key]\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n      if isinstance(tree, dict) and 'params' in tree:\n          return _get_from_tree(tree['params'], key)\n      return _get_from_tree(dict(tree),\
    \ key)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      # V orthogonality penalty: ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n      try:\n          V = _get_from_tree(params, 'V')\n          G = V.T @ V\n          I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n          v_ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      except Exception:\n          v_ortho = 0.0\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Specialist–Generalist Hybrid\"\ncontent: |\n  This is an excellent insight. I’ve just queued a hybrid model that explicitly mixes a specialist SSM branch with a low‑frequency trend head (per‑factor level+slope with per‑factor mixture gate m[b,k]). It keeps\
    \ our best invariances (LN after gating, factorized loadings, γ schedule) and adds the generalist trend you observed.\n\n  If it confirms your hypothesis, we can follow up with a joint analysis: spectrum of f_out by factor for SSM vs trend contributions, mixture statistics m[b,k], and step‑MAE attribution. I’ll share the eval ID and (if promising) export latents similarly for side‑by‑side comparison.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Exploring trend forecasting**\n\nI’m looking to forecast trends without direct y_t data. I think I can use a first-order IIR approach for a 32-step forecast. This would involve extracting a constant trend from the input, either by mean calculation or linear projection. Another idea is to create a small linear extrapolation head for polynomial coefficients, which would help model low-frequency trends. I want to develop a \"Trend head\" to predict levels and slopes while keeping things simple yet effective. Let's also consider optional quadratic curvature for more flexibility.**Implementing trend and gating**\n\nI’m considering a mixture approach for separating high and low trends. By introducing a per-factor mixture weight, I can compute it with a sigmoid based on context. The final output would mix the SSM and trend components while applying layer normalization and a gating gamma. \n\nI know from earlier observations that the order of layer normalization matters, so\
  \ I'll keep that in mind. For the trend head, I’m looking to produce outputs for level and slope per factor, ensuring proper scaling and clamping when necessary.**Finalizing the model design**\n\nEverything seems to be falling into place! I plan to keep the SSM branch with second-order oscillation and possibly keep the incremental MLP as well. \n\nThe mixture weight will be calculated using a sigmoid based on a mean of factors over time. The final combined output will incorporate the trend and the incremental residual. I will also apply layer normalization after gating, following my earlier findings. \n\nPlus, I'll manage the creation of a new file for hybrid models in storage and address token usage, since we're currently at 44%. Let’s get this done!**Developing the Hybrid model**\n\nI’m considering running a small ablation study. While plain addition could work, mixture gating helps specialize per factor, so I should define the class HybridSSMTrend_LN. Testing isn’t necessary right now,\
  \ but I must ensure compatibility with the Flax API and import flax.linen as nn. \n\nI’ll also set default hyperparameters similar to previous successful settings and ensure everything returns the correct shapes while checking that outputs from jax.lax.scan are assigned properly. Additionally, I need to wrap everything for submission, compute the loss, and maintain gradient clipping.**Implementing Hybrid model**\n\nI'm ready to implement the \"Hybrid: Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN + Trend\" model, which combines oscillatory factors with low-frequency trends using level and slope via mixture gating and layer normalization. I want to ensure the storage file is correctly quoted in YAML and carefully construct the model to compute the state space with a dense layer for trend parameters. \n\nAfter that, I'll set up the mixture gating, apply normalization, and compute the loss with curvature penalties. I’ll also plan to respond to Episteme about our hybrid implementation idea for co-analysis. Let’s wrap\
  \ this up!"
