role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write ariadne/models_hybrid_tm.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  HybridOscSSMTrend_LN_TMix: Time-dependent mixture between oscillatory SSM (specialist) and\n  low-frequency trend (generalist). Mixture is per-factor and varies over horizon:\n      m_t[b,t,k] = sigmoid(m0[k] + m_ctx[k]*c[b,k] + m_time[k]*t_norm[t])\n  where c[b,k] is input context (mean over 4-step factors_in), and t_norm ∈ [0,1].\n\n  Other components:\n  - Factorized loadings U (N×p), V (k×p) with optional column normalization\n  - Oscillatory 2nd-order SSM per factor (stable via a_max)\n  - Trend head (level+slope per factor) extrapolated across horizon\n  - Residual increment (4→32) in factor space\n  - Temporal gate S[b,t,k] from s_alpha[t,k] and s_beta[k]·c[b,k]\n  - LayerNorm across factor dim AFTER gating (empirically best)\n  - Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n  - Residual copy head\n\n  Intent: allow higher reliance on SSM early (oscillations) and trend later (slow drift).\n  \"\"\
    \"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead\n\n  def _logit(p):\n      p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\n  class HybridOscSSMTrend_LN_TMix(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_size: int = 96\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      normalize_v: bool = True\n      a_max: float = 0.993\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n          T = self.output_horizon\n\n          # Factorized loadings\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_used = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True)\
    \ + 1e-6) if self.normalize_u else U\n          V_used = V / (jnp.linalg.norm(V, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) if self.normalize_v else V\n\n          # Project inputs to factor space\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_used)              # (B,4,p)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,kp->btk', xU, V_used)     # (B,4,k)\n\n          # Initial states from 4-step input\n          f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)               # (B*k,4)\n          f0 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n          f1 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n\n          # Oscillatory 2nd-order SSM per factor\n          r_raw = self.param('r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)\n          w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)\n          a = r * jnp.cos(w)\n          b = r * r\n\n          def step(carry, _):\n              y_prev, y_prev2 = carry\n      \
    \        y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n              return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n          carry_init = (f1, f0)\n          _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=T - 2)  # (T-2,B,k)\n          y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n          y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n          f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Low-frequency Trend head (level + slope)\n          th = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); th = nn.gelu(th)\n          trend_params = nn.Dense(2)(th).reshape(B, k, 2)  # (B,k,2)\n          level = trend_params[:, :, 0]\n          slope = trend_params[:, :, 1]\n          t_norm = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T, dtype=level.dtype)  # (T,)\n          f_trend = level[:, None, :] + slope[:, None, :] * t_norm[None, :, None]  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Residual increment head\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          f_inc = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  #\
    \ (B,T,k)\n\n          # Context and time-dependent mixture m_t[b,t,k]\n          c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)  # (B,k)\n          m0 = self.param('mix_bias', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          m_ctx = self.param('mix_ctx', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          m_time = self.param('mix_time', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          # Broadcast terms: (B,1,k) + (B,1,k) + (1,T,1)\n          logits_m = m0[None, None, :] + (m_ctx[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :]) + (m_time[None, :, None] * t_norm[None, :, None])\n          m_t = nn.sigmoid(logits_m)  # (B,T,k)\n          f_mix = m_t * f_ssm + (1.0 - m_t) * f_trend  # (B,T,k)\n\n          f_comb = f_mix + f_inc  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Temporal gate S[b,t,k]\n          def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              TT, K = shape\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, TT, dtype=dtype)\n              base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t\n              base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n              return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n\
    \          alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (T, k))\n          beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          logits_S = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])\n          S = nn.sigmoid(logits_S)\n\n          # LayerNorm AFTER gating\n          f_pre = f_comb * S\n          f_out = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, use_bias=False, use_scale=True)(f_pre)\n\n          # Project back to neuron space\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V_used)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U_used)\n\n          # Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n          def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (T,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          y_factor\
    \ = gamma * y_factor\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n\n          return y_copy + y_factor\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid TrendMix-T (time-dependent mix): V-normalized, p=36, AdamW\"\ntags: \"hybrid, time-dependent-mix, trend, state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings\"\nabstract: \"Introduce time-dependent per-factor mixture m_t[b,t,k] between oscillatory SSM and low-frequency trend, allowing early oscillatory emphasis and late trend reliance. Keep LN-after-gating, V-normalized, p=36, AdamW; loss = MAE+curvature.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n\n  from models_hybrid_tm import HybridOscSSMTrend_LN_TMix\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n   \
    \       'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 36,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': True,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = HybridOscSSMTrend_LN_TMix(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 36)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', True)),\n\
    \          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_from_tree(tree, key):\n      try:\n          if key in tree:\n              return tree[key]\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n      if isinstance(tree, dict) and 'params' in tree:\n          return _get_from_tree(tree['params'], key)\n      return _get_from_tree(dict(tree), key)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      try:\n          V = _get_from_tree(params, 'V')\n          G = V.T @ V\n          I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n          v_ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      except Exception:\n          v_ortho = 0.0\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n\
    \          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to outline my next actions. Currently, I'm at the Research Counter with some high token levels left. I've got ongoing experiments, with ID 168 queued, and the previous experiments (160, 162, 164) yielded decent results around -0.02686 to -0.026876. Our best result is -0.026768, which is still behind Episteme's MLP at -0.026743 and Aether's top score of -0.026638. I need a more nuanced strategy for our hybrids, while keeping it simple with controlled complexity. I'll also update the archives and consider new public memory tasks.**Evaluating token usage and actions**\n\nI'm currently sitting at 56% of my tokens, so it's not urgent to act right away. I might consider exporting latents for the LN-before gating and the V-normalized SSM variant. I already queued the latents for ID 155, so that part's done. Right now, since experiment 168 is running and there's no concurrency limit showing, I can potentially queue more experiments. I think it's\
  \ safe to suggest a small improvement to the hybrid by introducing time-dependent mixtures instead of static factors, though that will add complexity.**Exploring model enhancements**\n\nI’m considering some simple augmentations. One option is to add a low-frequency damped 2nd-order SSM for trends instead of relying solely on a linear trend. Alternatively, I could incorporate smoothing to promote a low-frequency trend, perhaps using a 1D low-pass filter. Another direction could involve applying V normalization and V orthogonal regression to a larger p, maybe trying p=35 to avoid near duplicates, or increasing rank_k beyond 320, though that may increase memory usage. I'll aim to keep pushing forward, focusing on Atom-level invariances and minor sweeps.**Considering trend enhancements**\n\nI received a mail from Episteme suggesting trends, and I implemented a trend mixture. It could be beneficial if the trend branch utilizes MLP residuals across neurons instead of just per-factor linear trends.\
  \ I need to remember that I can only override functions within \"submission.py,\" but I can import from lineage modules. The models_hybrid I wrote uses a per-factor trend parameterization based on a 4-step context. I might adjust gamma_end to around 0.995 for the hybrid since we found 0.99 worked well in the past. Additionally, I should ensure that the compute loss uses curvature effectively and produce only one change per submission. I might also consider sending a summary to private memory later on.**Planning immediate next steps**\n\nFirst, I need to think about replying to the mail to propose a joint paper, but that's not essential. I could run a storage list for the hybrid latents with p=32, which is already done. It might be worthwhile to propose compressing the mix_gate to a per-factor mixture over time, refining it with a time-dependent schedule. I should implement a new model called model_hybrid_tm that focuses on time-varying mixtures. \n\nI'll use AdamW for optimization since\
  \ it performed well previously and adjust gamma_end to 0.995 while keeping it isolated. Token usage is at 151k, so I’ll need to keep this manageable as I prepare the code for submission. Lastly, I’ll ensure I draft everything carefully before executing the storage write and submission."
