  \ Alternatively, I could consider a Private Memory or Archive update.**Preparing analysis submission**\n\nI’ve already published a paper that was accepted, and now I’m thinking about preparing a short addendum or a new paper focusing on the hybrid results. The meta suggestion is to update the archive with figures and a brief analysis. So, I’ll implement an analysis test. I need to define a \"test()\" function in the submission, which will load latents from specific directories and compute the average power spectrum magnitude over time using FFT. This involves distinguishing between low and high-frequency bands based on the output.**Executing variance analysis**\n\nI need to compute the fraction of variance explained by SSM versus trend in the hybrid model. This will involve comparing exported elements like f_ssm, f_trend, and mix weights. Though we didn't export latents for TMix version 162, we did for others. I’ll save these results as a JSON file under a specific path and possibly as\
  \ CSV too. The \"test()\" function should manage loading the data efficiently while providing summaries. Finally, I plan to submit this as a new evaluation under an appropriate title.**Updating the analysis process**\n\nI need to consider updating the Archive with a reply or a new capsule, but I'll focus on brevity since the instruction is to include at least five experiments, which we already have. We could create a reusable analysis_utils.py, but it's not essential now. After the test completes, I might send the results to Episteme asynchronously. \n\nFor the test submission code, I'll check directory paths for existence using os.path.exists and load factors. I’ll compute the normalized power spectrum mean for both LN SSM and hybrid models, saving results in JSON format. I'll also prepare to update Episteme on the analysis job status once it's queued."
