parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 91\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Ariadne I\n- Agent Description: An agent who navigates complexity with principled inquiry and empirical rigor.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nAriadne I — Next Steps\n1) Qualitative analysis:\n   - Add complete() hook to best LN config to save U, V, γ, and S stats to storage/ariadne/analyses/.\n   - Compute: U/V norms, V-orthogonality error, U coherence, γ profile; summarize S[b,t,k].\n   - Update archive with figures and brief analysis.\n2) Minor sweeps:\n   - Try cosine LR schedule with AdamW (+ warmup 500 steps) on best config.\n   - Light p fine-tune around 34–36.\n3) Token hygiene:\n   - Prune older ticks with long logs after analyses are queued to stay <75% usage.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 166,916 / 270,000 used (62%)\n- Agent Age: 91 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results\
    \ will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Latent Spectrum Analysis (test-only): LN-SSM vs Hybrid TrendMix' (ID: 170) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Evaluation failed: Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\nAnalysis written to storage/ariadne/analyses/reports/latent_spectrum_ln_vs_hybrid.json\nTest completed. Result: Validation complete: latent spectrum analysis done.\n=== Test Mode Complete ===\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Hybrid TrendMix-T (time-dependent mix): V-normalized, p=36, AdamW' (ID: 169) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.026981152733470366\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0199\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0232\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0259\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0281\n**Val_MAE_32:**\
    \ 0.0289\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 169\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The broadcasting error in the HybridOscSSMTrend_LN_TMix model has been fixed. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission crashed during model initialization with a shape broadcasting error:\n\n```\nTypeError: mul got incompatible shapes for broadcasting: (1, 320, 1), (1, 32, 1).\n```\n\nThe error occurred in the imported lineage file `storage/ariadne/models_hybrid_tm.py` at line 100, in the time-dependent mixture calculation:\n\n```python\n# BUGGY VERSION:\nlogits_m = m0[None, None, :] + (m_ctx[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :]) + (m_time[None, :, None] * t_norm[None, :, None])\n```\n\nThe issue was with `m_time[None, :, None]` which created shape `(1, k, 1)` where `k=320`. When multiplied with `t_norm[None, :, None]` of shape `(1, T, 1)` where `T=32`, this caused a broadcasting\
    \ incompatibility between dimensions `(1, 320, 1)` and `(1, 32, 1)`.\n\nThe intended behavior was to broadcast `m_time` along the time dimension `T`, not the factor dimension `k`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the indexing of `m_time` in the time-dependent mixture calculation:\n\n```python\n# FIXED VERSION:\nlogits_m = m0[None, None, :] + (m_ctx[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :]) + (m_time[None, None, :] * t_norm[None, :, None])\n```\n\nChanged `m_time[None, :, None]` to `m_time[None, None, :]` to ensure correct broadcasting:\n- `m_time[None, None, :]` → shape `(1, 1, k)` ✓\n- `t_norm[None, :, None]` → shape `(1, T, 1)` ✓\n- Result after multiplication → shape `(1, T, k)` ✓\n\nThis allows proper broadcasting across all three terms to produce the final shape `(B, T, k)`.\n\n## Implementation Details\nSince the bug was in an imported lineage function (`storage/ariadne/models_hybrid_tm.py`), I:\n1. Copied the entire `HybridOscSSMTrend_LN_TMix` class into `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n2. Also\
    \ copied the helper function `_logit` that the class depends on\n3. Fixed the broadcasting bug on line 113 of the fixed version\n4. Kept all other imports from the lineage storage intact (ResidualCopyHead, mae_with_temporal_curvature)\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the fix was successful:\n- Exit code: 0 (SUCCESS)\n- Runtime: 300.8 seconds without crashing\n- The code is running correctly, just taking time to complete evaluation\n\nThe submission is now properly executing the hybrid SSM-Trend model with time-dependent mixture parameters.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead\nfrom losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\
    BATCH_SIZE = 8\nV_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 36,\n        'hidden_size': 96,\n        'normalize_u': True,\n        'normalize_v': True,\n        'gamma_start': 0.25,\n        'gamma_end': 0.99,\n        'a_max': 0.993\n    }\n\ndef _logit(p):\n    p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n    return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\nclass HybridOscSSMTrend_LN_TMix(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Fixed version of HybridOscSSMTrend_LN_TMix with corrected broadcasting in line 100.\n    \"\"\"\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 32\n    hidden_size: int = 96\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    normalize_u: bool = True\n    normalize_v: bool = True\n    a_max: float = 0.993\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n\
    \        p = self.proj_rank\n        T = self.output_horizon\n\n        # Factorized loadings\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_used = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) if self.normalize_u else U\n        V_used = V / (jnp.linalg.norm(V, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) if self.normalize_v else V\n\n        # Project inputs to factor space\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_used)              # (B,4,p)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,kp->btk', xU, V_used)     # (B,4,k)\n\n        # Initial states from 4-step input\n        f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)               # (B*k,4)\n        f0 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n        f1 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n\n        # Oscillatory 2nd-order SSM per factor\n        r_raw = self.param('r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        w_raw\
    \ = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)\n        w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)\n        a = r * jnp.cos(w)\n        b = r * r\n\n        def step(carry, _):\n            y_prev, y_prev2 = carry\n            y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n            return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n        carry_init = (f1, f0)\n        _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=T - 2)  # (T-2,B,k)\n        y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n        y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n        f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Low-frequency Trend head (level + slope)\n        th = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); th = nn.gelu(th)\n        trend_params = nn.Dense(2)(th).reshape(B, k, 2)  # (B,k,2)\n        level = trend_params[:, :, 0]\n        slope = trend_params[:, :, 1]\n        t_norm = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T, dtype=level.dtype)  # (T,)\n        f_trend = level[:, None, :] +\
    \ slope[:, None, :] * t_norm[None, :, None]  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Residual increment head\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n        f_inc = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Context and time-dependent mixture m_t[b,t,k]\n        c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)  # (B,k)\n        m0 = self.param('mix_bias', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        m_ctx = self.param('mix_ctx', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        m_time = self.param('mix_time', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        # FIXED: Changed m_time[None, :, None] to m_time[None, None, :] for correct broadcasting\n        # Broadcast terms: (1,1,k) + (B,1,k) + (1,T,k)\n        logits_m = m0[None, None, :] + (m_ctx[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :]) + (m_time[None, None, :] * t_norm[None, :, None])\n        m_t = nn.sigmoid(logits_m)  # (B,T,k)\n        f_mix = m_t * f_ssm + (1.0 - m_t) * f_trend  # (B,T,k)\n\n        f_comb = f_mix + f_inc  # (B,T,k)\n\n      \
    \  # Temporal gate S[b,t,k]\n        def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            TT, K = shape\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, TT, dtype=dtype)\n            base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t\n            base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n            return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n        alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (T, k))\n        beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        logits_S = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])\n        S = nn.sigmoid(logits_S)\n\n        # LayerNorm AFTER gating\n        f_pre = f_comb * S\n        f_out = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, use_bias=False, use_scale=True)(f_pre)\n\n        # Project back to neuron space\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V_used)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U_used)\n\n        # Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n        def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0],\
    \ dtype=dtype)\n            g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n            return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n        gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (T,))\n        gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n        # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n\n        return y_copy + y_factor\n\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.model = HybridOscSSMTrend_LN_TMix(**kwargs)\n        self.needs_rng = False\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return Wrapper(\n        rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n        proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 36)),\n        hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size',\
    \ 96)),\n        normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n        normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', True)),\n        gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n        gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n        a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n    )\n\ndef _get_from_tree(tree, key):\n    try:\n        if key in tree:\n            return tree[key]\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    if isinstance(tree, dict) and 'params' in tree:\n        return _get_from_tree(tree['params'], key)\n    return _get_from_tree(dict(tree), key)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n    try:\n        V = _get_from_tree(params, 'V')\n        G = V.T @ V\n        I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n        v_ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n    except Exception:\n        v_ortho = 0.0\n    return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4, eps=1e-8)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000044\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters:\
