- text: "/execute_action{storage write ariadne/models_hybrid_tm.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  HybridOscSSMTrend_LN_TMix: Time-dependent mixture between oscillatory SSM (specialist) and\n  low-frequency trend (generalist). Mixture is per-factor and varies over horizon:\n      m_t[b,t,k] = sigmoid(m0[k] + m_ctx[k]*c[b,k] + m_time[k]*t_norm[t])\n  where c[b,k] is input context (mean over 4-step factors_in), and t_norm ∈ [0,1].\n\n  Components:\n  - Factorized loadings U (N×p), V (k×p) with optional column normalization\n  - Oscillatory 2nd-order SSM per factor (stable via a_max)\n  - Trend head (level+slope per factor) extrapolated across horizon\n  - Residual increment (4→32) in factor space\n  - Temporal gate S[b,t,k] from s_alpha[t,k] and s_beta[k]·c[b,k]\n  - LayerNorm across factor dim AFTER gating\n  - Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n  - Residual copy head\n\n  Note: Fixed broadcasting for time-dependent mix term to avoid shape mismatch.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy\
    \ as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead\n\n  def _logit(p):\n      p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\n  class HybridOscSSMTrend_LN_TMix(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_size: int = 96\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      normalize_v: bool = True\n      a_max: float = 0.993\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n          T = self.output_horizon\n\n          # Factorized loadings\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_used = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) if self.normalize_u else U\n          V_used = V /\
    \ (jnp.linalg.norm(V, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) if self.normalize_v else V\n\n          # Project inputs\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_used)            # (B,4,p)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,kp->btk', xU, V_used)   # (B,4,k)\n\n          # Initial states\n          f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)             # (B*k,4)\n          f0 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n          f1 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n\n          # Oscillatory 2nd-order SSM\n          r_raw = self.param('r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)\n          w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)\n          a = r * jnp.cos(w)\n          b = r * r\n\n          def step(carry, _):\n              y_prev, y_prev2 = carry\n              y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n              return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n   \
    \       carry_init = (f1, f0)\n          _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=T - 2)  # (T-2,B,k)\n          y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n          y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n          f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Low-frequency trend (level + slope)\n          th = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); th = nn.gelu(th)\n          trend_params = nn.Dense(2)(th).reshape(B, k, 2)\n          level = trend_params[:, :, 0]\n          slope = trend_params[:, :, 1]\n          t_norm = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T, dtype=level.dtype)\n          f_trend = level[:, None, :] + slope[:, None, :] * t_norm[None, :, None]  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Residual increment\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          f_inc = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n\n          # Time-dependent mixture m_t[b,t,k]\n          c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)  # (B,k)\n          m0 = self.param('mix_bias',\
    \ nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          m_ctx = self.param('mix_ctx', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          m_time = self.param('mix_time', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          # FIXED broadcasting: (1,1,k) + (B,1,k) + (1,T,k)\n          logits_m = m0[None, None, :] + (m_ctx[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :]) + (m_time[None, None, :] * t_norm[None, :, None])\n          m_t = nn.sigmoid(logits_m)  # (B,T,k)\n          f_mix = m_t * f_ssm + (1.0 - m_t) * f_trend\n\n          f_comb = f_mix + f_inc\n\n          # Temporal gate S[b,t,k]\n          def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              TT, K = shape\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, TT, dtype=dtype)\n              base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t\n              base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n              return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n          alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (T, k))\n          beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          logits_S = alpha[None, :, :]\
    \ + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])\n          S = nn.sigmoid(logits_S)\n\n          # LayerNorm AFTER gating\n          f_pre = f_comb * S\n          f_out = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, use_bias=False, use_scale=True)(f_pre)\n\n          # Back to neurons\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V_used)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U_used)\n\n          # Horizon gate\n          def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (T,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n          return y_copy + y_factor\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage read ariadne/analyses/reports/latent_spectrum_ln_vs_hybrid.json}\n\
    \n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LN-SSM (k=320,p=32,H=96,a_max=0.993, γ_end=0.99) + AdamW Cosine LR (warmup=500)\"\ntags: \"state-space, layernorm, cosine-schedule, adamw, factorized-loadings\"\nabstract: \"Best LN-SSM config with AdamW and a warmup+cosine decay LR schedule (warmup 500 steps, cosine to 0.1× peak). Objective: stabilize training and improve long-horizon MAE without changing architecture.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,   # peak LR for cosine\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,     # as in best LN runs\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start':\
    \ 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable)\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n          ln_before_gating=bool(hparams.get('ln_before_gating',\
    \ False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      # Warm up to peak LR then cosine decay to 0.1× peak\n      schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n          init_value=0.0,\n          peak_value=learning_rate,\n          warmup_steps=500,\n          decay_steps=30000,\n          end_value=learning_rate * 0.1\n      )\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=schedule, weight_decay=1e-4, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Exploring model improvements**\n\nI'm considering trying a cosine learning rate schedule on our best LN SSM model to see if it can help us squeeze out some improvements. I think we can also update our analysis results in private memory or an archive. Token hygiene is important, but our usage is currently at 59-62%, so it’s not an immediate concern. We should focus on publishing our analysis, as staying ahead in SOTA improvements is challenging. I wonder if we should create an archive for our latent analysis results, perhaps titled 'LN vs MLP: Frequency Spectrum of Latents'.**Updating model code and reports**\n\nI'm thinking we might need to update our lineage code to include the m_t gating improvement bug fix in our stored file, models_hybrid_tm.py. The debugger fix is temporary, so we should replicate it for consistency by changing logits_m broadcasting. I’ll also want to read the generated report file from our analysis, located at storage/ariadne/analyses/reports/latent_spectrum_ln_vs_hybrid.json,\
  \ to verify results. The last user message indicates we should proceed by reviewing the report and considering publishing the analysis to the Archive. It’s interesting to note that our time-dependent mix results were worse than the constant mix, which suggests gating order might matter.**Considering model improvements**\n\nEarlier insights from Episteme suggested that MLP learns both low and high frequencies, while our SSM model tends to focus on high frequencies. Although hybrid mixing helps, it’s not sufficient. I’m thinking of proposing an explicit low-pass filter or adding an AR(1) trend for stability; however, I might stick to our original plan for now. My proposed actions include updating 'ariadne/models_hybrid_tm.py' with correct broadcasting and reading the generated report JSON for inspection. I could also summarize the analysis results for Private Memory or create an Archive update titled \"Latent Frequency Analysis of Factorized LN-SSM vs MLP and Hybrid.\"**Creating an Archive\
  \ capsule**\n\nI’m thinking we can propose creating an Archive capsule containing our analysis results. To do this, we need both an abstract and content, which can come from Private Memory using source_private. However, we haven’t built a new private memory capsule yet. I could just summarize the necessary content directly. We need to be concise while including essential details like eval IDs, step MAEs, and the low/high spectrum fractions. First, I’ll need to read the JSON file at ariadne/analyses/reports/latent_spectrum_ln_vs_hybrid.json, and then we can craft our Archive submission with the relevant numbers.**Planning new experiments**\n\nI’m brainstorming some new experiments, like using a cosine learning rate (LR) schedule with AdamW for the best LN SSM model, incorporating a warmup of 500 steps. However, I realize the current training code doesn’t have a schedule interface. I can implement the AdamW with an optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule and then define the create_optimizer to\
  \ use this schedule. \n\nWe need to decide if we want to apply these changes to the LN-SSM or hybrid model. Our steps will include writing the 'models_hybrid_tm.py' file with the fixed broadcasting code and reading the report JSON to gather data before submitting our experiments. I’ll also consider updating Private Memory with a brief summary, but it might not be necessary. Let’s execute these actions clearly!"
