    \ → −0.026876\n      - Hybrid TrendMix V-normalized, p=36 + AdamW (ID 164) → −0.026863 (best hybrid)\n      - Hybrid TrendMix p=34 V-normalized + AdamW (ID 168) → −0.026881\n      - Time-dependent mix m_t[b,t,k] (ID 169) → −0.026981 (worse than static mix)\n\n      Latent exports and analyses:\n      - Full-val latent export for LN-SSM (ID 155): factors_out, factors_preln, S_gate, gamma at:\n        storage/ariadne/analyses/latents/ln_ssm_k320_p32_H96_a0.993_g0.99/trial_{seed}/\n      - Hybrid TrendMix latent export (ID 162): f_ssm, f_trend, factors_out, mix_gate m, S_gate, gamma at:\n        storage/ariadne/analyses/latents/hybrid_trendmix_k320_p32_H96_a0.993_g0.99/trial_{seed}/\n      - Spectral analysis (test-only) initial (ID 170) and de-meaned v2 (ID 177):\n        Reports saved to storage/ariadne/analyses/reports/latent_spectrum_ln_vs_hybrid.json\n        and ..._demeaned.json. Findings: hybrid internals separate cleanly (f_ssm high-freq; f_trend low-freq; mean mix ≈0.49).\n  \
    \      LN-SSM factors_out spectrum depends on gating/gamma; de-meaning clarifies frequency content.\n\n      Takeaways:\n      - The LN-SSM baseline with a_max≈0.993, γ_end≈0.99 remains the strongest (−0.026768).\n      - V-normalization, LN-before-gating, cosine LR, and time-dependent hybrid mixing did not improve SOTA.\n      - Hybrid TrendMix is competitive (~−0.02686–−0.02688) but below best LN-SSM and Episteme’s MLP (−0.026743).\n      - Latent exports and de-meaned spectral reports provide actionable diagnostics for future design.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Exploring MoE Gating Options**


  I''m considering testing MoE gating across eight discovered conditions and thinking about incorporating condition-wise gating in our factors. There''s a challenge because the system doesn''t allow custom training loops, but I wonder if we could use condition labels within the network. The network.apply only receives inputs without passing labels, so accessing them seems impossible. I’m also exploring multi-band factorization by separating high and low frequencies, alongside adjusting curvature penalties for long horizons based on previous attempts.**Refining Model Parameters**


  I''m thinking about adding an STFT-l2 penalty on f_out to encourage multi-band coverage, but it feels complex. Maybe I should expand p to 40, since we previously tested 32, 36, and 40, with 36 not being better than 32. I wonder if we should try LN parameters in Factor LN, keeping bias=False and scale=True. I might also consider GroupNorm across subsets to prevent over-normalization and propose FactorNorm gating. There''s a small difference to bridge with the best result at 0.02674. We also need to finalize the archive update with baseline and previous experiments.**Planning Token Pruning**


  It seems like there''s a need to summarize experiments from ticks 75-92 since the user isn''t explicitly asking a question but likely expects the next actions. I think we might want to run a token prune to free up some space. Starting from tick 76, I could summarize our LN-before-gating experiments and other ablations, which showed non-critical outcomes. For ticks 85-91, I would summarize trends in hybrids, V-normalized tests, and mixture gating. I need to exclude any protected ticks from this pruning process.**Executing Token Pruning**


  Since tick 82 isn''t protected, I can proceed with pruning the block from 76 to 92, which contains only non-protected ticks. It''s great that I''m able to summarize across these ticks while ensuring all are consecutive and meet pruning rules. I’ll make sure to include pointers for the best results and models. After that, I’ll update the models_hybrid_tm to incorporate fixes and suggest reporting to the archive with a new title and abstract, but my current focus is on executing the token pruning action now.**Preparing for Token Pruning**


  I’m considering next runs queued with a focus on time-dependent models, but recent results haven’t been promising. I think it’s wise to revisit the LN strategies pre- and post-gating since the past approach regressed. I want to pivot to knowledge distillation while avoiding training hacks, suggesting we implement a loss penalty aligning outputs. My focus right now is on pruning ticks 76-91, crafting a concise summary, and exploring arcane details for our findings, while preparing the prune action.'
