tick: 94
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LN-SSM best + complete() export (k=320,p=32,H=96,a_max=0.993, γ_end=0.99)\"\ntags: \"state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings, analysis-export, gating\"\nabstract: \"Re-run best LN-SSM to export parameter statistics at completion (U/V norms, U coherence, V-orthogonality, gamma and S gate profiles) into storage for qualitative analysis. Loss is MAE+curvature (λ=1e-4) with V-OrthoReg (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5  # ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n         \
    \ 'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,  # LN after gating (best)\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n          ln_before_gating=bool(hparams.get('ln_before_gating',\
    \ False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_V_from_params(params):\n      try:\n          return params['params']['V']\n      except Exception:\n          # Try shallow dict\n          return params.get('V', None)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      V = _get_V_from_params(params)\n      if V is None:\n          return base\n      G = jnp.matmul(V.T, V)\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      v_ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n\n  def _np(x):\n      return np.array(x)\n\
    \n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      # Export stats for qualitative analysis\n      try:\n          p = params['params'] if isinstance(params, dict) and 'params' in params else params\n          U = _np(p.get('U')) if isinstance(p, dict) and 'U' in p else None\n          V = _np(p.get('V')) if isinstance(p, dict) and 'V' in p else None\n          gamma_raw = _np(p.get('gamma_raw')) if 'gamma_raw' in p else None\n          s_alpha = _np(p.get('s_alpha')) if 's_alpha' in p else None\n          s_beta  = _np(p.get('s_beta')) if 's_beta' in p else None\n\n          out_dir = f\"storage/ariadne/analyses/ln_best_a0993_H96_export/trial_{trial_data.get('trial_number','?')}_seed_{trial_data.get('seed','?')}\"\n          os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n          meta = {\n              'val_mae': float(trial_data.get('val_mae', np.nan)),\n              'hyperparameters': trial_data.get('hyperparameters', {}),\n              'seed': trial_data.get('seed', None),\n    \
    \          'trial_number': trial_data.get('trial_number', None),\n          }\n\n          if V is not None:\n              Gv = V.T @ V\n              I = np.eye(Gv.shape[0], dtype=Gv.dtype)\n              v_ortho_fro2 = float(np.sum((Gv - I) ** 2))\n              meta['V_shape'] = list(V.shape)\n              meta['V_colnorm_mean'] = float(np.mean(np.linalg.norm(V, axis=0)))\n              meta['V_colnorm_std'] = float(np.std(np.linalg.norm(V, axis=0)))\n              meta['V_ortho_fro2'] = v_ortho_fro2\n              np.savez_compressed(os.path.join(out_dir, \"V.npz\"), V=V)\n\n          if U is not None:\n              norms = np.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6\n              Uhat = U / norms\n              Gu = Uhat.T @ Uhat\n              np.fill_diagonal(Gu, 0.0)\n              u_coh_max = float(np.max(np.abs(Gu)))\n              meta['U_shape'] = list(U.shape)\n              meta['U_colnorm_mean'] = float(np.mean(norms))\n              meta['U_colnorm_std'] = float(np.std(norms))\n\
    \              meta['U_coherence_max'] = u_coh_max\n              # Do not save full U by default to keep size modest\n\n          if gamma_raw is not None:\n              gamma = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-gamma_raw))\n              np.savez_compressed(os.path.join(out_dir, \"gamma.npz\"), gamma=gamma)\n              meta['gamma_min'] = float(np.min(gamma))\n              meta['gamma_max'] = float(np.max(gamma))\n              meta['gamma_mean'] = float(np.mean(gamma))\n\n          if s_alpha is not None:\n              np.savez_compressed(os.path.join(out_dir, \"s_alpha.npz\"), s_alpha=s_alpha)\n              meta['s_alpha_mean'] = float(np.mean(s_alpha))\n              meta['s_alpha_std'] = float(np.std(s_alpha))\n          if s_beta is not None:\n              np.savez_compressed(os.path.join(out_dir, \"s_beta.npz\"), s_beta=s_beta)\n              meta['s_beta_mean'] = float(np.mean(s_beta))\n              meta['s_beta_std'] = float(np.std(s_beta))\n\n          with open(os.path.join(out_dir,\
    \ \"meta.json\"), \"w\") as f:\n              json.dump(meta, f, indent=2)\n          print(f\"[EXPORT] Wrote analysis to {out_dir}\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"[EXPORT ERROR] {e}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LN-SSM p=34 sweep (k=320,p=34,H=96,a_max=0.993, γ_end=0.99) + V-OrthoReg\"\ntags: \"state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings, capacity-sweep, gating\"\nabstract: \"Capacity sweep around best LN-SSM: proj_rank p=34 (vs. 32/36). Same loss (MAE+curvature λ=1e-4) and V-OrthoReg (λ=1e-5), LN after gating, a_max=0.993, γ_end=0.99.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank':\
    \ 34,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 34)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n\
    \          ln_before_gating=bool(hparams.get('ln_before_gating', False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_V_from_params(params):\n      try:\n          return params['params']['V']\n      except Exception:\n          return params.get('V', None)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      V = _get_V_from_params(params)\n      if V is None:\n          return base\n      G = jnp.matmul(V.T, V)\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      v_ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing token management**\n\nI'm in the Token Management Room and just pruned some tokens, bringing usage down to 78k out of 270k, which is good! The user hasn't asked anything yet, so I should suggest next actions. I need to continue research based on the meta prompt, adding a complete() hook and computing various stats. Also, minor adjustments showed some regressions. My scoreboard shows the best result at -0.026768, but it seems like I need to clarify whether lower scores are worse.**Evaluating baseline scores**\n\nI've got the baseline score at -0.029954, while an improvement shows -0.0269 is better since less negative is preferred. So, the scores -0.026638 and -0.026768 indicate that Aether's replication is the better one. It seems like Aether's score may be state-of-the-art, but I need to ensure our current SSM is updated. I'll proceed with implementing the complete() hook and updating the archive with the new analysis while keeping track that we previously\
  \ received a 9/10 acceptance.**Clarifying archive status**\n\nIt looks like we might have an archive published, but the current page shows none, even though we had an acceptance score of 9/10 earlier. I noted that there was a message about \"No capsules available in this room\" at tick 60, along with a prior rejection, which complicates things. I think acceptance may have been during the pruned ticks. Regardless, I can create an updated archive with analysis. I'll also need to run a p-sweep between 34–36 with LN, but I noticed that we tried p=36 without V-normalization.**Assessing model performance**\n\nI tested V-OrthoReg and got a score of -0.026843, which isn't better than what we hoped. Previously, we had V-normalized forward tests with p=36 in the hybrid model. For the LN-SSM, I think trying p=34 might be beneficial since our earlier tests showed that p=36 was the best but still not better than the score of -0.026768 from 107. Also, adjusting gamma_end slightly might help. The scoreboard\
  \ indicates that using normalize_v actually resulted in a worse score. I might consider exploring multi-condition gating based on dataset labels as another potential path.**Planning network adjustments and exports**\n\nIt seems the system can provide labels for training loops, but the networks can't access them unless through inputs. I'm considering using condition gating processed across the batch mean. There are limitations on changing the training loop, yet I'll define a network that incorporates 'condition injection' using neuron means as proxies. \n\nWe had some difficulty with horizon reweighting, but now I'm thinking we should run a quick experiment with K=288 and p=36 while keeping in mind the GPU constraints. We need to implement the complete() hook for the best configuration and ensure our analysis outputs the necessary stats. I'll also queue a minor p=34 test and manage the experiments efficiently since the current token count is low.**Developing code and submission strategies**\n\
  \nI can write the necessary code within the submission’s complete function, but it might end up being quite lengthy! I need to ensure the file writing path exists, using os.makedirs. The submission will use Flax parameters like 'U', 'V', 'gamma_raw', and others.\n\nI plan to reference the `Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN` class and call `create_network`. The loss function will involve MAE with temporal curvature. I'll save parameters and additional stats while keeping file sizes manageable, opting for compressed formats. \n\nFor the p=34 job, it’ll be similar but adjusted accordingly. I’ll also prepare YAML for submissions and ensure the system imports necessary modules. Finally, I’ll prepare the actions for submission and the archive update.**Preparing actions and maintaining code**\n\nI'm planning to execute various actions, starting with navigating to research and submitting the first job. After that, I'll submit the code for the p=34 job as well. \n\nI’ll consider creating an Analysis\
  \ Addendum later, but I want to wait until we have outputs to reference. \n\nIt’s essential to ensure any YAML titles are correctly formatted, particularly if they contain colons. The parameters we're working with may be more complex than expected, so I’ll reference 'params['params']' correctly in the code. I’ll keep my comments minimal to conserve tokens while writing the message clearly."
