    \ optax\n\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 128,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 128)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n          ln_before_gating=bool(hparams.get('ln_before_gating', False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_V_from_params(params):\n      try:\n          return params['params']['V']\n      except Exception:\n          return params.get('V', None)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      V = _get_V_from_params(params)\n      if V is None:\n          return base\n      G = jnp.matmul(V.T, V)\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0],\
    \ dtype=G.dtype)\n      v_ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,H=80, a_max=0.993, γ_end=0.99) + V-OrthoReg\"\ntags: \"state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings, capacity, gating\"\nabstract: \"Hidden size sweep on best LN-SSM: narrow increment MLP to H=80 (vs H=96) to test parsimony–generalization trade-off. Same training and regularization.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n \
    \         'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 80,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 80)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u',\
    \ True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n          ln_before_gating=bool(hparams.get('ln_before_gating', False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_V_from_params(params):\n      try:\n          return params['params']['V']\n      except Exception:\n          return params.get('V', None)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      V = _get_V_from_params(params)\n      if V is None:\n          return base\n      G = jnp.matmul(V.T, V)\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      v_ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n \
    \         optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering architecture replication**\n\nI want to propose replicating the state-of-the-art (SOTA) factorized MLP architecture with layer normalization (LN) but with our own adaptations. The rules state we can clone code via official research channels but not import it directly, which makes replicating concepts tricky. Others have achieved a better score, but I think small modifications to our approach could yield improvements. The guidelines suggest focusing on novelty while achieving a high score, but we could run an alternative method using micro-sweeps and adjusting parameters like gamma end.**Analyzing performance metrics**\n\nI've been reviewing the performance metrics, and it looks like there's been a decline with 104 at p=36 scoring -0.026843, and even worse with p=40. It appears p=32 is the best. I've noted that V-normalized forward improved slightly in one attempt, but overall results are not encouraging. Also, it seems recurrence isn't critical, as performance\
  \ is mainly driven by increment head/gating. I’m considering simplifying the network to use increment MLP with gating, which might lead to better results. Additionally, I think tweaking gamma_end to 1 or 0.995 and enhancing the S_init schedule could help.**Exploring training strategies**\n\nI'm considering using increment dropout, but it hasn’t helped much. Another option is to propose step weighting in the loss function focused on long horizons, even though horizon-weighted attempts didn't improve things previously. I’m thinking about a two-stage training approach where we freeze certain loadings and fine-tune gating, but custom loops aren't allowed. Instead, I might look into using weight decay with AdamW, though that hasn’t shown improvement either. I could explore a mixture-of-experts approach using provided condition labels, but it seems our current code doesn't access them properly.**Considering architectural changes**\n\nI'm exploring alternatives, like scaling the layer normalization\
  \ (LN) epsilon or modifying how it's applied across dimensions. Adding something like residual gating with LN bias could require significant modifications to the models. I wonder about using RMSNorm or a scale-only LN approach to create learnable scales and reduce shifts, but I realize big changes are tough to implement simultaneously given the time constraints. \n\nFor now, I want to read the analysis export to compute statistics before moving on to submit new experiments. I’ll also need to update the model configuration to allow for the LN epsilon parameter.**Exploring training modifications**\n\nThe instructions allow customization of network code but not training loops, so I’m thinking of making modifications accordingly. I want to try replicating Aether I's MLP architecture while focusing on improving our LN-SSM with H=128 since increasing H is cost-effective. \n\nFor experiments, I might increase k to 352 or 384 while monitoring performance impacts. We can also adjust the gamma schedule\
  \ and S gate shape, but I’ll propose to queue submissions with H=128 and H=80. Finally, I need to read the exported analysis files to summarize our findings before submitting these changes while keeping the code minimal."
