parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LN-SSM + U-coherence reg + s_beta centering (k=320,p=32,H=96,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99)\"\ntags: \"state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings, regularization, gating\"\nabstract: \"Add two lightweight priors to best LN-SSM: (1) U coherence regularizer on column-normalized U to reduce factor overlap; (2) s_beta L2 centering to stabilize temporal gating across seeds. Keep V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5   # ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n  U_COH_LAM   = 1e-6   # off-diagonal power of U_hat^T U_hat\n  SBETA_LAM   = 1e-4   # L2 centering on s_beta\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank':\
    \ 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def _get_param(tree, name):\n      if isinstance(tree, dict):\n          if 'params' in tree and isinstance(tree['params'], dict) and name in tree['params']:\n              return tree['params'][name]\n          if name in tree:\n              return tree[name]\n      return None\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base\
    \ = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n      # V orthogonality\n      V = _get_param(params, 'V')\n      v_pen = 0.0\n      if V is not None:\n          Gv = jnp.matmul(V.T, V)\n          I  = jnp.eye(Gv.shape[0], dtype=Gv.dtype)\n          v_pen = jnp.sum((Gv - I) ** 2)\n\n      # U coherence on normalized columns\n      U = _get_param(params, 'U')\n      ucoh_pen = 0.0\n      if U is not None:\n          norms = jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6\n          Uhat  = U / norms\n          Gu    = jnp.matmul(Uhat.T, Uhat)  # (p,p)\n          off   = Gu - jnp.diag(jnp.diag(Gu))\n          ucoh_pen = jnp.sum(off ** 2)\n\n      # s_beta centering\n      sb = _get_param(params, 's_beta')\n      sb_pen = 0.0\n      if sb is not None:\n          sb_pen = jnp.mean(sb ** 2)\n\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_pen + U_COH_LAM * ucoh_pen + SBETA_LAM * sb_pen\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n\
    \          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LN-SSM + stronger U-coherence reg (λ=5e-6) + s_beta centering\"\ntags: \"state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings, regularization, gating\"\nabstract: \"Same as prior but sweep U-coherence strength to 5e-6 to test sensitivity. Other settings unchanged (k=320,p=32,H=96,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99; V-ortho λ=1e-5; s_beta L2 λ=1e-4).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n  U_COH_LAM   = 5e-6   # stronger\n  SBETA_LAM   = 1e-4\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size':\
    \ 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def _get_param(tree, name):\n      if isinstance(tree, dict):\n          if 'params' in tree and isinstance(tree['params'], dict) and name in tree['params']:\n              return tree['params'][name]\n          if name in tree:\n              return tree[name]\n      return None\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions,\
    \ targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n      V = _get_param(params, 'V')\n      v_pen = 0.0\n      if V is not None:\n          Gv = jnp.matmul(V.T, V)\n          I  = jnp.eye(Gv.shape[0], dtype=Gv.dtype)\n          v_pen = jnp.sum((Gv - I) ** 2)\n\n      U = _get_param(params, 'U')\n      ucoh_pen = 0.0\n      if U is not None:\n          norms = jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6\n          Uhat  = U / norms\n          Gu    = jnp.matmul(Uhat.T, Uhat)\n          off   = Gu - jnp.diag(jnp.diag(Gu))\n          ucoh_pen = jnp.sum(off ** 2)\n\n      sb = _get_param(params, 's_beta')\n      sb_pen = 0.0\n      if sb is not None:\n          sb_pen = jnp.mean(sb ** 2)\n\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_pen + U_COH_LAM * ucoh_pen + SBETA_LAM * sb_pen\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating results for strategy**\n\nI’m at the Research Counter reviewing results from H sweeps. It looks like H=128 gives -0.02693 and H=80 shows -0.026943. The best score remains ID 107 at -0.026768, while Aether's score is better at -0.026638, which is less negative. I realize that a higher score (less negative) is better. Aether is indeed the best option, with Ariadne trailing by a difference of about 0.00013. So, I should strategize from here!**Planning coherence regularization**\n\nI'm planning to implement coherence regularization on U's normalized columns and a centering penalty for s_beta. I think a small improvement would be to add an orthogonality penalty for V, currently set at λ=1e-5, while U_coherence could be around λ=1e-7 to 5e-7. I should ensure that compute_loss pulls the normalized U from params, as we previously normalized it during forward propagation. The s_beta parameter, which has a single vector shape, should have an L2 regularization to penalize\
  \ its mean. I'll add this additional term!**Implementing penalties in compute_loss**\n\nI’m considering adding a gamma prior or gating smoothing, but since the gamma prior didn’t help earlier, I’ll focus on coherence for U and the s_beta centering penalty. I need to ensure that I don’t break the compilation. In compute_loss, I’ll implement the following: calculate the base using mae_with_temporal_curvature, apply the V_ortho penalty, compute the U_coherence penalty, and ensure the off-diagonal squared Frobenius norm is calculated correctly. For s_beta, I’ll penalize mean(s_beta**2) to center it near zero, selecting λ_UC around 1e-6 and λ_sb to avoid overshadowing the base. Finally, I’ll create a submission titled \"LN-SSM + U coherence + s_beta center.\"**Preparing submission for improved generalization**\n\nI’ve noticed that the drift in s_beta across seeds suggests that adding a centering penalty may reduce variability and help with generalization, which could slightly improve our results.\
  \ I’ll prepare a submission that references the existing models_fact_ln import, incorporating the new terms in compute_loss. It's also a good idea to add complete() for validating stats. I need to ensure consistent BATCH_SIZE and BASE_SEED, and I’ll propose one or two concurrent submissions—one with λ_UC at 1e-6 and λ_sb at 1e-4, and another to test sensitivity with λ_UC adjusted.**Preparing for submissions and updating code**\n\nRight now, I have no running experiments, so it’s a good time to submit two. Maybe updating the paper could wait until later. I’m preparing the code content, starting with importing jax.numpy as jnp and defining the constants, like V_ORTHO_LAM and U_COH_LAM. \n\nI’ll implement compute_loss to include the coherence and centering penalties for U and s_beta. I’ll ensure robust retrieval for parameters and calculate the penalties accordingly. \n\nFor submission, I’m planning IDs like “LN-SSM + U-coh reg + s_beta center” with specified lambda values. Also, I’ll read\
  \ results of p=34 since prior outputs underperformed. Let's execute!"
