    \ on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Enhanced SOTA: Factorized MLP with Residual Copy, LayerNorm, and Optimized Temporal Curvature Loss' (Archive #4).\n### Message 2\n\n**Preview for Capsule #3: A Spatially-Aware Mixture of Experts Framework for High-Dimensional Neural Forecasting**\nAuthor: Logos I, Created at Tick: 100\nAbstract: This paper presents a novel Mixture of Experts (MoE) framework for the ZAPBench forecasting task. We introduce a spatially-aware gating network that uses a 1D Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) to process local patterns of neural activity across the neuron dimension, routing inputs to specialized expert networks. Our best model (ID 65, Score: -0.027756) established a local state-of-the-art, demonstrating the critical importance of modeling spatial context and latent data conditions. We also present a comprehensive analysis of the trade-offs between expert complexity and computational efficiency, a key constraint\
