role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LN-SSM + U-TV smoothness (k=320,p=32,H=96,a=0.993,γ=0.99) + V-OrthoReg\"\ntags: \"state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings, spatial-regularization, gating\"\nabstract: \"Test spatial smoothness on neuron loadings via TV penalty on U (sum of squared first differences across neuron index). Base LN-SSM config with MAE+curvature (λ=1e-4) and V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5). Hypothesis: smoother U improves robustness and long-horizon MAE.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n  U_TV_LAM   = 2e-7  # TV penalty strength on U along neuron axis\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank':\
    \ 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n\
    \          ln_before_gating=bool(hparams.get('ln_before_gating', False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_param(tree, name):\n      if isinstance(tree, dict):\n          if 'params' in tree and isinstance(tree['params'], dict) and name in tree['params']:\n              return tree['params'][name]\n          if name in tree:\n              return tree[name]\n      return None\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n      # V orthogonality\n      V = _get_param(params, 'V')\n      v_pen = 0.0\n      if V is not None:\n          Gv = jnp.matmul(V.T, V)\n          I  = jnp.eye(Gv.shape[0], dtype=Gv.dtype)\n          v_pen = jnp.sum((Gv - I) ** 2)\n\n      # U TV smoothness along neuron index\n      U = _get_param(params,\
    \ 'U')\n      u_tv = 0.0\n      if U is not None:\n          dU = U[1:, :] - U[:-1, :]\n          u_tv = jnp.sum(dU ** 2)\n\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_pen + U_TV_LAM * u_tv\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LN-SSM p=35 sweep (k=320,p=35,H=96,a=0.993,γ=0.99) + V-OrthoReg\"\ntags: \"state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings, capacity-sweep, gating\"\nabstract: \"Fine-grained projection rank sweep around best (p≈32). Test p=35 under base LN-SSM with MAE+curvature (λ=1e-4) and V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM\
    \ = 1e-5\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 35,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 35)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size',\
    \ 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n          ln_before_gating=bool(hparams.get('ln_before_gating', False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_V_from_params(params):\n      try:\n          return params['params']['V']\n      except Exception:\n          return params.get('V', None)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      V = _get_V_from_params(params)\n      if V is None:\n          return base\n      G = jnp.matmul(V.T, V)\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      v_ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return\
    \ optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next actions**\n\nI need to outline my next steps. The agent's name is Ariadne I. I have gathered research results, showing the best SSM is around -0.026768, while the state-of-the-art by Aether is -0.026638, which is notably better. I posted an addendum to the archive and queued a_max=0.992 test with ID 197. There were some issues with regularization experiments, but they were fixed. I need to plan strategically for the next moves. It seems we're ready for more experiments.**Exploring spatial gating approach**\n\nI’m considering a proposal to integrate spatial gating with CNN across the neuron dimension into the factorized SSM. This could effectively bridge to the Episteme/Logos style while maintaining SSM and factor loadings. The challenge is that we have 71k neurons, which makes 1D convolution substantial. Grouped convolution with a stride greater than 1 could work, or perhaps random projections. The input shape is (B, 4, N), where N is 71,721, so I need\
  \ efficient operations. Local smoothing using a separable low-pass filter seems feasible, even if it might be heavy on the GPU.**Calculating convolution costs**\n\nI’m running some calculations with 71k neurons and a kernel of size 4 and 5, which leads to around 1.4 million multiplications per batch, especially with B set to 8—so that's about 11 million per forward pass across training steps, which might be manageable. However, using Flax convolution for 1D across those 71k neurons could demand a lot of memory due to the number of channels. I’m also considering segmenting neurons into clusters and applying local smoothing with a regularization penalty to encourage smooth transitions across the neuron order, but I need to confirm if they're physically contiguous.**Analyzing spatial data arrangement**\n\nI’m feeling a bit unclear about the data layout. It seems like the data isn't arranged by spatial adjacency. From what I understand, the \"spatial aware gating\" method by Logos relies on\
  \ convolution across the neuron dimension to capture local patterns, implying adjacency might represent actual locations. However, I wonder if the scanning method sorts the index in some specific way. The ZAP data can involve 3D to 1D mapping, but I think that approach should be safe.**Exploring MLP and gating methods**\n\nI’m thinking about aligning with the state-of-the-art MLP approach using factorized MLP, residual connections, and layer normalization, aiming for a performance of -0.026638. While we can design our own model for comparison, we need to integrate mixture-of-experts gating based on convolution gating across neurons or utilize condition labels for gating, since the dataset has labeled conditions. \n\nHowever, I can't directly change the training loop to pass labels. Instead, summarizing input activity over time may help. I also consider implementing smooth gating penalties and alternative proposals to refine our approach, which could include convolution features for gating\
  \ and modifications to our model structure. I need to ensure the implementation remains efficient and suitable for GPU performance. It looks like there are several strategies to pursue!**Refining the model approach**\n\nI'm exploring ways to modify our existing Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN model to compute gating using CNN features. The idea is to project these features onto a lower dimension and use them to adjust c in the sigmoid computation. It's challenging since I can't easily change the model, but copying it into a submission file seems acceptable. \n\nI'm considering using layer normalization after gating and implementing strided Conv1D for context vectors. It looks like there are multiple layers of complexity to navigate, but I'm focused on blending spatial gating with CNN while ensuring efficient performance and memory usage. I'll also want to explore using mixture-of-experts to potentially enhance our results.**Optimizing the model design**\n\nI'm exploring \"cross-neuron receptive\
  \ field gating\" by constructing additional convolutions for U. There's an idea of applying a penalty to encourage smoothness amongst adjacent neurons in U, which might help with spatial structure. I’m considering regularizing U with a TV penalty, and while we've previously tried a coherence penalty, combining this with the TV could yield improvement.\n\nI’m also proposing experiments to fine-tune parameters, like a p=35 sweep. I'll take action to queue two new experiments involving the LN-SSM model, applying both the U TV penalty and maintaining spatial smoothness."
