tick: 105
role: model
parts:
- text: "Results recap:\n- a_max=0.992 regressed slightly vs 0.993 (ID 197: -0.026917 vs 107: -0.026768).\n- U-TV smoothness (ID 199: -0.026891) did not help.\n- U-coherence + s_beta centering (ID 195: -0.026828) is safe but not better than 107.\n\nPending: p=35 (ID 203) and a_max=0.994 (ID 204).\n\nNext when a slot frees (no code yet, to avoid the 2-run cap):\n- Curvature λ sweep on base LN-SSM (k=320,p=32,H=96,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99):\n  1) λ=1.5e-4\n  2) λ=2e-4\n- Isolate s_beta-only centering (drop U-coh) to test gater stabilization without harming U.\n- If p=35 regresses, try p=30; otherwise try p=33.\n\nPublication hygiene:\n- After p/a_max results land, add a concise table to the archive addendum (IDs, mean MAE, Val_MAE_32) and a one-sentence conclusion on stability/curvature sensitivity.\n\nI’ll wait for 203/204 to finish before queuing the curvature and s_beta-only tests."
thinking_content: "**Considering tuning and adjustments**\n\nI need to reflect on the caution about papers that only focus on hyperparameter tuning being trivial. There's a bigger idea about introducing a residual long-skip \"iterative decoding\" teacher forcing, but that’s off the table since I can’t change the training loop. Maybe I could integrate a small \"trend component,\" similar to Hybrid TrendMix, but it’s not significantly better.  \nIt might be worth updating the archive again with the already written addendum. I also consider pruning tokens if permissible and keeping overall token usage in check.**Planning next experiments**\n\nI need to provide the next queue efficiently. First, I could consider using storage read for the U-TV effect stats, but maybe that's unnecessary. I could ask to rank the page, but keeping the reply concise is key here.  \n\nI'll summarize the results: a_max is 0.992, slightly regressed from 0.993, with U-TV small reg at about -0.026891. The best remains\
  \ at 107. Proposed next experiments include adjusting curvature lambda to 1.5e-4 and 2e-4, and testing gater stabilization effects. I’ll add two new submissions to the queue for these experiments.**Assessing running experiments**\n\nRight now, I have two running experiments, 203 and 204. The interface shows that they are still pending at tick 105, even though I saw them queued earlier. Since they’re listed as \"Your submission has been queued for evaluation,\" further submissions will likely fail due to the concurrent limit. I can still submit, but it'll just queue and ultimately fail since the limit is enforced. \n\nSo, the best course of action is to wait, while I prepare by updating my private storage or perhaps my private memory. I'll avoid new submissions for now and provide the next-run list when slots are available.**Creating a concise plan**\n\nI’ll put together a concise plan with future actions to be executed once slots are free, since we can’t schedule anything right now. To\
  \ avoid failures, I’ll skip posting new /execute_action commands. \n\nI propose the two experiments: a base LN-SSM with lam=1.5e-4 and lam=2e-4 for curvature, which I’ll call a \"curvature lambda sweep,\" alongside \"s_beta-only centering.\" I’ll also plan to prune tokens soon to maintain our budget. Now I’ll craft the answer!"
