tick: 106
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LN-SSM (best) + Curvature λ=1.5e-4\"\ntags: \"state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings, curvature, regularization\"\nabstract: \"Base LN-SSM (k=320,p=32,H=96,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99) with a stronger temporal curvature penalty λ=1.5e-4 (vs 1e-4). Tests whether smoother trajectories improve long-horizon MAE. V-orthogonality λ=1e-5 retained.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  LAM_CURV = 1.5e-4\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n\
    \          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n          ln_before_gating=bool(hparams.get('ln_before_gating', False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end',\
    \ 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_V_from_params(params):\n      try:\n          return params['params']['V']\n      except Exception:\n          return params.get('V', None)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=LAM_CURV)\n      V = _get_V_from_params(params)\n      if V is None:\n          return base\n      G = jnp.matmul(V.T, V)\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      v_ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LN-SSM (best) + Curvature λ=2e-4\"\ntags: \"state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings, curvature, regularization\"\nabstract: \"Base LN-SSM\
    \ (k=320,p=32,H=96,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99) with temporal curvature λ=2e-4. Probes smoothing–bias trade-off beyond 1.5e-4. V-orthogonality λ=1e-5 retained.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  LAM_CURV = 2e-4\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self,\
    \ rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n          ln_before_gating=bool(hparams.get('ln_before_gating', False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_V_from_params(params):\n      try:\n          return params['params']['V']\n      except Exception:\n          return params.get('V', None)\n\
    \n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=LAM_CURV)\n      V = _get_V_from_params(params)\n      if V is None:\n          return base\n      G = jnp.matmul(V.T, V)\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      v_ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning code for loss calculation**\n\nI need to create a code where `compute_loss` calls `mae_with_temporal_curvature` with different lambda values: 1.5e-4 and 2e-4. They recommended both for testing. We’ll make two submissions using our best baseline configuration. \n\nI also want to look into a separate test for s_beta-only centering but can save that for another time, focusing first on the curvature sweeps. I’ll ensure everything is set up to avoid fallback issues during submission.**Setting up YAML for submission**\n\nI need to propose two submit actions with YAML code. I’ll follow the station commands, ensuring that each action is on a new line with appropriate code blocks to pass. I also want to examine the s_beta distribution across seeds to see if curvature helps, though only commands and code will get parsed. \n\nThe YAML should include fields like \"title,\" \"tags,\" \"abstract,\" and \"content.\" I'll import `mae_with_temporal_curvature` from the losses\
  \ module, keeping the same hyperparameters and maintaining the V orthogonality penalty of 1e-5. We’ll ensure `compute_loss` uses the lambda variable for both values, possibly defining `LAM_CURV` as 1.5e-4.**Preparing submission details**\n\nI’ve noticed a previous CPU test in \"Test mode\" where `compute_loss` returns 0.0000—likely because both predictions and targets were zeros. That's not a huge issue, though. Now, I’m getting ready for two submissions with specific titles for the curvature values: \n\n1. \"LN-SSM (best) + Curvature λ=1.5e-4\"\n2. \"LN-SSM (best) + Curvature λ=2e-4\"\n\nI will define constants for `BASE_SEED`, `BATCH_SIZE`, and `LAM_CURV`, including `create_network`, which will link `compute_loss` to `LAM_CURV` and the V-Ortho penalty. I also want to ensure the parameter retrieval works correctly with a `Wrapper` class around `Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN` to maintain reliability. Lastly, I’ll incorporate `optax` for the optimizer and ensure compliance with YAML quoting\
  \ guidelines."
