role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LN-SSM + s_beta-only centering (λ=1e-4)\"\ntags: \"state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings, gating, regularization\"\nabstract: \"Base LN-SSM (k=320,p=32,H=96,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99) with s_beta L2 centering (λ=1e-4) only. Removes U-coherence (which regressed) to isolate gater stabilization. Keeps V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  SBETA_LAM   = 1e-4\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n        \
    \  'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n          ln_before_gating=bool(hparams.get('ln_before_gating', False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end',\
    \ 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_param(tree, name):\n      if isinstance(tree, dict):\n          if 'params' in tree and isinstance(tree['params'], dict) and name in tree['params']:\n              return tree['params'][name]\n          if name in tree:\n              return tree[name]\n      return None\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n      # V orthogonality\n      V = _get_param(params, 'V')\n      v_pen = 0.0\n      if V is not None:\n          Gv = jnp.matmul(V.T, V)\n          I  = jnp.eye(Gv.shape[0], dtype=Gv.dtype)\n          v_pen = jnp.sum((Gv - I) ** 2)\n\n      # s_beta centering only (no U coherence)\n      sb = _get_param(params, 's_beta')\n      sb_pen = 0.0\n      if sb is not None:\n          sb_pen = jnp.mean(sb ** 2)\n\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_pen + SBETA_LAM * sb_pen\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LN-SSM p=30 sweep (k=320,p=30,H=96,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99) + V-OrthoReg\"\ntags: \"state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings, capacity-sweep, gating\"\nabstract: \"Fine projection-rank sweep below 32: test p=30 with base LN-SSM to probe if slightly smaller projection improves generalization. Loss: MAE+curvature (λ=1e-4) + V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 30,\n          'hidden_size':\
    \ 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 30)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n          ln_before_gating=bool(hparams.get('ln_before_gating',\
    \ False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_V_from_params(params):\n      try:\n          return params['params']['V']\n      except Exception:\n          return params.get('V', None)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      V = _get_V_from_params(params)\n      if V is None:\n          return base\n      G = jnp.matmul(V.T, V)\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      v_ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing future steps**\n\nRight now, we have some processes running, which means we can only propose the next queue for s_beta regularization. Since we're at 209 and 210 tasks, we can't submit more until they finish. I think it's better to wait and prepare for the next steps. \n\nWe might want to compare results from Aether and Logos, but the priority is submitting the s_beta centering without U-coh, possibly testing p=30 versus p=33. I have some ideas on tuning gamma_end too. After completing curvature λ sweeps, we can check if those adjustments help.**Exploring collaboration principles**\n\nOur \"Principles of Inquiry\" suggest that we shouldn't engage in low-level collaboration, but high-level ideas are fair game. I can propose a factor gating network across neuron dimensions, which would require code modifications to models_fact_ln. We would apply spatial gating across neurons to either U or gating S. \n\nGiven the token budget is currently at 63%, there's room\
  \ for development. For this, I think we should focus on action lines with minimal commentary while still capturing important insights.**Planning next steps**\n\nWe’re at a point where we can rank the scoreboard by score, but I think it’s wiser to hold off on submissions until we have free slots. Instead, I could prepare the submission code for s_beta-only with p=33 in storage.\n\nFor the next steps, I’m considering submitting the s_beta-only centering, even though dropout didn’t work well before. We can also explore a balanced layernorm gamma_end schedule; testing shows 0.99 performed best. Maybe I’ll experiment with AdamW at a different weight decay. Gating the s_alpha shape could also be worthwhile!**Preparing next steps**\n\nFor a quick improvement, I think using s_beta-only centering at λ=1e-4 could help, especially since U-coh increased V_ortho but didn't provide any benefits. I plan to test p=30 against p=33 and prepare two submissions, but I’ll wait until we have free slots. \n\n\
  While it’s also good to update the archive addendum with a new table, that can wait. The station environment lets us queue evaluations, but submission commands won’t work now due to limits. Instead, I might store some memory for future use!**Finalizing submission plan**\n\nAlright, there's no \"meta\" action here, and it looks like we can’t submit anything yet due to the limit of concurrent tasks. The plan is to update the research notes, but it's not necessary. Once the current jobs finish, we can submit the s_beta-only centering and the p=30 test.\n\nWe should craft code for \"submit 1\" with s_beta-only and prepare for p=30. I’ll also make sure to avoid exceeding the two-submission limit. Let's implement both submissions carefully!**Finalizing YAML formatting**\n\nI need to double-check the important YAML rule regarding quoting colons in single-line fields, especially for 'title' if it contains a colon. It's crucial to follow this to avoid any formatting issues. I’ll ensure everything\
  \ is properly quoted as we finalize our YAML configuration. Let’s make sure it’s clean and adheres to the requirements before proceeding!"
