- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SGate-Input: Spatial 1D Conv Gating over Neurons + LN-SSM (k=320,p=32,H=96,a=0.993,γ=0.99)\"\ntags: \"state-space, factorized-loadings, layernorm, spatial-gating, conv1d\"\nabstract: \"Augment base LN-SSM with a lightweight spatial gate: a 1D conv across the neuron dimension produces per-neuron gates w[b,n] (in [0.5,1]) applied to the 4-step inputs before projection (x←x*w). Hypothesis: spatial awareness improves robustness without large compute. Loss: MAE+curvature (λ=1e-4) + V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  # Regularizers\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5  # ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n\
    \          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993,\n          'gate_features': 8,\n          'gate_kernel': 9\n      }\n\n  class SpatialGatedLNSSM(nn.Module):\n      inner_kwargs: dict\n      gate_features: int = 8\n      gate_kernel: int = 9\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T, N = x.shape\n          # Mean over time to get (B, N, 1) features\n          x_mean = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)[..., None]   # (B, N, 1)\n          h = nn.Conv(self.gate_features, (self.gate_kernel,), padding='SAME')(x_mean)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(1, (self.gate_kernel,), padding='SAME')(h)  # (B, N, 1)\n          # Gate in [0.5, 1.0] to avoid over-attenuation\n          w = 0.5 + 0.5 * nn.sigmoid(h).squeeze(-1)\
    \              # (B, N)\n          x_g = x * w[:, None, :]                                 # (B, 4, N)\n          inner = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**self.inner_kwargs)\n          return inner(x_g, training=training)\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          gate_features = int(kwargs.pop('gate_features', 8))\n          gate_kernel = int(kwargs.pop('gate_kernel', 9))\n          self.model = SpatialGatedLNSSM(inner_kwargs=kwargs, gate_features=gate_features, gate_kernel=gate_kernel)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size',\
    \ 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n          ln_before_gating=bool(hparams.get('ln_before_gating', False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993)),\n          gate_features=int(hparams.get('gate_features', 8)),\n          gate_kernel=int(hparams.get('gate_kernel', 9))\n      )\n\n  def _find_param(tree, name):\n      if isinstance(tree, dict):\n          if name in tree:\n              return tree[name]\n          for v in tree.values():\n              out = _find_param(v, name)\n              if out is not None:\n                  return out\n      return None\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      V = _find_param(params, 'V')\n      if V is\
    \ None:\n          return base\n      G = jnp.matmul(V.T, V)\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      v_ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LN-SSM + s_beta-only centering (λ=1e-4)\"\ntags: \"state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings, gating, regularization\"\nabstract: \"Re-submit s_beta L2 centering (λ=1e-4) without U-coherence to isolate temporal-gate stabilization effects. Base LN-SSM (k=320,p=32,H=96,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99). Retains V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED\
    \ = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  SBETA_LAM   = 1e-4\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank',\
    \ 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n          ln_before_gating=bool(hparams.get('ln_before_gating', False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_param(tree, name):\n      if isinstance(tree, dict):\n          if 'params' in tree and isinstance(tree['params'], dict) and name in tree['params']:\n              return tree['params'][name]\n          if name in tree:\n              return tree[name]\n      return None\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n      # V orthogonality\n      V = _get_param(params, 'V')\n      v_pen = 0.0\n      if V is not None:\n         \
    \ Gv = jnp.matmul(V.T, V)\n          I  = jnp.eye(Gv.shape[0], dtype=Gv.dtype)\n          v_pen = jnp.sum((Gv - I) ** 2)\n\n      # s_beta centering only\n      sb = _get_param(params, 's_beta')\n      sb_pen = 0.0\n      if sb is not None:\n          sb_pen = jnp.mean(sb ** 2)\n\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_pen + SBETA_LAM * sb_pen\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Implementing gating concepts**


  I''m thinking about implementing w = 0.5 + 0.5 * sigmoid(logit_base + conv_out). This gives w a range from 0.5 to 1 without the base. I’ll set it as w = 0.5 + 0.5*nn.sigmoid(h. So, we’ll include “spatially-aware input gating” to the MoE concept in a cost-effective way. Also, there''s "s_beta-only centering" and p=30 to consider. Previously, they failed due to the 2-run cap, but now I can submit both for Tick 108.**Reissuing submissions**


  The assistant previously tried to submit in Tick 107 but encountered failures due to a pending status. Now, I can reissue those submissions. I remember we need the YAML content from before. The last attempt failed because we hit the concurrent evaluation cap. Although the limit is 2 concurrent submissions, with 209 and 210 finished, I can choose two to queue. It seems that prioritizing spatial gating and s_beta-only is smarter for novelty, so let''s go with those two!**Preparing new submissions**


  The assistant previously attempted to submit "s_beta-only centering (λ=1e-4)" and "p=30 sweep" in tick 106, but those submissions failed. Now in tick 108, I can resubmit s_beta-only and either p=30 or spatial gating. For spatial gating, I need to prepare the code for a new evaluation, which can fit within one submission. I think it''s prudent to go with s_beta-only again because it isolates gating simply. So, I’ll submit both "spatial gating" and "s_beta-only" in this round!**Crafting the spatial gating code**


  I need to write the code for spatial gating. To start, I’ll import necessary modules like sys path from storage/ariadne, flax.linen as nn, jax, jnp, and optax. Then, I’ll import the Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN class from models_fact_ln. I’ll create a class called SpatialGatedLNSSM that will implement the gating. There’ll be a wrapper to hold this module, and I’ll compute the loss the same way as the base model. I’ll also define some hyperparameters, keeping in mind that the inner module will create its own parameter collections.**Handling V retrieval for orthogonality**


  I’m focused on retrieving V for the orthogonality check in compute_loss. Initially, I used _get_V_from_params, but since we''re dealing with nested submodules, I need to implement a tree traversal function. This function will recursively search for ''V'' in the nested dictionaries. I plan to define find_param_by_name, which will facilitate this search.


  For submissions, I’m resubmitting "SpatialGated LNSSM" and "s_beta-only centering" since previous attempts failed. I''ll make sure to set proper titles, tags, and hyperparameters. Ensuring all components are well-crafted, including appropriate imports and functions, is essential!'
