parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,H=128,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99) + V-OrthoReg\"\ntags: \"state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings, capacity-sweep, increment-width\"\nabstract: \"Increment MLP width sweep: test H=128 on the LN-SSM baseline (k=320,p=32,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99). Loss: MAE+temporal-curvature (λ=1e-4) with V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 128,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start':\
    \ 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 128)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n          ln_before_gating=bool(hparams.get('ln_before_gating', False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end',\
    \ 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_V(params):\n      try:\n          return params['params']['V']\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      V = _get_V(params)\n      if V is None:\n          return base\n      G = V.T @ V\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      v_ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Deciding next actions**


  I need to determine our next steps in the Token Management Room. We''re currently evaluating experiment 217, where ID 107 shows promise at -0.026768, but it still lags slightly behind SOTA at -0.026612. We''ve pruned ticks 92-109, and there''s a cooldown period before further pruning. Token usage is at 31%. My options include adding complete() hooks, performing minor sweeps, or potentially archiving updates or preparing a new analytical paper. I''ve noted an accepted revision earlier, which scored 9/10.**Analyzing archive and experiments**


  So, there''s some confusion about the Archive Room list, which previously indicated "No capsules available." However, it noted an acceptance score of 9/10, even if I''m not seeing it now. I think it''s reasonable to assume an archive capsule could exist. While in the Token Management Room, I''ll head to the Research Counter to monitor experiment 217 and set up new tests with different p values. I''ve explored p=30, but I haven''t tested it officially yet. Previous minor sweeps show p=36 performed best, followed by others. Let''s keep moving forward!**Exploring p values and collaboration**


  I might want to look at p=34 as a pure LN-SSM base instead of hybrid since I don’t see "Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN p=34." It could be useful for future tests. I’ve noticed that earlier adjustments for gamma_end near 0.99 didn’t exceed the best of 0.99. I could also consider testing per-step weighting and time decay, though prior horizon weighting didn’t help. Mixing our LN-SSM with Episteme''s MLP approach could be interesting, but there are restrictions on low-level collaboration. I can review and clone others'' code through official channels at the Research Counter, so that’s an option!**Planning hybrid approach and publications**


  Bridging the gap between our current plateau and the competitor SOTA of -0.026612 using an MLP approach might be a challenge. I’m considering a hybrid "SSM+MLP MoE gating" that combines factorized SSM and MLP, but it could end up being quite complex. We should start with incremental ablations to maintain our publication pace, aiming for at least one every 100 ticks. We''re currently at 111, so it’s time to prepare a second analytical paper comparing LN-SSM and MLP. We can utilize Reflection or Private Memory for logging, which seems like a good plan since token usage is acceptable right now!**Setting up experiments and next actions**


  I can run a "complete()" analysis hook for p=30, although we need to define it during submission. My focus should be on executing p=34 for LN-SSM and adjusting gamma_end around 0.993. We should also consider testing dropout incrementally for the MLP approach but remember that prior tests with a small drop harmed performance. I need to evaluate options like learned gamma schedule and testing hidden sizes. We have one experiment running at 217, and I can submit another, possibly with H=128. I’ll prepare the necessary actions now!'
