- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=34,H=96,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99) + V-OrthoReg\"\ntags: \"state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings, capacity-sweep, proj-rank\"\nabstract: \"Projection-rank sweep: test p=34 on the LN-SSM baseline (k=320,H=96,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99). Loss: MAE+temporal-curvature (λ=1e-4) with V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 34,\n          'hidden_size': 96,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n\
    \          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 34)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 96)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n          ln_before_gating=bool(hparams.get('ln_before_gating', False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n\
    \          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_V(params):\n      try:\n          return params['params']['V']\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      V = _get_V(params)\n      if V is None:\n          return base\n      G = V.T @ V\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      v_ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,H=80,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99) + V-OrthoReg\"\ntags: \"state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings, capacity-sweep, increment-width\"\nabstract: \"Increment MLP width sweep down:\
    \ test H=80 on the LN-SSM baseline (k=320,p=32,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99). Loss: MAE+temporal-curvature (λ=1e-4) with V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from models_fact_ln import Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 80,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'normalize_v': False,\n          'ln_before_gating': False,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'a_max': 0.993\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n   \
    \       return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 80)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n          normalize_v=bool(hparams.get('normalize_v', False)),\n          ln_before_gating=bool(hparams.get('ln_before_gating', False)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          a_max=float(hparams.get('a_max', 0.993))\n      )\n\n  def _get_V(params):\n      try:\n          return params['params']['V']\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n\
    \      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      V = _get_V(params)\n      if V is None:\n          return base\n      G = V.T @ V\n      I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n      v_ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * v_ortho\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating research strategies**


  I''m thinking about crafting our next response since we''re at tick 112. Our research shows a state-of-the-art result from Aether I at -0.026612, which is actually better than our previous -0.026768. We experimented with different parameters, but some gave worse results. We may want to consider pivoting to the MLP family since it currently seems to be winning. Plus, while we should publish our findings, we''ve already accepted one paper earlier. But I''m curious if we need to address the current context for acceptance again.**Planning a new paper**


  I''m thinking we can draft a new paper that analytically compares LN-SSM to MLP in terms of state-of-the-art performance. Currently, I''m noting that we''ve used 89k out of 270k tokens, which is manageable. For our next experiment, we could look at different parameters like p=34-36, since previous ones have shown degradation. Our best is ID 107, and with a plateau, reproducing MLP SOTA could help us understand differences. I''m considering additional analyses and exports, but we might already have the necessary code. I''ll also think about scheduling a "test()" for exporting latents.**Optimizing analysis methods**


  I''m considering how to compute analyses offline using a Python file, but it seems I can only run tests through the "test()" function, which stops training and doesn''t use GPU. However, I could set up a separate evaluation job to process stored latents, even if it''s just for evaluation and not training, and that’s fine. Since MLP Factorized RC+LN is state-of-the-art, we could also think about integrating FC MLP and SSM. Still, earlier hybrids didn''t perform better, so I might need to rethink and propose something like "per-condition-specific gating" based on the provided condition labels in the dataset.**Incorporating condition labels**


  I''m noticing we haven''t explicitly used condition labels yet, even though others like Aether implemented local gating. I could incorporate "condition embedding" as an additional context to enhance our gating and outputs. This might aid generalization since our dataset has 8 conditions. But I need to confirm if using these condition labels is allowed, as they seem to be provided within the system. It seems we may need to adjust the network creation to accept this additional input, but the current function structure doesn''t directly cater to labels. I''ll need to check how the training loop handles this.**Exploring model improvements**


  I''m realizing the system may offer "trial_data" that includes labels, but I can''t see them in the API. There might be a way for the dataset loader to attach condition information. Although I''ve noted that the system logs show training labels, I wonder how they pass to the network. Since MLP Factorized RC+LN is state-of-the-art, I''m considering various approaches, like condition-coded gating or preconditioned MLP with learned bases. Another option involves incorporating temporal dropout. However, I''ll need to ensure that my proposals maintain novelty. There are many paths ahead, including preparing an analytical report on LayerNorm and MLP performance, which could still allow for valuable contributions.**Preparing experiment submissions**


  I''m planning to submit two experiments: one for p=34 with the LN baseline and another for H=80 width. I realize we haven''t tested p=34 for the LN-SSM baseline yet, so this should fill in a gap. Since we can only have two concurrent evaluations, I’ll queue these up. For gamma_end, I’ll stick with 0.99 since it worked best before, although testing 0.985 is an option. I’ll also ensure that our code references our model correctly and keeps the normalization settings as they were. Finally, I’ll craft the submit commands accordingly.'
