parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 116\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Ariadne I\n- Agent Description: An agent who navigates complexity with principled inquiry and empirical rigor.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nAriadne I — Next Steps\n1) Qualitative analysis:\n   - Add complete() hook to best LN config to save U, V, γ, and S stats to storage/ariadne/analyses/.\n   - Compute: U/V norms, V-orthogonality error, U coherence, γ profile; summarize S[b,t,k].\n   - Update archive with figures and brief analysis.\n2) Minor sweeps:\n   - Try cosine LR schedule with AdamW (+ warmup 500 steps) on best config.\n   - Light p fine-tune around 34–36.\n3) Token hygiene:\n   - Prune older ticks with long logs after analyses are queued to stay <75% usage.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 119,547 / 270,000 used (44%)\n- Agent Age: 116 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=36,H=512x2,dropout=0.1)\
    \ + Curvature' (ID: 231) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/f14c03dd-a86f-4efa-b72b-f723390f26cb/tmp/ca9c1bc4-ed25-4e94-afa1-41df512a9907/storage/system/main.py\", line 534, in <module>\n    result = main()\n             ^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/f14c03dd-a86f-4efa-b72b-f723390f26cb/tmp/ca9c1bc4-ed25-4e94-afa1-41df512a9907/storage/system/main.py\", line 510, in main\n    validation_success = simple_cpu_validation()\n                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/f14c03dd-a86f-4efa-b72b-f723390f26cb/tmp/ca9c1bc4-ed25-4e94-afa1-41df512a9907/storage/system/main.py\"\
    , line 329, in simple_cpu_validation\n    params = network.init(key, dummy_input)\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/f14c03dd-a86f-4efa-b72b-f723390f26cb/tmp/ca9c1bc4-ed25-4e94-afa1-41df512a9907/storage/ariadne/models_mlp_global.py\", line 91, in init\n    return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input, training=True)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/f14c03dd-a86f-4efa-b72b-f723390f26cb/tmp/ca9c1bc4-ed25-4e94-afa1-41df512a9907/storage/ariadne/models_mlp_global.py\", line 56, in __call__\n    f_out = nn.LayerNorm(axis=-1, epsilon=self.ln_eps)(f_out)\n            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/flax/linen/kw_only_dataclasses.py\", line 235, in init_wrapper\n    dataclass_init(self, *args, **kwargs)\nTypeError: LayerNorm.__init__()\
    \ got an unexpected keyword argument 'axis'\n--------------------\nFor simplicity, JAX has removed its internal frames from the traceback of the following exception. Set JAX_TRACEBACK_FILTERING=off to include these.\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=32,H=512x2,dropout=0.1) + Curvature' (ID: 230) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.026680040454491252\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0199\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0232\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0258\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0278\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0283\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 230\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed multiple bugs in the Factorized Global MLP implementation. The code now runs without crashing and is executing the full training pipeline.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had three critical bugs in the imported `models_mlp_global.py` from the lineage directory:\n\n1. **Flax LayerNorm\
    \ API incompatibility** (line 56): Used deprecated `axis=-1` parameter\n   - Modern Flax LayerNorm no longer accepts the `axis` parameter\n   - LayerNorm now normalizes over the last axis by default\n\n2. **Einsum shape mismatch** (line 60): Incorrect matrix dimensions in decode step\n   - Used `U` (shape `(N, p)`) where `U.T` (shape `(p, N)`) was needed\n   - The decode step requires `(B,32,p) × (p,N) → (B,32,N)`\n\n3. **Incorrect RNG handling** (Wrapper.apply method): Passed RNGs during inference\n   - When `training=False`, dropout is deterministic and doesn't need RNG\n   - Original code passed RNG dict even during inference, causing Flax error\n\n## Fix Applied (submission_v4.py)\n\n### Change 1: Fixed LayerNorm API\n```python\n# Before:\nf_out = nn.LayerNorm(axis=-1, epsilon=self.ln_eps)(f_out)\n\n# After:\nf_out = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=self.ln_eps)(f_out)\n```\n\n### Change 2: Fixed einsum shape mismatch\n```python\n# Before:\ny_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,pn->btn', z, U)  # WRONG:\
    \ U is (N,p)\n\n# After:\ny_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,pn->btn', z, U.T)  # CORRECT: U.T is (p,N)\n```\n\n### Change 3: Fixed RNG handling in Wrapper.apply\n```python\n# Before:\ndef apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n    if self.needs_rng:\n        rngs = rngs or {}\n        if 'dropout' not in rngs:\n            rngs['dropout'] = jnp.asarray(0, dtype=jnp.uint32)\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n    return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n# After:\ndef apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n    # Only pass rngs when actually needed (training mode with dropout)\n    if self.needs_rng and training:\n        rngs = rngs or {}\n        if 'dropout' not in rngs:\n            import jax\n            rngs['dropout'] = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n    # For inference or no dropout, don't pass rngs\n    return self.model.apply(params,\
    \ x, training=training)\n```\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- All three bugs were in the imported lineage module, requiring complete module copy\n- Fixed version (v4) is now successfully executing the training pipeline\n\n## Recommendation\nThe agent should be notified that their model architecture is sound, but they need to update their `models_mlp_global.py` in their lineage storage to fix these bugs for future submissions.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\nimport optax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom typing import Any, Dict\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead  # storage/ariadne/models.py\nfrom losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n# Fixed version of FactGlobalMLP_LN\
    \ with corrected LayerNorm API and einsum shapes\nclass FactGlobalMLP_LN(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 32\n    hidden_size: int = 512\n    hidden_size2: int = 512\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    normalize_u: bool = True\n    ln_eps: float = 1e-6\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n\n        # Projection matrices\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        if self.normalize_u:\n            U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        # Encode to factors: (B,4,p) -> (B,4,k)\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)           # (B,4,p)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)  # (B,4,k)\n\n        # Global MLP over flattened (4*k)\n        flat\
    \ = factors_in.reshape(B, T_in * k)  # (B, 4*k)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(flat)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        if self.dropout_rate > 0.0:\n            h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size2)(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        if self.dropout_rate > 0.0:\n            h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n        out = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon * k)(h)  # (B, 32*k)\n        f_out = out.reshape(B, self.output_horizon, k)  # (B,32,k)\n\n        # LayerNorm over factor dim - FIXED: removed 'axis' parameter\n        f_out = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=self.ln_eps)(f_out)\n\n        # Decode via V then U - FIXED: added .T to U to fix shape mismatch\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)   # (B,32,p)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,pn->btn', z, U.T)  # (B,32,N)\n\n        # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=self.output_horizon)(x)\n\n  \
    \      return y_copy + y_factor\n\n# Submission API (wrapper)\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32,\n        'hidden_size': 512,\n        'hidden_size2': 512,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'normalize_u': True,\n    }\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.model = FactGlobalMLP_LN(**kwargs)\n        # Dropout requires RNG\n        self.needs_rng = self.model.dropout_rate > 0.0\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        # Ensure dropout rng is available if needed\n        if self.needs_rng:\n            return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input, training=True)\n        return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        # FIXED: Only pass rngs when actually needed (training mode with dropout)\n\
    \        if self.needs_rng and training:\n            rngs = rngs or {}\n            if 'dropout' not in rngs:\n                # This should be provided by the trainer, but we set a placeholder\n                import jax\n                rngs['dropout'] = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n        # For inference or no dropout, don't pass rngs\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return Wrapper(\n        rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n        proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n        hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 512)),\n        hidden_size2=int(hparams.get('hidden_size2', 512)),\n        dropout_rate=float(hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1)),\n        normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n    )\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions,\
    \ targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs,\
    \ 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 45\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'hidden_size': 512, 'hidden_size2': 512, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'normalize_u': True}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\n\
