- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write ariadne/models_mlp_global.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Fixed Factorized Global MLP with LayerNorm + Residual Copy (RC).\n  - Neuron projection: U ∈ R^{N×p} (column-normalized) and V ∈ R^{k×p}\n  - Latent factors: xU (B,4,p) → (B,4,k) via V^T\n  - Global MLP over flattened (4*k) to (32*k), then LayerNorm over k at each t\n  - Decode: (B,32,k) → (B,32,p) via V, then → (B,32,N) via U^T\n  - ResidualCopyHead adds strong short-horizon anchor\n\n  Fixes:\n  - Use LayerNorm without deprecated 'axis' arg (Flax API)\n  - Correct decode einsum to use U.T (p×N)\n  - Pass RNGs only during training when dropout is active\n  \"\"\"\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead  # storage/ariadne/models.py\n\n  class FactGlobalMLP_LN(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_size: int = 512\n      hidden_size2:\
    \ int = 512\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      ln_eps: float = 1e-6\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n\n          # Projection matrices\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          # Encode to factors: (B,4,p) -> (B,4,k)\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)              # (B,4,p)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)   # (B,4,k)\n\n          # Global MLP over flattened (4*k)\n          flat = factors_in.reshape(B, T_in * k)            # (B, 4*k)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(flat)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n\
    \          if self.dropout_rate > 0.0:\n              h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size2)(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          if self.dropout_rate > 0.0:\n              h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n          out = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon * k)(h)        # (B, 32*k)\n          f_out = out.reshape(B, self.output_horizon, k)    # (B,32,k)\n\n          # LayerNorm over factor dim (last axis)\n          f_out = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=self.ln_eps)(f_out)\n\n          # Decode via V then U.T\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)           # (B,32,p)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,pn->btn', z, U.T)      # (B,32,N)\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=self.output_horizon)(x)\n\n          return y_copy + y_factor\n\n  # Submission API (wrapper)\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 512,\n          'hidden_size2': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = FactGlobalMLP_LN(**kwargs)\n          # Dropout requires RNG during training\n          self.needs_rng = self.model.dropout_rate > 0.0\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          if self.needs_rng:\n              return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input, training=True)\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          # Only pass rngs when needed (training with dropout)\n          if self.needs_rng and training:\n              rngs = rngs or {}\n              if 'dropout' not in rngs:\n                  import jax\n\
    \                  rngs['dropout'] = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 512)),\n          hidden_size2=int(hparams.get('hidden_size2', 512)),\n          dropout_rate=float(hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=36,H=512x2,dropout=0.1) + Curvature — fixed LN and decode\"\ntags: \"mlp, factorized-loadings, layernorm, residual-copy, curvature, capacity-sweep\"\nabstract: \"Re-run p=36 after fixing LayerNorm API and decode einsum in lineage module. Global factorized MLP (512x2, dr=0.1)\
    \ with MAE+temporal curvature (λ=1e-4).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_mlp_global import create_network, _define_hyperparameters as _def_base, BASE_SEED, BATCH_SIZE\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      hp = _def_base()\n      hp['proj_rank'] = 36\n      return hp\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=32,H=512x2,dropout=0.05) + Curvature\"\ntags: \"mlp, factorized-loadings, layernorm, residual-copy, curvature, regularization-sweep\"\nabstract: \"Dropout sweep for the global factorized MLP: reduce\
    \ dropout from 0.1 to 0.05 to test under-regularization effects. Keep k=320, p=32, 512x2 MLP, MAE+curvature (λ=1e-4).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_mlp_global import create_network, _define_hyperparameters as _def_base, BASE_SEED, BATCH_SIZE\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      hp = _def_base()\n      hp['dropout_rate'] = 0.05\n      return hp\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating experiments and next steps**


  I need to outline the next actions based on our experiments. We’re in the Private Memory Room, with evaluations for experiments 230 and 231. Experiment 231 failed, but 230 succeeded with a score of -0.026680, which is better than our previous score of -0.026768 and close to the MLP SOTA of -0.026612. It''s good to see improvement! I’ll update the global MLP module and write the necessary fixes to resubmit for the p=36 run that previously failed.**Planning MLP actions and updates**


  I''m considering a parameter sweep for MLP with values 30, 34, and 36 as planned. We saw some improvement with 36 was previously affected by a bug, so we need to resubmit the 231 variant after fixing that. I’m also thinking about trying different dropout rates and hidden sizes, but we need to be strategic as we might be saturating. MLP is performing well compared to our LN-SSM. I should update the Private Memory with a summary and think about the Archive paper update later. We''ve used 119k tokens, which is good!**Updating and resubmitting MLP experiments**


  I need to fix the global MLP file and resubmit the p=36 evaluation. I''m considering whether to also run p=34 or p=28, but I need to weigh the cost since there''s a two-experiment limit. As of tick 116, no experiments are running, and since the last two (230 and 231) are complete, I can go ahead. I’ll update models_mlp_global.py with the necessary code fixes from the debugger and then resubmit the p=36 variant with the appropriate settings.**Planning next MLP submissions**


  I''m set to submit "FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320, p=40, H=512x2, dropout=0.1)." While p=40 is larger, I’ve seen some regressions at this size in SSM, although it may be fine for MLP. Aether and Episteme used p=32, which suggests small changes might not make a difference. I want to explore dropout rates, trying 0.05, and could implement AdamW with a weight decay of 1e-4. Therefore, I''ll resubmit the p=36 run with this configuration and adjust the other parameters accordingly in Private Memory.**Updating code and implementing actions**


  The station requires YAML code after /execute_action, and since the automatic debugger changed our code, I need to rewrite the file accordingly. I’ll construct updated file content with the fixes from the Debugger Report, including using jax.random PRNGKey for dropout RBC. My action plan involves writing the updated code to models_mlp_global.py and submitting the fixed p=36 run, while also conducting a dropout sweep with p=32 and a dropout rate of 0.05. I''ll make sure the commands are executed correctly without oversharing unnecessary details.'
