    \ best so far in MLP line; closes gap to station SOTA (Aether ID 212: −0.026612).\n\n      Archive/notes:\n      - Archive addendum posted with these results and next-step plan (capacity/regularization sweeps, latent export).\n      - Private memory updated with plan and reproducibility notes.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering next steps in research**


  I''m at the Research Counter with experiments 241 and 242 queued. We''re using a factorized global MLP, and ID 230 has improved to -0.026680, which is near the state-of-the-art. I’ve updated the addendum in the archive. Next, I need to consider submitting more capacity sweeps, but we''re limited to two concurrent evaluations. So, I''ll wait for 241 and 242 to finish before planning the next submissions. I''ll also check the lineage storage outputs to ensure everything is saved correctly.**Planning experiment adjustments**


  I''ve completed the submission code for experiment 242, but I need to check if it''s working in the module. I''m considering running p=34/36 with dropout rates of 0.1/0.05, since p=36 with a dropout of 0.1 performed well. I might also test p=30 or p=28. Additionally, I should evaluate AdamW versus Adam with weight decay options. However, I can’t submit new runs right now, but I can manage tokens by pruning earlier heavy ticks to keep everything running smoothly.**Deciding on pruning and next steps**


  The system suggests that I prune heavy logs occasionally, so I’m considering pruning logs 112-115. Log 115 has 1727, 114 has 6887, among others. I can''t prune logs that overlap with already pruned ones, so maybe I can prune 111-115, but 115 might still have useful content. It''s important to provide a summary of results and any code issues. I also want to review ID 230’s training logs for more metrics and make a plan to try dropout rates of 0.0 and 0.15.**Exploring dropout and parameters**


  I’m wondering if using a dropout of 0.0 could help with under-regularization, but I’m cautious because it might lead to overfitting. While 0.05 is under, testing 0.0 could provide insights. Increasing p to 34 didn’t improve results, and I’m considering p at 28 or 40 next. ID 236 with p=36 resulted in -0.026761, which is worse than the previous result. I think sticking to p=32 might be the best move for now. I also want to implement AdamW with a weight decay of 1e-4 and run with dropout to see if that helps.**Planning pruning and evaluations**


  I need to consider LayerNorm positioning and whether to apply it over the factor dimension after decoding or over the output dimension. It might be beneficial to test this, but I want to avoid complicating things too much. We should also evaluate a larger MLP single hidden layer at 1024, but that requires more compute. Given our limit on pending tasks, I’ll prioritize pruning logs 112-116 since they contain heavy entries. I must include an evaluation summary containing all relevant IDs and metrics to ensure comprehensive documentation. After pruning, I might look at the scoreboard, but that isn’t critical right now.'
