tick: 134
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto token_management}\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"129-133\"\n    summary: |\n      Global MLP line consolidation and analyses.\n      - Reviewed Aether’s new SOTA (ID 259: −0.026573) and ablations (ID 266: −0.026608).\n      - Our capacity/regularization sweeps:\n        * p=34 (ID 264) → −0.026653; p=36 (ID 265) → −0.026762 (worse).\n        * Dropout 0.08 (ID 269) → −0.026680; Dropout 0.12 (ID 272) → −0.026715; baseline 0.10 remains best (ID 247: −0.026645).\n        * Curvature λ=8e−5 (ID 273) → −0.026704 (worse than 1e−4).\n      - Exported U stats via complete() (ID 268) and saved per-seed JSON under storage/ariadne/analyses/mlp_best_wd1e4/trial_{seed}/.\n      - Key conclusion: AdamW wd=1e−4, dropout=0.10, p=32 stays best in our line; we’re within ~7e−5 of SOTA. Next: richer decoder (add V) and normalized-U/V analyses.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FactGlobalMLP-UV-LN\
    \ (k=384,p=32,H=512x2,dr=0.10) + AdamW (wd=1e-4)\"\ntags: \"mlp, factorized-loadings, layernorm, residual-copy, uv-decoder, optimizer\"\nabstract: \"Augment global MLP with separate V (k×p) loadings and decode via V then U^T. Increase latent k to 384 to enhance expressivity while keeping p=32. AdamW wd=1e-4, curvature λ=1e-4, grad clip=1.0.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_mlp_global_uv import create_network as create_net_uv, _define_hyperparameters as _def_uv\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      hp = _def_uv()\n      hp['rank_k'] = 384\n      hp['proj_rank'] = 32\n      hp['dropout_rate'] = 0.10\n      return hp\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      # curvature λ=1e-4 (same as best runs)\n      import losses\n      return losses.mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return create_net_uv(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FactGlobalMLP-LN Export (normalized U, plus V stats) — best wd=1e-4\"\ntags: \"mlp, analysis, export, normalized-U, v-orthogonality, layernorm\"\nabstract: \"Re-run best global MLP (p=32, dropout=0.10, AdamW wd=1e-4) and export stats with normalized U (coherence) and V orthogonality error to storage/ariadne/analyses/mlp_best_wd1e4_norm/.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_mlp_global import create_network, _define_hyperparameters as _def_base\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      hp = _def_base()\n      hp['proj_rank'] = 32\n      hp['dropout_rate'] = 0.10\n      return hp\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n \
    \     return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n\n  # --- helpers ---\n  def _find_param(tree, key):\n      if isinstance(tree, dict):\n          if key in tree:\n              return tree[key]\n          for v in tree.values():\n              out = _find_param(v, key)\n              if out is not None:\n                  return out\n      return None\n\n  def _u_v_stats(U, V):\n      import jax.numpy as jnp\n      # Normalize U columns before stats (effective U_hat used at runtime)\n      u_norms = jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6\n      U_hat = U / u_norms\n      # U coherence on normalized columns\n      Gu = U_hat.T @ U_hat\n      off = jnp.abs(Gu - jnp.eye(Gu.shape[0], dtype=Gu.dtype))\n      u_coh_max = float(jnp.max(off))\n\
    \      u_coh_mean = float(jnp.mean(off))\n      u_col_norms_mean = float(jnp.mean(jnp.linalg.norm(U_hat, axis=0)))\n      u_col_norms_std = float(jnp.std(jnp.linalg.norm(U_hat, axis=0)))\n      # V orthogonality\n      Gv = V.T @ V\n      Iv = jnp.eye(Gv.shape[0], dtype=Gv.dtype)\n      v_ortho_frob2 = float(jnp.sum((Gv - Iv) ** 2))\n      return {\n          \"u_col_norms_mean\": u_col_norms_mean,\n          \"u_col_norms_std\": u_col_norms_std,\n          \"u_coherence_max\": u_coh_max,\n          \"u_coherence_mean\": u_coh_mean,\n          \"v_ortho_frob2\": v_ortho_frob2,\n          \"p\": int(U.shape[1]),\n          \"N\": int(U.shape[0]),\n      }\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      out_dir = os.path.join(\"storage\", \"ariadne\", \"analyses\", \"mlp_best_wd1e4_norm\",\n                             f\"trial_{trial_data.get('trial_number','NA')}\")\n      os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n      # Extract U, V if present\n      U = _find_param(params, 'U')\n\
    \      V = _find_param(params, 'V')\n      rec = {\n          \"val_mae\": float(trial_data.get(\"val_mae\", -1.0)),\n          \"seed\": int(trial_data.get(\"seed\", -1)),\n          \"trial_number\": int(trial_data.get(\"trial_number\", -1)),\n          \"hyperparameters\": trial_data.get(\"hyperparameters\", {}),\n      }\n      try:\n          if U is not None:\n              stats = _u_v_stats(U, V if V is not None else None if False else (U[:1].T @ U[:1]))  # dummy to satisfy type\n              # Correct handling: recompute V stats only if V exists\n              if V is not None:\n                  import jax.numpy as jnp\n                  Gv = V.T @ V\n                  Iv = jnp.eye(Gv.shape[0], dtype=Gv.dtype)\n                  stats[\"v_ortho_frob2\"] = float(jnp.sum((Gv - Iv) ** 2))\n              rec[\"stats\"] = stats\n      except Exception as e:\n          rec[\"stats_error\"] = str(e)\n\n      with open(os.path.join(out_dir, \"summary.json\"), \"w\") as f:\n      \
    \    json.dump(rec, f, indent=2)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Assessing anomalies in trials**\n\nI need to decide what to do next as we're at tick 134 with 196k tokens out of 270k. It’s time to prune soon since the user sent outputs for reading analysis files summary.json. I see an anomaly with trial_0 having a val_mae of 0.05, while others are around 0.02654. More importantly, the U column stats suggest they aren't normalized to unit norm in saved parameters, which might explain the inconsistencies.**Correcting analyses on U parameters**\n\nI realized that while the complete() function found U via _find_param and computed stats on the raw U parameters after training, the stored U remains unconstrained. If we normalize U before use, this could inflate the coherence, making it meaningless. We need to correct our analysis by transforming U to its normalized form for stats. It seems I should either write a corrected analysis function or adjust complete() to handle normalized U, but we can run another export job for that.**Evaluating\
  \ model performance**\n\nOur best score remains -0.026645, but we're still off by about 7.2e-5. I've observed that gradient clipping might help, and it seems Aether uses it alongside a deeper factor MLP. Our global MLP pipeline does use gradient clipping with clip_by_global_norm(1.0), so that's covered. We also explored dropout rates of 0.08 and 0.12, but neither improved the score. The next steps could include implementing a Cosine LR schedule with a warmup of 500 while considering testing different gradient clipping thresholds like 0.7 or 1.5.**Exploring parameter adjustments**\n\nI’m considering using Exponential Moving Average (EMA) of parameters during evaluation to reduce validation loss, but it seems the system prohibits custom training loops. Although we can set the optimizer to use optax.ema, the interface limits us to compute_loss, create_network, and optimizer, so applying EMA across steps may not be feasible. However, optax does include Polyak averaging, though that modifies\
  \ state. I’m also pondering label-aware gating since the dataset has eight condition labels and exploring weight decay values, as we’ve previously tested several without much improvement. Maybe testing 9e-5 or 1.1e-4 could yield marginal gains!**Planning model adjustments and submissions**\n\nI'm considering replicating Aether's deeper factor-space MLP, which had a score of -0.026608. While we already include gradient clipping, we might need to explore different training seeds to reduce noise. Additionally, we could try increasing dropout and testing condition labels, which are available in the dataset. I can also think about increasing the capacity by adjusting k, possibly to 384, to improve expressiveness while being cautious of overfitting. \n\nFor the next steps, we need to prune tokens soon and submit both the UV model run and an export job that corrects the U stats by computing normalized values. I’ll draft two submissions for this.**Preparing submissions and pruning**\n\nI'm planning\
  \ to reuse the 'create_network' function from models_mlp_global and implement a complete function to compute normalized U_hat and optional V stats for orthogonality errors. I’ll also calculate the coherence of U columns and save this to the specified analyses path. For pruning, I can propose pruning ticks \"129-133,\" ensuring we respect cooldown rules; earlier, we pruned at tick 128. \n\nI'll compile a summary of previous results while keeping minimal commentary. The next steps involve going to token management, performing the prune, and preparing for the UV submission with appropriate imports and functions."
