thinking_content: "**Evaluating model improvements**\n\nI'm considering potential improvements like adjusting the learning rate schedule. We previously tried a cosine schedule with warmup, but it caused regression. I explored weight decay sweeps and tested dropout rates, finding 0.10 to be the best. While experimenting with parameters, it seems important to isolate variables like testing UV with k=320. The export U stats show anomalies that need addressing, particularly with earlier unified analysis presenting unexpected values, which need clarification.**Analyzing trial results**\n\nThe first trial indicated a u_col_norms_mean of 0.9999 for trial_0, but trial_1 showed 34.28, suggesting we didn’t normalize U previously. A normalized export is planned for 276, which is good. Token usage is at 60%, and with the pruning cooldown active, we can continue with submissions. I see that experiments 275 and 276 are both running, but since the system limits concurrent tasks, I can only prepare storage\
  \ or code in the meantime. I'll implement models_mlp_global_uv if it's not done yet.**Planning action summary**\n\nThe instructions say that only executed actions are parsed, but I can still include planning text alongside actions for clarity. Since I'm limited to two concurrent submissions, I could either note my plan in Private Memory or review Aether's archive (#6) using specific commands. The archive seems accessible to all agents, which is helpful for potential improvements. I also want to review evaluation details for ID 259, as it can provide insights on gradient clipping and LR schedules by retrieving logs and submitted solutions.**Planning evaluations and actions**\n\nI’m allowed to conduct a high-level review using the station's research counter, which lets me review any code lineage. This will help refine our configuration to replicate state-of-the-art results and propose fair ablations. I’ll start by executing actions to review evaluations 259 and 266, focusing on the impacts\
  \ of gradient clipping. \n\nOnce I finish these reviews, I’ll write a plan in Private Memory. Since I can’t submit new experiments yet, I can prepare improved code for the UV model variant with k=320 and create a YAML for later submission when a slot is available.**Updating models and planning reviews**\n\nI can update the models_mlp_global_uv.py to address memory and time constraints, assuming it’s done. I noticed that the export summary for trial_0 showing a val_mae of 0.05 seems incorrect; it might just be a placeholder. I need to ensure the complete() function calculates the correct val_mae. \n\nNext, I’ll review evaluations 259, 266, and 271 for insights on gradient clipping values. While I can’t submit new experiments until current ones finish, I can prepare a submission script and write a summary to Private Memory if needed. Let’s proceed with the reviews!"
