    \ model from `storage/ariadne/models_mlp_global_uv.py`, which used an outdated Flax LayerNorm API. Specifically, lines 38 and 51 in the imported file called:\n\n```python\nnn.LayerNorm(axis=-1, epsilon=self.ln_eps)\n```\n\nIn newer versions of Flax, the `LayerNorm` constructor no longer accepts an `axis` parameter. This caused the initialization to fail with:\n\n```\nTypeError: LayerNorm.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'axis'\n```\n\nThe error occurred during the \"Simple CPU Validation\" phase when attempting to initialize the network parameters.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Copied the entire `FactGlobalMLP_UV` class** from the lineage file into the submission (lines 13-60)\n2. **Updated LayerNorm calls** on lines 38 and 51:\n   - **Before:** `nn.LayerNorm(axis=-1, epsilon=self.ln_eps)(xU)`\n   - **After:** `nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=self.ln_eps)(xU)`\n3. **Kept the wrapper class and API functions** to maintain compatibility\
    \ with the evaluation system\n\nThe fix preserves all functionality while using the correct Flax LayerNorm API. LayerNorm normalizes over the last axis by default, so removing the `axis=-1` parameter maintains the intended behavior.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission_v2.py has been running successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing. The code passed the CPU validation phase and is now executing the full training pipeline.\n\n## Notes\n- This is a simple API compatibility fix that doesn't change the model architecture or behavior\n- The issue affected both LayerNorm calls in the model (input factor normalization and output factor normalization)\n- The fix allows the agent's sophisticated factorized global MLP architecture to run correctly in the current Flax environment\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version\
    \ v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\n\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead  # storage/ariadne/models.py\n\n# Fixed version of FactGlobalMLP_UV with corrected LayerNorm API\nclass FactGlobalMLP_UV(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 32\n    hidden_size: int = 512\n    hidden_size2: int = 512\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    ln_eps: float = 1e-6\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n\n        # Loadings\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        # Project to p factors and normalize\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp',\
    \ x, U)  # (B,4,p)\n        # FIX: Remove axis parameter from LayerNorm\n        f_in = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=self.ln_eps)(xU)  # LN over last axis (p)\n\n        # Global MLP over flattened (4*p)\n        h = f_in.reshape(B, T_in * p)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size2)(h)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n\n        # Predict (32*k) factor outputs and LN over k\n        fac_out = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon * k)(h).reshape(B, self.output_horizon, k)\n        # FIX: Remove axis parameter from LayerNorm\n        fac_out = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=self.ln_eps)(fac_out)\n\n        # Decode via V and U^T: (B,32,k) -> (B,32,p) -> (B,32,N)\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', fac_out, V)    # (B,32,p)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,pn->btn', z, U.T) # (B,32,N)\n\n     \
    \   # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=self.output_horizon)(x)\n\n        return y_copy + y_factor\n\n# Submission API wrappers\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.model = FactGlobalMLP_UV(**kwargs)\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n                               dummy_input, training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        rngs = rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n        if mutable is not None:\n            out, updates = self.model.apply(params, x, training=training,\n                                            mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs)\n            return out, updates\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 384,\n        'proj_rank': 32,\n        'hidden_size': 512,\n        'hidden_size2': 512,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n    }\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    # curvature λ=1e-4 (same as best runs)\n    import losses\n    return losses.mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return Wrapper(\n        rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n        proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n        hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 512)),\n        hidden_size2=int(hparams.get('hidden_size2', 512)),\n        dropout_rate=float(hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4, eps=1e-8)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON\
