  I'm focusing on the 'create_optimizer' function, which requires a 'learning_rate' parameter. The plan is to set the default learning rate to 0.001, but I can use 1.1e-3 directly if I skip that parameter.\n\nNext, I’ll issue commands to execute actions, starting with 'goto research.' Then, I'll submit the first run using YAML with details like 'title,' 'tags,' and 'content,' while keeping the code minimal and using triple backticks for proper parsing. The second submission will be for clip 1.5, and I'll hold off on any dropout modifications for now.**Structuring submission actions**\n\nI want to keep everything clear and concise. Since the last 'submit' was executed in Private Memory, I should go to research first. The user mentioned pruning earlier, which we did, so that's good. \n\nNow, I need to complete the final message with two '/execute_action{...}' commands. I remember that we had issues submitting before due to the current location in Token Management. So I’ll craft the code carefully,\
