- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=32,H=512x2,dr=0.09) + Adam(lr=1e-3) + GradClip(1.0)\"\ntags: \"mlp, factorized-loadings, layernorm, residual-copy, optimizer, regularization\"\nabstract: \"Under Adam (no wd) + global grad clipping (norm=1.0), lightly reduce dropout from 0.10 to 0.09 to probe regularization sweet spot. Base is our best global MLP with curvature loss (λ=1e-4).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_mlp_global import create_network, _define_hyperparameters as _def_base\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      hp = _def_base()\n      hp['proj_rank'] = 32\n      hp['dropout_rate'] = 0.09  # was 0.10\n      hp['learning_rate'] = 1e-3\n      return hp\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating submission limits**


  I see we currently have 292 experiments running, so we''re on the limit of one more submission. The capacity allows for just one more now, which is good. I could consider providing an archive update too, but experiments are the priority. I might adjust the curvature lambda to 1.2e-4; earlier, 8e-5 was regressing. I''ll consider either 0.75 or 0.9 for clipping with minimal difference. However, we can only submit one action at a time, even if they''re in the same response.**Deciding on experiment submissions**


  I know the system allows submissions until we hit the limit, but I have to be careful since the second will only queue if there''s a slot free. Currently, we can submit one more experiment, which means it''s better to choose the most promising one. I’m thinking about dropout 0.09 with p=32 and regularization in mind, though dropout 0.1 was used in Aether. Using Adam seems better because AdamW didn’t perform as well. For now, I’ll test with "dr=0.09" and may consider updating the Private Memory with a summary.**Planning experiment submission**


  I’m ready to submit dropout 0.09 with Adam and clipping. I''ll keep the code concise and consider sorting the scoreboard by "rank score," but that’s not essential right now. I’ve already pruned the tokens, so I''m all set there. I’ll craft the action to execute: submit 1 with the title "FactGlobalMLP-LN (p=32, dr=0.09) + Adam + Clip(1.0)." The dropout rate will be set properly, and I might slightly adjust the learning rate to 1e-3, ensuring everything aligns with the default settings. Let''s go for just one submission now.'
