role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=32,H=704x2,dr=0.10) + Adam(lr=1e-3) + GradClip(1.0)\"\ntags: \"mlp, factorized-loadings, layernorm, residual-copy, optimizer, capacity\"\nabstract: \"Scale factor-MLP width from 640x2 (−0.026619) to 704x2 under Adam (no wd) with global grad clipping (norm=1.0). Curvature loss λ=1e-4. Tests whether moderate capacity increase closes gap to SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_mlp_global import create_network, _define_hyperparameters as _def_base\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      hp = _def_base()\n      hp['proj_rank'] = 32\n      hp['dropout_rate'] = 0.10\n      hp['hidden_size'] = 704\n      hp['hidden_size2'] = 704\n      hp['learning_rate'] = 1e-3\n      return hp\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params,\
    \ x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=32,H=512x2,dr=0.10) + Adam(lr=9e-4) + GradClip(1.0)\"\ntags: \"mlp, factorized-loadings, layernorm, residual-copy, optimizer, gradient-clipping\"\nabstract: \"Learning-rate sensitivity around 1e-3: Adam (no wd) at lr=9e-4 with global grad clipping (norm=1.0) on the best global MLP. Curvature loss λ=1e-4.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_mlp_global import create_network, _define_hyperparameters as _def_base\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      hp = _def_base()\n      hp['proj_rank'] = 32\n      hp['dropout_rate'] = 0.10\n      hp['learning_rate'] = 9e-4\n      return hp\n\n  def\
    \ compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing learning rates**\n\nIt seems that the learning rate of 1.1e-3 performed worse than 1e-3 and 8e-4. The 9e-4 option could be slightly better, but we ran into concurrency issues. Right now, there are no experiments running, even though the table indicates 296 and 297 have been evaluated. I’m considering replicating Aether's configuration with 512x2 and gradient clipping, which achieved better results. My 640x2 isn’t quite there yet, so I’ll also think about tweaking depth or adding spectral smoothing.**Exploring MLP adjustments**\n\nI'm thinking we can adjust the MLP width or depth for our experiments. Keeping the projection rank p at 32 seems wise since using 34 with Adam+clip yielded worse results. I might experiment with dropout rates around 0.095 or 0.105, even though 0.09 didn't work out well. \n\nI can submit new runs now that we have the token budget available. The focus will be on submitting configurations like 512x3 or 640x3 with dropout of 0.1 and a\
  \ learning rate of 1e-3, but complexity could increase. I just need to ensure it still fits in the 24GB memory space.**Configuring MLP runs**\n\nI'm considering how the Factor MLP is set up with an input flatten parameter of 4*p, where p is 32. The key focus is on hidden dimensions. Using 640x2 seems fine, and 640x3 might be okay too. I’m thinking of proposing two runs: one with 640x3 and another with either 576x2 or maybe even 704x2 just to test the shape. \n\nI think it makes sense to try 512x3 first since it simplifies things. I’ll also explore using a learning rate of 9.5e-4 for this run.**Modifying the MLP model**\n\nI need to make some changes to models_mlp_global, which seems to only support hidden_size and hidden_size2, indicating it's limited to a 2-layer MLP. To add a third layer, I might need to modify the module file. \n\nHowever, I can write a wrapper network for submission that uses three layers while keeping the training loop unchanged. To save tokens, I also want to test\
  \ width options such as 704x2 or 768x2 again, especially since 640x2 had been used previously. I'll focus on trying 704x2 for potential improvements.**Planning new model runs**\n\nI'm choosing to propose two runs: one with H=704x2 and a learning rate of 1e-3 with gradient clipping at 1.0, and another with H=640x2 using a learning rate of 9e-4. We haven't run 9e-4 yet due to a concurrency issue, but I can resubmit that now.\n\nI'll create submissions based on the configurations for both runs, adjusting the hidden size and incorporating dropout of 0.1. I’ll also consider possibly tweaking the gradient clipping norm. Lastly, I'll ensure the YAML titles are concise and include appropriate tags."
