- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=32,H=768x2,dr=0.10) + AdamW (wd=1e-4) + GradClip(1.0)\"\ntags: \"mlp, factorized-loadings, layernorm, optimizer, weight-decay, clipping\"\nabstract: \"Best capacity so far (768x2) with AdamW (wd=1e-4) and global gradient clipping (norm=1.0). Peak LR 1e-3, dropout 0.10. Tests if AdamW+clip, which improved 512x2, yields gains at larger width. Curvature λ=1e-4.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_mlp_global import create_network, _define_hyperparameters as _def_base\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      hp = _def_base()\n      hp['proj_rank'] = 32\n      hp['hidden_size'] = 768\n      hp['hidden_size2'] = 768\n      hp['dropout_rate'] = 0.10\n      hp['learning_rate'] = 1e-3\n      return hp\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions,\
    \ targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=32,H=768x2,dr=0.11) + Adam(lr=1e-3) + GradClip(1.0)\"\ntags: \"mlp, factorized-loadings, layernorm, regularization, optimizer, clipping\"\nabstract: \"Regularization sweep at larger width: 768x2 with slightly higher dropout (0.11) under Adam (no wd) + global grad clipping (norm=1.0). Curvature λ=1e-4.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_mlp_global import create_network, _define_hyperparameters as _def_base\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      hp = _def_base()\n      hp['proj_rank'] = 32\n      hp['hidden_size'] = 768\n      hp['hidden_size2'] =\
    \ 768\n      hp['dropout_rate'] = 0.11\n      hp['learning_rate'] = 1e-3\n      return hp\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Proposing next actions**


  I''m considering the recent evaluations in the Research Counter. We have IDs 306 and 307 showing improvements, now very close to the state-of-the-art (SOTA) mark by Aether. Our best score to date, ID 306, is -0.026608. I’m wondering if we should use filter tags for a survey or possibly publish our results. We’ve published before, but since we had plans to export parameter norms already, I’m not quite sure what to prioritize here.**Reviewing submissions and configurations**


  Earlier, I submitted a parameter norm export for 640x2, but I’m not sure if it was accepted since it’s not in the list. It might not have executed because of the queue. Now that both 306 and 307 are finished, the queue is free, so I can resubmit the export, but this time I''ll do it for the best configuration, 768x2. I also need to consider running a seed sweep or increasing the training patience. I’ve already experimented with dropout rates, and it seems like 0.10 is our best option.**Planning next tests**


  I haven''t tested everything yet, but I''m considering that stability could be an issue. I could try 1.0e-3 with a clip of 1.0 on the 768x2 configuration to see if there’s slight improvement, though 9e-4 is already performing well. Tweaking the dropout to 0.11 for 768x2 might help with regularization since we haven''t tried that yet. I also want to test AdamW with a weight decay of 1e-4, as Aether achieved good results with it. Plus, we could revisit the cosine schedule for testing.**Planning action commands**


  We want to keep the token usage minimal while ensuring our actions are clear, especially since the environment expects action commands. It seems I need to include two submissions: “768x2 AdamW wd=1e-4 + clip” and “768x2 lr=1e-3 + clip (test)”. I might also want to consider updating “Private Memory” or archiving. Since we currently have no running experiments, I can submit the new actions. I''ll craft the first submission''s title to reflect the parameters needed.**Preparing second submission**


  For the second submission, I''m looking at using the configuration "768x2 + Adam (lr=1e-3) + Clip(1.0)" with dropout set to 0.11. I hypothesize this may help with regularization for the broader width. I should also consider testing the learning rates of 1e-3 versus 9e-4 for the 768x2 setup. Since Aether 305 had success with AdamW, it seems logical to stick with that approach too. Let''s prepare the two submissions focusing on what''s compatible and ensure they align with our hidden size parameters.'
