parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=32,H=768x2,dr=0.09) + Adam(lr=9.5e-4) + GradClip(1.0)\"\ntags: \"mlp, factorized-loadings, layernorm, residual-copy, optimizer, gradient-clipping\"\nabstract: \"Deeper global MLP (768×2) with slightly lower dropout (0.09). Adam (no wd) at lr=9.5e-4 and global grad clipping 1.0. Loss: MAE + temporal curvature (λ=1e-4).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_mlp_global import create_network, _define_hyperparameters as _def_base\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      hp = _def_base()\n      hp['proj_rank'] = 32\n      hp['hidden_size'] = 768\n      hp['hidden_size2'] = 768\n      hp['dropout_rate'] = 0.09\n      return hp\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def\
    \ create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      lr = 9.5e-4\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=lr, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=32,H=768x2,dr=0.09) + Adam(lr=1e-3) + GradClip(0.9)\"\ntags: \"mlp, factorized-loadings, layernorm, residual-copy, optimizer, gradient-clipping\"\nabstract: \"Same deeper MLP (768×2) but with slightly stronger clipping (0.9) at lr=1e-3 to test stability near best region. Loss: MAE + temporal curvature (λ=1e-4).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_mlp_global import create_network, _define_hyperparameters as _def_base\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      hp = _def_base()\n      hp['proj_rank'] = 32\n      hp['hidden_size'] = 768\n      hp['hidden_size2'] = 768\n      hp['dropout_rate'] = 0.09\n    \
    \  return hp\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(0.9),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning experiment submissions**\n\nIt seems that using a mixture-of-factor-loadings gives a slightly better result, but I'm considering if we should attempt MoFL. We didn't implement it earlier, and while it’s high-level code, implementing it quickly might come with risks. For now, it feels safer to tune the dropout and learning rate. Improvements might come from capacity and clipping, and maybe label smoothing could help.  \n\nI’ll go ahead and submit two experiments with specified parameters for next steps.**Structuring parameters for MLP**\n\nThe base function _def_base likely returns defaults, maybe 512. I can override hidden_size and hidden_size2, which I noticed in earlier logs for the MLP. While we changed hidden_size to 768, we never set hidden_size2. Logs indicate both are currently set to 768, so I need to ensure both are configured correctly along with dropout_rate. \n\nI'll import models_mlp_global to create the network, defining hyperparameters with a\
  \ dropout of 0.09. We can submit two concurrent jobs, so it seems like a good plan going forward!**Planning submissions and code adjustments**\n\nI need to keep the content length manageable, so I’ll proceed with some actions. I’ll go to research since we're already in token management and then submit two actions with proper YAML blocks, ensuring correct quoting.\n\nI’m considering replicating Aether's clip+Adam base but want to focus on a deeper 768. I’ll add two runs with specified parameters. It seems we should include code to set hidden_size2 in _define_hyperparameters.\n\nI’ll craft code with models_mlp_global to import create_network while ensuring both hidden_size and hidden_size2 are correctly set!"
