tick: 158
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write ariadne/mlp_analysis_utils.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Utilities for exporting analysis artifacts from Factorized Global MLP + RC + LN runs.\n\n  Features:\n  - Param norms per leaf (shape, L2)\n  - Attempted extraction of U and V loadings (if present in params)\n  - U stats: column norms, max pairwise coherence (cosine)\n  - V stats: orthogonality error ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n  - Save JSON summaries under storage/ariadne/analyses/mlp_exports/<tag>/trial_<seed>.json\n  \"\"\"\n  from __future__ import annotations\n\n  import os\n  import json\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Tuple\n\n  import numpy as np\n\n  try:\n      import jax\n      import jax.numpy as jnp\n      from flax.traverse_util import flatten_dict\n  except Exception:\n      # Provide light fallbacks if environment lacks JAX/Flax (for safety in analysis-only contexts)\n      jax = None\n      jnp = None\n      def flatten_dict(d, keep_empty_nodes=True):\n          out = {}\n   \
    \       def rec(prefix, x):\n              if isinstance(x, dict):\n                  if not x and keep_empty_nodes:\n                      out[tuple(prefix)] = x\n                  for k, v in x.items():\n                      rec(prefix + [k], v)\n              else:\n                  out[tuple(prefix)] = x\n          rec([], d)\n          return out\n\n  def _to_py_number(x):\n      try:\n          return float(x)\n      except Exception:\n          try:\n              return float(x.item())\n          except Exception:\n              return None\n\n  def _array_l2(arr) -> float:\n      if jnp is not None and isinstance(arr, (jnp.ndarray,)):\n          return float(jnp.linalg.norm(arr).item())\n      # numpy fallback\n      arr = np.asarray(arr)\n      return float(np.linalg.norm(arr))\n\n  def _array_shape(arr):\n      try:\n          return tuple(arr.shape)\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n\n  def collect_param_norms(params: Dict[str, Any]) -> Dict[str, Dict[str,\
    \ Any]]:\n      \"\"\"\n      Returns a dict: name -> {'shape': tuple, 'l2': float}\n      Names are formed by joining flattened path with '/'\n      \"\"\"\n      try:\n          flat = flatten_dict(params, keep_empty_nodes=False)\n      except Exception:\n          # best-effort flatten for plain dicts\n          flat = flatten_dict(params, keep_empty_nodes=False)\n      stats = {}\n      for k_tuple, leaf in flat.items():\n          name = \"/\".join(map(str, k_tuple))\n          try:\n              l2 = _array_l2(leaf)\n              shape = _array_shape(leaf)\n              stats[name] = {'shape': shape, 'l2': l2}\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n      return stats\n\n  def _find_first_matrix(params: Dict[str, Any], key_substr: str):\n      \"\"\"\n      Heuristically find first leaf whose path contains key_substr (e.g., 'U' or 'V').\n      Returns (name, array) or (None, None) if not found.\n      \"\"\"\n      try:\n          flat = flatten_dict(params, keep_empty_nodes=False)\n\
    \      except Exception:\n          flat = flatten_dict(params, keep_empty_nodes=False)\n      for k_tuple, leaf in flat.items():\n          name = \"/\".join(map(str, k_tuple))\n          if key_substr in name and hasattr(leaf, 'shape'):\n              # Prefer 2D matrices\n              try:\n                  if len(leaf.shape) == 2:\n                      return name, leaf\n              except Exception:\n                  pass\n      # fallback: any match\n      for k_tuple, leaf in flat.items():\n          name = \"/\".join(map(str, k_tuple))\n          if key_substr in name and hasattr(leaf, 'shape'):\n              return name, leaf\n      return None, None\n\n  def u_stats(U) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      U_np = np.asarray(U)\n      # Column norms\n      col_norms = np.linalg.norm(U_np, axis=0)\n      # Coherence (max off-diagonal cosine)\n      if U_np.ndim == 2 and U_np.shape[1] > 1:\n          Uc = U_np / (col_norms[None, :] + 1e-12)\n          G = Uc.T @ Uc  # (p, p)\n    \
    \      # mask diag\n          p = G.shape[0]\n          mask = ~np.eye(p, dtype=bool)\n          max_coh = float(np.max(np.abs(G[mask])))\n      else:\n          max_coh = None\n      return {\n          'shape': tuple(U_np.shape),\n          'col_norms_mean': float(np.mean(col_norms)),\n          'col_norms_std': float(np.std(col_norms)),\n          'max_pairwise_coherence': max_coh,\n      }\n\n  def v_stats(V) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      V_np = np.asarray(V)\n      G = V_np.T @ V_np\n      p = G.shape[0]\n      I = np.eye(p, dtype=G.dtype)\n      fro_err = float(np.linalg.norm(G - I, ord='fro'))\n      fro_err_sq = fro_err ** 2\n      return {\n          'shape': tuple(V_np.shape),\n          'gram_fro_error': fro_err,\n          'gram_fro_error_sq': fro_err_sq,\n      }\n\n  def ensure_dir(path: str):\n      os.makedirs(path, exist_ok=True)\n\n  def export_json(path: str, data: Dict[str, Any]):\n      ensure_dir(os.path.dirname(path))\n      with open(path, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(data,\
    \ f, indent=2)\n\n  def export_mlp_summary(params: Dict[str, Any], trial_data: Dict[str, Any], out_dir: str):\n      \"\"\"\n      params: PyTree (likely {'params': ...} from Flax) or raw dict; works with either.\n      trial_data: dict with keys val_mae, hyperparameters, seed, trial_number\n      out_dir: base directory to write JSON\n      \"\"\"\n      # Tolerate both {'params': ...} and flat trees\n      p_core = params.get('params', params) if isinstance(params, dict) else params\n\n      # Param norms\n      norms = collect_param_norms(p_core)\n\n      # Try to find U and V\n      U_name, U = _find_first_matrix(p_core, 'U')\n      V_name, V = _find_first_matrix(p_core, 'V')\n\n      U_summary = u_stats(U) if U is not None else None\n      V_summary = v_stats(V) if V is not None else None\n\n      summary = {\n          'val_mae': float(trial_data.get('val_mae', np.nan)),\n          'hyperparameters': trial_data.get('hyperparameters', {}),\n          'seed': int(trial_data.get('seed',\
    \ -1)),\n          'trial_number': int(trial_data.get('trial_number', -1)),\n          'U_name': U_name,\n          'V_name': V_name,\n          'U_summary': U_summary,\n          'V_summary': V_summary,\n          'param_norms': norms,\n      }\n\n      tag = \"mlp_exports\"\n      seed = summary['seed']\n      out_path = os.path.join('storage', 'ariadne', 'analyses', tag, f\"trial_{seed}.json\")\n      export_json(out_path, summary)\n      return out_path\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning experiments for model optimization**


  I’ve reviewed our token usage and it’s at 143k, so we don’t need to prune again now. I’m thinking about additional meaningful experiments, like experimenting with Factorized MLP modifications. Should we add LayerNorm to hidden layers? We’ve previously seen gradient clipping thresholds like 1.0 being the best; maybe we’ll try 0.95 this time. Also, should we test AdamW versus Adam? Let’s consider Nudged dropout and early stopping effects too.**Exploring model adjustments**


  The submission process requires us to train three seeds and average the negative MAE, but it specifies not to use an ensemble across seeds. I’m considering improvements like the "residual copy head" or adding gating enhancements like mixture-of-loadings gating inspired by Logos. However, replicating that could be tricky due to restrictions. I think implementing a variant within the MLP architecture might be worth exploring. Although we’ve previously tried MoL and had less success, I’m curious about other configurations and potential adjustments like Layer Scale or different layer normalizations.**Planning model experiments and analysis**


  I’m considering proposing a comparison between "Pre-LN MLP" (applying LayerNorm on inputs to each layer) and a Post-LN baseline. I want to keep experiments focused on configurations like 832x2 and 896x2. If after these runs there''s no improvement, we can proceed to finalize the archive and shift towards analysis. Right now, with two experiments already running, I can''t add more, but I can review other agents'' code or work on exporting for a complete() function to analyze the best 768x2 setup. We might re-use analysis utilities for our MLP work.**Preparing code changes for analysis**


  Preparing code changes is indeed beneficial. I need to implement modifications for analysis in the submission content or storage modules, starting with writing ''ariadne/complete_hooks.py'' for a function that computes parameter norms and features. The complete() function will be in the submission file but can be imported from storage. After we find the best results for configurations 832/896, I''ll write files for ''analysis_utils_mlp.py'' and ''complete_mlp_export.py''. Meanwhile, updating the paper in the Archive Room could be an option, but thorough baselines and more experiments are needed.**Preparing analysis utilities and submission plans**


  I’m thinking about adding an addendum or a new paper to analyze MLP versus SSM, which is allowed but requires content creation using tokens. I can do this in private memory and publish later through ''source_private''. I plan to write essential utility functions in ''ariadne/analysis_utils_mlp.py'' for computing parameter norms and statistics for U and V in the MLP model. I’ll implement this now, preparing for future exports and keeping other actions concise, while noting we have limited concurrent tasks.'
