parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write ariadne/models_fourier.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead  # storage/ariadne/models.py\n\n  def _logit(p):\n      p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\n  class FourierHarmonicHead(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Per-factor multi-frequency harmonic forecaster.\n      Predicts amplitudes A[b,k,M], phases phi[b,k,M], and freqs w[b,k,M] from input context.\n      Generates f_freq[b,t,k] = sum_m A * cos(w * t + phi), t=1..T.\n      \"\"\"\n      M: int = 12\n      hidden: int = 96\n      T: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, f_in):  # f_in: (B, 4, k)\n          B, Tin, K = f_in.shape\n          # Per-factor context from 4-step input\n          c = jnp.mean(f_in, axis=1)  # (B, k)\n          # Small MLP over per-factor context\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(c)  # (B,hidden)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n\
    \          # Predict per-factor, per-harmonic params\n          A_raw = nn.Dense(self.M * K, use_bias=True)(h).reshape(B, self.M, K)  # (B,M,K)\n          phi_raw = nn.Dense(self.M * K, use_bias=True)(h).reshape(B, self.M, K)\n          w_raw = nn.Dense(self.M * K, use_bias=True)(h).reshape(B, self.M, K)\n\n          A = nn.softplus(A_raw)  # >= 0\n          phi = (2.0 * jnp.pi) * nn.sigmoid(phi_raw) - jnp.pi  # [-pi, pi]\n          w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)  # [0, pi]\n\n          t = jnp.arange(1, self.T + 1, dtype=f_in.dtype)[None, :, None, None]  # (1,T,1,1)\n          # Broadcast to (B,T,M,K)\n          A_b = A[:, None, :, :]          # (B,1,M,K)\n          phi_b = phi[:, None, :, :]      # (B,1,M,K)\n          w_b = w[:, None, :, :]          # (B,1,M,K)\n          f_freq = jnp.sum(A_b * jnp.cos(w_b * t + phi_b), axis=2)  # (B,T,K)\n          return f_freq\n\n  class FourierMixFLoad(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Factorized-loadings + per-factor harmonic forecast + residual copy\
    \ + gamma gating.\"\"\"\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_inc: int = 96\n      M: int = 12\n      T: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, Tin, N = x.shape\n          K = self.rank_k\n          P = self.proj_rank\n\n          # Factorized loadings: L = U @ V^T\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, P))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (K, P))\n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          # Project inputs to factor space: (B,4,N)->(B,4,P)->(B,4,K)\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)              # (B,4,P)\n          f_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)         # (B,4,K)\n\n          # Harmonic head in factor space\n          f_harm\
    \ = FourierHarmonicHead(M=self.M, hidden=self.hidden_inc, T=self.T)(f_in)  # (B,T,K)\n\n          # Small per-factor increment head for flexibility\n          f_flat = f_in.reshape(B * K, Tin)                             # (B*K,4)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_inc)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          f_inc = nn.Dense(self.T)(h).reshape(B, K, self.T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,K)\n\n          f_out = f_harm + f_inc  # (B,T,K)\n\n          # Project back to neurons: (B,T,K)->(B,T,P)->(B,T,N)\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)        # (B,T,P)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)     # (B,T,N)\n\n          # Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n          def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init,\
    \ (self.T,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=self.T)(x)  # (B,T,N)\n\n          return y_copy + y_factor\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FourierMix-FLoad (k=320,p=32,M=12,H=96, γ_end=0.99) + Curvature\"\ntags: \"fourier, factorized-loadings, harmonic, residual, forecasting, curvature\"\nabstract: \"Our implementation of a hybrid harmonic forecaster in factor space: factorized loadings U@V^T; per-factor multi-frequency head (M=12) predicts amplitudes/phases/frequencies to generate 32-step harmonics, plus a small per-factor increment head and residual copy. Global horizon gate γ. Trained with MAE+temporal curvature (λ=1e-4).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_fourier import FourierMixFLoad\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED =\
    \ 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_inc': 96,\n          'M': 12,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kw):\n          self.model = FourierMixFLoad(**kw)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_inc=int(hparams.get('hidden_inc', 96)),\n          M=int(hparams.get('M', 12)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n\
    \          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FourierMix-FLoad (k=320,p=32,M=16,H=96, γ_end=0.99) + Curvature\"\ntags: \"fourier, factorized-loadings, harmonic, residual, forecasting, curvature\"\nabstract: \"Same as FourierMix-FLoad but with a larger harmonic bank M=16 to test capacity vs. stability in frequency-space forecasting.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_fourier import FourierMixFLoad\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_inc': 96,\n          'M': 16,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kw):\n          self.model = FourierMixFLoad(**kw)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_inc=int(hparams.get('hidden_inc', 96)),\n          M=int(hparams.get('M', 16)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99))\n\
    \      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering implementation options**


  I want to explore how we can implement our own Fourier mixture without using existing code. I can read the gist to understand the concepts, but I shouldn’t copy it directly. The rules allow us to read any lineage''s storage, but we can''t write. I think it''s clear we can import from official sources; this could open up some possibilities for collaboration. However, we should aim for novelty by proposing our own design, like a Factorized MLP with a Fourier head.**Planning model proposal**


  To avoid replicating existing code, I’m thinking about designing our own ''FourierFactorHead'' within our storage path instead of importing their module. I need to focus on keeping things concise and not overly verbose. Since there’s no explicit question at hand, I should decide on the next steps. I’ll propose a Fourier hybrid model and plan to update the archive using /execute_action. This model, "FourierMix-FLoad-LN," will transform input data and predict future steps, which might be a bit complex, but I’ll aim to work through it!**Developing forecasting model**


  We only have 4 timesteps, and using FFT on those gives us 4 complex bins. For 32-step forecasting, I’m considering modeling the spectral envelope and reconstructing it with an inverse transform based on predicted phase progression. I think a parameterized harmonic model could work well, where each factor has a frequency and amplitude derived from the 4-step input to produce the next 32 time points. Integrating frequency domain modulators with our MLP could enhance predictions. I’ll propose computing factor space and a DFT of a padded length of 36.**Designing forecasting model**


  We’re starting with only 4 inputs, so I can compute the DFT. But since we want to forecast, I’ll define a frequency basis with M=16. I think using a learned bank of sine and cosine functions with predicted amplitudes from an MLP could work. We can generate a 32-step frequency based on the sum of the cosine functions. I’ll propose a "HarmonicMixer" with multi-frequency mixtures. We’ll use k=320 and M=12 frequencies, incorporating dropout and layer normalization. I also need to define the network in our storage module for training.**Crafting harmonic forecast experiments**


  I’ll submit two experiments: one with a baseline harmonic mixture using layer normalization and another with per-frequency gating combined with a mixture-of-loadings approach, using M=16. We need to implement our storage write for "FourierHarmonicHead" in our factorized MLP architecture using JAX/Flax. The model should compute factor loadings, use a small MLP for amplitude and phase predictions, and project back to neuron space appropriately. I’ll set parameters like rank_k=320 and BATCH_SIZE 8, ensuring we meticulously organize the code and methods before submission.'
