- text: "/execute_action{goto token_management}\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"150-156\"\n    summary: |\n      Near-SOTA Factorized Global MLP + RC + LN sweeps at larger widths with gradient clipping.\n      Key results (3-seed means):\n      - ID 306 (768×2, dr=0.10, Adam lr=9e−4, Clip=1.0) → −0.026608 (our best in this line).\n      - ID 315 (768×2, AdamW wd=1e−4, Clip=1.0) → −0.026714; ID 316 (dr=0.11) → −0.026693 (worse than dr=0.10).\n      - Fine LR/clip: ID 318 (dr=0.09, 9.5e−4, Clip=1.0) → −0.026682; ID 319 (dr=0.09, 1e−3, Clip=0.9) → −0.026669.\n      - ID 321 (dr=0.10, 9.25e−4, Clip=1.0) → −0.026663; ID 322 (dr=0.10, 9e−4, Clip=1.05) → −0.026734.\n      - Schedules: ID 326 (warmup+cosine to 1e−4) → −0.026999 (regressed).\n      - Dropout sweep: ID 327 (dr=0.095, 9e−4) → −0.026722 (no gain over 0.10).\n      - Capacity up: ID 329 (832×2) → −0.026732; ID 330 (896×2) → −0.026714 (no gain vs 768×2).\n      - Analysis export: ID 333 (best 768×2\
    \ with complete()) → −0.026676; saved param norms and U/V summaries at storage/ariadne/analyses/mlp_exports/trial_{42,43,44}.json.\n      Takeaways: Clip=1.0 consistently best; dr≈0.10 best; Adam no-wd with clip slightly better than AdamW. Larger widths >768 do not improve mean beyond −0.026608; warmup+cosine regressed.\n  - ticks: \"157-161\"\n    summary: |\n      Fourier hybrids exploration and benchmarking vs MLP SOTA.\n      - Episteme Fourier Forecaster Phase 1 (ID 331) → −0.026471; Phase 2 with latent norm (ID 335) → −0.026367 (new SOTA line).\n      - Our FourierMix-FLoad (factorized U@V^T + per-factor harmonic head + residual copy):\n        * ID 336 (M=12) → −0.026985; ID 337 (M=16) → −0.026949 (under MLP baseline).\n      - MLP exports continued (ID 333) with saved analysis JSONs.\n      Conclusions: Our harmonic factor model underperforms current MLPs; Episteme’s frequency-domain approach shows strong promise. Next: add LayerNorm in factor space for FourierMix and re-test\
    \ (M=12/16).\n```\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write ariadne/models_fourier_ln.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead  # storage/ariadne/models.py\n\n  def _logit(p):\n      p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\n  class FourierHarmonicHead(nn.Module):\n      M: int = 12\n      hidden: int = 96\n      T: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, f_in):  # f_in: (B, 4, K)\n          B, Tin, K = f_in.shape\n          c = jnp.mean(f_in, axis=1)  # (B, K)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(c)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          A_raw = nn.Dense(self.M * K, use_bias=True)(h).reshape(B, self.M, K)\n          phi_raw = nn.Dense(self.M * K, use_bias=True)(h).reshape(B, self.M, K)\n          w_raw = nn.Dense(self.M * K, use_bias=True)(h).reshape(B, self.M, K)\n          A = nn.softplus(A_raw)\n          phi = (2.0 * jnp.pi)\
    \ * nn.sigmoid(phi_raw) - jnp.pi\n          w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)\n          t = jnp.arange(1, self.T + 1, dtype=f_in.dtype)[None, :, None, None]  # (1,T,1,1)\n          f_freq = jnp.sum(A[:, None, :, :] * jnp.cos(w[:, None, :, :] * t + phi[:, None, :, :]), axis=2)  # (B,T,K)\n          return f_freq\n\n  class FourierMixFLoadLN(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_inc: int = 96\n      M: int = 12\n      T: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, Tin, N = x.shape\n          K = self.rank_k\n          P = self.proj_rank\n\n          # Factorized loadings\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, P))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (K, P))\n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U,\
    \ axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          # Project to factor space\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)              # (B,4,P)\n          f_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)         # (B,4,K)\n\n          # LayerNorm in factor space (across K)\n          f_in = nn.LayerNorm()(f_in)  # normalize last dim K\n\n          # Harmonic head + small increment\n          f_harm = FourierHarmonicHead(M=self.M, hidden=self.hidden_inc, T=self.T)(f_in)  # (B,T,K)\n          f_flat = f_in.reshape(B * K, Tin)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_inc)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          f_inc = nn.Dense(self.T)(h).reshape(B, K, self.T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,K)\n          f_out = f_harm + f_inc  # (B,T,K)\n\n          # Back to neurons\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n\n          # Global gamma[t]\n          def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0],\
    \ dtype=dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (self.T,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n          # Residual copy\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=self.T)(x)\n          return y_copy + y_factor\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FourierMix-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,M=12,H=96, γ_end=0.99) + Curvature\"\ntags: \"fourier, layernorm, factorized-loadings, harmonic, residual, forecasting\"\nabstract: \"Add LayerNorm in factor space to FourierMix-FLoad (M=12) before the harmonic and increment heads. Hypothesis: LN stabilizes frequency head and improves generalization. Train with MAE+curvature (λ=1e-4), Adam, Clip=1.0.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_fourier_ln import FourierMixFLoadLN\n\
    \  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_inc': 96,\n          'M': 12,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kw):\n          self.model = FourierMixFLoadLN(**kw)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_inc=int(hparams.get('hidden_inc', 96)),\n          M=int(hparams.get('M', 12)),\n\
    \          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FourierMix-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,M=16,H=96, γ_end=0.99) + Curvature\"\ntags: \"fourier, layernorm, factorized-loadings, harmonic, residual, forecasting\"\nabstract: \"Same FourierMix-FLoad with LayerNorm but larger harmonic bank M=16 to test capacity after LN. Train with MAE+curvature (λ=1e-4), Adam, Clip=1.0.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  from models_fourier_ln import FourierMixFLoadLN\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\
    \n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_inc': 96,\n          'M': 16,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kw):\n          self.model = FourierMixFLoadLN(**kw)\n          self.needs_rng = False\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_inc=int(hparams.get('hidden_inc', 96)),\n          M=int(hparams.get('M', 16)),\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start',\
    \ 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99))\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Managing token overflow**\n\nI need to make sure we don’t exceed token limits, so I'll start by managing the tokens and summarizing blocks 150-159 about MLP sweeps and Fourier results. I aim for a concise yet thorough summary. \n\nI’m considering scheduling another experiment, focusing on an MLP with specific configurations. The Adam optimizer seems to perform well, but earlier attempts with AdamW didn’t surpass results. I may replicate experiments similar to Aether’s setup but with our parameters in mind. Overall, there seems to be a small gap in performance to address.**Updating paper archives**\n\nFor now, I want to focus on updating the archive to include the Fourier results and propose an analysis of step MAEs. I’ll create a quick update for the archive, but I’m concerned that writing up the content might use too many tokens. Instead, I can reference evaluation IDs without including code, which has been accepted before. I’ll reply to the Archive about allowing this\
  \ update. \n\nSince we have 176k tokens, I should prune ticks 150-159 with relevant summaries to keep things efficient.**Grouping MLP and Fourier results**\n\nI can group the results from ticks 150-156, which detail \"Near-SOTA MLP 768x2 sweeps.\" The best results range from -0.026608 to -0.026998 for various configurations, including warmup and cosine regresses. It seems this summary will keep the necessary information intact.\n\nFor ticks 157-162, we also have our Fourier experiments, which performed decently but indicate that the Fourier approach without some gating underperformed. I should consider applying LayerNorm in the factor space before the Fourier harmonic head, which could enhance performance. Also, maybe I'll update the model storage with this new variant.**Implementing FourierMixFLoadLN**\n\nI’ll go ahead and implement the \"FourierMixFLoadLN\" variant, incorporating nn.LayerNorm across the factor dimension. Since Flax LayerNorm expects the last dimension for shapes like\
  \ f_in (B, 4, K), I'll apply it using axis=-1. \n\nIn the __call__ method, after projecting to f_in, I’ll add nn.LayerNorm for stabilization. Then, I’ll pass the result to FourierHarmonicHead. Once that’s done, I can submit two runs, one with M=12 and another with M=16. I need to be mindful of the token limit, but it looks manageable for writing this code.**Implementing models_fourier_ln.py**\n\nI’m ready to create the models_fourier_ln.py file with LayerNorm integrated. After that, I’ll submit two experiments and also check the results from Episteme’s Fourier to compare methodologies. \n\nI will implement nn.LayerNorm across the last axis on f_in, and I might include a gamma_end adjustment. Next, I’ll execute the actions to write to storage and submit for M=12 and M=16. \n\nI need to ensure I prune my response summarizing the relevant blocks, sticking to the allowed range, and keeping a close eye on pending experiments to avoid exceeding limits."
