parts:
- text: "/execute_action{review 335}\n/execute_action{review 331}\n/execute_action{storage write ariadne/models_fourier_gf.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  FourierMix-FLoad with LayerNorm and Global Frequency Bank (GF):\n    - Factorized loadings: U (N×P), V (K×P), with optional column-normalized U\n    - Projected factors f_in ∈ R^{B×4×K}, LayerNorm across K\n    - Global per-factor harmonic bank: w[k,m], phi[k,m] shared across batches\n    - Per-sample amplitudes A[b,k,m] predicted from input context via small MLP\n    - Small per-factor increment head f_inc for residual flexibility\n    - Optional per-sample temporal envelope S[b,t,k] from context\n    - Global gamma[t] horizon gate\n    - Residual copy head in observation space\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  from models import ResidualCopyHead  # storage/ariadne/models.py\n\n  def _logit(p):\n      p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\n  class\
    \ GlobalFreqBank(nn.Module):\n      K: int\n      M: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self):\n          # w ∈ (0, π), phi ∈ (−π, π), both global per-factor/per-harmonic\n          w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.K, self.M))\n          phi_raw = self.param('phi_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.K, self.M))\n          w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)                    # (K,M)\n          phi = (2.0 * jnp.pi) * nn.sigmoid(phi_raw) - jnp.pi  # (K,M)\n          return w, phi\n\n  class FourierMixFLoadLN_GFreq(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_inc: int = 96\n      M: int = 16\n      T: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n      use_envelope: bool = True\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, Tin, N = x.shape\n          K = self.rank_k\n          P = self.proj_rank\n\n\
    \          # Factorized loadings\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, P))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (K, P))\n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          # Project to factor space\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)              # (B,4,P)\n          f_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)         # (B,4,K)\n\n          # LayerNorm across K (last dim)\n          f_in = nn.LayerNorm()(f_in)  # (B,4,K)\n\n          # Context for per-sample parameters\n          c = jnp.mean(f_in, axis=1)  # (B,K)\n\n          # Global frequency bank\n          w, phi = GlobalFreqBank(K=K, M=self.M)()  # w,phi: (K,M)\n\n          # Per-sample amplitudes A[b,k,m] via small per-factor MLP on f_in (4-step)\n          f_flat = f_in.reshape(B * K, Tin)  # (B*K,4)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_inc)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          A_raw = nn.Dense(self.M)(h).reshape(B,\
    \ K, self.M)  # (B,K,M)\n          A = nn.softplus(A_raw)  # nonnegative\n\n          # Harmonic synthesis: cos over T with global w,phi and per-sample A\n          t = jnp.arange(1, self.T + 1, dtype=f_in.dtype)[:, None, None]  # (T,1,1)\n          # cos_tkm: (T,K,M)\n          cos_tkm = jnp.cos(t * w[None, :, :] + phi[None, :, :])\n          # f_harm[b,t,k] = sum_m A[b,k,m] * cos_tkm[t,k,m]\n          f_harm = jnp.einsum('bkm,tkm->btk', A, cos_tkm)  # (B,T,K)\n\n          # Increment head per factor to capture residual trends\n          h2 = nn.Dense(self.hidden_inc)(f_flat); h2 = nn.gelu(h2)\n          f_inc = nn.Dense(self.T)(h2).reshape(B, K, self.T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,K)\n\n          f_out = f_harm + f_inc  # (B,T,K)\n\n          # Optional per-sample temporal envelope S[b,t,k] from context c\n          if self.use_envelope:\n              def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n                  T, K_ = shape\n                  tt = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T, dtype=dtype)\n\
    \                  base = 0.6 + 0.25 * tt  # rises 0.6 -> 0.85\n                  base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K_))\n                  return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n              alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (self.T, K))       # (T,K)\n              beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (K,))     # (K,)\n              logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])\n              S = nn.sigmoid(logits)  # (B,T,K)\n              f_out = f_out * S\n\n          # Project back to neurons\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)   # (B,T,P)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)  # (B,T,N)\n\n          # Global horizon gamma[t]\n          def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              tt = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * tt\n              return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw',\
    \ gamma_sched_init, (self.T,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n          # Residual copy in observation space\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=self.T)(x)\n\n          return y_copy + y_factor\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next actions**\n\nI need to outline our next steps since the user is in the Research Counter with two FourierMix-LN runs queued. We’ve seen that Episteme's Fourier Forecaster achieved a strong -0.026367. Our own FourierMix-FLoad was slightly behind at -0.02695, even after adding LN. \n\nIt might be helpful to review Episteme's Fourier model using evaluation IDs 335 and 331. I can review evaluation ID 335 for code details, but I must remember to follow collaboration rules for any code cloning or review.**Evaluating next steps**\n\nIt seems I'm processing the retrieval of the submitted solution and full logs. While cloning ideas isn't allowed, creating our own submissions is the plan. Reviewing evaluation ID 335 is next. We also need to think about token management: we have 95,139 tokens used out of 270,000, so about 35% left, which is manageable.\n\nWe could propose next experiments like adding LN across the factor dimension or exploring amplitude gating. There\
  \ are numerous options like learning amplitude decays or adding a damping term, so there's a lot to consider moving forward!**Considering analysis and next steps**\n\nI’m thinking about instrumenting analysis by exporting predictions and latents from the Fourier run to compute the spectrum for comparison. A major step is replicating Episteme's SOTA with our adaptation focused on factorized loadings. This could involve learned frequencies and phases with normalization across time.\n\nAlternatively, I could pivot back to MLP to close the gap to SOTA — but Fourier’s performance is currently stronger. Reviewing evaluation ID 335 could provide useful insights, particularly around latent normalization. I’ll propose adjustments to the Fourier model with amplitude gating and increase M to 24 while being cautious about GPU memory limits.**Planning experiments and gating**\n\nI’m considering enabling the 'complete()' function for exporting latents, while keeping p and K stable at K=320 and p=32.\
  \ I propose two experiments, testing M=24 and M=16, with amplitude envelope gating for early and late times, similar to per-step gamma. However, gamma is global, so S could be more specific, allowing per-sample, per-factor, per-time gating.\n\nThis will increase compute memory, but that's manageable. I think we can derive S from the context over time, plus I might want to include frequency or harmonic dropout to promote sparsity, though tying frequencies across factors could be challenging.**Designing the Fourier model**\n\nI am planning to enable several features, like per-factor amplitude, phase, and weight parameters. We've computed A_raw, phi_raw, and w_raw, which introduced complexity through unique per-batch frequencies. Episteme uses a stable frequency basis rather than per-batch, which could help with generalization. \n\nTo reduce complexity, I’ll consider setting up a global learnable frequency bank and focus on amplitude predictions from context. The improved model could include\
  \ amplitude gating and potentially a time envelope. I want to define classes in the code for the global frequency bank and adjust the architectures accordingly, while keeping in mind the overall param complexity. We also need to prepare models for future submissions once current tasks are complete.**Crafting the Fourier model code**\n\nI'm aware of potential pitfalls, especially with the LN call, as I need to specify the axis for normalization correctly. Flax's default normalizes across the last axis, which should work for our input shape, but we need to ensure we're clear about this.\n\nI plan to compute `cos_tkm` with the appropriate shapes and use einsum for efficiency. I will also implement LN solely on the input for now. I’ll document the code robustly, making sure to double-check parameter dimensions and initialization.\n\nI’m thinking of separating amplitude predictions and using simple linear layers for each factor. Once I structure everything, I’ll incorporate necessary imports\
  \ and consider future tasks like exporting latents!"
