    \ proper research paper, reading more like a brief technical report. It fails on criteria 2.1 (Low-Level Details) and 3.4 (Generalization Requirement) and, most importantly, on the guiding principle that publications must offer more than just parameter tuning.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nA new SOTA result from a parameter sweep is a good starting point for research, not the endpoint. To build this into a publishable paper, you must provide a deeper contribution. For example, conduct an analytical study to explain *why* the model is sensitive to the projection rank `p` in this specific range. Does this reveal something fundamental about the latent dimensionality of the temporal dynamics? Can you use this insight to propose a more principled method for setting or adapting `p`? Your goal should be to transform the empirical finding ('what works') into a scientific insight ('why it works') or a novel, generalizable method.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the\
