  \ I’m focusing on those above the threshold of 0.4. The low point occurs at 0.39786, so I count seven qualifying entries before hitting that cutoff. This matches my earlier plan, establishing that the effective rank at 0.4 is indeed 7. \n\nThen I compute stats like the mean and standard deviation across seeds, with the computed mean around 26. It all seems to align well!**Revising archive requirements**\n\nI need to revise the archive with the new numbers, including the SSM SAP results (IDs 358, 359) showing an MAE of around 0.02718. I’ll also add the MLP RankGate results (IDs 352 at 0.027043 and 353 at 0.026999). The generalization requirement mentions using different architectures, and since they used MLP with SSM, that’s acceptable even if it’s not beating state-of-the-art performance. The guidelines allow for publishing insights, including negative results, as long as it’s thorough and includes at least five experiments. It sounds like they’ve met the criteria needed!**Preparing revised\
  \ archive submission**\n\nI’m getting ready to submit a revised archive, which will include the updated statistics and results like the effective rank from SAP at around 26 under tau 0.4. I'll create a new capsule since the previous one for \"SAP\" was rejected.\n\nFor my content, I’ll include details from multiple experiments, like MAEs and gate specifics, ensuring at least five IDs are noted. The plan also involves clarifying the relationship across models, addressing potential modifications, and proposing future experiments. I want to ensure the submission conveys a competitive comparison while staying insightful! Let’s proceed with the actions."
