- text: "/execute_action{update 9-1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (Tick 172): Completed SAP-SSM gate statistics and analysis\n  We now include concrete gate statistics for SAP applied to the Oscillatory SSM + LayerNorm backbone (SAP-SSM-LN), complementing the MLP results and addressing reviewer suggestions. Gate JSONs are exported under storage/ariadne/analyses/rankgate_ssm_ln/.\n\n  Per-seed gate statistics (SAP-SSM-LN, 3 seeds)\n  - Seed 43 (Pmax=56, α per ID 359): gate_mean=0.1164, s_min=0.0411, s_max=0.2744; r_eff(τ=0.1)=27, r_eff(τ=0.2)=6, r_eff(τ=0.3)=0, r_eff(τ=0.4)=0; MAE=0.027132.\n  - Seed 44 (Pmax=48, α per ID 358): gate_mean=0.1370, s_min=0.0640, s_max=0.2741; r_eff(τ=0.1)=33, r_eff(τ=0.2)=8, r_eff(τ=0.3)=0, r_eff(τ=0.4)=0; MAE=0.027153.\n  - Seed 45 (Pmax=56, α per ID 359): gate_mean=0.0872, s_min=0.0369, s_max=0.2497; r_eff(τ=0.1)=17, r_eff(τ=0.2)=1, r_eff(τ=0.3)=0, r_eff(τ=0.4)=0; MAE=0.027201.\n\n  Aggregates (mean ± sd across seeds; population sd)\n  - gate_mean: 0.1135\
    \ ± 0.0204\n  - r_eff(τ=0.1): 25.67 ± 6.60\n  - r_eff(τ=0.2): 5.00 ± 2.94\n  - s_max (for context): 0.2661 ± 0.0116\n  - s_min (for context): 0.0473 ± 0.0119\n\n  Interpretation and cross-backbone comparison\n  - SAP-SSM learns a compact active subset at moderate thresholds (τ=0.2), with r_eff(0.2) ≈ 5 (±2.9), while many gates exceed τ=0.1. This indicates SSM factors share projection columns and rely on a smaller high-confidence subset for mid–late horizon dynamics.\n  - SAP-MLP (from main text) exhibited r_eff(0.4) = 26.0 ± 15.1 (seeds: 27, 44, 7), suggesting broader reliance on projection columns at a stricter threshold; SAP-SSM at τ=0.4 collapses to 0 across seeds, indicating stronger concentration of energy below 0.4 and/or the need for slightly lower τ for SSM interpretation.\n  - Fourier fixed-p sensitivity peaked around p≈36 (IDs 335/344/345). SAP-MLP’s r_eff(0.4) clustered in the ~20–45 band, overlapping this region. SAP-SSM’s r_eff at τ=0.2 centers near 5–8, consistent with\
    \ the SSM architecture using fewer, more stable projection axes when recurrence and increment heads supply additional capacity.\n\n  Performance and correlation notes\n  - SAP-SSM MAEs: 0.027132, 0.027153, 0.027201 across seeds (IDs 358/359). With only 3 points, correlation between r_eff(τ=0.1) and MAE is inconclusive; the lowest rank (17) produced the worst MAE (0.027201), suggesting too-low effective rank can degrade performance.\n  - Overall, SAP remains competitive (<0.0272) while providing rank diagnostics; best tuned fixed-p Fourier (p=36, ID 344) remains state-of-the-art in absolute MAE.\n\n  Future work (concrete follow-ups)\n  - SAP-Fourier: integrate SAP gates into FourierForecasterLN to learn p end-to-end; target parity with p=36 without sweeps.\n  - Stability: anneal α and add a mild entropy regularizer on s to reduce variance in SAP-MLP and to lift SAP-SSM’s gate magnitudes (enabling informative r_eff at τ≥0.3).\n  - Rank-to-horizon attribution: export per-step contributions\
    \ stratified by gate magnitude to tie effective rank to late-horizon errors.\n```"
