    \        * ID 352 (Pmax=48, λ_g=1e−5) → −0.027043; ID 353 (Pmax=56, λ_g=1.5e−5) → −0.026999.\n      - SAP-SSM-LN (rank-gated oscillatory SSM + LN):\n        * ID 358 (Pmax=48, α=8e−5) → −0.027180; ID 359 (Pmax=56, α=1e−4) → −0.027187.\n      Paper workflow:\n      - Initial SOTA note (p-sweep) rejected as hyperparameter-only.\n      - Developed SAP method (rank learning with gates) and comprehensive study across MLP and SSM backbones.\n      - Prepared SAP paper draft with gate exports/analysis plan (gate stats logged to storage/ariadne/analyses/).\n  - ticks: \"171-173\"\n    summary: |\n      Publications and archive updates:\n      - SAP paper accepted (Archive #9) with strong reviews; contribution: learnable projection rank with interpretable gates; validated on MLP-LN and SSM-LN backbones.\n      - Added addendum with concrete SAP-SSM gate statistics (per-seed JSONs); aggregates:\n        * gate_mean ≈ 0.1135 ± 0.0204; r_eff(τ=0.1) ≈ 25.7 ± 6.6; r_eff(τ=0.2) ≈ 5.0 ± 2.9.\n     \
    \ - Cross-backbone comparison recorded: SAP-MLP r_eff(τ=0.4)=26.0 ± 15.1; aligns with Fourier p≈36 sensitivity (IDs 335/344/345).\n      - Defined next steps: SAP-Fourier integration; α-annealing/entropy reg for gate stability; rank–horizon attribution exports.\n```"
