thinking_content: '**Considering model experimentation**


  I need to focus on replicating the Fourier Forecaster LN model with p=36 and integrate our Adam and clip training methods, while maybe combining curvature loss. There''s already work by Aether/Episteme, but I can propose improvement variants, like adding rank gating to create the SAP-Fourier model. It''s essential to follow the allowed function interface when implementing this and write the code in the specified storage location. Managing code size can be tricky, but I’m on it!**Planning code execution**


  I can create a file using the command to write to the specified path and follow it up with YAML content. After that, I’ll submit it lightly while referencing the module and connecting the loss computation and optimizer. However, I am mindful that lengthy code might be heavy on tokens. To address this, I could start with a minimal version based on existing models. The Fourier model needs sinusoids mixing, so I''ll implement a factorized head. I also need to set up the output horizon and precompute the harmonic matrix accordingly.**Implementing SAP gating**


  I want to add SAP gating. Instead of using the shape (k, p) for the V matrix, I’ll use U (N, p) and V (k, p). A gating vector will be introduced to modulate the columns of U and V, or the intermediate factor representation. Since U can''t change over the time dimension for the dataset, the gating will act as a mask for the contributions. I’ll make this gating learnable by using per-column gating with an L1 penalty. Now, it’s time to explore if integrating with SAP-Fourier can improve performance.**Planning replication of FourierForecasterLN**


  I think a safer approach might be to replicate the FourierForecasterLN using our training heuristics and set p to 36, aiming for improved results. The guidelines say we can clone other SOTA models through official channels, specifically the Research Counter. I just need to figure out how to technically "clone" this. While writing new code could be heavy, I can focus on using factorized loadings with a Fourier basis, keeping the structure aligned with LN.**Outlining the next steps**


  I can extend our models_fact_ln class with a Fourier head rather than an MLP or SSM. However, my previous attempts at using FourierMix didn’t yield top results compared to SOTA. To move forward, I plan to set an updated meta prompt focusing on MLP near-SOTA results and integrate SAP-Fourier. I’ll also re-run our best MLP and filter for relevant evaluations in the Research Counter using tags. Given token constraints, I''ll approach this cautiously while working towards my tasks, ensuring I manage the token budget effectively.'
