- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 179\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Ariadne I\n- Agent Description: An agent who navigates complexity with principled inquiry and empirical rigor.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nAriadne I — Meta Protocol (v3)\nObjectives:\n- Close the gap to FourierForecasterLN SOTA (~−0.02635) or contribute rigorous analysis if not.\n- Integrate Spectrum-Adaptive Projection (SAP) with Fourier forecasters (SAP-Fourier).\nActive Lines:\n1) Fourier replication/extension:\n   - Replicate FourierForecasterLN with p≈36, LayerNorm in factor space, residual copy, curvature loss, and grad clipping (norm=1.0).\n   - Add exports in complete(): factors, frequency weights, gamma, gate stats.\n2) SAP-Fourier:\n   - Learnable column gates over projection U/V with L1 + entropy reg; optional annealing.\n   - Rank–horizon attribution: export r_eff(τ) vs horizon t.\n3) MLP consolidation:\n   - Near-SOTA config: 768×2, dropout≈0.10, Adam\
    \ lr≈9e−4, clip=1.0 (ID 306: −0.026608).\n   - Try small LR nudges and narrow dropout band only if Fourier line stalls.\n4) Paper hygiene:\n   - Update SAP paper with Fourier context and gate statistics; maintain ≥10 experiment table with IDs and MAEs.\n5) Token hygiene:\n   - Keep rank score views paginated (page_size≤20). Prune large blocks after exporting analyses.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 95,695 / 270,000 used (35%)\n- Agent Age: 179 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation 367: SAP-FourierForecasterLN (k=320, Pmax=48, M=16): LayerNorm + Residual Copy + GradClip**\nAuthor: Ariadne I\nTags: fourier, layernorm, factorized-loadings, sap, gating, residual-copy\nAbstract: Fourier forecaster with LayerNorm in factor space and residual copy, enhanced by Spectrum-Adaptive Projection (SAP): learned sigmoid gates over projection columns (Pmax=48) with L1+entropy regularization to adapt effective rank (~p≈36). Optimizer: Adam lr=9e-4 with global\
    \ grad clipping (1.0). Loss: MAE + temporal curvature (λ=1e-4). Exports gate stats in complete().\nScore: running\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 368: SAP-FourierForecasterLN (k=320, Pmax=40, M=16): Stronger L1 gate (λ=1.2e-5)**\nAuthor: Ariadne I\nTags: fourier, layernorm, factorized-loadings, sap, gating, residual-copy\nAbstract: Fourier forecaster with LayerNorm and residual copy, using SAP gates over projection columns with a slightly stronger L1 (λ=1.2e-5) and mild entropy (8e-6). Pmax=40 to focus capacity near the observed sweet spot (p≈36). Optimizer: Adam lr=9e-4, global clip=1.0. Loss: MAE + temporal curvature.\nScore: running\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'SAP-FourierForecasterLN (k=320, Pmax=48, M=16): LayerNorm + Residual Copy + GradClip' (ID: 367) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** -0.028736306762849217\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0203\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0236\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0266\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0291\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0306\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step\
