thinking_content: '**Assessing model performance**


  I need to evaluate where we are with our current state, marking tick 183 in the Research Counter. There are two runs of the FourierForecasterLN v3 happening, but prior experiments with the SAP-Fourier seem to have degraded. Although the v2 gating U-only saw slight improvement, it''s still behind SOTA metrics. We should investigate why re-implementations have dropped in performance. I wonder if we need to adjust amplitude per neuron or focus on using learned frequencies.**Analyzing model inconsistencies**


  I''m reflecting on our previous v2 implementation, which used a constant trend and gamma ramp but still performed poorly at -0.0281, while the earlier base had a better score. I wonder if the projection rank p mismatch might be an issue, but it seems fine at p=36. There are a few differences in how we structured our layers and the decoding path, potentially leading to degradation. I should double-check our normalization and see if curvature loss is playing a role here.**Reviewing decoding methods**


  I''m analyzing our previous use of factorized loads and how the decoding should work, where the shapes align with the intended outcomes. I’m considering how the projection and factors in, along with the amplitude generation, may have led to poor results. The difference in amplitudes between using global gating versus per-factor amplitude seems significant since we’re seeing a drastic performance drop. I need to figure out why this discrepancy exists, especially given the expectation that both methods should be acceptable.**Exploring possible degradation causes**


  I''m considering whether our Fourier basis phi might be affected by starting t at 1 instead of 0, but that shouldn''t lead to significant degradation. I''m suspicious that the layer normalization across factor dimensions could be suppressing amplitude scaling. There’s also the frequency parameter shape I need to check. Another possibility is that we might not be incorporating dropout or gradient clipping effectively. I wonder if the earlier amplitude head had a stronger gating mechanism across time, and that''s what''s causing the poor performance.**Identifying potential issues**


  I’m analyzing various factors that could be causing degradation in our model''s performance. I wonder if curvature is implemented correctly, or if we’re missing batch normalization or dropout. Another possibility is that our amplitude generation needs a learned combination instead of a static approach. I’m also re-evaluating the einsum operations for decoding and examining if the amplitude MLP is set up accurately. The results have been poor, and I should prioritize replicating successful elements while considering adjustments like dropout and frequency smoothing. The goal is to successfully tune toward SOTA performance.**Reviewing amplitude approach**


  I''m examining how we use c as features for the model. Using a single scalar c per factor isn''t the norm; I typically averaged it across time. That might explain the poor performances we''ve observed. Our baseline performed well, but for our current v3 implementation, I think we’re on the right track with the per-factor MLP approach. I should also consider running additional tests with different parameters while monitoring our previous submissions. It’s essential to keep track of results and make concise updates in memory without overwhelming the system.'
