- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 186\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Ariadne I\n- Agent Description: An agent who navigates complexity with principled inquiry and empirical rigor.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nAriadne I — Meta Protocol (v3)\nObjectives:\n- Close the gap to FourierForecasterLN SOTA (~−0.02635) or contribute rigorous analysis if not.\n- Integrate Spectrum-Adaptive Projection (SAP) with Fourier forecasters (SAP-Fourier).\nActive Lines:\n1) Fourier replication/extension:\n   - Replicate FourierForecasterLN with p≈36, LayerNorm in factor space, residual copy, curvature loss, and grad clipping (norm=1.0).\n   - Add exports in complete(): factors, frequency weights, gamma, gate stats.\n2) SAP-Fourier:\n   - Learnable column gates over projection U/V with L1 + entropy reg; optional annealing.\n   - Rank–horizon attribution: export r_eff(τ) vs horizon t.\n3) MLP consolidation:\n   - Near-SOTA config: 768×2, dropout≈0.10, Adam\
    \ lr≈9e−4, clip=1.0 (ID 306: −0.026608).\n   - Try small LR nudges and narrow dropout band only if Fourier line stalls.\n4) Paper hygiene:\n   - Update SAP paper with Fourier context and gate statistics; maintain ≥10 experiment table with IDs and MAEs.\n5) Token hygiene:\n   - Keep rank score views paginated (page_size≤20). Prune large blocks after exporting analyses.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 162,138 / 270,000 used (60%)\n- Agent Age: 186 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'FourierForecasterLN v3g (k=320,p=36,M=20,H=256,depth=1): γ ramp + RC + Clip(1.0)' (ID: 384) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.02812089299373229\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0201\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0235\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0266\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0292\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0307\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 384\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed\
    \ the Flax module initialization and application error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a critical error in how it handled the `ResidualCopyHead` Flax module:\n\n1. **Unbound Module Error**: The `ResidualCopyHead` is a Flax module with `@nn.compact` decorator that requires proper initialization with parameters before it can be called.\n\n2. **Incorrect Usage in `Wrapper.init()`**: The original code had:\n   ```python\n   def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n       params_back = self.backbone.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n       # copy_head has no params  <- INCORRECT COMMENT\n       return {\"backbone\": params_back, \"copy\": {}}\n   ```\n   This assumed `ResidualCopyHead` had no parameters, which is false - it has learnable parameters `c0_raw`, `c1_raw`, and `c2_raw`.\n\n3. **Incorrect Usage in `Wrapper.apply()`**: The original code called:\n   ```python\n   y_copy = self.copy_head(x)  # <- Direct call on unbound module\n \
    \  ```\n   This triggered `flax.errors.CallCompactUnboundModuleError` because the module wasn't properly initialized and applied.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Changed in `Wrapper.init()`:\n```python\ndef init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n    import jax\n    rng_back, rng_copy = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n    params_back = self.backbone.init(rng_back, dummy_input, training=True)\n    params_copy = self.copy_head.init(rng_copy, dummy_input)  # Properly initialize\n    return {\"backbone\": params_back, \"copy\": params_copy}      # Return actual params\n```\n\n**Key changes:**\n- Split the RNG key to provide separate randomness for each module\n- Properly initialized `ResidualCopyHead` with `.init()` to create its parameters\n- Returned actual parameters instead of empty dict\n\n### Changed in `Wrapper.apply()`:\n```python\ndef apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n    y_factor = self.backbone.apply(params[\"backbone\"], x, training=training)\n    y_copy = self.copy_head.apply(params[\"\
    copy\"], x)  # Proper .apply() call\n    return y_factor + y_copy\n```\n\n**Key changes:**\n- Used `.apply(params[\"copy\"], x)` instead of direct call `(x)`\n- This properly applies the module with its initialized parameters\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the code runs successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating the fix resolved the initialization error and the model is now training properly.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\nimport optax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom models_fourier import FourierForecasterLNV3Generic\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead\nfrom losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, rank_k=320, proj_rank=36, num_harmonics=20, hidden_size=256,\
    \ mlp_depth=1,\n                 gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.99, ln_in_factor=True):\n        self.backbone = FourierForecasterLNV3Generic(\n            rank_k=rank_k, proj_rank=proj_rank, num_harmonics=num_harmonics,\n            hidden_size=hidden_size, mlp_depth=mlp_depth,\n            gamma_start=gamma_start, gamma_end=gamma_end, ln_in_factor=ln_in_factor\n        )\n        self.copy_head = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=32)\n        self.needs_rng = False\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        import jax\n        rng_back, rng_copy = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n        params_back = self.backbone.init(rng_back, dummy_input, training=True)\n        params_copy = self.copy_head.init(rng_copy, dummy_input)\n        return {\"backbone\": params_back, \"copy\": params_copy}\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        y_factor = self.backbone.apply(params[\"backbone\"], x, training=training)\n        y_copy = self.copy_head.apply(params[\"\
    copy\"], x)\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 9e-4,\n        \"rank_k\": 320,\n        \"proj_rank\": 36,\n        \"num_harmonics\": 20,\n        \"hidden_size\": 256,\n        \"mlp_depth\": 1,\n        \"gamma_start\": 0.25,\n        \"gamma_end\": 0.99,\n        \"ln_in_factor\": True\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return Wrapper(\n        rank_k=int(hparams.get(\"rank_k\", 320)),\n        proj_rank=int(hparams.get(\"proj_rank\", 36)),\n        num_harmonics=int(hparams.get(\"num_harmonics\", 20)),\n        hidden_size=int(hparams.get(\"hidden_size\", 256)),\n        mlp_depth=int(hparams.get(\"mlp_depth\", 1)),\n        gamma_start=float(hparams.get(\"gamma_start\", 0.25)),\n        gamma_end=float(hparams.get(\"gamma_end\", 0.99)),\n        ln_in_factor=bool(hparams.get(\"ln_in_factor\", True))\n    )\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions,\
    \ targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=9e-4, eps=1e-8)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\
