    ### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'FourierForecasterLN v3g (k=320,p=36,M=16,H=192,depth=2): γ ramp + RC + Clip(1.0)' (ID: 385) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.027826789218766107\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0201\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0236\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0265\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0287\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0305\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 385\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission has been fixed and is now running without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a `flax.errors.CallCompactUnboundModuleError` when trying to use the `ResidualCopyHead` Flax module. The error occurred because:\n\n1. `ResidualCopyHead` is a Flax module (inherits from `nn.Module`) that needs to be properly initialized and applied with parameters\n2. The `Wrapper` class is NOT a Flax module - it's a plain Python class\n3. In the `Wrapper.init()` method, the copy head was never\
    \ initialized - it returned `{\"copy\": {}}` with empty parameters\n4. In the `Wrapper.apply()` method, the code called `self.copy_head(x)` directly without binding parameters, which triggered the Flax error about calling compact methods on unbound modules\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the `Wrapper` class to properly handle the ResidualCopyHead as a Flax module:\n\n**In `Wrapper.init()` method:**\n```python\n# Before (WRONG):\nparams_back = self.backbone.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\nreturn {\"backbone\": params_back, \"copy\": {}}\n\n# After (CORRECT):\nimport jax\nrng_back, rng_copy = jax.random.split(rng_key)\nparams_back = self.backbone.init(rng_back, dummy_input, training=True)\nparams_copy = self.copy_head.init(rng_copy, dummy_input)\nreturn {\"backbone\": params_back, \"copy\": params_copy}\n```\n\n**In `Wrapper.apply()` method:**\n```python\n# Before (WRONG):\ny_copy = self.copy_head(x)\n\n# After (CORRECT):\ny_copy = self.copy_head.apply(params[\"copy\"], x)\n```\n\
    \n## Key Changes\n1. Split the RNG key to provide separate randomness for backbone and copy head initialization\n2. Properly initialized the copy head module with `self.copy_head.init(rng_copy, dummy_input)`\n3. Stored copy head parameters in the returned dictionary\n4. Changed the apply call from `self.copy_head(x)` to `self.copy_head.apply(params[\"copy\"], x)`\n\n## Outcome\nThe code now runs without crashing. The evaluation is proceeding successfully with the fixed implementation.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\nimport optax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom models_fourier import FourierForecasterLNV3Generic\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead\nfrom losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self,\
    \ rank_k=320, proj_rank=36, num_harmonics=16, hidden_size=192, mlp_depth=2,\n                 gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.99, ln_in_factor=True):\n        self.backbone = FourierForecasterLNV3Generic(\n            rank_k=rank_k, proj_rank=proj_rank, num_harmonics=num_harmonics,\n            hidden_size=hidden_size, mlp_depth=mlp_depth,\n            gamma_start=gamma_start, gamma_end=gamma_end, ln_in_factor=ln_in_factor\n        )\n        self.copy_head = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=32)\n        self.needs_rng = False\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        import jax\n        rng_back, rng_copy = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n        params_back = self.backbone.init(rng_back, dummy_input, training=True)\n        params_copy = self.copy_head.init(rng_copy, dummy_input)\n        return {\"backbone\": params_back, \"copy\": params_copy}\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        y_factor = self.backbone.apply(params[\"backbone\"\
    ], x, training=training)\n        y_copy = self.copy_head.apply(params[\"copy\"], x)\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 9e-4,\n        \"rank_k\": 320,\n        \"proj_rank\": 36,\n        \"num_harmonics\": 16,\n        \"hidden_size\": 192,\n        \"mlp_depth\": 2,\n        \"gamma_start\": 0.25,\n        \"gamma_end\": 0.99,\n        \"ln_in_factor\": True\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return Wrapper(\n        rank_k=int(hparams.get(\"rank_k\", 320)),\n        proj_rank=int(hparams.get(\"proj_rank\", 36)),\n        num_harmonics=int(hparams.get(\"num_harmonics\", 16)),\n        hidden_size=int(hparams.get(\"hidden_size\", 192)),\n        mlp_depth=int(hparams.get(\"mlp_depth\", 2)),\n        gamma_start=float(hparams.get(\"gamma_start\", 0.25)),\n        gamma_end=float(hparams.get(\"gamma_end\", 0.99)),\n        ln_in_factor=bool(hparams.get(\"ln_in_factor\", True))\n    )\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions,\
    \ targets, params, x):\n    return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=9e-4, eps=1e-8)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\n\
