role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  class FourierForecasterLNScalarRamp(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Fourier forecaster (LN, scalar context) with gamma[t] ramp initialization.\n\n      - Factorized loadings U (N,p) and V (k,p)\n      - Amplitudes from per-factor scalar context c[b,k] = mean_t factors_in[b,t,k]\n      - LayerNorm across factor dim (k)\n      - Gamma[t] gate initialized via 0.25 -> 0.99 sigmoid-logit ramp\n      \"\"\"\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 36\n      num_harmonics: int = 16\n      hidden_size: int = 128\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n      ln_in_factor: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          T_out = 32\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n       \
    \   M = self.num_harmonics\n\n          # Factorized projections\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))   # (N,p)\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))   # (k,p)\n\n          # Encode: x -> p -> k\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)                         # (B,4,p)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)               # (B,4,k)\n\n          # Per-factor scalar context\n          c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)                              # (B,k)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(c[..., None])                  # (B,k,H)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          A = nn.Dense(2 * M)(h)                                        # (B,k,2M)\n\n          # Harmonic basis with learned per-factor frequencies\n          freq_raw = self.param('freq_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k, M))     # (k,M)\n          w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(freq_raw)                                    # (k,M) in [0,pi]\n  \
    \        t = jnp.arange(1, T_out + 1, dtype=x.dtype)[:, None, None]           # (T,1,1)\n          cos = jnp.cos(t * w[None, :, :])                                     # (T,k,M)\n          sin = jnp.sin(t * w[None, :, :])                                     # (T,k,M)\n          phi = jnp.concatenate([cos, sin], axis=2)                            # (T,k,2M)\n\n          # Latent factors\n          f_lat = jnp.einsum('bkd,tkd->btk', A, phi)                           # (B,T,k)\n          if self.ln_in_factor:\n              f_lat = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(f_lat)\n\n          # Gamma[t] ramp initialization (sigmoid logits)\n          def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              tt = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              g_sched = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * tt\n              return jnp.log(g_sched) - jnp.log(1.0 - g_sched)\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (T_out,))\n          gamma\
    \ = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]                         # (1,T,1)\n\n          f_out = gamma * f_lat                                                # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Decode k->p->N\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)                              # (B,T,p)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)                           # (B,T,N)\n          return y_factor\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Next immediate actions (after IDs 389/390 finish):\n  - Submit FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,M=16,H=128) with RC, Clip=1.0, lr=1e-3 and lr=9e-4 using storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py.\n  - If ramp baselines recover ~−0.02635–−0.02640, add amplitude-MLP dropout 0.05 (depth=1) as a single-variable ablation.\n  - Export gamma/frequency stats in complete() for best Fourier config.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Assessing performance updates**\n\nI need to focus on our recent exploration of the Fourier forecaster. The latest submissions show an improvement to -0.02780, but it's still not as good as the top Fourier SOTA at -0.026314. Our LN-SSM had -0.026768, while the MLP was at -0.026608. We submitted two baseline Fourier LN checks, and I'm considering next steps. There’s still some token budget left, and previous gating attempts didn't yield great results. Let's keep moving forward!**Exploring model improvements**\n\nI’m considering some adjustments we might make, like removing or tuning the LN position. I’m curious if our amplitude MLP with c[b,k] compared to f_flat is significant, especially since their SOTA uses latent normalization. There might be a missing constant ramp issue. I wonder if a potential bug could be affecting our base v2 and v3. Given our unusual decode pipeline, perhaps the training schedule difference is crucial. The Fourier SOTA by Logos seems interesting,\
  \ but I'm not sure about the details.**Planning minimal ablations**\n\nWith limited time, I propose running minimal ablations. For the base LN, removing it might degrade performance, but it could still be necessary for Fourier. I’m considering adding frequency dropout or regularization. Many improvements aren't in the current specifications, yet we can still export latents for debugging gamma and amplitude magnitude. I could replicate our previous best result, 344 at -0.026355. Surprisingly, our modifications seem to have hurt performance, suggesting that the simpler LN baseline might actually be better.**Reverting architecture and adjustments**\n\nI’m considering reverting to the 344 architecture and integrating SAP gating, focusing only on encoder gating U. The goal would be to set gates to near-binary saturation to maintain an effective p around 36, possibly with Pmax at 48, and applying L1 regularization to check performance. Gating has caused issues in the past, so I wonder if we\
  \ need to refine our training approach. Another thought is to analyze the poor performance in v3, as the amplitude MLP might be overfitting. I think adding a dropout of 0.05 could help!**Managing token usage and submissions**\n\nWe’re at 66% token usage, so I think it’s okay to explore MLP lines again, although the priority is still Fourier. Since we got close to SOTA with 344, I want to write an archive analysis on Fourier gating experiments. I have a plan: I’ll replicate 344 while adding complete() to export frequency distribution and gamma. I’m also considering adjusting gamma_end and increasing proj_rank to 38 for testing. My main goal is to create effective submissions without overloading the evaluation system.**Planning updates and submissions**\n\nIt might be best to wait for results to come in, which should happen in the next ticks. In the meantime, I can work on updating the stored models to fix the copy head initialization pattern issue. Our earlier setups had some bugs, so I\
  \ plan to enhance \"models_fourier.py\" as well. I’ll write an optional analysis note in private memory, but it's not essential. I’ll focus on preparing to submit a ramp version after the current submissions finish. \n\nThe next steps will be to write the new code and track our progress."
