role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FourierForecasterLN-RFFT (p=36, drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=1e-3\"\ntags: \"fourier, layernorm, factorized-loadings, replication, optimization, gradient-clipping\"\nabstract: \"Replicate the strong FourierForecasterLN (RFFT-based, p=36) and ablate dropout to 0.05 (vs 0.10) in both the frequency MLP and ResidualCopyHead. Optimizer: Adam lr=1e-3 with global clip=1.0. Loss: MAE + temporal curvature (λ=1e-4).\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from jax import random\n\n  # Residual copy head with parameterized dropout\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)         # (B*N, 4)\n          h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n      \
    \    h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n          residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)     # (B, 32, N)\n          out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N))\n          out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)                         # copy last 4\n          return out + residual\n\n  # FourierForecaster with RFFT pipeline and parameterized dropout\n  class FourierForecasterLN_RFFT(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 36\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n          # Loadings with column-normalized U\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          # RFFT on time dim\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)                       # (B,\
    \ T_in_freq, N)\n          x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))            # (B, N, T_in_freq)\n\n          # Project to factor space in frequency domain\n          factors_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bni,np->bip', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T  # (B, T_in_freq, k)\n\n          # Flatten real+imag and process with MLP\n          f_real = factors_in_fft.real\n          f_imag = factors_in_fft.imag\n          f_flat = jnp.concatenate([f_real, f_imag], axis=-1).reshape(B, -1)  # (B, 2*T_in_freq*k)\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n          # Predict frequency-domain outputs (complex) for T_out_freq bins\n          T_out = self.output_horizon\n          T_out_freq = T_out // 2 + 1\n          out_flat = nn.Dense(T_out_freq * k * 2)(h)            # real+imag\n          out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B,\
    \ T_out_freq, k, 2)\n          out_real, out_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n          factors_out_fft = out_real + 1j * out_imag            # (B, T_out_freq, k)\n\n          # LayerNorm separately on real/imag across k\n          norm_real = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft.real)\n          norm_imag = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft.imag)\n          f_fft_norm = norm_real + 1j * norm_imag               # (B, T_out_freq, k)\n\n          # Decode to neuron frequency domain and IFFT to time\n          y_fft = (f_fft_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T                    # (B, T_out_freq, N)\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)     # (B, 32, N)\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n          return y_fourier + y_copy\n\n  # API\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'drop': 0.05}\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n\
    \          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = FourierForecasterLN_RFFT(\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n              proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n              drop=hparams.get('drop', 0.05)\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = True  # for dropout\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      return mae\
    \ + 1e-4 * jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FourierForecasterLN-RFFT (p=36, drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4\"\ntags: \"fourier, layernorm, factorized-loadings, replication, optimization, gradient-clipping\"\nabstract: \"Same RFFT-based FourierForecasterLN (p=36) with reduced dropout (0.05) and a slightly lower Adam lr=9e-4 to test stability. Loss: MAE + temporal curvature (λ=1e-4); Clip=1.0.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from jax import random\n\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat);\
    \ h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n          residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N)); out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return out + residual\n\n  class FourierForecasterLN_RFFT(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 36\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n          x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))            # (B, N, T_in_freq)\n          factors_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bni,np->bip', x_fft_bn,\
    \ U_eff) @ V.T\n          f_flat = jnp.concatenate([factors_in_fft.real, factors_in_fft.imag], axis=-1).reshape(B, -1)\n\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n          T_out = self.output_horizon\n          T_out_freq = T_out // 2 + 1\n          out_flat = nn.Dense(T_out_freq * k * 2)(h)\n          out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, T_out_freq, k, 2)\n          out_real, out_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n          f_fft = out_real + 1j * out_imag\n\n          norm_real = nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real)\n          norm_imag = nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n          f_fft_n = norm_real + 1j * norm_imag\n\n          y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)\n\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n\
    \          return y_fourier + y_copy\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {'learning_rate': 9e-4, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'drop': 0.05}\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = FourierForecasterLN_RFFT(\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n              proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n              drop=hparams.get('drop', 0.05)\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = True\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params,\
    \ x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      return mae + 1e-4 * jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning submission details**


  I''m working on a submission using RFFT-based FourierRecon to match 344, adjusting the dropout to 0.05 and considering weight decay or AdamW, though AdamW didn’t help with the MLP before. I''m comparing Adam with learning rates of 0.001 and 0.0009. The token usage is currently at 75%, and I might prune additional ticks soon. I''m focused on crafting the submission ‘FourierForecasterLN (RFFT)’ with proper RNG for dropout and reusing the station mae_with_temporal_curvature if available.**Creating submission for FourierForecaster**


  I want to make the FourierForecaster consistent with other lines by importing losses.mae_with_temporal_curvature, although for matching 344 and staying close to SOTA, I''ll stick with manual curvature. I''ll adapt code from 361 for RFFT, adjusting the dropout to 0.05 and keeping the hidden dimension at 512. I''ll define two submissions: "FourierForecasterLN-RFFT (p=36, drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=1e-3" and another with lr=9e-4. I might also test dropout at 0.08, but I’ll prioritize 0.05 for now.**Writing submission code**


  I will start by defining the ResidualCopyHead similar to what''s in 361, but with a parameterized dropout rate. Then I’ll move on to create the FourierForecasterLN_RFFT, incorporating a dropout rate parameter for both the MLP and copy head. I’ll make sure to provide the create_network function with those values and use mae_with_temporal_curvature for compute_loss to stay consistent. I''ll ensure to follow 361’s wrapper pattern and include RNGs in the apply function as well. Time to compose!'
