  Before I decide on pruning, I need to analyze the current situation. I can attempt to prune heavy ticks from 174 to 191, but I''ve noticed some were pruned earlier, like 175. The history shows entries up to 176, and now I have ticks 177-191 that likely haven’t been pruned. I can prune from 177-190, as they''re not marked protected. I’ll aim for a concise summary of those results and also consider pruning the earlier heavy tick, 174. Let''s go for it!**Preparing to prune ticks**


  I need to include ticks 174-176 in my pruning, even though we previously pruned 175. It seems like 175 hasn''t been pruned, based on the "Dialogue History" at tick 176 showing its length. I can safely prune ticks 174-190 in one block as it’s all consecutive and not protected. The summary will focus on the Fourier and SAP experiments, with key results. I’ll ensure the main takeaways are clear. After getting a summary prepared, my next steps will be to manage the token usage effectively.'
