parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 193\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Ariadne I\n- Agent Description: An agent who navigates complexity with principled inquiry and empirical rigor.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNext immediate actions (after IDs 389/390 finish):\n- Submit FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,M=16,H=128) with RC, Clip=1.0, lr=1e-3 and lr=9e-4 using storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py.\n- If ramp baselines recover ~−0.02635–−0.02640, add amplitude-MLP dropout 0.05 (depth=1) as a single-variable ablation.\n- Export gamma/frequency stats in complete() for best Fourier config.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 93,705 / 270,000 used (35%)\n- Agent Age: 193 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 398**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** FourierForecasterLN-RFFT (p=36, drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4\n**ID:** 398\n**Tags:** fourier, layernorm, factorized-loadings, replication,\
    \ optimization, gradient-clipping\n**Abstract:** Same RFFT-based FourierForecasterLN (p=36) with reduced dropout (0.05) and a slightly lower Adam lr=9e-4 to test stability. Loss: MAE + temporal curvature (λ=1e-4); Clip=1.0.\n**Score:** -0.026355249540594736\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0196\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0228\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0254\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0274\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0282\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom jax import random\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n        residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0,\
    \ 2, 1)\n        out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N)); out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return out + residual\n\nclass FourierForecasterLN_RFFT(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 36\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))            # (B, N, T_in_freq)\n        factors_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bni,np->bip', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n        f_flat = jnp.concatenate([factors_in_fft.real, factors_in_fft.imag], axis=-1).reshape(B, -1)\n\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h,\
    \ deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n        T_out = self.output_horizon\n        T_out_freq = T_out // 2 + 1\n        out_flat = nn.Dense(T_out_freq * k * 2)(h)\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, T_out_freq, k, 2)\n        out_real, out_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft = out_real + 1j * out_imag\n\n        norm_real = nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real)\n        norm_imag = nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n        f_fft_n = norm_real + 1j * norm_imag\n\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)\n\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n        return y_fourier + y_copy\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {'learning_rate': 9e-4, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'drop': 0.05}\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n \
    \       self.model = FourierForecasterLN_RFFT(\n            rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n            proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n            drop=hparams.get('drop', 0.05)\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = True\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {})\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    return mae + 1e-4 * jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n     \
    \   optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from\
    \ submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 416959 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 416960\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'drop': 0.05}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n\
    \ Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.032471   |   0.029532  \n   2    |   0.029203   |   0.029336  \n   3    |   0.029007   |   0.029219  \n   4    |   0.028913   |   0.029346  \n   5    |   0.028865   |   0.029216  \n   6    |   0.028803   |   0.029217  \n   7    |   0.028728   |   0.028896  \n   8    |   0.028506   |   0.028566  \n   9    |   0.028173   |   0.028732  \n  10    |   0.027880   |   0.028327  \n  11    |   0.027681   |   0.027950  \n  12    |   0.027508   |   0.027834  \n  13    |   0.027312   |   0.027416  \n  14    |   0.027051   |   0.027260  \n  15    |   0.026728   |   0.027305  \n  16    |   0.026533   |   0.027047  \n  17    |   0.026304   |   0.026981  \n  18    |   0.026135   |   0.026945  \n  19    |   0.026048   |   0.027049  \n  20    |   0.025881   |   0.026786  \n  21    |   0.025792   |   0.026923  \n  22    |   0.025673   |   0.026671  \n  23    |   0.025597   |   0.026882  \n  24    |   0.025505\
