- text: "/execute_action{storage write ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import json, os\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)        # (B*N, 4)\n          h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(h)                                  # (B*N, 32)\n          residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)    # (B, 32, N)\n          out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n          out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)                        # copy last 4 steps\n          return out + residual\n\n  class FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n\
    \      proj_rank: int = 36\n      hidden_size: int = 128\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n      learn_gamma: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n          # Factorized loadings\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          # RFFT over time on inputs\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)                     # (B, F_in, N), F_in=3\n          x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))          # (B, N, F_in)\n          # Project to p then to k in frequency space: (B,F_in,k)\n          f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n\n          #\
    \ Build compact feature: concat real/imag, flatten freq and factors\n          f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)  # (B, F_in, 2k)\n          f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)                                     # (B, F_in*2k)\n\n          # Small head to map to output Fourier coefficients\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n          T_out = self.output_horizon\n          F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n          out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)                            # real+imag\n          out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n          f_fft_real, f_fft_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n          f_fft = f_fft_real + 1j * f_fft_imag                              # (B,F_out,k)\n\n          # LayerNorm on real/imag\
    \ separately (stabilizes scaling across factors/freqs)\n          f_fft_n = (\n              nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n          )                                                                 # (B,F_out,k)\n\n          # Decode back to neurons in frequency space: (B,F_out,N)\n          y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\n          # Inverse RFFT to time domain\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)                # (B,32,N)\n\n          # Scalar ramp gamma over horizon (fixed or learned)\n          if self.learn_gamma:\n              gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n              gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          else:\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              gamma = g[None, :, None]                                     # (1,32,1)\n\n          y_fourier\
    \ = gamma * y_fourier\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n          return y_copy + y_fourier\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n              rank_k=hparams.get('rank_k', 320),\n              proj_rank=hparams.get('proj_rank', 36),\n              hidden_size=hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n              drop=hparams.get('drop', 0.05),\n              gamma_start=hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25),\n              gamma_end=hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99),\n              learn_gamma=bool(hparams.get('learn_gamma', False))\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params,\
    \ x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=(rngs or {}))\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(hparams)\n\n  def export_stats(params, trial_data, hparams, out_dir=\"storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_ramp\"):\n      try:\n          os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n          # Extract U,V if present\n          p = params.get('params', params)\n          U = p.get('U', None)\n          V = p.get('V', None)\n          stats = {\n              'trial_number': trial_data.get('trial_number'),\n              'seed': trial_data.get('seed'),\n              'val_mae': float(trial_data.get('val_mae', -1.0)),\n              'hyperparameters': hparams,\n          }\n          if U is not None:\n              col_norms = jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0)\n              stats['U_col_norms_mean'] = float(jnp.mean(col_norms))\n              stats['U_col_norms_min'] = float(jnp.min(col_norms))\n              stats['U_col_norms_max']\
    \ = float(jnp.max(col_norms))\n          if V is not None:\n              G = V.T @ V\n              I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n              stats['V_gram_fro_error'] = float(jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2))\n\n          # Gamma profile (deterministic ramp from hparams)\n          T_out = 32\n          t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out)\n          g = hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25) + (hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99) - hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)) * t\n          stats['gamma_profile'] = [float(x) for x in g.tolist()]\n\n          out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, f\"trial_{trial_data.get('seed','na')}.json\")\n          with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(stats, f, indent=2)\n      except Exception as e:\n          # Best-effort; do not crash training completion\n          pass\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=128,drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=1e-3\"\ntags: \"fourier, layernorm, factorized-loadings, scalar-ramp, residual-copy,\
    \ replication, gradient-clipping\"\nabstract: \"RFFT-based Fourier forecaster with LayerNorm on real/imag, residual copy head, and a fixed scalar ramp γ over horizon (0.25→0.99). Small head H=128. Tests if ramp baseline can match LN-RFFT results at lr=1e-3.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from models_fourier_ramp import create_network, export_stats\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 1e-3,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 36,\n          'hidden_size': 128,\n          'drop': 0.05,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'learn_gamma': False\n      }\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      return mae + 1e-4 * jnp.mean(curv\
    \ * curv)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      export_stats(params, trial_data, _define_hyperparameters())\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=128,drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4\"\ntags: \"fourier, layernorm, factorized-loadings, scalar-ramp, residual-copy, replication, gradient-clipping\"\nabstract: \"Same as the lr=1e-3 ScalarRamp but with a slightly lower Adam lr=9e-4 to test stability. Exports γ profile and U/V stats in complete().\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from models_fourier_ramp import create_network, export_stats\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n          'rank_k':\
    \ 320,\n          'proj_rank': 36,\n          'hidden_size': 128,\n          'drop': 0.05,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'learn_gamma': False\n      }\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      return mae + 1e-4 * jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      export_stats(params, trial_data, _define_hyperparameters())\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating ramp baselines**


  I''m reflecting on previous results regarding ramp baselines, which seem poor. I wonder if they might improve with a corrected pipeline. However, past results consistently indicate that the ramp isn''t effective. The plan suggests submitting the FF-LN ScalarRamp after working on specific tasks. But should we adapt the plan based on those negative results? I must consider how to manage submission cooldown while ensuring we can submit two experiments if needed and create the required model if it doesn''t exist yet.**Planning gamma and frequency analysis**


  I''m considering exporting gamma and frequency statistics in the complete function. I’ll provide code to compute the gamma schedule and top frequency contributions and store results appropriately. The system allows storage writes, so that’s good to know! With the complexity, a minimal model and complete hook might work. Alternatively, I’m thinking of adding amplitude-MLP dropout as an ablation, but only if the ramp baselines improve. Replicating Logos 369 could help me get to SOTA, so I’ll aim for small, incremental changes where possible.**Planning Fourier Forecaster**


  The request from the user isn''t very specific—they haven''t asked to go anywhere, but I can submit new experiments at Research Counter. I should also think about archiving results or updating papers. I can implement the complete function for the Fourier Forecaster LN to export gamma and frequency stats, which seems beneficial. For actions, I''ll write storage for the model code, implementing a Fourier Forecaster with a scalar ramp. This involves using predicted Fourier coefficients and applying gamma gating across the horizon.**Exploring scalar ramp implementation**


  I’m considering that the scalar ramp baseline they tested likely mixed copy with predicted elements, resulting in poor outcomes around -0.02865. To keep things efficient with tokens and time, I can implement an alternative. I’d retain the RFFT LN with the same amplitude MLP while adding a learned global scalar ramp function, which gradually increases the predicted component. I’ll run two learning rates, but it’s essential to follow the plan. While I’m at it, I can implement the complete function to dump gamma and frequency energy into storage.**Implementing models and storage**


  I see that the system allows persistent storage, so I can use Python’s file I/O to write code to ''storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py''. This will include the ResidualCopyHead with dropout and set up the FourierForecasterLN_RFFT_Ramp, utilizing a straightforward linear output head. I''ll apply a gamma ramp through time-domain gating, ensuring parameters are adjustable. I''ll also implement the complete function to compute gamma schedules and frequency energy, writing the results in JSON format. Finally, I’ll submit two evaluations with different learning rates while managing the concurrency and storage effectively.**Addressing potential pitfalls**


