tick: 194
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write ariadne/models_fourier_ramp_amp.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import json, os\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)        # (B*N, 4)\n          h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(h)                                  # (B*N, 32)\n          residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)    # (B, 32, N)\n          out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n          out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)                        # copy last 4 steps\n          return out + residual\n\n  class FourierForecasterLN_RampAmp(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n\
    \      RFFT-based Fourier forecaster with:\n        - Factorized loadings U (N×p), V (k×p); U column-normalized\n        - LayerNorm on real/imag of predicted Fourier coeffs\n        - Fixed scalar ramp gamma[t] over horizon\n        - Amplitude MLP producing per-(freq, factor) gate in (0.5, 1.5)\n      \"\"\"\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 36\n      hidden_size: int = 128       # head size\n      amp_hidden: int = 128        # amplitude MLP hidden size\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n      learn_gamma: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n          # Factorized loadings\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n         \
    \ U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          # RFFT over time on inputs\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)                     # (B, F_in, N), F_in=3\n          x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))          # (B, N, F_in)\n          # Project to p then to k in frequency space: (B,F_in,k)\n          f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T  # (B,F_in,k)\n\n          # Features for heads: concat real/imag, flatten freq and factors\n          f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)  # (B,F_in,2k)\n          f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)                                     # (B, F_in*2k)\n\n          # Main head to predict output Fourier coefficients\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not\
    \ training)\n\n          T_out = self.output_horizon\n          F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n          out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)                            # real+imag\n          out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n          f_fft_real, f_fft_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n          f_fft = f_fft_real + 1j * f_fft_imag                              # (B,F_out,k)\n\n          # Amplitude MLP: produce per-(freq, factor) gate in (0.5, 1.5)\n          ah = nn.Dense(self.amp_hidden)(f_flat); ah = nn.relu(ah)\n          ah = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(ah, deterministic=not training)\n          amp_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k)(ah)                                # (B, F_out*k)\n          amp = nn.sigmoid(amp_flat).reshape(B, F_out, k)\n          amp = 0.5 + amp                                                   # (0.5, 1.5)\n\n          # LayerNorm on real/imag separately (stabilizes scaling across factors/freqs)\n          f_fft_n = nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n\
    \          f_fft_n = amp * f_fft_n                                           # apply amplitude gate\n\n          # Decode back to neurons in frequency space: (B,F_out,N)\n          y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\n          # Inverse RFFT to time domain\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)                # (B,32,N)\n\n          # Scalar ramp gamma over horizon (fixed or learned)\n          if self.learn_gamma:\n              gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n              gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          else:\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              gamma = g[None, :, None]                                     # (1,32,1)\n\n          y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n      \
    \    return y_copy + y_fourier\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = FourierForecasterLN_RampAmp(\n              rank_k=hparams.get('rank_k', 320),\n              proj_rank=hparams.get('proj_rank', 36),\n              hidden_size=hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n              amp_hidden=hparams.get('amp_hidden', 128),\n              drop=hparams.get('drop', 0.05),\n              gamma_start=hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25),\n              gamma_end=hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99),\n              learn_gamma=bool(hparams.get('learn_gamma', False))\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params,\
    \ x, training=training, rngs=(rngs or {}))\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(hparams)\n\n  def export_stats(params, trial_data, hparams, out_dir=\"storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_ramp_amp\"):\n      try:\n          os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n          # Extract U,V if present\n          p = params.get('params', params)\n          U = p.get('U', None)\n          V = p.get('V', None)\n          stats = {\n              'trial_number': trial_data.get('trial_number'),\n              'seed': trial_data.get('seed'),\n              'val_mae': float(trial_data.get('val_mae', -1.0)),\n              'hyperparameters': hparams,\n          }\n          if U is not None:\n              col_norms = jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0)\n              stats['U_col_norms_mean'] = float(jnp.mean(col_norms))\n              stats['U_col_norms_min'] = float(jnp.min(col_norms))\n              stats['U_col_norms_max'] = float(jnp.max(col_norms))\n          if V is not None:\n       \
    \       G = V.T @ V\n              I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n              stats['V_gram_fro_error'] = float(jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2))\n\n          # Gamma profile (deterministic ramp from hparams)\n          T_out = 32\n          t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out)\n          g = hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25) + (hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99) - hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)) * t\n          stats['gamma_profile'] = [float(x) for x in g.tolist()]\n\n          out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, f\"trial_{trial_data.get('seed','na')}.json\")\n          with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(stats, f, indent=2)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to respond with careful actions and planning. Recently, our FourierForecasterLN-RFFT replication achieved a result of -0.026355, which matches our earlier work. Aether improved with -0.026272, surpassing previous benchmarks. The immediate next actions involve submitting ScalarRamp baselines and setting up an amplitude-MLP dropout ablation if our ramp baseline recovers well. We've already submitted a couple of ScalarRamp versions that are currently running. I'll plan additional tests while managing our tokens, which are at a good level after pruning.**Assessing next actions**\n\nI might consider adding 'complete' to our LN-RFFT run to help export gamma/frequency data, but we already have that in ramp models. I could suggest creating a small analysis script to compute frequency contributions, though it’s not really necessary. Previewing everything in the Archive might give us insights, but I need to be mindful of token usage. Additionally,\
  \ I should hold off on any heavy experiments until our current ones finish. I can draft code for amplitude-MLP ablation but won’t submit it yet.**Preparing amplitude-MLP code**\n\nIt's good to prepare and store the amplitude-MLP variant code. The plan is to implement amplitude-MLP gating after computing f_in_fft features. This will produce an amplitude gate from earlier features and use a small MLP that incorporates context from x. I realize that adding this MLP will change invariances, but that’s okay. Also, I must ensure that any titles using colons are quoted, as we did previously. \n\nProposed next actions include writing the storage file for the amplitude-MLP variant while keeping an eye on the pending count, as we can’t exceed two experiments running at the same time.**Managing experiments and tokens**\n\nLooking at the running experiments, I see that only 403 and 404 are pending, so no more submissions can happen right now. However, I can prepare the code in the meantime. I could\
  \ also go to the archive to preview all entries, which might help, but I need to be cautious since tokens are at 35%—that’s still safe. The preview may bring up too much text, so I'll keep exposure minimal. \n\nAlternatively, I could manage tokens and prune some, but I need to confirm the cooldown state, which seems to be at a good point now.**Finalizing amplitude-MLP code**\n\nSince we’re at tick 194 and the cooldown from tick 191 is almost over, we can prepare our actions. Once we get results from experiments 403 and 404, I’ll compare them to 398 and 344 to see if we should queue the amplitude-MLP variant with dropout 0.05 or adjust F_out. I’ll write the storage file for the amplitude gating code and create a note in Private Memory summarizing our plans. I’ll ensure the code, particularly for the activation functions, aligns with the previous structure while keeping everything well-commented. For now, we’ll write the code but won't submit it just yet."
