- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 207\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Ariadne I\n- Agent Description: An agent who navigates complexity with principled inquiry and empirical rigor.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNext immediate actions (after IDs 389/390 finish):\n- Submit FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,M=16,H=128) with RC, Clip=1.0, lr=1e-3 and lr=9e-4 using storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py.\n- If ramp baselines recover ~−0.02635–−0.02640, add amplitude-MLP dropout 0.05 (depth=1) as a single-variable ablation.\n- Export gamma/frequency stats in complete() for best Fourier config.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 188,705 / 270,000 used (70%)\n- Agent Age: 207 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'FactGlobalMLP-LN + ScalarRampFirst4 (p=32, H=512x2, dr=0.10) + Adam(lr=1e-3), Clip=1.0' (ID: 427) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.026811189640188318\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0199\n\
    **Val_MAE_4:** 0.0232\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0259\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0279\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0285\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 427\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed AttributeError in optimizer creation. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission attempted to call `create_optimizer.__wrapped__()` to access the imported function from the lineage module, but regular Python functions don't have a `__wrapped__` attribute. This attribute only exists on decorated functions using `functools.wraps`.\n\nThe problematic code was:\n```python\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    # Adam, no weight decay\n    return create_optimizer.__wrapped__(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=None)\n```\n\nThe agent was trying to override the `create_optimizer` function by calling the original imported version, but the function shadowing and incorrect\
    \ attribute access caused an `AttributeError: 'function' object has no attribute '__wrapped__'`.\n\n## Fix Applied\n**File**: `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n\nThe solution was to use Python's import aliasing to avoid function name shadowing:\n\n```python\nfrom submissions.mlp_scalar_ramp_first4 import (\n    _define_hyperparameters, create_network, compute_loss,\n    create_optimizer as base_create_optimizer  # ← Aliased import\n)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    # Adam, no weight decay - call the imported function with weight_decay=None\n    return base_create_optimizer(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=None)\n```\n\n**Key changes**:\n1. Imported `create_optimizer` as `base_create_optimizer` to avoid name collision\n2. Called `base_create_optimizer()` directly instead of trying to access a non-existent `__wrapped__` attribute\n3. Maintained the same functionality - passing `weight_decay=None` to use Adam instead of AdamW\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor\
    \ script confirmed the fix was successful:\n- **Runtime**: Code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- **Exit code**: 0 (success)\n- **Status**: The evaluation is processing normally (just takes time to complete training)\n\nThe fix resolved the immediate AttributeError and allows the training to proceed as intended.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\nfrom submissions.mlp_scalar_ramp_first4 import (\n    _define_hyperparameters, create_network, compute_loss, create_optimizer as base_create_optimizer\n)\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    # Adam, no weight decay - call the imported function with weight_decay=None\n    return base_create_optimizer(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=None)\n\n```\n\n**Full\
    \ Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n\
    \  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 44\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'hidden_size': 512, 'hidden_size2': 512, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'normalize_u': True, 'gamma_start': 0.25, 'gamma_end': 0.99}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch\
