parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{update 11-1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (MLP “First4” variant) — Tick 207\n  We tested whether preserving the early RC-anchored steps (t=1..4) resolves the negative generalization on the MLP backbone by applying ScalarRamp only for t≥4:\n  - MLP + ScalarRampFirst4 (p=32, 512×2, dr=0.10, Clip=1.0)\n    • ID 426 (AdamW wd=1e−4): −0.026919\n    • ID 427 (Adam, lr=1e−3): −0.026811\n  These are slightly better than the naive all-steps ramp (ID 418: −0.026890; ID 419: −0.027007) but still worse than strong MLP baselines without ramp (e.g., ID 247: −0.026645). Conclusion: even with early-step preservation, the fixed ScalarRamp does not help the factorized MLP backbone.\n  \n  Current synthesis across backbones:\n  - Fourier (LN-RFFT): ScalarRamp helps and sets SOTA (ID 411: −0.026269).\n  - MLP (factorized): ScalarRamp hurts (naive and First4).\n  - LN-SSM: ScalarRamp hurts (ID 424: −0.027316 vs best −0.026768).\n  \n  Next: Test a learnable\
    \ γ[t] on MLP initialized to the fixed ramp with weak priors (ramp closeness + smoothness), letting the model discover if/where temporal modulation is helpful.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write ariadne/submissions/mlp_learn_gamma.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import jax.nn as jnn\n  from flax import linen as nn\n\n  # Base factorized MLP forecaster (with RC + LN inside)\n  from models_mlp_global import create_network as base_create_network\n  from models_mlp_global import _define_hyperparameters as base_def_hparams\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  class MLPWithLearnableGamma:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrap the base factorized Global MLP forecaster and apply a learnable\n      horizon ramp gamma[t] over the 32-step horizon. gamma[t] is a sigmoid of\n      unconstrained parameters gamma_raw[t], initialized near a fixed ramp\n      (0.25 ->\
    \ 0.99). We add weak priors encouraging closeness to the ramp\n      and smoothness along t but allow adaptation.\n      \"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.99, base_hparams=None):\n          self.base = base_create_network(base_hparams or {})\n          self.gamma_start = float(gamma_start)\n          self.gamma_end = float(gamma_end)\n          # propagate RNG need (dropout)\n          self.needs_rng = getattr(self.base, 'needs_rng', True)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          # Initialize base params\n          variables = self.base.init(rng_key, dummy_input)\n          # Add learnable gamma_raw at top-level 'params'\n          # We assume base.init returns a FrozenDict {'params': ...}\n          params = variables['params'].unfreeze()\n          # Initialize gamma_raw so that sigmoid(gamma_raw) ≈ ramp(0.25->0.99)\n          T_out = dummy_input.shape[1] * 8  # dummy_input likely (B,4,N); we need 32\n          T_out = 32  # Explicit\n\
    \          t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=jnp.float32)\n          g_ramp = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n          # inverse sigmoid\n          eps = 1e-6\n          g_ramp = jnp.clip(g_ramp, eps, 1 - eps)\n          gamma_raw_init = jnp.log(g_ramp) - jnp.log1p(-g_ramp)\n          params['gamma_raw'] = gamma_raw_init\n          from flax.core import FrozenDict\n          return FrozenDict({'params': params})\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          y = self.base.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs)\n          # y: (B, 32, N)\n          gamma = jnn.sigmoid(params['params']['gamma_raw'])  # (32,)\n          return y * gamma[None, :, None]\n\n  # Hyperparameters and priors\n  LAM_PRIOR = 5e-5\n  LAM_SMOOTH = 1e-5\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      hp = base_def_hparams()\n      hp['proj_rank'] = 32\n      hp['dropout_rate'] = 0.10\n      hp['gamma_start'] = 0.25\n  \
    \    hp['gamma_end'] = 0.99\n      hp['learning_rate'] = 1e-3\n      return hp\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      base_hp = base_def_hparams()\n      base_hp['proj_rank'] = int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32))\n      base_hp['dropout_rate'] = float(hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.10))\n      return MLPWithLearnableGamma(\n          gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n          gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n          base_hparams=base_hp\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      # Base MAE + curvature penalty\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n      # Priors on gamma[t]\n      try:\n          gamma_raw = params['params']['gamma_raw']\n          T_out = predictions.shape[1]\n          t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=gamma_raw.dtype)\n          g_ramp = 0.25 + (0.99 - 0.25) * t\n          gamma = jnn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)\n          prior = LAM_PRIOR * jnp.mean((gamma\
    \ - g_ramp) ** 2)\n          smooth = LAM_SMOOTH * jnp.mean(jnp.diff(gamma) ** 2)\n          return base + prior + smooth\n      except Exception:\n          return base\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float | None = None):\n      chain = [optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0)]\n      if weight_decay is None:\n          chain.append(optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8))\n      else:\n          chain.append(optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay))\n      return optax.chain(*chain)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FactGlobalMLP-LN + LearnableGamma (p=32, H=512x2, dr=0.10) + AdamW(wd=1e-4), Clip=1.0\"\ntags: \"mlp, layernorm, factorized-loadings, residual-copy, scalar-ramp, learnable\"\nabstract: \"MLP generalization with a learnable horizon ramp γ[t] initialized to 0.25→0.99, with weak priors for ramp closeness and smoothness. Base: p=32, H=512×2, dr=0.10, AdamW\
    \ wd=1e−4, clip=1.0. Loss: MAE+curvature (λ=1e−4) + priors.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  from submissions.mlp_learn_gamma import (\n      _define_hyperparameters, create_network, compute_loss, create_optimizer\n  )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      # AdamW wd=1e-4\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FactGlobalMLP-LN + LearnableGamma (p=32, H=512x2, dr=0.10) + Adam(lr=1e-3), Clip=1.0\"\ntags: \"mlp, layernorm, factorized-loadings, residual-copy, scalar-ramp, learnable\"\nabstract: \"Same learnable γ[t] as above but with Adam (no weight decay), lr=1e−3. Tests optimizer sensitivity for the learnable ramp on MLP.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  from submissions.mlp_learn_gamma import (\n      _define_hyperparameters, create_network, compute_loss,\
    \ create_optimizer\n  )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      # Adam, no weight decay\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=None)\n```"
