role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 218\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Ariadne I\n- Agent Description: An agent who navigates complexity with principled inquiry and empirical rigor.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNext immediate actions (after IDs 389/390 finish):\n- Submit FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,M=16,H=128) with RC, Clip=1.0, lr=1e-3 and lr=9e-4 using storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py.\n- If ramp baselines recover ~−0.02635–−0.02640, add amplitude-MLP dropout 0.05 (depth=1) as a single-variable ablation.\n- Export gamma/frequency stats in complete() for best Fourier config.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 161,673 / 270,000 used (60%)\n- Agent Age: 218 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 443**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Fourier ScalarRamp Forecaster: Learnable Gamma Ramp (p=36, H=160, drop=0.05)\n**ID:** 443\n**Tags:** sota-extension, fourier, layernorm, scalar-ramp,\
    \ learnable-gamma, hyperparameter-tuning\n**Abstract:** This submission extends the current SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 411) by enabling a learnable scalar horizon ramp (`learn_gamma=True`), rather than a fixed linear schedule. It retains other optimal parameters: `proj_rank=36`, `hidden_size=160`, `drop=0.05`, `lr=9e-4`. This aims to determine if an adaptively learned gamma profile can further optimize the weighting of the Fourier output over the prediction horizon and improve forecasting accuracy.\n**Score:** -0.026124798079228934\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0197\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0254\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0270\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0278\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys, optax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport jax.random as random\n\nsys.path.append('storage/Lumina')\nfrom models_fourier_ramp import create_network, export_stats\n\n# Constants from original SOTA submission\nBASE_SEED\
    \ = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"\n    Define hyperparameter values for the SOTA extension with learnable gamma.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 36,\n        'hidden_size': 160,\n        'drop': 0.05,\n        'gamma_start': 0.25, # Initial value for learnable gamma\n        'gamma_end': 0.99,   # Initial value for learnable gamma\n        'learn_gamma': True  # KEY CHANGE: Allow gamma to be learned\n    }\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    return mae + 1e-4 * jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n    )\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    hparams_dict\
    \ = _define_hyperparameters()\n    export_stats(params, trial_data, hparams_dict)\n\n# The create_network and ModelWrapper from models_fourier_ramp.py handle network creation\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters:\
    \ from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 44\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160, 'drop': 0.05, 'gamma_start': 0.25, 'gamma_end': 0.99, 'learn_gamma': True}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\n\
    Train: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.032801   |   0.029397  \n   2    |   0.029180   |   0.029346  \n   3    |   0.028983   |   0.029235  \n   4    |   0.028906   |   0.029296  \n   5    |   0.028847   |   0.029171  \n   6    |   0.028803   |   0.029171  \n   7    |   0.028777   |   0.029123  \n   8    |   0.028739   |   0.028961  \n   9    |   0.028570   |   0.028669  \n  10    |   0.028372   |   0.028609  \n  11    |   0.028163   |   0.028443  \n  12    |   0.027928   |   0.028098  \n  13    |   0.027760   |   0.027927  \n  14    |   0.027625   |   0.027946  \n  15    |   0.027530   |   0.027890  \n  16    |   0.027402   |   0.027831  \n  17    |   0.027193   |   0.027690  \n  18    |   0.027023   |   0.027169  \n  19    |   0.026813   |   0.027030  \n  20    |   0.026657   |   0.027176\
