- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 230\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Ariadne I\n- Agent Description: An agent who navigates complexity with principled inquiry and empirical rigor.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNext immediate actions (after IDs 389/390 finish):\n- Submit FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,M=16,H=128) with RC, Clip=1.0, lr=1e-3 and lr=9e-4 using storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py.\n- If ramp baselines recover ~−0.02635–−0.02640, add amplitude-MLP dropout 0.05 (depth=1) as a single-variable ablation.\n- Export gamma/frequency stats in complete() for best Fourier config.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 130,434 / 270,000 used (48%)\n- Agent Age: 230 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Learnable Horizon Weights for Fourier LN Forecasters: Data-Adaptive γ[t] Sets New SOTA on ZAPBench' was not accepted for publication. Score: 4/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\n\
    This paper is rejected for failing to meet the generalization requirement (3.4). While the submission is otherwise of high quality—presenting a new SOTA with a simple and effective method, supported by an extensive suite of experiments—this single failure is critical. The proposed 'learnable gamma' method is only ever tested on the Fourier Forecaster backbone. To be accepted, a new method must be validated in at least two distinct architectural settings to demonstrate that its benefits are not just an artifact of one specific model. This is especially important given the author's own prior work (Archive #11) showing that the fixed ramp failed to generalize.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo make this paper publishable, you must perform a generalization study. The path is straightforward: apply your `learnable gamma` method to a different, high-performing architectural family, such as one of the strong factorized MLP models from Aether I (Archive #6) or Episteme I (Archive #7).\
    \ Reporting the results of this experiment—whether positive, negative, or null—would satisfy the generalization requirement and make this a complete and publishable contribution.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History\
    \ (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Learnable Horizon Weights for Fourier LN Forecasters: Data-Adaptive γ[t] Sets New SOTA on ZAPBench' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 11 | Fourier ScalarRamp Forecaster: Simple Horizon Gating Sets SOTA and Fails to Generalize to MLP (Ablation Study) | Ariadne I | Tick 203 | 747 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Global SOTA: The Fourier Forecaster, a Hybrid Time-Frequency Domain Model | Episteme I | Tick 172 | 724 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 9 | Spectrum-Adaptive Projection (SAP): Learnable Projection Rank for Factorized Neural Forecasters on ZAPBench\
    \ | Ariadne I | Tick 170 | 510 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Mixture of Factor Loadings (MoFL): A Spatially-Gated Architecture for Neural Forecasting | Logos I | Tick 159 | 791 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a State-of-the-Art Factorized Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 142 | 877 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 6 | Global SOTA: Disentangling the Contributions of Deeper Factor-Space MLP and Gradient Clipping for Enhanced Neural Forecasting | Aether I | Tick 133 | 3259 | 10 | (10 unread) |\n| 5 | Veritas I: Advancing ZAPBench Forecasting with Factorized SSMs and Contextual Modulation | Veritas I | Tick 109 | 1975 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Enhanced SOTA: Factorized MLP with Residual Copy, LayerNorm, and Optimized Temporal Curvature Loss | Aether I | Tick 101 | 954 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | A Spatially-Aware Mixture of Experts Framework for High-Dimensional Neural Forecasting | Logos I | Tick 100 | 836 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 2 | A Parsimonious Path to State-of-the-Art\
    \ Neural Forecasting | Episteme I | Tick 72 | 720 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
