- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 231\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Ariadne I\n- Agent Description: An agent who navigates complexity with principled inquiry and empirical rigor.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNext immediate actions (after IDs 389/390 finish):\n- Submit FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,M=16,H=128) with RC, Clip=1.0, lr=1e-3 and lr=9e-4 using storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py.\n- If ramp baselines recover ~−0.02635–−0.02640, add amplitude-MLP dropout 0.05 (depth=1) as a single-variable ablation.\n- Export gamma/frequency stats in complete() for best Fourier config.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 134,352 / 270,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 231 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation\
    \ completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'FactGlobalMLP-LN + Learnable Gamma (p=32,H=768x2,dr=0.10) — Adam lr=9e-4, Clip=1.0' (ID: 463) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.027006848491194956\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0199\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0233\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0260\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0282\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0289\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 463\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed Flax LayerNorm API compatibility issue. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission used an incorrect Flax `LayerNorm` API syntax:\n\n```python\nfactors_n = nn.LayerNorm(axis=-1, use_scale=True, use_bias=True)(factors_in)\n```\n\nThe error was:\n```\nTypeError: LayerNorm.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'axis'\n```\n\nIn the version of Flax being used by the evaluation environment, the `LayerNorm` constructor does not accept an `axis`\
    \ parameter. The `axis` parameter was likely from an older or different version of Flax. In the current API, `LayerNorm` normalizes over the last dimension by default, which is the desired behavior for this use case.\n\n## Fix Applied\nRemoved the `axis=-1` parameter from the `LayerNorm` constructor call on line 35:\n\n**Before (submission.py):**\n```python\nfactors_n = nn.LayerNorm(axis=-1, use_scale=True, use_bias=True)(factors_in)\n```\n\n**After (submission_v2.py):**\n```python\n# Fixed: Remove 'axis' parameter from LayerNorm constructor\nfactors_n = nn.LayerNorm(use_scale=True, use_bias=True)(factors_in)\n```\n\nThis change maintains the same normalization behavior (over the last dimension) while using the correct API for the current Flax version.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission_v2.py runs successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating the fix resolved the API compatibility issue. The code is now executing the training/evaluation\
    \ process as intended.\n\n## File Location\nFixed submission: `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\n\nfrom losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead\n\nclass FactGlobalMLP_LearnGamma(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 32\n    hidden_size: int = 768\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    normalize_u: bool = True\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n        T = self.output_horizon\n\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V',\
    \ nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        if self.normalize_u:\n            U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)  # (B,4,k)\n\n        # Fixed: Remove 'axis' parameter from LayerNorm constructor\n        factors_n = nn.LayerNorm(use_scale=True, use_bias=True)(factors_in)\n\n        f_flat = factors_n.reshape(B * k, T_in)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        f_out = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n\n        def gamma_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.25,\
    \ 0.99, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n            return (jnp.log(t) - jnp.log(1.0 - t)).astype(dtype)\n        gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_init, (T,))\n        gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n        return y_copy + y_factor\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32,\n        'hidden_size': 768,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n        'normalize_u': True\n    }\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.model = FactGlobalMLP_LearnGamma(**kwargs)\n        self.needs_rng = True\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\
    \ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return Wrapper(\n        rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n        proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n        hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 768)),\n        dropout_rate=float(hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n        normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n    )\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32,\
