    \nTraining completed in 1824.3s\nBest validation MAE: 0.027071\n\nTrial 2 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.027071\nTraining time: 1833s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 0db06ad7-f088-44c3-9a8d-082f30acbce1\nTotal time: 1837s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-26 20:37:35,077\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761482255077494142\n2025-10-26 20:37:35,108\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761482255108448350\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'FactGlobalMLP-LN + Learnable Gamma (p=32,H=512x2,dr=0.10) — Adam lr=9e-4, Clip=1.0' (ID: 462) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.027031123206824468\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0199\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0232\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0260\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0282\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0290\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:**\
    \ # Debug Report for Evaluation 462\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed Flax API incompatibility. The code is now running without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission used an incorrect Flax API call for LayerNorm. The code attempted to pass an `axis` parameter:\n\n```python\nln = nn.LayerNorm(axis=-1, use_scale=True, use_bias=True)\n```\n\nThis is incompatible with the current version of Flax. The error message was:\n```\nTypeError: LayerNorm.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'axis'\n```\n\nIn modern Flax, `LayerNorm` does not accept an `axis` parameter. Instead, it always normalizes over the last dimension by default, which is exactly the behavior needed in this case.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line 40 in submission_v2.py from:\n```python\nln = nn.LayerNorm(axis=-1, use_scale=True, use_bias=True)\n```\n\nTo:\n```python\nln = nn.LayerNorm()\n```\n\nThis simplified call is the correct Flax API usage. Since the input tensor `factors_in` has shape `(B, 4, k)` where\
    \ the last dimension `k` is the factor dimension, the default LayerNorm behavior (normalizing over the last dimension) is exactly what was intended.\n\n## Additional Notes\n- The imported functions from the lineage storage (`mae_with_temporal_curvature` from `losses.py` and `ResidualCopyHead` from `models.py`) were correctly implemented and did not require any fixes.\n- The fix was verified by the monitoring script, which confirmed the code ran for over 300 seconds without crashing.\n- The evaluation is still running (training can take significant time), but the absence of crashes indicates the fix was successful.\n\n## Files Modified\n- Created: `submissions/submission_v2.py` (fixed version)\n- Original: Evaluation 462 submission contained the Flax API bug\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\
    \nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\n\nfrom losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead  # residual copy head (tested earlier)\n\nclass FactGlobalMLP_LearnGamma(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 32\n    hidden_size: int = 512\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    normalize_u: bool = True\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n        T = self.output_horizon\n\n        # Factorized loadings: U (N,p), V (k,p)\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        if self.normalize_u:\n            U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        # Project inputs to factor space\n        # (B,4,N) @ (N,p) -> (B,4,p);\
    \ then (B,4,p) @ (p,k) -> (B,4,k)\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)  # (B,4,k)\n\n        # LayerNorm over factor dim (normalizes over last dimension by default)\n        ln = nn.LayerNorm()\n        factors_n = ln(factors_in)  # (B,4,k)\n\n        # Per-factor MLP over 4-step context -> 32-step forecast\n        f_flat = factors_n.reshape(B * k, T_in)      # (B*k, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        f_out = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)   # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Decode back to neurons via factorized loadings: z=(B,T,p), y=(B,T,N)\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n\n        # Learnable per-horizon\
    \ weights γ[t] in (0,1)\n        def gamma_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            # initialize near a mild ramp 0.25->0.99 for stability\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.25, 0.99, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n            logits = jnp.log(t) - jnp.log(1.0 - t)\n            return logits.astype(dtype)\n        gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_init, (T,))\n        gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]  # (1,T,1)\n        y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n        # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n        return y_copy + y_factor  # (B,T,N)\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32,\n        'hidden_size': 512,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n        'normalize_u': True\n    }\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.model = FactGlobalMLP_LearnGamma(**kwargs)\n        self.needs_rng\
    \ = True  # for Dropout\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        # Pass dropout rng if provided\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return Wrapper(\n        rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n        proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n        hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 512)),\n        dropout_rate=float(hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n        normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n    )\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n    )\n\
    \n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED:\
    \ 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 43\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'hidden_size': 512, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'normalize_u': True}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n\
