tick: 232
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FactGlobalMLP-NoRC + Learnable Gamma (p=32,H=512x2,dr=0.10) — Adam lr=9e-4, Clip=1.0\"\ntags: \"mlp, no-residual-copy, layernorm, factorized-loadings, learnable-gamma, generalization\"\nabstract: \"Generalization study per reviewer: remove residual copy (RC) from the Factorized Global MLP + LN backbone and add learnable per-horizon γ[t]. Config: p=32, H=512×2, dr=0.10, Adam lr=9e−4, clip=1.0, curvature λ=1e−4, 60‑min trials. Tests if γ helps when RC is absent.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  class FactGlobalMLP_NoRC_LearnGamma(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_size: int = 512\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n          T = self.output_horizon\n\n          # Factorized loadings\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          # Project to factor space\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)           # (B,4,p)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T) # (B,4,k)\n\n          # LayerNorm over factor dim (last dim)\n          factors_n = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_in)          # (B,4,k)\n\n          # Per-factor MLP: 4 -> H -> H -> 32\n          f_flat = factors_n.reshape(B * k, T_in)         # (B*k,4)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h,\
    \ deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          f_out = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          # Decode back to neurons\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)         # (B,T,p)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)      # (B,T,N)\n\n          # Learnable per-horizon weights γ[t] in (0,1)\n          def gamma_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.25, 0.99, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              return (jnp.log(t) - jnp.log(1.0 - t)).astype(dtype)\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_init, (T,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]    # (1,T,1)\n          y = gamma * y_factor                            # No residual copy\n          return y\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n\
    \          'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'normalize_u': True\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = FactGlobalMLP_NoRC_LearnGamma(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = True  # for Dropout\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 512)),\n          dropout_rate=float(hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n      )\n\n\
    \  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FactGlobalMLP-NoRC Baseline (p=32,H=512x2,dr=0.10) — No γ, Adam lr=9e-4, Clip=1.0\"\ntags: \"mlp, no-residual-copy, layernorm, factorized-loadings, baseline, generalization\"\nabstract: \"Control for the generalization study: Factorized Global MLP + LN without residual copy and without learnable γ. Config: p=32, H=512×2, dr=0.10, Adam lr=9e−4, clip=1.0, curvature λ=1e−4, 60‑min trials. Paired with the Learnable‑γ variant to isolate γ’s effect when RC is removed.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import\
    \ optax\n\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  class FactGlobalMLP_NoRC(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      hidden_size: int = 512\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      normalize_u: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n          T = self.output_horizon\n\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)            # (B,4,p)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)  # (B,4,k)\n\n          factors_n = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_in)           # (B,4,k)\n\n          f_flat = factors_n.reshape(B\
    \ * k, T_in)          # (B*k,4)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          f_out = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)          # (B,T,p)\n          y = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)              # (B,T,N), no γ, no RC\n          return y\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'hidden_size': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'normalize_u': True\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.model = FactGlobalMLP_NoRC(**kwargs)\n          self.needs_rng = True  # for\
    \ Dropout\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Wrapper(\n          rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n          proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n          hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 512)),\n          dropout_rate=float(hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n          normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n      )\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning model adjustments**\n\nI need to map out our next steps after getting the reviewer’s feedback. They suggest we could ablate the MLP RC head and possibly reduce the MLP's depth. The tokens are currently at 55%, so pruning more might be necessary, but we need to consider the cooldown. I think we should implement an MLP variant with a single hidden layer while adding learnable gamma, then test performance compared to the baseline. We should also run a control MLP to gauge effects.**Designing experiments for model testing**\n\nI need to plan out two or three experiments for our MLP models. First, I want to test the MLP without an RC with dimensions 2x512 and learnable gamma to see if that helps performance. Then, I'll run a control without gamma. The third experiment will involve an MLP with an RC at a depth of 1 layer and incorporating learnable gamma. Since we can submit two experiments concurrently, I'll prioritize the most informative pair to directly address\
  \ the feedback. I'll also need to modify the model to remove the residual copy head for the no RC version.**Preparing submission content**\n\nI’m working on creating the submission content, including hyperparameters and network code. I'm setting parameters like dropout at 0.10, with a hidden size of 512 and 2 layers; p is 32, and Adam's learning rate will be 9e-4 with clipping at 1.0 and curvature lambda at 1e-4. I plan to run two submissions: one with learnable gamma and one as a baseline without gamma. I'll ensure LayerNorm is included in the MLP baseline while removing y_copy for no RC. I also need to make sure we're passing RNGs properly for dropout.**Coding the network structure**\n\nI need to define an optional test() function, but it’s not completely necessary. I’m writing code for the network with factorized loadings U and V, ensuring normalize_u is set to True. The input shape will be (B, 4, N). I’ll compute xU and factors_in, then apply LayerNorm. The structure will flatten to\
  \ B*k x 4, followed by MLP layers. For learnable gamma, I'll define a parameter with a stable initialization. \n\nIn the baseline, I’ll skip gamma and ensure the return dimension is correct. I’ll also set the batch size to 8 and use Optax for optimization, exporting gamma and stats later.**Preparing submissions and code**\n\nSince the `complete()` function is allowed, I can pass it in without issues. I need to write two separate submissions, so I’ll create one with learnable gamma and the other as a baseline without gamma. It might be simpler to use separate classes, like \"FactGlobalMLP_NoRC_LearnGamma\" and \"FactGlobalMLP_NoRC,\" to avoid any collisions. I’ll make sure to set `self.needs_rng` to True and use `nn.LayerNorm()` without arguments for LayerNorm. \n\nAfter submission, I'll think about updating archives, but for now, let's just focus on submitting these experiments. I'll import necessary libraries and set our hidden size to 512 as planned. I'll start by going to research followed\
  \ by the submission commands."
