tick: 236
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FF-LN LearnableGamma + MonotoneReg (λm=1e-5) + SmoothReg (λs=5e-6) — p=36,H=160,drop=0.05\"\ntags: \"fourier, layernorm, learnable-gamma, monotonicity, smoothness, regularization\"\nabstract: \"Add small priors to learned horizon weights γ[t]: monotonicity penalty and slope smoothness. Base config p=36, H=160, drop=0.05, Adam lr=9e−4, clip=1.0, curvature λ=1e−4. Hypothesis: priors yield more stable late-horizon emphasis and slight MAE gains over 0.026125.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  from models_fourier_ramp import create_network, export_stats\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  LAM_CURV = 1e-4\n  LAM_MONO = 1e-5    # penalize decreases in gamma\n  LAM_SMOOTH = 5e-6  # penalize large step-to-step changes\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n\
    \          'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 36,\n          'hidden_size': 160,\n          'drop': 0.05,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'learn_gamma': True\n      }\n\n  # Robust param fetch (handles nested PyTrees)\n  def _get_param(tree, key):\n      if isinstance(tree, dict):\n          if key in tree:\n              return tree[key]\n          for v in tree.values():\n              try:\n                  out = _get_param(v, key)\n                  if out is not None:\n                      return out\n              except Exception:\n                  pass\n      return None\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=LAM_CURV)\n      raw = _get_param(params, 'gamma_raw')\n      if raw is None:\n          return base\n      gamma = jax.nn.sigmoid(raw)  # shape (T,)\n      # Monotonicity: penalize decreases (gamma[t]\
    \ < gamma[t-1])\n      dg = gamma[1:] - gamma[:-1]\n      mono_pen = jnp.sum(jnp.square(jnp.clip(-dg, a_min=0.0)))\n      # Smoothness: penalize large slopes\n      smooth_pen = jnp.sum(jnp.square(dg))\n      return base + LAM_MONO * mono_pen + LAM_SMOOTH * smooth_pen\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      export_stats(params, trial_data, _define_hyperparameters(), out_dir=\"storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_priors/mono_smooth_l1e5_s5e6\")\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FF-LN LearnableGamma + Stronger MonotoneReg (λm=2e-5) — p=36,H=160,drop=0.05\"\ntags: \"fourier, layernorm, learnable-gamma, monotonicity, regularization\"\nabstract: \"Sweep monotonicity prior strength on γ[t]. Same base as SOTA (p=36, H=160, drop=0.05, Adam lr=9e−4, clip=1.0, curvature\
    \ λ=1e−4). No smoothness term; only monotone penalty λm=2e−5.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  from models_fourier_ramp import create_network, export_stats\n  from losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  LAM_CURV = 1e-4\n  LAM_MONO = 2e-5  # stronger monotonicity penalty\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 36,\n          'hidden_size': 160,\n          'drop': 0.05,\n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'learn_gamma': True\n      }\n\n  def _get_param(tree, key):\n      if isinstance(tree, dict):\n          if key in tree:\n              return tree[key]\n          for v in tree.values():\n              try:\n                  out = _get_param(v, key)\n                  if out is not None:\n                      return out\n\
    \              except Exception:\n                  pass\n      return None\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=LAM_CURV)\n      raw = _get_param(params, 'gamma_raw')\n      if raw is None:\n          return base\n      gamma = jax.nn.sigmoid(raw)\n      dg = gamma[1:] - gamma[:-1]\n      mono_pen = jnp.sum(jnp.square(jnp.clip(-dg, a_min=0.0)))\n      return base + LAM_MONO * mono_pen\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      export_stats(params, trial_data, _define_hyperparameters(), out_dir=\"storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_priors/mono_l2e5\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to figure out our next actions based on the progress in the Archive Room. The paper is accepted, but there's an addenda. They've made significant progress on MLP generalization without visible benefits, and the shallow ablation didn’t yield any gains either. Token usage is at 59%, so pruning isn’t urgent. One option is to explore Fourier priors on gamma as mentioned earlier or consider a condition-wise gamma since condition labels are available in the dataset.**Updating archive strategy**\n\nI'm considering updating the archive with the shallow results since we've already added Addendum 3. My plan is to propose and submit two controlled experiments. The first involves learnable gamma with entropy regularization or a monotonicity constraint using cumulative sigmoid parameterization, which means modifying the models to include this regulation term in the compute_loss. The second experiment focuses on condition-wise gamma by adjusting it\
  \ with a scale vector derived from labels, but I'm unsure how to access those labels in the compute interface.**Evaluating gamma and labels**\n\nIn the earlier code, I noticed it mentions \"Loading ZAPBench data with condition labels,\" but it seems the methods don't actually use those labels. However, the training loop might leverage labels if the model incorporates them. Since the network only receives x, I could consider implementing condition-agnostic gamma priors. Another option is to adjust dropout or tweak H around 160. Combining a monotonic prior on gamma with mild dropout and exporting gamma profiles could also help. Given the accepted capsule, I might propose a new archive explaining why learnable gamma fails to assist MLP, referencing our ablation results already included in Addenda to capsule #12.**Preparing for Fourier runs**\n\nNow that I'm within the station, I'm ready to submit two Fourier LN runs. The first will involve learnable gamma with a monotonicity penalty set to\
  \ lambda_m (like 1e-5) for negative slopes, and we might include optional entropy regularization to prevent extremes. I plan to add a penalty term in compute_loss to discourage high curvature in gamma while encouraging smoothness. For submission, I'll reference models_fourier_ramp with 'learn_gamma' set to True, and retrieve gamma parameters appropriately, ensuring they are computed correctly within the provided setup. I'll decide on specifics like H=160, p=36, dropout at 0.05, and a learning rate of 9e-4, with a clipping baseline of 1.0.**Planning two runs with regularization**\n\nI can set up two runs using regularization techniques. The first involves a monotonicity penalty, where I add a term to the loss that penalizes the differences between consecutive gamma values. The second run will apply slope L2 smoothness to encourage a smoother transition in gamma. I'll set small values for the penalties: lam_m at 1e-5 and lam_s at 5e-6. \n\nAlternatively, I could test non-decreasing parameterization\
  \ using cumulative softplus deltas, but that would require more invasive changes to the network. To keep things simple, I'll implement regularization in compute_loss instead. My plan is to submit two experiments: one with the initial lam parameters, and another with a stronger monotonicity penalty. I'll also hook into the export stats for tracking purposes."
