thinking_content: "**Analyzing the export issue**\n\nI see that the gamma profile is showing as a fixed ramp, and the seed 42 file has an incorrect val_mae of 0.05 when it should be around 0.026. This means there was a bug in the earlier export. The new export will write to a specific storage path with gamma extracted from params after evaluation finishes.\n\nNow, I’m wondering what I can do. We could analyze existing evaluation predictions for per-condition step MAEs, but we lack saved predictions for Fourier LN learnable gamma. However, I noticed we might be able to access labels from earlier logs. So, possibly we can write a script for loading the dataset and running inference.**Evaluating analysis options**\n\nI could write an offline analysis script to parse gamma_profile and compute monotonicity metrics, but I think I'll hold off for now. \n\nAlternatively, I could shift to Token Management to prune more ticks, considering cooldowns. The last prune was at tick 240, and now I'm at tick\
  \ 245. It seems I can prune again soon, as the system mentioned another prune action available after 4 ticks. \n\nI might prune larger ticks like 239, 234, or 233, but I need to ensure I keep enough context for summaries while doing this.**Interpreting app instructions**\n\nThe instructions are clear: the app requires commands mainly for rooms, and responses should include only the necessary commands. It looks like only /execute_action blocks and immediate YAML blocks will be parsed, treating everything else as commentary. \n\nSo I think I should keep things minimal. I could either wait for evaluation 485 or check for running experiments. In the meantime, I can compute gamma monotonicity from the previously saved ramp. However, this might not be very helpful. Maybe I should plan to create an archive addendum for capsule #12 about the export fix once I have gamma.**Optimizing actions**\n\nConsidering the focus on minimal verbosity, I think I should issue only a small set of actions. One\
  \ optional step could be ranking scores to see if any new experiments showed improvement. Staying in research seems unnecessary for now. \n\nAdditionally, I might go to Token Management to prune large ticks since I'm at tick 245, and the last prune was at tick 240. I need to check if the typical cooldown of 4 ticks applies, as I might still be in cooldown. Reducing tokens would be a good move!**Planning pruning actions**\n\nI think I should attempt to prune ticks 239 and 233, but wait, 233 was already pruned earlier. It's confusing since it's still showing with a length of 3811, even after I pruned 231-233 at tick 240. \n\nIt looks like I can still prune more ticks like 229, 230, 234, 236, 237, and 239. I get that the default is to avoid heavy content, so I'll need concise yet informative summaries for my prune blocks.\n\nI can create blocks for 228-230, 234, 236-237, and 239, providing summaries for each as follows. For 228-230, I'll mention the p-sweep with learnable γ results, and for\
  \ 234, I’ll highlight the shallow MLP runs and archive addendum. The 236-237 summary can note the submitted monotone regs, and for 239, I'll just reflect on the archive addendum and the cooldown situation. \n\nAfter crafting these, I’ll execute the prune action and move over to Token Management!"
