thinking_content: '**Finalizing research actions**


  I recognize that the user is continuing their research and token management without asking specific questions. Right now, we''re at the Research Counter, and I''ve analyzed per-condition residual gating, regressing IDs 492 and 494. It seems like it would be best to consolidate our efforts and stop this line for now. I could update the archive, which is already done, and consider pruning tokens since the cooldown might be over. Additionally, I want to compare our results with global SOTA!**Analyzing SOTA results**


  I noticed we had even better SOTA with ID 344 at around -0.026355, but our result of -0.026125 shows improvement, surpassing the earlier MLP SOTA of -0.026573. So far, our Fourier LN with learnable gamma is performing well. Now, for the next steps: we can do analysis by compiling figures, but since we can''t produce images in our system, I might write JSON to update the archive. I could compute aggregated metrics across seeds and summarize differences between residual gating and baseline MAEs to verify any degradation.**Finalizing pruning strategy**


  I’m considering proposing a “Best-Settings reproduction & seeds list” along with a private memory note. However, my current role requires focusing on progress and publishing, especially since I’ve already published multiple times. It''s crucial to maintain token hygiene, so I should prune large ticks since the cooldown might have expired. I see that the last prune at tick 257 indicated a cooldown. Now, at tick 258, I should be able to prune again, targeting large ticks from 248 to 256, excluding 248 since it was pruned previously.**Reviewing pruning actions**


  I see that tick 248 still shows a count of 3743, even though we attempted to prune it along with 249 and 250 earlier at tick 256. It seems the prune didn''t go through due to a cooldown. Since it didn''t happen before, I should run the prune again for the 248-250 range to compress. Both ticks 249 and 250 are heavy, so I’ll add a summary that we''ve already written. Maybe I should also consider pruning 251-256, but not 256 since it includes evaluation results. I’ll work on this while making sure not to overlap prune blocks!**Preparing to prune tokens**


  I can prune ticks 251-256 with a summary of the negative residual gating results and updates to the archive. I’ll create prune blocks like this: for ticks 248-250, I’ll reuse the summary from our previous analysis and exports. For ticks 251-256, the summary will focus on the residual gating regressions of ±7% (ID 492) and ±5% (ID 494), detailing the rolled archive addenda. I need to ensure proper YAML formatting as we proceed. Since we’re in the Research Counter, I first need to move to Token Management before executing the prune response. Let’s keep the messages concise!'
