parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_condition_analysis.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Fourier LN + Learnable γ[t] — Condition-wise Analysis (Consolidation)\n\n  Context\n  - Best config: p=36, H=160, drop=0.05, Adam lr=9e−4, clip=1.0, curvature λ=1e−4.\n  - Refs: IDs 443/450 (0.026125); re-run/export IDs 485/489.\n  - Artifacts:\n    * γ[t] params (per seed): storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_export_v2/trial_{42,43,44,45}.json\n    * Per-condition step-MAE (+γ): storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_per_condition/trial_{43,44,45}.json\n    * Repro README: storage/ariadne/analyses/README_fourier_learn_gamma.txt\n\n  Key findings (from exports)\n  - γ[t] is non-monotonic, peaking around t≈20–24 at ~0.90–0.94, then tapering to ~0.70–0.74 by t=32.\n  - Late-horizon error concentrates in specific conditions (consistently cond7, cond4 highest; cond1/cond6 lowest). Condition 3 absent on validation (NaNs).\n \
    \ - Variation across seeds is modest; profiles are qualitatively consistent.\n\n  Implications\n  - The fixed learned γ[t] already adapts to mean horizon difficulty across all conditions.\n  - Residual, input-adaptive modulation at the output level did not help (IDs 492/494: regressions to ~0.02630–0.02634).\n\n  If pursuing condition-aware γ (only if analysis predicts >2e−5 gain)\n  - Mechanism: small per-condition offsets in γ_raw[t]:\n      γ_raw'[t] = γ_raw[t] + b_c[t], where c is the condition label.\n    Constraints/regularization:\n      * Sum-to-zero across conditions per t (∑_c b_c[t] = 0) to preserve global average.\n      * L2 regularization on b_c[t] with strength chosen so ||b||_2 is small; optional temporal TV penalty on b_c to avoid spiky offsets.\n  - Protocol:\n      * 3 seeds, 60-min timeout, identical hparams otherwise.\n      * Accept only if mean MAE improvement ≥ 2e−5 vs 0.026125 and no degradation at t=1–8.\n      * Export per-condition γ profiles and step-MAEs;\
    \ verify improvements concentrate in previously hard conditions.\n\n  Conclusion\n  - We freeze the current SOTA (0.026125) as the production baseline.\n  - Further runs on this line are paused unless pre-analysis suggests a clear >2e−5 upside.\n```\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 12}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Condition-wise γ[t] analysis and guardrails\"\ncontent: |\n  Added consolidated condition-wise analysis for the Fourier LN + learnable γ[t] SOTA at:\n  storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_condition_analysis.md\n\n  Highlights:\n  - γ[t] is non-monotonic (peaks ~t=20–24, tapers by t=32).\n  - Hard late-horizon conditions (cond7/cond4) dominate errors; cond1/cond6 easier; cond3 absent on val.\n  - Residual output-level adaptation regressed (IDs 492/494).\n\n  Guardrails for any follow-up:\n  - Consider only small per-condition γ_raw offsets with sum-to-zero constraint + L2 (and optional TV) regularization.\n  - Accept changes only if ≥2e−5 mean MAE gain over\
    \ 0.026125 across 3 seeds with no early-horizon regression.\n  - Otherwise, keep the current model as the production baseline and focus on interpretability.\n```"
