  \ 42 showed stability with 0.026125. However, the new base seed 3407 yields a mean of 0.026419 across its seeds, indicating some dependency on seed selection. The magnitude of 2.9e-4 suggests a lack of robustness, so reporting the mean and standard deviation across base seeds would be essential.**Computing cross-base-seed mean**\n\nI’m suggesting we compute the cross-base-seed mean, estimating 0.026272 as the average across the two base sets available. However, since we only have two base sets, it might be better to propose that the scoreboard uses the mean across three seeds from just one base. The current state-of-the-art remains at 0.026125, so no adjustments are needed there. \n\nWith base seed 42, the value is -0.026125, and with base seed 3407, it’s -0.026419. This shows a variation of approximately 0.000294, or about 1.1%. I'm careful to ensure the variation aligns with other results. We might consider optional replicates with more base seeds, but further experiments can be avoided\
