    \  - Roadmap + README: storage/ariadne/analyses/ROADMAP.md, README_fourier_learn_gamma.txt\n\n  Negative results (avoid)\n  - γ-priors (monotone/smooth): regressed to ~0.02632–0.02633 (IDs 472/473).\n  - Output-level residual γ modulation: regressed to ~0.02630–0.02634 (IDs 492/494).\n  - MLP generalization (factorized MLP + RC + LN): no improvement (~0.0270, IDs 462/463); shallow MLP also no help (IDs 467/468).\n\n  Reproduction (submission interface)\n  - Use models_fourier_ramp.py with learn_gamma=True; set p=36, H=160, drop=0.05, lr=9e−4, clip=1.0; curvature λ=1e−4 in compute_loss.\n  - Export via complete(): call export_stats(params, trial_data, hparams) to write γ[t] and per-condition metrics.\n\n  Guardrails and Next Work (only if clearly >2e−5 projected gain)\n  - Analysis-only: correlate γ[t] with condition difficulty using existing exports.\n  - If a robust pattern emerges, consider condition-aware γ offsets (label-based) with strong regularization; otherwise stop.\n  - Always\
    \ cite both base-seed sets when reporting; include artifact paths for reproducibility.\n\n  Alternative strong line (for pivot)\n  - Factorized Global MLP + RC + LN, p=32, H=512×2, dropout=0.10, AdamW wd=1e−4: ~0.026645 (ID 247).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating project steps**\n\nI'm thinking about proposing a text file aggregator that focuses on analysis only, where we don’t execute computations ourselves but derive numbers from previous results. For example, we can calculate a mean using given numbers. \n\nNext, I want to create a \"CHECKLIST.md\" with acceptance criteria related to gamma. It'd be useful to summarize a note about closing and exiting, yet I’m considering proceeding to reflect on our progress. There's also a \"Critical Notice: Research Inactivity\" that we previously managed.**Finalizing documentation steps**\n\nI’m thinking of storing a \"final_handoff.md\" that includes an ordered list of seeds, configurations, and commands to reproduce things, along with a warning about base seed variations. Then I’ll wrap up this task. \n\nI need to manage tokens too, but there’s a cooldown after previous pruning, so I can't do that right now. I’ll focus on a few key actions: moving to the Research Counter, writing\
  \ the file summary, and potentially considering an exit, though it might not be necessary.**Executing final steps**\n\nI see it’s not strictly necessary, but the Next Steps meta suggests I maintain analysis only, which I’ve done. Now, I’m ready to execute a couple of actions. \n\nI’ll head to the research section and store the \"final_handoff.md\" with a concise summary. This should include the recommended reproduction configuration, artifact paths, seeds, any negative results, future candidate thresholds, and contact information. It’s important to keep everything clear and brief. Alright, let’s get to it!"
