tick: 275
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage list ariadne/analyses}\n/execute_action{storage list ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_per_condition}\n/execute_action{storage list ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_export_v2}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis v2: Recursive scan γ[t] vs per-condition difficulty (robust paths)\"\ntags: \"analysis, fourier, learnable-gamma, condition-wise, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"CPU-only test() that recursively scans storage/ariadne/analyses for γ profiles and per-condition MAEs, then computes correlations and saves summary to cond_gamma_correlation_v2.json.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, re\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def _is_gamma_json(obj):\n      if not isinstance(obj, dict): return False\n      for k in (\"gamma\", \"gamma_profile\", \"gamma_t\", \"gamma_values\"):\n          v = obj.get(k, None)\n          if isinstance(v, (list, tuple)) and len(v) in (32,):\n              return True\n      # occasional nested storage\n      if \"\
    params\" in obj and isinstance(obj[\"params\"], dict):\n          v = obj[\"params\"].get(\"gamma\", None)\n          if isinstance(v, (list, tuple)) and len(v) in (32,):\n              return True\n      return False\n\n  def _extract_gamma(obj):\n      for k in (\"gamma\", \"gamma_profile\", \"gamma_t\", \"gamma_values\"):\n          v = obj.get(k, None)\n          if isinstance(v, (list, tuple)):\n              arr = np.array(v, dtype=float)\n              if arr.ndim == 1 and arr.size == 32:\n                  return arr\n      if \"params\" in obj and isinstance(obj[\"params\"], dict):\n          v = obj[\"params\"].get(\"gamma\", None)\n          if isinstance(v, (list, tuple)):\n              arr = np.array(v, dtype=float)\n              if arr.ndim == 1 and arr.size == 32:\n                  return arr\n      return None\n\n  def _is_percond_json(obj):\n      if not isinstance(obj, dict): return False\n      cand = None\n      if \"per_condition_step_mae\" in obj: cand = obj[\"\
    per_condition_step_mae\"]\n      elif \"val_mae_by_condition\" in obj: cand = obj[\"val_mae_by_condition\"]\n      if isinstance(cand, dict):\n          # at least one condition has a length-32 list\n          for v in cand.values():\n              if isinstance(v, (list, tuple)) and len(v) == 32:\n                  return True\n      return False\n\n  def _extract_percond(obj):\n      if \"per_condition_step_mae\" in obj:\n          cand = obj[\"per_condition_step_mae\"]\n      elif \"val_mae_by_condition\" in obj:\n          cand = obj[\"val_mae_by_condition\"]\n      else:\n          return {}\n      out = {}\n      for ck, v in cand.items():\n          arr = np.array(v, dtype=float)\n          if arr.ndim == 1 and arr.size == 32 and not np.isnan(arr).any():\n              out[str(ck)] = arr\n      return out\n\n  def test():\n      base_dir = \"storage/ariadne/analyses\"\n      T = 32\n      gamma_list = []\n      percond_list = []\n      # recursive scan\n      for root, _, files\
    \ in os.walk(base_dir):\n          for fn in files:\n              if not fn.endswith(\".json\"): continue\n              path = os.path.join(root, fn)\n              try:\n                  with open(path, \"r\") as f:\n                      obj = json.load(f)\n              except Exception:\n                  continue\n              if _is_gamma_json(obj):\n                  g = _extract_gamma(obj)\n                  if g is not None and g.size == T:\n                      gamma_list.append((path, g))\n              if _is_percond_json(obj):\n                  pc = _extract_percond(obj)\n                  if pc:\n                      percond_list.append((path, pc))\n\n      summary = {\n          \"gamma_files\": len(gamma_list),\n          \"per_condition_files\": len(percond_list),\n          \"base_dir\": base_dir,\n      }\n\n      if not gamma_list or not percond_list:\n          out = {\"ok\": False, \"reason\": \"Insufficient files\", **summary}\n      else:\n          G =\
    \ np.vstack([g for _, g in gamma_list])        # (S,T)\n          gamma_mean = G.mean(axis=0)\n          gamma_std  = G.std(axis=0)\n\n          # Merge per-condition across all files by keyed union\n          cond_acc = {}\n          for _, pc in percond_list:\n              for ck, arr in pc.items():\n                  cond_acc.setdefault(ck, []).append(arr)\n          cond_stats = {}\n          for ck, lst in cond_acc.items():\n              M = np.vstack(lst)\n              if M.shape[1] != T or np.isnan(M).any(): continue\n              cond_stats[ck] = {\n                  \"mean\": M.mean(axis=0).tolist(),\n                  \"std\":  M.std(axis=0).tolist(),\n                  \"count\": int(M.shape[0]),\n              }\n\n          # Overall step difficulty\n          if cond_stats:\n              step_mae_mean = np.vstack([np.array(v[\"mean\"]) for v in cond_stats.values()]).mean(axis=0)\n          else:\n              step_mae_mean = np.full((T,), np.nan)\n\n          def\
    \ safe_corr(a, b):\n              a = np.asarray(a, dtype=float); b = np.asarray(b, dtype=float)\n              if np.isnan(a).any() or np.isnan(b).any(): return None\n              if a.std() == 0 or b.std() == 0: return None\n              return float(np.corrcoef(a, b)[0,1])\n\n          corr_gamma_vs_mean = safe_corr(gamma_mean, step_mae_mean)\n\n          # heuristic potential alignment score\n          def z(x): x=np.asarray(x,dtype=float); return (x-x.mean())/(x.std()+1e-8)\n          potential = None if np.isnan(step_mae_mean).any() else float(np.dot(-z(gamma_mean), z(step_mae_mean))/T)\n\n          out = {\n              \"ok\": True,\n              **summary,\n              \"gamma_mean\": gamma_mean.tolist(),\n              \"gamma_std\": gamma_std.tolist(),\n              \"corr_gamma_vs_step_mae_mean\": corr_gamma_vs_mean,\n              \"potential_alignment_score\": potential,\n              \"conditions_analyzed\": {k: {\"count\": v[\"count\"]} for k,v in cond_stats.items()},\n\
    \          }\n\n      out_path = os.path.join(base_dir, \"cond_gamma_correlation_v2.json\")\n      with open(out_path, \"w\") as f:\n          json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n      print(\"Analysis v2 complete ->\", out_path)\n      return \"OK\"\n```"
thinking_content: "**Listing storage directories**\n\nI need to list storage directories to identify the missing files. The earlier summary mentioned that the per-condition step-MAEs are saved under a specific path, but the indication that \"loaded_per_condition_count\" is 0 suggests they might not be found. The files previously listed suggest that the directory could exist under similar names, so I think I'll explore variations. I'll run commands to check available files and identify the right directory to potentially re-run the analysis if needed.**Fixing correlation file issues**\n\nI see that the `test()` function created a file cond_gamma_correlation.json with an error indicated by \"ok:false.\" To resolve this, I'll need to read from the correct path. First, I should list the storage directories to find the accurate location. Once I identify it, I might want to run `test()` again by submitting the updated path, though I'm aware of potential high token usage. I'll issue storage list\
  \ commands to locate the directories, which will guide my next steps effectively.**Exploring alternative pathways**\n\nI’m considering the option to use the 'Lumina 509' experiment, but there’s limited storage for other lineages, and I need to check if we can read those storages. Per my notes, I can read but not write or delete, which means listing from 'storage/ariadne/analyses' first is essential. Once I identify the files, I could either resubmit the analysis to those paths or create a new script to dynamically scan for directories containing \"per_condition.\" Let's start with the storage list commands.**Planning analysis submission**\n\nFirst, I’ll execute a sequence of storage list commands to find the necessary directories: 'storage/ariadne/analyses', 'fourier_learn_gamma_per_condition', and 'fourier_learn_gamma_export_v2'. After that, I plan to submit an analysis that recursively scans those directories. I need to remember that during this test mode, scoring isn’t an option, but\
  \ that’s fine. \n\nI’ll walk through the directories to collect gamma JSON files that match 'trial_*.json' and look for per-condition files with specific keys. Then I’ll compute the correlation and save the output. Let’s get started!"
