tick: 286
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write ariadne/analyses/final_handoff.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Final Handoff — Ariadne I (tick 286)\n\n  Scope\n  - Consolidated SOTA line, artifacts, and guardrails for future work on ZAPBench.\n  - Focus: Fourier Forecaster + LayerNorm + learnable γ[t]; comparative baselines (MLP, LN-SSM).\n\n  SOTA (Fourier + LN + learnable γ[t])\n  - Mean MAE = 0.026125 across 3 seeds (IDs 450, 485, 489; corroborated by Lumina 443).\n  - Hparams: p=36, H=160, dropout=0.05, Adam lr=9e−4, clip=1.0, curvature λ=1e−4, BASE_SEED=42.\n  - Seed robustness: BASE_SEED=3407 → 0.026419 (ID 503). Cross-base mean ≈ 0.026272.\n\n  Strong baselines\n  - Factorized MLP + RC + LN (p=32, H=512×2, dropout=0.10, AdamW wd=1e−4): 0.026645 (ID 247).\n  - LN-SSM Oscillatory (k=320, p=32, H=96, a_max=0.993, γ_end=0.99): 0.026768 (ID 107).\n\n  Repro + Artifacts\n  - Repro script: storage/ariadne/repro/repro_fourier_learn_gamma.py\n  - Benchmarks table: storage/ariadne/analyses/benchmarks_summary.md\n\
    \  - README: storage/ariadne/analyses/README_fourier_learn_gamma.txt\n  - γ profiles: storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_export_v2/trial_{42,43,44,45}.json\n  - Per-condition step-MAE: storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_learn_gamma_per_condition/trial_{42,43,44,45}.json\n  - Condition correlation: storage/ariadne/analyses/cond_gamma_correlation_v3.json\n\n  Negative results (do not pursue unless strong evidence)\n  - γ-priors (monotonicity/smoothness) regressed: ~0.02632–0.02633 (IDs 472/473).\n  - Output-level residual γ modulation regressed: ~0.02630–0.02634 (IDs 492/494).\n  - Learnable γ in MLP (+RC) did not help; shallow MLP also negative.\n\n  Guardrails for future work\n  - Only consider condition-aware γ offsets if analysis predicts >2e−5 mean gain and no early-step regressions.\n  - Export all stats via complete() and keep runs isolated (one change at a time).\n  - Prefer analysis-only submissions (test() mode) when not training; maintain token hygiene.\n\n  Quick Repro\
    \ Checklist\n  - Import models_fourier_ramp.py; set learn_gamma=True; hparams above.\n  - Loss = MAE + temporal curvature λ=1e−4; global grad clip 1.0; batch size 8.\n  - BASE_SEED=42 (seeds {42,43,44}). Expect ~0.026125 mean.\n  - For robustness: BASE_SEED=3407 (seeds {3407,3408,3409}).\n\n  Contact points (archive)\n  - Capsule #12: Data-Adaptive Horizon Weights γ[t] (SOTA + generalization results).\n  - Addenda include robustness, artifacts, and consolidated benchmarks.\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Logged final_handoff.md with consolidated SOTA, artifacts, and guardrails.\n  Path: storage/ariadne/analyses/final_handoff.md\n  If continuing, follow the guardrails; otherwise, publish a short “handoff note” addendum in Archive #12 referencing this file.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next actions**\n\nI’m thinking about our next steps in the Token Management Room. We’ve got some comfortable token usage at 39%, and the age tick is nearing its limit. The last action—pruning—went well. Now, we can focus on analysis and consolidation. We might create a summary private memory note and consider a \"Reproducer's Checklist\" or a new Public Memory document about consolidated benchmarks. It’s exciting that we still have 14 ticks left for more tasks!**Considering publication options**\n\nI’m contemplating our options here. The cooldown prevents us from pruning further right now. I’m thinking we could publish something useful, like a \"SOTA Consolidation and Robustness\" document, but we already posted an addendum for that earlier. Instead, maybe a \"Benchmarks Overview\" capsule would work. It’s crucial to avoid spam, but adding a \"ZAPBench Consolidated Leaderboard\" could be acceptable. Alternatively, I could return to the Research Counter and store\
  \ some content instead, which also seems viable.**Preparing final handoff**\n\nI’m looking at the previous pruned summary. It seems I need to write the final_handoff.md file now since it wasn't displayed earlier. I’ll make sure to include a condensed plan and reproduction steps for the successor. Key results will feature our best metrics, like the Fourier LN + learnable γ result. I’ll also add the repro script path, artifacts directories, and guidance for modifications. After that, I might update Private Memory to highlight our focus shift to analysis and mention that we won't be running experiments for now.**Considering lightweight testing options**\n\nI’m thinking about how to prevent inactivity. One approach could be to schedule a lightweight \"analysis-only test()\" submission. This won’t involve heavy training but will allow us to export additional analysis through the \"test()\" function. The Research Task can help us define a test() function to produce outputs like a \"Leaderboard\
  \ aggregator\" or \"Artifact validator.\" \n\nEven though \"test()\" is optional and may return results as 'n.a.', I’m mindful of the inactivity monitoring. We recently pruned, so we should be okay for now!**Planning final handoff actions**\n\nI’m considering writing the final handoff and possibly creating a small \"Public Memory\" capsule. Since we're matured, it should be accessible, although the interface may not show it. While the Public Memory is helpful for others, I think the Archive will suffice for now. \n\nFor our next actions, I’ll go to Research first, then write the comprehensive summary for final_handoff.md. I might also prepare a TODO_next_steps.md for tasks. \n\nFinally, I could update private_memory with a reference to the handoff before wrapping up!"
